INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(1, 86, 30, 'EOI/EMPL/CHiPS/PMU/SUDA/AMRUT 2.0/2024', 1, 'Project Management Unit (PMU) for Technical Support and Transaction Advisory Support For AMRUT 2.0', '36', '<p>The objective of the assignment is to provide assistance to State Urban Development Agency (SUDA) for Program Management Unit (PMU) for Technical Support and Transaction Advisory Support for AMRUT 2.0.<br><br>DGM/CHiPS is inviting all empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No. 68733 /CEO /CHiPS /Empanelment /2020&nbsp;dated 31/10/2020) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as&nbsp; mentioned in this EOI.</p>', 2, 30, '2024-09-20 18:13:23', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 216010800, 10800540, 226811340, 0, 18, 5, '<p>The State Urban Development Agency (SUDA) is a state level nodal agency of Government of Chhattisgarh for&nbsp;various central and state sponsored schemes with mandate of sustainable and planned growth of cities and towns&nbsp;with adequate infrastructure, amenities and services provided to the citizens through the Urban Local Bodies&nbsp;(ULBs). SUDA is involved in ensuring proficient management &amp; service delivery to citizens and civic services like&nbsp;provision of affordable housing, safe drinking water, sanitation including solid waste&nbsp; management, storm water<br>drainage, sewerage, roads, public transport; and creation of livelihood opportunities by accelerating economic<br>growth of cities/ towns, building capacity of all the stake holders of urban development sector and reform<br>implementation</p>', NULL, NULL, '<ul>\r\n<li>The scope of work of Project Management Unit (PMU) shall broadly cover Program Management, Transaction<br>Advisory &amp; Contract Management, Technical Assistance &amp; Support, etc. to the State Urban Development<br>Agency.<br>I. Program Management<br>ï‚· Assist in the adherence of State Action Plan (SAP), Annual Action Plan (AAP) and convergence of AMRUT 2.0<br>Urban with other program&rsquo;s/ schemes.<br>ï‚· Supervise the work of appointed PDMC according to their scope of work including but limited to verification of<br>resources deployed in the projects, evaluation and monitoring of projects implemented by PDMC, etc.<br>ï‚· Assist in the preparation of infrastructure demand gaps.<br>ï‚· The PMU will be responsible for managing and overseeing planning and monitoring activities as per AMRUT 2.0<br>guidelines.<br>ï‚· Coordination with ULB&rsquo;s for regular progress for the mission projects and maintaining all the records and<br>documentation of the project.<br>ï‚· The PMU will facilitate periodic monitoring of projects to review performance against key performance indicators<br>of the contract under the mission.<br>ï‚· Coordination with Government of India and State Government for fund provisioning, planning, financial analysis,<br>utilization, etc.<br>ï‚· Study of best practices for private sector participation/ PPP in Water Supply and Sewerage sector across the globe<br>and bringing relevant experience in Chhattisgarh.<br>ï‚· Assist Mission Directorate in representing State by making all arrangements and documentation for various<br>meetings to review proposals viz. Apex Committee, State High Power Steering Committee (SHPSC), State Level<br>Technical Committee (SLTC) meetings, seminars, conclaves, competition\'s/awards, etc.<br>ï‚· Prepare road map for PPP projects, rejuvenation of water bodies, and reuse of treated water up to maximum extent.<br>ï‚· Preparing Strategy for waterbody restoration development projects.<br>ï‚· Assist in development of Operations and Maintenance policy &amp; Urban Water Supply Policy as per AMRUT 2.0<br>guidelines.<br>ï‚· Assist State in ensuring that all the projects/contract are complying in both, financial and objective of the reform<br>ï‚· Assisting State in identifying and developing projects under the AMRUT 2.0 incentive reforms guidelines.<br>ï‚· Assist in determination and financial planning for User Charges of water supply and sewerage.<br>ï‚· Assist in creating a Dashboard with online monitoring with inbuilt mechanisms for monitoring of schemes as per<br>AMRUT 2.0 guidelines<br>ï‚· Planning, scheduling and monitoring of the projects using PMIS / latest IT tools and techniques. Cost related to<br>procurement of tools or any software/effort estimation for successful implementation of the project monitoring<br>tool, if any shall be considered/borne by the Authority.<br>ï‚· Assist in implementation of overall AMRUT 2.0 mission as per the guidelines.<br>7<br>II. Transaction Advisory &amp; Contract Management<br>ï‚· Evaluate the implementation modalities to execute the projects on Public Private Partnership (PPP) model.<br>ï‚· Financial advice on the development of projects. This includes option assessments, risk identification, analysis<br>and management, development of financial models, funding options, assisting clients in presenting projects to the<br>market and procurement projects.<br>ï‚· The PMU shall develop Standard Bidding Documents for selection of DPR consultants, Third-Party Inspection<br>Agency (TPA), Implementing Support Agency (ISAs) and provide other necessary procurement support as and<br>when required.<br>ï‚· PMU will devise strategy for fast implementation of the project by suitable procurement methods by following<br>General Financial Rules and other related Government of India instructions concerning procurement of goods and<br>services.<br>ï‚· PMU will facilitate the selection of various agencies for carrying out impact assessment studies if any, focused<br>on measuring the impact of these schemes beyond the intended outputs and outcomes.<br>ï‚· PMU shall evaluate the framed tender documents including connected design proposals / drawings, assist the<br>department in tender floating, carry out bid evaluation, drafting responses to queries, award of works, drafting of<br>contract agreements and assist in identifying and reaching out to competent organizations /vendors for<br>participation in the tenders through various mediums such as conducting Investor Consultation Meet,<br>Presentations, Mailers etc.<br>ï‚· Contract administration and management of the projects.<br>III. Technical Assistance &amp; Support<br>ï‚· Provide technical inputs for planning and implementation of the schemes to suit the AMRUT 2.0 Urban<br>requirements.<br>ï‚· Framing innovative models for water supply, sewerage and reuse of treated water projects.<br>ï‚· Prepare Standardized Templates for evaluation of DPRs for the State and District level agencies.<br>ï‚· To guide DPR Consultants in the preparation of feasible and sustainable DPRs considering geographical terrain<br>and climatic conditions.<br>ï‚· Assess the potential reuse of treated waste water from STP&rsquo;s for other non-potable uses in industries and power<br>plants.<br>ï‚· Assist in preparation of Urban Aquifer Management plans<br>ï‚· Advising the authority on various waterbody restoration projects, including review of the project development,<br>cost monitoring, time scheduling and quality control<br>IV. Monitoring &amp; Evaluation<br>ï‚· The PMU will facilitate in tracking of progress.<br>ï‚· The key parameters for tracking the physical and financial progress, both in project preparatory as well<br>implementation phase shall be defined and the follow up for data collection is to be rigorously monitored by PMU<br>Cell.<br>ï‚· Create a platform for AMRUT 2.0, where data/ information is integrated with other projects/ programs.<br>ï‚· Prepare consolidated progress reports or project management including identification of problems, bottlenecks in<br>project implementation, and providing specific recommendation.<br>ï‚· Prepare regular progress report based on IMIS data for different periodicity.<br>ï‚· Guide and facilitate ULBs in providing accurate and timely data.<br>ï‚· Provide inputs for enhancement of existing grievance redressal/ and citizen&rsquo;s feedback system and analyze data<br>and recommend action for grievance redressal.<br>ï‚· Capturing the Statewide information on the demand of Water supply and sewerage requirement along with the<br>supply and gap analysis.<br>ï‚· Assist in convergence of AMRUT 2.0 &amp; State flagship missions.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to&nbsp;this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful&nbsp;study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.<br><br>The last date for submission of response is 07/10/2024, 05:00 PM. Any response received after the above deadline&nbsp;will be rejected. The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to</p>', '<p>ï‚· The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the agreed empanelment<br>terms on the submission of Monthly Progress Report.<br>ï‚· For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or CHiPS, as the case may be selected bidder shall be paid<br>the requisite man month payment in the event that selected bidder has performed on its obligations in compliance<br>with the terms of this contract.<br><br>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>', NULL, '<p>Evaluation committee shall be formed decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression<br>of Interest.<br>ï‚· No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/ discussion with the Committee.<br>ï‚· The bidding company will make a presentation about their understanding of the scope of work and the proposed<br>team for the project<br>ï‚· The committee shall review the projects and CV submitted along with the presentation and award the marking.<br>ï‚· The marking shall be as per the table below &ndash;<br>12<br>Presentation on A&amp;M Firm&rsquo;s Experience<br>50 Marks 50 Marks<br>Key Evaluation<br>Criteria<br>ï‚· Understanding of the Project<br>ï‚· Approach and Methodology<br>ï‚· Execution Plan for the Chhattisgarh State<br>ï‚· On technical experience of the firm<br>Note:<br>i. All experience should be in the name of the firm bidding for the project. Experience of sister / associate firms<br>shall not be eligible.<br>ii. Only assignments where work order is issued directly by a govt. entity/ Donor Agency to the firm bidding for<br>the project shall be eligible. Assignments which are carried out via any third party/ private agency/ Sub-let<br>shall not be considered for evaluation.<br>iii. The assignments involving construction supervision/ payment certification shall not be considered as eligible<br>assignments. Further, standalone assignments for preparation of DPR / construction supervision consultancy<br>/ payment certificate / Design supervision consultancy / Owner\'s Engineer assignments or similar assignments<br>shall not be considered as eligible assignments.<br>iv. Only assignments undertaken directly by the agency will be considered eligible. Experiences or assignments<br>from sister, associate or subsidiary firms will not be recognized or considered. Further, to be eligible, the<br>contract signing or work order must be exclusively issued by a Government Entity</p>', '<p>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to&nbsp;this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful&nbsp;study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.&nbsp;The last date for submission of response is 07/10/2024, 05:00 PM. Any response received after the above deadline&nbsp;will be rejected. The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to<br>Chief Executive Officer<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS), State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil<br>Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001, Tel.: +91-771-4014158<br>Email: ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in</p>', '<p>ï‚· Signed copy of this EOI<br>ï‚· Copy of Approach and methodology presentation<br>ï‚· Resumes of resources. The format of resumes will be as per empanelment tender number<br>68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020.</p>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-28 18:23:19', 4, 1, '2025-10-28 18:17:47', 30, '2025-10-28 18:23:19', NULL, '2025-10-28 18:28:18', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-28', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Program Management Unit (PMU) For Technical Support And Transaction Advisory Support For AMRUT 2.0.', '2024-09-20', '2024-09-23 17:00:00', '2024-10-07 00:00:00', '2024-10-08 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-10', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/f3OvDkkxEIFin3yeXnh1gXVHaXqs0dIn6934EPvp.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 154812712.5, 0, 0, 27866288.25, 182679000.75, 1, 0, NULL, NULL),
(2, 79, 29, 'EOI/EMPL/CHIPS/PMU/PRD/Samvad/2025', 1, 'For selection of Project Management Unit (PMU) for Chhattisgarh Samvad, Public Relations Department', '12', '<p>CHiPS is inviting all empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No. 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/31-10-2020) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.<br><br>Chhattisgarh Samvad, Public Relations Department is seeking to establish a Program Management Unit&nbsp;(PMU) with professional consultants for the planning, implementation, and monitoring of various&nbsp;activities of the department. The scope of work for the PMU will broadly encompass the comprehensive&nbsp;management of projects, activities, and components of Chhattisgarh Samvad, ensuring alignment with&nbsp;the government guidelines.<br><br>The PMU will provide end-to-end consultancy support and handholding to Chhattisgarh Samvad,&nbsp;facilitating the preparation of all necessary plans for the State to fulfil its role as a medium and a liaison&nbsp;in the regular exchange of government information between the government and the public. This support&nbsp;will include planning, policy formulation, and the monitoring of progress of the projects. Additionally,&nbsp;the PMU will focus on capacity building, knowledge management, and other critical aspects of program&nbsp;management and implementation.</p>', 2, 29, '2025-01-04 19:16:36', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 17416800, 870840, 18287640, 0, 18, 5, '<p>The Public Relations Department plays an important role as a medium and a liaison in the regular exchange&nbsp;of government information between the government and the public. The department acts as a bridge between&nbsp;the government, administration, public and the fourth pillar of democracy, media. The main objective of the&nbsp;department is to convey information about the policies, programs and public welfare decisions of the state&nbsp;government to the general public with the help of various means of mass communication (newspapers, radio,&nbsp;television, social media and outdoor publicity etc.).<br><br>The work of government publicity is being done by the Directorate of Public Relations located in Nava Raipur&nbsp;and Chhattisgarh Information Center, New Delhi along with all the 33 district public relations offices under it.&nbsp;Through these offices, publication material such as news, special articles, success stories etc. based on various&nbsp;government activities and achievements are regularly made available to the news media. Under area publicity,&nbsp;the department also does government publicity work through photo exhibition and selected art groups,&nbsp;information camps. For the exchange of information between the Directorate, District Public Relations Offices<br>and the media, news and information are communicated through website, e-mail and social media.<br><br>Chhattisgarh Samvad - Associate organization of Public Relations Department<br><br>Chhattisgarh Samvad is a self-financed organization, formed by the state government as an associate&nbsp;organization of the Public Relations Department under the Firm and Society Act 1973 and as a registered&nbsp;society. Chhattisgarh Samvad has been registered as a charitable trust by the Income Tax Commissioner&nbsp;under Section 12 (1) of the Income Tax Act 1961 and income tax is determined accordingly.<br><br>Chhattisgarh Samvad does not receive any kind of budget/grant from the state government. As per the decision&nbsp;taken by the government, the work of publicity and printing and publication of the schemes of the government&nbsp;departments, undertakings, corporations and government institutions is done through Chhattisgarh Samvad.&nbsp;Chhattisgarh Samvad charges 10% over the actual cost for the work done and 5% extra is charged in the&nbsp;advertisement dues of Public Relations Directorate and Chhattisgarh State Electricity Company.</p>', NULL, NULL, '<p>The scope of work to be undertaken by Project Management Unit is given herein after and the same is merely<br>illustrative and not exhaustive. The Project Management Unit shall thus have to consider the required output<br>and include all further incidental activities that may be necessary for efficient and successful implementation<br>and for achieving the ultimate objective of the assignment.<br>The key activities for the proposed engagement will primarily consist of the following:<br>ï‚§ Planning and Management Support: Assisting in the strategic planning and management of Chhattisgarh<br>Samvad projects and activities.<br>ï‚§ Project Design and Development: Developing detailed project designs and ensuring they meet the<br>required standards and guidelines.<br>ï‚§ Bid Process Management: Assist Chhattisgarh Samvad during the entire bidding process, including the<br>preparation of bid documents, evaluation of bids, and contract management.<br><br>ï‚§ Progress Monitoring: The monitoring of progress of projects and activities, ensuring they remain on track<br>and within budget.<br>ï‚§ MIS Support: Design solutions for Management Information Systems (MIS) for better project and<br>activities tracking and reporting.<br>ï‚§ IEC and Capacity Building: Conducting IEC campaigns and capacity-building programs to enhance the<br>skills and knowledge of stakeholders.<br>ï‚§ Coordination and Stakeholder Management: Ensuring effective coordination among various<br>stakeholders, including state authorities, district authorities and other partners.<br>ï‚§ Other Support: Providing additional support as required for the successful implementation of<br>Chhattisgarh Samvad initiatives.</p>', NULL, '<p>Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule.<br>ï‚· The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the agreed<br>empanelment terms.<br>ï‚· For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or CHiPS, as the case may be selected bidder<br>shall be paid the requisite man month payment in the event that selected bidder has performed on<br>its obligations in compliance with the terms of this contract.<br><br>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>', NULL, '<p>ï‚· CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the&nbsp;evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be&nbsp;entertained outside the process of negotiation/ discussion with the Committee.<br>ï‚· A presentation will be made by the bidding company about their understanding of the&nbsp;proposed area of work and their experience if any in similar area of expertise (Via Video&nbsp;Conference).<br>ï‚· During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the&nbsp;proposed candidates (Physically/Via Video Conference).<br>ï‚· The marking for presentation and Interview will be done as followsBidder Presentation Candidate Interview&nbsp;50 Marks 50 Marks<br>Key&nbsp;Evaluation&nbsp;Criteria<br>ï‚· Approach and Methodology<br>ï‚· Understanding of the Project&nbsp;Framework<br>ï‚· Quality of proposed methodology&nbsp;for such specific kind of a project<br>ï‚· Prior experience in project&nbsp;interaction with senior Government&nbsp;officials<br>ï‚· Prior exposure to Auditing&nbsp;Government projects<br>ï‚· Resource deployment at multiple&nbsp;government officesin multiple locations<br>ï‚· Understanding of key SLAs of project&nbsp;management<br>ï‚· Suitability of profile<br>ï‚· Years of relevant experience<br>ï‚· Good understanding of&nbsp;project management best&nbsp;practicesframework<br>ï‚· Ability to&nbsp;Negotiate/Persuade/Influence<br>ï‚· Strong ability to understand&nbsp;and deliberate and report&nbsp;monitor the key SLAs<br>ï‚· Excellent communication&nbsp;abilities</p>', '<p>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in<br>response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions&nbsp;and implications.<br>The last date for submission of response is 10/01/2025, 17:00 Hrs; Any response received after the above&nbsp;deadline will be rejected.</p>', '<p>Signed copy of this EOI.<br>ï‚· Experience of the bidding firm along with relevant Work Orders/ documents.<br>ï‚· Copy of Approach and methodology presentation.<br>ï‚· Resumes of resources that will face the interview. The format of resumes will be as<br>per empanelment tender number 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020.</p>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-28 19:21:32', 4, 1, '2025-10-28 19:20:45', 29, '2025-10-28 19:21:32', NULL, '2025-10-28 19:24:01', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-28', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Selection of PMU for Chhattisgarh Samvad, Public Relations Department', '2025-01-03', '2025-11-03 17:00:00', '2025-11-19 00:00:00', '2025-11-26 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-10', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/Y4VcmMf6AZHWOrqo3y8ze5gIJNIbs4j49uNrqbJW.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/Y4VcmMf6AZHWOrqo3y8ze5gIJNIbs4j49uNrqbJW.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 8729032.26, 0, 0, 1571225.81, 10300258.06, 1, 0, NULL, NULL),
(3, 88, 30, 'EOI/EMPL/CHiPS/PMU/SUDA/SBM/2024', 1, 'SWACHHA BHARAT MISSION- URBAN', '36', '<p class=\"p1\">The State Urban Development Agency (SUDA) is seeking to establish a Program Management Unit (PMU) with</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">professional consultants for the planning, implementation, and monitoring of Swachh Bharat Mission - Urban 2.0</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">(SBM-U 2.0). The scope of work for the PMU will broadly encompass the comprehensive management of</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">projects, activities, and components under SBM-U 2.0, ensuring alignment with the Government of India</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">guidelines and the Ministry\'s directives.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The PMU will provide end-to-end consultancy support and handholding to SUDA, facilitating the preparation of</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">all necessary plans for the State under SBM-U 2.0 for submission to both the State Government and the</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Government of India. This support will include planning, policy formulation, and the monitoring of physical and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">financial progress of the projects. Additionally, the PMU will focus on capacity building, knowledge management,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Information, Education, and Communication (IEC), and other critical aspects of program management and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">implementation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">CHiPS is inviting all empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No. 68733 /CEO /CHiPS /Empanelment</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">/2020 dated 31/10/2020) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.</p>', 2, 30, '2024-06-26 20:40:00', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 142732800, 7136640, 149869440, 0, 18, 5, '<p class=\"p1\">The Swachh Bharat Mission - Urban (SBM-U) 2.0 in Chhattisgarh, managed by the State Urban Development</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Agency (SUDA), aims to sustain cleanliness achievements in urban areas. It focuses on solid waste management,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">sanitation infrastructure, and behavior change. SBM-U 2.0 receives central government funding, monitored by</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">SUDA and urban local bodies, for efficient implementation and impact assessment. For detailed updates, refer to</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">official government sources on progress and ongoing projects.</p>', NULL, NULL, '<p class=\"p1\"><strong>4.1.</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>Key Activities</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The PMU will work in close collaboration with SUDA, providing support in key activities such as:</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">ï‚·</span> Project Planning and Management Support: Assisting in the strategic planning and management of SBM-</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">U 2.0 projects. Project Design and Development: Developing detailed project designs and ensuring they</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">meet the required standards and guidelines.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">ï‚·</span> Bid Process Management: Managing the entire bidding process, including the preparation of bid</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">documents, evaluation of bids, and contract management.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">ï‚·</span> Progress Monitoring the progress of projects, both physically and financially, ensuring they remain on</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">track and within budget.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">ï‚·</span> Solid &amp; Liquid Waste Management: Implementing effective solid and liquid waste management strategies</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">and technologies</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">ï‚·</span> MIS Support: Developing and maintaining Management Information Systems (MIS) for better project</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">tracking and reporting IEC and Capacity Building: Conducting IEC campaigns and capacity-building</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">programs to enhance the skills and knowledge of stakeholders. Coordination and Stakeholder</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Management: Ensuring effective coordination among various stakeholders, including ULBs, state</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">authorities, and other partners.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">ï‚·</span> Other Support: Providing additional support as required for the successful implementation of SBM-U 2.0</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">initiatives.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The PMU will be deployed in phases, potentially through a single agency or multiple agencies, to ensure</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">comprehensive and effective coverage of all aspects of SBM-U 2.0. This multi-stage exercise will involve close</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">collaboration with SUDA and other stakeholders to achieve the mission\'s objectives efficiently and effectively.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The scope of work for the PMU will broadly encompass the comprehensive management of projects, activities,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">and components under SBM-U 2.0, ensuring alignment with the Government of India guidelines and the Ministry\'s</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">directives.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>4.2.</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>Functional Scope</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>4.2.1 Project Planning and Management Support</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">a) Prepare all plans as per Ministry\'s guidelines of SBM-U 2.0 based on the latest data available at the</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">State/city level.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Page <strong>6</strong> of <strong>31</strong>b) Support for project identification, planning, design, procurement, monitoring, and reporting required for</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">the project.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">c) Support in planning, scheduling, and monitoring the projects using MIS/PMIS/latest IT tools and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">techniques.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">d) Assist in conducting regular meetings with all stakeholders, contractors, and other government entities to</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">discuss progress and issues related to implementation, and prepare minutes for recording and circulation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">e) f) Establish all necessary records and procedures for maintaining/updating records for the entire project</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Support in identifying activities eligible under Capacity Building, IEC funds, and developing annual</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">action plans for the same.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">g) Assist in project planning for major project components, including:</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>4.2.2 Scientific Management of Solid and Liquid Waste</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">a) Sewerage, septage management, and recycling and reuse of treated used water</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">b) Remediation of Legacy waste dumpsites</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">c) Construction &amp; Demolition (C&amp;D) Waste Management</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">d) Sanitary Landfills</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">e) Waste-to-Energy initiatives</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">f) Develop and implement strategies for SUDA under Swachh Survekshan, Garbage Free Cities Protocol,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">ODF+/ODF++/Water+ Protocols, and Safai Mitra Suraksha Challenge.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">g) Assist in developing a reuse plan for treated used water and support in planning and selecting appropriate</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">technology options for the treatment of used water based on the potential for reuse in the region.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">h) Provide handholding support to SUDA for all Survekshan and Competitions under SBM-U 2.0 by</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">conducting workshops on key survey indicators, conducting awareness programs, etc.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">i) Prepare all plans as per mission guidelines of SBM-U 2.0, including but not limited to City Sanitation</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Action Plans (CSAPs), City Solid Waste Action Plans (CSWAPS), City Water Balance Plans (CWBPs),</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">City Water Action Plans (CWAPs), Capacity Building plans, and IEC plans based on the latest data</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">available at the State/City level, and suggest corrections where necessary.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">j) Provide suggestions on the capacity building of human resources in consonance with the vision of the</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">mentioned schemes.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">k) Overall coordination with MoHUA with respect to SBM 2.0</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>4.2.3 Project Design and Development</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">a) b) Study the available documents such as existing sanitation plans, SWM plans, etc.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Review the existing status of physical infrastructure based on the above documents and other available</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">secondary data, and identify data gaps.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">c) Identify key stakeholders from the city, elected representatives, concerning NGOs, eminent citizens,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">representatives from premium institutes in the state, and representatives of business organizations in</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">consultation with SUDA.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">d) Prepare conceptual plans and preliminary designs, including the feasibility of the infrastructure to be</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">provided for the mentioned schemes under SBM 2.0.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">e) Assist in the first stage of consultation with stakeholders for each subproject or group of sub-projects, as</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">applicable, to discuss the conceptual plan and technical options, and prepare minutes for recording and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">circulation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">f) g) h) i) Identify the possibility of private/public participation in service delivery, as applicable.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Prepare a strategy and action plans for the IEC program, including public participation</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Identify requirements for surveys, studies, and investigations.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Based on the above, conduct an analysis of the technical options with respect to best practices, smart</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">options, priorities, and consultation</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Page <strong>7</strong> of <strong>314.2.4 Bid Process and Contract Management</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">a) Assist in all aspects of procurement, including issuing bid invitations, addenda/corrigenda, and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">clarifications to bidders\' queries, bid evaluation, selection of contractors, awarding contracts, and signing</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">contracts.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">b) Prepare contract documentation, including Letters of Invitation, conditions of contract, specifications,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">design parameters, bills of quantities, etc., for all sub-project components in close coordination with</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">SUDA.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">c) Finalize arrangements for contracting, including exploring options for PPP/Service Level Agreements/by</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">documents.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">d) Assist SUDA in developing concession agreements for PPP projects.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">e) Provide advice and guidance on modern procedures and guidelines for project implementation and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">management in general.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">f) Arrange and coordinate multi-stage consultations proposed under the project and ensure modification of</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">project components accordingly.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">g) h) Assist in contract administration and management of sub-projects.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Interpret the technical specifications for each sub-project.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>4.2.5 Progress Monitoring and Reporting Support</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">a) b) c) d) e) f) g) h) Support monitoring and reviewing project progress in terms of physical and financial targets and against</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">overall monitoring parameters.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Support developing the framework for Monitoring &amp; Evaluation (M&amp;E) under the SBM- U 2.0 program</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">at the State level.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Support and assist in developing the project M&amp;E system.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Support and assist in integrating the State Management Information System (MIS) with the MoHUA</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">SBM-U 2.0 MIS System.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Support developing and monitoring annual work plans and budgets, including annual milestones.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Prepare consolidated progress reports for project management, including identifying emerging issues and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">recommendations to resolve them.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Generate monthly reports on physical and financial progress. The reports will summarize the State-wise</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">and project-wise work performed during the reported period, identifying problems encountered, and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">indicating corrective actions taken or recommended.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Prepare and submit monthly project progress reports on behalf of SUDA, describing the physical and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">financial progress of each sub-project, highlighting impediments to the quality and progress of the works,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">and recommending remedial actions.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>4.2.6 Solid &amp; Liquid Waste Management</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">a) Provide technical assistance to achieve fresh waste processing (Dry and Wet Waste) and legacy waste</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">dumpsite remediation</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">b) Support monitoring C&amp;D Waste Management Plants, mechanical sweeping, door-to- door collection</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">vehicles, and other mobile waste carriers.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">c) d) Assist in implementing different components of SBM (Urban) 2.0.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Prepare documents and provide handholding support to achieve the maximum attainable Garbage Free</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">City status certification.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">e) f) Assist in implementing guidelines for ODF+, ODF++, Water+, and GFC.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Assist in issuing notifications and ensuring compliance of Bulk Waste Generators, as per SWM-2016 and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">its amendments.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">g) Assist in onboarding private players to execute SWM/LWM projects on the PPP model as per StatePage <strong>8</strong> of <strong>31</strong>guidelines.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">h) Support executing capacity-building activities for officials, including conducting workshops, seminars,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">and training programs for ULB officials on different components as required.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">i) j) k) l) Support drafting bylaws along with user charges for different components.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Assist in strengthening the Citizen Grievance Redressal and feedback system.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Assist in forming the City Sanitation Monitoring Committee, etc.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Assist in preparing sanitation plans specifying time frames, finances, operational components, and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">guidelines for components, to enable the earmarking of appropriate resources.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">m) Assist in implementing sanitation plans, channeling financial resources from Central, State and externally</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">aided sources, if any.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">n) Assist in procurement-related requirements.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>4.2.7 Data Engineer and Visualization Expert</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">a) b) Maintain, upload, and update data on various portals developed by the Ministry for SBM 2.0.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Execute capacity building and handholding support for effective management of MIS at the State/City</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">level.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">c) Develop and deploy appropriate MIS (including M&amp;E) systems.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">d) Conduct suitable analysis of MIS data to generate insights for improving performance and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">implementation outcomes under the programs.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">e) f) Develop reporting and dashboards for management reviews.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Provide technical handholding support in creating effective MIS databases</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>4.2.8 IEC and Capacity Building</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">a) b) Develop a strategy and action plan for IEC and capacity building.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Aid the State Government in identifying training needs, finalizing capacity-building-eligible activities,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">and formulating annual Capacity Building action plans.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">c) Conduct capacity-building workshops, seminars, and training programs</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">d) Assist in drafting the training needs document for stakeholders, developing training programs, and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">monitoring and evaluating the implementation of these programs for successful outcomes and continuous</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">improvement.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">e) Prepare an IEC plan to undertake activities like awareness programs on source segregation, sanitation,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">and relevant issues.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>4.3 Team Deployment</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The Successful Agency shalt deploy a team of Specialists (consultants) on a full-time basis at SUDA.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Collectively, the team shall demonstrate adequate experience in the field of SBM-U 2.0 to ensure service</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">delivery to the Authority. The PMU team will be responsible for providing comprehensive support to SUDA,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">ensuring the successful planning, implementation, and monitoring of all SBM-U 2.0 components and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">activities.</p>', NULL, '<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt; </span>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>', NULL, '<p class=\"p1\">CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">discussion with the Committee.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> A presentation will be made by the bidding companies about their understanding of the proposed area of work</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">and their past experience if any in similar area of expertise.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> During the presentation by the companies the proposed candidates will be interviewed (face to face) by the</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Evaluation Committee.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> The marking for presentation and Interview will be done as follows-</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>Bidder Presentation </strong><strong>Candidate Interview</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>50 Marks </strong><strong>50 Marks</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>Key</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>Evaluation</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>Criteria</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Approach and Methodology</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Understanding of the Project Framework</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Quality of proposed methodology</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Suitability of profile</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Years of relevant experience</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Good understanding of project management best</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Page <strong>30</strong> of <strong>31</strong><strong>Bidder Presentation </strong><strong>Candidate Interview</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">for such specific kind of a</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">project</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Prior experience in project</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">interaction with senior</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">government officials</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Prior exposure to implementing</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">government projects in Bid</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Management and Exit</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Management</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Understanding of key SLAs for</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">the project management</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">practices framework</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Ability to Negotiate/Persuade/Influence</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Strong ability to understand and deliberate and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">report</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">monitor the key SLAs</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Excellent communication abilities</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">&nbsp;</p>', '<p class=\"p1\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The last date for submission of response is 15/07/2024, 05:00 hrs. Any response received after the above</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">deadline will be rejected.</p>', '<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt; </span>Signed copy of this EOI</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Copy of Approach and methodology presentation</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Resumes of resources that will face the interview. The format of resumes will be as per</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">empanelment tender number __________.</p>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-28 20:47:27', 4, 1, '2025-10-28 20:45:39', 30, '2025-10-28 20:47:27', NULL, '2025-10-28 20:48:09', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-28', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Expression of Interest (EOI) for State Level Project Management Unit (PMU) under Swachh Bharat Mission - Urban 2.0 in State Urban Development Agency, ', '2024-06-26', '2024-07-01 17:00:00', '2024-07-03 00:00:00', '2024-07-16 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-10', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/W4cjwcYqFkKPdTb0EGjLoxLiY0sWsuB5Saf1DaJN.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 85866480, 0, 0, 15455966.4, 101322446.4, 1, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(4, 82, 31, 'EOI/EMPL/PMU/RAMP/2024', 1, 'For Selection of Project Support Consultant for Implementation of SIP under RAMP Program in the State of Chhattisgarh', '30', '<p>The selected agency will be responsible to set up the Programme Implementation Unit to support the State in implementation and monitoring of the World Bank assisted Raising and Accelerating MSME Performance &ldquo;RAMP&rdquo; (&ldquo;the Programme&rdquo;). The appointed/hired agency for SPIU will be deployed fulltime at CSIDC, Udyog Bhawan, Raipur/ Industries Department for the implementation of approved projects as per the SIP as well as the guidelines of Government of India (GOI).</p>', 2, 31, '2024-11-19 20:53:32', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 54870000, 2743500, 57613500, 0, 18, 5, '<p>1 RAMP Programme background: -<br>To support the overall Covid Resilience and Recovery Programme of Ministry of MSME (MoMSME), the<br>Government of India, has launched a new World Bank supported Central Sector Scheme, i.e., \"Raising and<br>Accelerating MSME Performance (RAMP)\". The scheme has been launched for a period of five years, to be jointly<br>funded by the World Bank and Government of India. The RAMP program is a Programme-for-Results (P for R)<br>and aims at improving MSMEs\' access to market and credit, strengthening institutions and governance at the Centre<br>and State, improving Centre-State linkages and partnerships, addressing issues of delayed payments and greening<br>of MSMEs. RAMP programme seeks to address the generic and COVID related challenges in the MSME sector<br>by way of impact enhancement of existing MSME schemes, especially on the competitiveness front.<br>In addition to building the Ministry of MSME&rsquo;s capacity at the National level, the RAMP Programme also seeks<br>to scale up implementation capacity and firm coverage in the participating States and UTs. Thus, as per the design<br>of the programme the State has prepared a long-term roadmap, through a Strategic Investment Plan (SIP), for<br>enhancing the performance of the MSME sector through greater outreach as per the design of the program and<br>submitted it to the Ministry. As per the programme guidelines the State Programme Implementation Unit (SPIU)<br>is intended to be set up at Chhattisgarh State Industrial Development Corporation (CSIDC)/ Industries department<br>for implementation, monitoring, and evaluation of the approved projects of the SIP.<br>2.2 RAMP Programme development objective and result areas<br>The Programme development objective is to strengthen institutions and markets for MSMEs at the Central<br>Government level and in States.<br>RA#1: Strengthening Institutions and Governance of the MSME Programme<br>This will target results at the Central and State levels to address institutional capacity and coordination constraints.<br>This RA aims to strengthen Central and State institutions to deliver on the MSME agenda through better Central<br>Government level and Central Government -State coordination on the MSME sector; enhanced policy capacity of<br>MoMSME to undertake evidence-based policy and Programme design; improved and interoperable portals to<br>deliver online services to MSMEs at scale and in a cost-effective manner; and a more decentralized, flexible and<br>cohesive MSME Programme led by States.<br>RA#2: Support to Firm Capabilities and Access to Markets, Access to Finance<br>The interventions will aim to use technology-driven solutions and leverage platform approaches to achieve<br>economies of scale and better outreach of quality market-based private sector service provision in the areas of firm<br>capabilities and access to finance. This RA aims to improve the quality, coverage and delivery of the existing Firm<br>Capabilities schemes and strengthen the market for BDS; improve access to finance and working capital by<br>strengthening receivable financing markets for MSMEs through well-functioning digital factoring platforms;<br>improve access to finance for women entrepreneurs and greening investments through CGTMSE; and strengthen<br>dispute resolution mechanisms for delayed payments to MSMEs by incorporating online dispute resolution and<br>private sector provision of these services.<br>The following Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) are proposed to measure progress towards this Project<br>Development Objectives (PDO):<br><br>ï‚· Improved Firm Capabilities from utilizing Schemes - measured by MSME Champions Scheme and linked<br>schemes uptake.<br>ï‚· Increased access to finance for female-headed businesses - measured by the volume of credit guarantees.<br>ï‚· Increased access to finance for green investments - measured by the volume of credit guarantees.<br>ï‚· Increased MSME access to factoring &ndash; measured by the value of invoices placed on the TReDS platform.<br>ï‚· Increased resolution rate for delayed payments &ndash; measured by the number of MSMEs able to unblock payments<br>via ODR platforms accessed via the MoMSME Samadhaan portal.<br>ï‚· The principal beneficiaries of this operation are: MSMEs in the target States. The principal beneficiaries are<br>formal MSMEs with the intention and potential to grow, invest in themselves and improve productivity.<br>ï‚· The Ministry of MSMEs - Primary CG (Credit Guarantee) agency supported by the operation.<br>ï‚· State Governments - The specific departments and agencies of the focus State Governments who will be the<br>primary beneficiaries of the operation will be identified as part of the State MSME SIPs</p>', NULL, NULL, '<p>1. Support in implementation of activities as approved by Ministry of MSME in SIP<br>i. Understand the interventions, budgeting, and mode of operations defined in the SIP &amp; approved by the<br>MoMSME, GOI.<br>ii. Stakeholder consultation for better implementation and monitoring of the interventions as per approved<br>SIP and budget.<br>iii. Design the Project Implementation Plan (PIP) for activities approved in SIP including responsible<br>agencies, timelines, targets and KPIs for the performance monitoring.<br>iv. Support the State departments in implementation and monitoring according to the submitted Strategic<br>Investment Plan (SIP) and its approval given by the MoMSME, GOI.<br>v. Support the State in all matters relating to Programme implementation as defined in the Programme<br>implementation manual.<br>vi. Review of Project Implementation Plan (PIP) every quarter and modify the PIPs for resubmission to the<br>Centre every half yearly in case of any modifications / updates in the plans.<br>vii. Ensuring the budget expenditure according to the approved SIP as per the guidelines of RAMP scheme &amp;<br>GFR rules.<br>viii. Any other activity related to SIP implementation and management of the RAMP Programme, not specified<br>within the above scope of services.&nbsp;</p>', '<p>1. Support in implementation of activities as approved by Ministry of MSME in SIP<br>i. Understand the interventions, budgeting, and mode of operations defined in the SIP &amp; approved by the<br>MoMSME, GOI.<br>ii. Stakeholder consultation for better implementation and monitoring of the interventions as per approved<br>SIP and budget.<br>iii. Design the Project Implementation Plan (PIP) for activities approved in SIP including responsible<br>agencies, timelines, targets and KPIs for the performance monitoring.<br>iv. Support the State departments in implementation and monitoring according to the submitted Strategic<br>Investment Plan (SIP) and its approval given by the MoMSME, GOI.<br>v. Support the State in all matters relating to Programme implementation as defined in the Programme<br>implementation manual.<br>vi. Review of Project Implementation Plan (PIP) every quarter and modify the PIPs for resubmission to the<br>Centre every half yearly in case of any modifications / updates in the plans.<br>vii. Ensuring the budget expenditure according to the approved SIP as per the guidelines of RAMP scheme &amp;<br>GFR rules.<br>viii. Any other activity related to SIP implementation and management of the RAMP Programme, not specified<br>within the above scope of services.&nbsp;<br><br><br></p>', '<p>Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule.<br>ï‚· The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the agreed empanelment<br>terms.<br>ï‚· For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or CHiPS, as the case may be selected bidder shall be<br>paid the requisite man month payment in the event that selected bidder has performed on its obligations in<br>compliance with the terms of this contract.<br>ï‚· Quarterly Progress Report to be shared and submitted by the SPIU to CSIDC as per the RAMP Programme<br>implementation manual. Payments shall be made to the consultant quarterly based on the deployment of the<br>engagement team. SPIU&rsquo;s Progress Reports should also contain information on meeting of various compliance<br>requirements of Government of India (GoI) and World Bank and progress on KPIs related to implementation<br>and monitoring of the RAMP Programme.<br><br>ï‚· Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.<br>Payment to the selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule.<br>Important Note: All other terms and conditions of tender 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020 shall be<br>applicable to this EOI.</p>', NULL, '<p>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses<br>to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/<br>discussion with the Committee.<br><br></p>\r\n<p>A presentation will be made by the bidding companies about their understanding of the proposed area of work<br>and their experience if any in similar area of expertise</p>\r\n<p>During the presentation by the companies the proposed candidates will be interviewed (face to face) by the<br>Evaluation Committee.</p>\r\n<p>Further, any deviation from proposal and resource CV submitted as bid response to this EOI would not be<br>considered and would be duly ruled as rejection. Therefore it is instructed to bidders that the actual resource<br>who will be deployed for assignment should be present for interview (in person/Skype/VC)</p>\r\n<p>The marking for presentation and Interview will be done as follows:-<br><br><br></p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.036%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>Bidder Presentation</td>\r\n<td>Candidate Interview</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>50 Marks</td>\r\n<td>50 Marks</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>Key&nbsp;Evaluation&nbsp;Criteria</td>\r\n<td>ï‚· Approach and Methodology<br>ï‚· Understanding of the Project<br>ï‚· Quality of proposed methodology for<br>such specific kind of a project<br>ï‚· Prior exposure to implementing<br>government projects in Bid<br>Management and Exit Management<br>ï‚· Understanding of key SLAs for the<br>project management</td>\r\n<td>ï‚· Suitability of profile<br>ï‚· Years of relevant experience<br>ï‚· Good understanding of project&nbsp;management best practices&nbsp;framework<br>ï‚· Ability to&nbsp;Negotiate/Persuade/Influence<br>ï‚· Strong ability to understand&nbsp;and deliberate and report monitorthe&nbsp;key SLAs<br>ï‚· Excellent communication abilities</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals inresponse<br>to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to be done after careful<br>study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.<br>The last date for submission of response is 10/12/2024, 17:00 Hrs. Any response received after the above<br>deadline will be rejected.<br>The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to<br>CEO, CHiPS, State Data Centre, Civil Lines,<br>Raipur 492001<br>Email ID: ceochips@nic.in empl.chips@cgchips.in<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax:+91 771-4014158</p>', '<p>ï‚· Signed copy of this EOI<br>ï‚· Copy of Approach and methodology presentation<br>ï‚· Resumes of resources that will face the interview. The format of resumes will be as per empanelment tender<br>number 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020 dated 31/10/2020.</p>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-28 21:02:38', 4, 1, '2025-10-28 21:01:39', 31, '2025-10-28 21:02:38', NULL, '2025-10-28 21:03:17', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-28', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Selection of Project Support Consultant for Implementation of SIP under RAMP Program in the State of Chhattisgarh', '2024-11-19', '2024-11-25 17:00:00', '2024-12-10 00:00:00', '2025-12-15 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-10', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/CCxxBWLBjpctyv8Zaov5wLkR0ujevNSHb36JRXDB.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 37500000, 0, 0, 6750000, 44250000, 1, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(5, 84, 23, 'EOI/EMP/PMU/CGHB/2024', 1, 'PMU for CG Housing Board', '36', '<p class=\"p1\">CGHB intends to engage an agency to establish a Project Support Consultant (PSC) Unit, to expedite its:</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Housing initiatives</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Manage unsold inventory</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Execute redevelopment projects, and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\">-&gt;</span> Strategize for the future with business plans and sector strategies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">This PSC will bolster CGHB by aiding in project identification, development, and marketing management&nbsp;endeavors. The selected consultant will collaborate closely with CGHB and other stakeholders to ensure seamless&nbsp;coordination and effective implementation of housing projects and related activities.</p>', 2, 23, '2024-10-04 01:20:15', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 197107200, 9855360, 206962560, 0, 18, 5, '<p class=\"p1\">The Chhattisgarh Housing Board (CGHB) stands as a pivotal public sector entity under the aegis of the&nbsp;Government of Chhattisgarh, established in accordance with the Chhattisgarh Housing Board Act of 1972 (No. 3&nbsp;of 1973). As the primary agency responsible for executing the state\'s Housing Policy, CGHB plays a crucial role&nbsp;in ensuring housing provisions for all strata of society and spearheading infrastructure development initiatives&nbsp;across Chhattisgarh.&nbsp;CGHB has implemented various housing schemes such as Atal Vihar Yojana, Atal Awas Yojana, Deen Dayal&nbsp;Awas Yojana, General Housing Scheme, Kushabhau Thakre Awas Yojana, Nava Raipur Atal Nagar Pradhan&nbsp;Mantri/ Mukhya Mantri Awas Yojana and Special Housing Scheme, exemplifying its commitment to addressing&nbsp;diverse housing needs and fostering inclusive urban development within the state.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Chhattisgarh is poised to witness a substantial urban population surge, estimated to reach around 63.21 lakh by&nbsp;2031. This growth projection is anticipated to drive the demand for housing and public infrastructure development&nbsp;across key sectors and growth hubs, including the Capital city agglomeration encompassing Raipur, Durg-Bhilai,&nbsp;Rajnandgaon, Mahasamund; Raigarh, Korba, and Bilaspur; Ambikapur in the North; and Jagdalpur in the South in line with this trajectory, the Government of Chhattisgarh has introduced the Chhattisgarh Redevelopment Policy&nbsp;- 2022, designating CGHB as a pivotal overseeing entity for the execution of redevelopment projects in the state.&nbsp;To align with the Board\'s objectives, CGHB intends to engage a Project Support Consultant (PSC) to facilitate the&nbsp;identification and implementation of redevelopment initiatives. The PSC will play a crucial role in providing&nbsp;comprehensive support to CGHB for various housing sector endeavors, empowering the Board to efficiently&nbsp;navigate the evolving landscape of housing development in the region.</p>', NULL, NULL, '<p class=\"p1\"><strong>I.</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>Broad scope of services</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">PSC\'s comprehensive scope of work will encompass the following key areas:</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">1. Reviewing the Chhattisgarh Redevelopment Policy 2022 and providing assistance in project&nbsp;development and implementation support statewide.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">2. Support in review, feasibility, project development and monitoring for ongoing &amp; proposed housing&nbsp;scheme/ projects and deposit work.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">a. Atal Vihar Yojana Ph-II. across state</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">b. General Housing Schemes across state</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">c. Deposit works of state &amp; central departments</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">3. Assessment of Profitability of projects and CGHB&rsquo;s Division offices.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">4. Evaluating CGHB\'s unsold inventory, devising disposal strategies and outlining an implementation&nbsp;roadmap for the same.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">5. Development of state housing vision for vision 2047.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">6. Assisting the board in evaluating various procurement-related initiatives to enhance operational&nbsp;efficiency and effectiveness.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">7. Assisting the board for Organization restructuring and reforms of CGHB.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">8. Activities to be performed at Circle Level office.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>II.</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>Detailed scope of work</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Detailed scope of work along with the activities is detailed out below.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>1)</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>Reviewing the Chhattisgarh Redevelopment Policy 2022 and providing assistance in project </strong><strong>development and implementation support statewide.</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">PSC will be tasked with a comprehensive set of responsibilities to support CGHB in the successful&nbsp;implementation of the Chhattisgarh Redevelopment Policy 2022. The outlined tasks include:</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Reviewing and comparing the Chhattisgarh Redevelopment Policy-2022 with similar policies&nbsp;from other states such as Madhya Pradesh, MHADA, Andhra Pradesh, and Tamil Nadu Housing&nbsp;Boards to understand the best practices.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Examining the process flow for project implementation under the Chhattishgarh redevelopment&nbsp;policy.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Evaluating the role of supervising agencies like CGHB and recommending necessary&nbsp;amendments, if required.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Identifying redevelopment projects throughout the state and creating a phased pipeline plan for&nbsp;the next three years.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Conducting feasibility studies for projects, including site assessments, development potential,&nbsp;infrastructure evaluation, market analysis, land use optimization and financial projections.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Compiling project appraisal reports and presentation for approval by competent authorities and&nbsp;also extending support during the approval process.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assisting in selection and appointment of various consultants like architects, DPR consultants and&nbsp;Project Management Consultants (PMCs) through bid process management.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Providing support in reviewing DPRs and other technical reports prepared by consultants.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Offering transaction advisory services for selection of developer including preparation of tender&nbsp;documents, pre-bid meetings minutes, support in bid evaluation and developer outreach activities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Contributing to the monitoring of physical and financial progress of projects under implementation&nbsp;based on the data received from the concerned circle offices.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assisting in Public Private Partnership (PPP) projects, if planned by CGHB.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>2)</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>Support for review, feasibility, project development and monitoring for ongoing &amp; proposed </strong><strong>housing scheme/ projects and deposit work</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The PSC is tasked with supporting CGHB throughout the entire lifecycle of housing projects,&nbsp;encompassing review, feasibility studies, project development, and progress monitoring for both ongoing&nbsp;and proposed housing projects under various schemes such as.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">A. Atal Vihar Yojana</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">B. Atal Awas Yojana</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">C. Deen Dayal Awas Yojana</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">D. General Housing Scheme</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">E. Kushabhau Thakre Awas Yojana</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">F. Nava Raipur Atal Nagar Pradhan Mantri/ Mukhya Mantri Awas Yojana, and</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">G. Special Housing Scheme.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The PSC is expected to undertake the following tasks:</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Evaluate ongoing and proposed housing projects.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Develop a project pipeline with a phased plan for the next three years for Atal Vihar Yojana &amp;&nbsp;General housing in accordance with CGHB policy.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Conduct market feasibility studies for proposed housing projects.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assist CGHB in finalizing the product mix and unit sizes based on market assessments.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Identify best practices from other State Housing Boards for implementing special projects like&nbsp;housing for Members of Legislative Assembly, staff of All India Services, Chhattisgarh&nbsp;Administrative Services, etc.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Review procurement documents and processes, providing recommendations for enhancements.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assist in the selection and appointment of various consultants such as Architects, Project&nbsp;Management Consultants (PMCs), etc., through the preparation of tender documents and bid&nbsp;evaluations.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Review of Detailed Project Reports (DPRs) and any other reports prepared by technical&nbsp;consultants or architects to ensure compliance with SOPs.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assist in the preparation of documents for obtaining loans from various financial institutions,&nbsp;banks, or the government for project implementation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Prepare monthly progress reports containing updates on ongoing housing and deposit projects.&nbsp;This includes addressing any implementation delays, fund disbursements, or other challenges in&nbsp;successfully executing CGHB\'s projects. This activity will be conducted in coordination with the&nbsp;concerned Additional Housing Commissioner</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>3) </strong><strong>Assessment of profitability of projects and CGHB&rsquo;s Division offices.</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assessment of profitability based on data received from CGHB for all Division offices in every 3&nbsp;months.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assistance in preparation of yearly budget of CGHB.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>4) Evaluating CGHB\'s unsold inventory, devising disposal strategies, and outlining an </strong><strong>implementation roadmap for the same.</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">CGHB currently has approximately INR 600 Cr. worth of unsold inventory spread across Chhattisgarh.&nbsp;The PSC is tasked with executing the following activities for the disposal of unsold inventory.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Review and assess the volume and geographical distribution of the unsold inventory.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\"><strong>&nbsp;</strong></span><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Evaluate the physical condition, pricing, sizes, amenities, etc., of the unsold inventory projects&nbsp;and propose interventions for enhancing or rejuvenating the existing inventory.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Develop an overarching marketing and disposal strategy on a project-by-project basis within each&nbsp;division for CGHB. This includes establishing the necessary policy framework and engaging with&nbsp;various government departments, as required.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Conduct a market assessment to support the marketing efforts for the identified projects.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Plan and implement a system for the regular monitoring of the marketing team and their efforts.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Review and reassess the advertisement process currently in place and recommend amendments to&nbsp;align with the requirements of CGHB.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Prepare a plan &amp; implementation support to increase the sale velocity of unsold properties and&nbsp;regularly update the strategy with marketing team of CGHB.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>5) </strong><strong>Development of state housing vision for vision 2047</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">This component comprises preparation of short-term plan (3-5 years) and long-term plan (15 years), for&nbsp;housing development in the State. To achieve this objective, the scope of work shall include the following&nbsp;tasks:</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assessment of housing provided by both public and private sector across major urban centers of&nbsp;the state.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assessment of urbanization patterns, city master plans, and demand factors for housing, including&nbsp;supply of land for residential use.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Identification of new growth centers/ corridors and proposing housing development strategy for&nbsp;the same.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Examine prevailing policies at state and city level, including town planning and building&nbsp;regulations related to housing &amp; urban sector, and suggest amendments to be undertaken in the&nbsp;relevant provisions of the acts and rules governing CGHB.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assess medium to long-term trends in market rates for housing supply. Arrive at demand for&nbsp;housing across different economic segments, and the spatial spread of the same.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assess the housing demand and prepare short-term and long-term plan to be undertaken by CGHB.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Explore various land pooling policies of various states and housing boards and suggest a&nbsp;suggestive policy for CGHB.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>6) Assisting the board in evaluating various procurement-related initiatives to enhance operational&nbsp;</strong><strong>efficiency and effectiveness.</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Consultant to assist in overall procurement/ contract procedure opted by CGHB for selection and&nbsp;appointment of various consultants like architects, DPR consultants, and PMC through tender&nbsp;document preparation and bid evaluation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Review the tender documents and suggest the revisions as per requirement.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Support in preparation of tender documents, pre-bid meetings and bid evaluation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Prepare tender evaluation report for review by housing commissioner.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Any other procurement related activity.&nbsp;In addition to the above, PSC to assist CGHB in developing appropriate for project monitoring tools (by&nbsp;using MS office tools) for monitoring of various projects and schemes.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>7)</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>Organization restructuring and reforms of CGHB</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Review the organization structure of the CGHB.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assess the current process flow for various activities and delineated responsibilities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assess the reforms required for sustainable growth of CGHB.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Evaluate the established processes for quality monitoring and progress review.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Review the roles and responsibilities of various committees within CGHB.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Based on the assessment, recommend organization restructuring and reforms of CGHB.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>8) Activities to be performed at Circle Level office:</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assessment of all the unsold inventory in various projects of CGHB in the circle.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Market assessment for real estate trends, housing unit prices, new launches and urban growth in&nbsp;the cities within the circle.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assist the headquarter team to suggest strategies for disposal of inventory based on ground&nbsp;situation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Proactive assessment of market for new projects and deposit works.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Preparation of project pipeline including new projects and redevelopment projects.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Assist the circle office in project progress monitoring of all the ongoing/ new projects.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s2\">-&gt;</span> Identify the constraints in implementation of the projects and provide necessary action plan for&nbsp;the same.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Note: The scope of the PSC&rsquo;s work does not include technical/ engineering investigations such as physical or geo-technical surveys, detailed design &amp; estimates, structural assessment, construction supervision, payment&nbsp;certification and sales &amp; marketing of inventory.</p>', '<h2 data-start=\"257\" data-end=\"280\"><strong data-start=\"260\" data-end=\"280\">Payment Terms</strong></h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"282\" data-end=\"389\">Payment to the selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"391\" data-end=\"734\">\r\n<li data-start=\"391\" data-end=\"516\">\r\n<p data-start=\"393\" data-end=\"516\">The successful bidder shall submit the <strong data-start=\"432\" data-end=\"476\">invoice for payment on a man-month basis</strong>, as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"517\" data-end=\"734\">\r\n<p data-start=\"519\" data-end=\"734\">For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder, the bidder shall be <strong data-start=\"594\" data-end=\"634\">paid the requisite man-month payment</strong>, provided the bidder has performed its obligations in compliance with the terms of this contract.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-start=\"736\" data-end=\"760\"><strong data-start=\"740\" data-end=\"760\">Payment Schedule</strong></h3>\r\n<div class=\"_tableContainer_1rjym_1\">\r\n<div class=\"group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"762\" data-end=\"1396\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"762\" data-end=\"793\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"762\" data-end=\"793\">\r\n<th data-start=\"762\" data-end=\"778\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"764\" data-end=\"777\">Milestone</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"778\" data-end=\"793\" data-col-size=\"xl\"><strong data-start=\"780\" data-end=\"791\">Payment</strong></th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"828\" data-end=\"1396\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"828\" data-end=\"1099\">\r\n<td data-start=\"828\" data-end=\"872\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"830\" data-end=\"871\">Submission of Monthly Progress Report</strong></td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"xl\" data-start=\"872\" data-end=\"1099\">90% of the total man-month rates shall be released to PSC on deployment of the complete team at CGHB/Circle Office as per Section 3.3 of this document. <br><br>The payment shall be released on a man-month basis every month.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1100\" data-end=\"1371\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1100\" data-end=\"1151\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"1102\" data-end=\"1150\">Submission of Deliverables as per Annexure 1</strong></td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"xl\" data-start=\"1151\" data-end=\"1371\">10% of the total man-month rates shall be released to the PSC consultant on achieving the quarterly targets as set by CGHB as per Annexure 1. <br><br>The payment of this amount shall be released on a quarterly basis.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1372\" data-end=\"1396\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1372\" data-end=\"1384\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"1374\" data-end=\"1383\">Total</strong></td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1384\" data-end=\"1396\" data-col-size=\"xl\"><strong data-start=\"1386\" data-end=\"1394\">100%</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr data-start=\"1398\" data-end=\"1401\">\r\n<h2 data-start=\"1403\" data-end=\"1426\"><strong data-start=\"1406\" data-end=\"1426\">Penalty Terms</strong></h2>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1428\" data-end=\"1503\">\r\n<li data-start=\"1428\" data-end=\"1503\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1430\" data-end=\"1503\">Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1505\" data-end=\"1612\">Payment to the selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1614\" data-end=\"1746\"><strong data-start=\"1614\" data-end=\"1633\">Important Note:</strong> All other terms and conditions of tender <strong data-start=\"1675\" data-end=\"1711\">68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020</strong> shall be applicable to this EOI.</p>\r\n<h3 data-start=\"1748\" data-end=\"1773\"><strong data-start=\"1752\" data-end=\"1773\">Penalty Structure</strong></h3>\r\n<div class=\"_tableContainer_1rjym_1\">\r\n<div class=\"group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1775\" data-end=\"2557\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1775\" data-end=\"1837\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1775\" data-end=\"1837\">\r\n<th data-start=\"1775\" data-end=\"1789\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"1777\" data-end=\"1788\">Sl. No.</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"1789\" data-end=\"1804\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"1791\" data-end=\"1803\">Incident</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"1804\" data-end=\"1822\" data-col-size=\"lg\"><strong data-start=\"1806\" data-end=\"1821\">Description</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"1822\" data-end=\"1837\" data-col-size=\"lg\"><strong data-start=\"1824\" data-end=\"1835\">Penalty</strong></th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1905\" data-end=\"2557\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1905\" data-end=\"2172\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1905\" data-end=\"1913\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"1907\" data-end=\"1912\">1</strong></td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1913\" data-end=\"1993\" data-col-size=\"md\">Change of selected resources as part of EOIs issued based on this empanelment</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1993\" data-end=\"2066\" data-col-size=\"lg\">Any change of resource within four (4) months from the deployment date</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2066\" data-end=\"2172\" data-col-size=\"lg\">0.5% of the person-month rate for the respective position per event shall be deducted from the payment</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2173\" data-end=\"2444\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2173\" data-end=\"2181\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"2175\" data-end=\"2180\">2</strong></td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2181\" data-end=\"2215\" data-col-size=\"md\">Delay in deployment of resource</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2215\" data-end=\"2345\" data-col-size=\"lg\">Any delay in deployment of the resource against the resource deployment plan mentioned in EOIs issued based on this empanelment</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2345\" data-end=\"2444\" data-col-size=\"lg\">1.0% of the person rate for the respective position per week shall be deducted from the payment</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2445\" data-end=\"2557\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2445\" data-end=\"2453\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"2447\" data-end=\"2452\">3</strong></td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2453\" data-end=\"2471\" data-col-size=\"md\">Other penalties</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2471\" data-end=\"2518\" data-col-size=\"lg\">As per EOIs issued based on this empanelment</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2518\" data-end=\"2557\" data-col-size=\"lg\">Maximum 10% of the work order value</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', '<h3 data-start=\"181\" data-end=\"205\"><strong data-start=\"185\" data-end=\"205\">1. Payment Terms</strong></h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"207\" data-end=\"312\">Payment to the selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"314\" data-end=\"660\">\r\n<li data-start=\"314\" data-end=\"438\">\r\n<p data-start=\"316\" data-end=\"438\">The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on a <strong data-start=\"380\" data-end=\"399\">man-month basis</strong> as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"439\" data-end=\"660\">\r\n<p data-start=\"441\" data-end=\"660\">For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder, the bidder shall be paid the requisite man-month payment in the event that the bidder has performed its obligations in compliance with the terms of this contract.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"662\" data-end=\"682\"><strong data-start=\"662\" data-end=\"682\">Payment Schedule</strong></p>\r\n<div class=\"_tableContainer_1rjym_1\">\r\n<div class=\"group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"1298\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"715\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"715\">\r\n<th data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"700\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"686\" data-end=\"699\">Milestone</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"700\" data-end=\"715\" data-col-size=\"xl\"><strong data-start=\"702\" data-end=\"713\">Payment</strong></th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"749\" data-end=\"1298\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"749\" data-end=\"1014\">\r\n<td data-start=\"749\" data-end=\"789\" data-col-size=\"md\">Submission of Monthly Progress Report</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"xl\" data-start=\"789\" data-end=\"1014\">90% of the total man-month rates shall be released to the PSC upon deployment of the complete team at CGHB/Circle Office as per Section 3.3 of this document. The payment shall be released on a man-month basis every month.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1015\" data-end=\"1273\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1015\" data-end=\"1062\" data-col-size=\"md\">Submission of deliverables as per Annexure 1</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"xl\" data-start=\"1062\" data-end=\"1273\">10% of the total man-month rates shall be released to the PSC Consultant upon achieving the quarterly targets set by CGHB as per Annexure 1. The payment of this amount shall be released on a quarterly basis.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1274\" data-end=\"1298\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1274\" data-end=\"1286\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"1276\" data-end=\"1285\">Total</strong></td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"xl\" data-start=\"1286\" data-end=\"1298\"><strong data-start=\"1288\" data-end=\"1296\">100%</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr data-start=\"1300\" data-end=\"1303\">\r\n<h3 data-start=\"1305\" data-end=\"1329\"><strong data-start=\"1309\" data-end=\"1329\">2. Penalty Terms</strong></h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1331\" data-end=\"1647\">\r\n<li data-start=\"1331\" data-end=\"1406\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1333\" data-end=\"1406\">Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1407\" data-end=\"1512\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1409\" data-end=\"1512\">Payment to the selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the above schedule.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1513\" data-end=\"1647\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1515\" data-end=\"1647\"><strong data-start=\"1515\" data-end=\"1534\">Important Note:</strong> All other terms and conditions of tender <strong data-start=\"1576\" data-end=\"1612\">68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020</strong> shall be applicable to this EOI.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1649\" data-end=\"1669\"><strong data-start=\"1649\" data-end=\"1669\">Penalty Schedule</strong></p>\r\n<div class=\"_tableContainer_1rjym_1\">\r\n<div class=\"group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1671\" data-end=\"2446\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"1671\" data-end=\"1733\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1671\" data-end=\"1733\">\r\n<th data-start=\"1671\" data-end=\"1685\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"1673\" data-end=\"1684\">Sl. No.</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"1685\" data-end=\"1700\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"1687\" data-end=\"1699\">Incident</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"1700\" data-end=\"1718\" data-col-size=\"lg\"><strong data-start=\"1702\" data-end=\"1717\">Description</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"1718\" data-end=\"1733\" data-col-size=\"lg\"><strong data-start=\"1720\" data-end=\"1731\">Penalty</strong></th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1799\" data-end=\"2446\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1799\" data-end=\"2064\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1799\" data-end=\"1803\" data-col-size=\"sm\">1</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1803\" data-end=\"1883\" data-col-size=\"md\">Change of selected resources as part of EOIs issued based on this empanelment</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1883\" data-end=\"1957\">Any change of resource within four (4) months from the deployment date.</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1957\" data-end=\"2064\">0.5% of the person-month rate for the respective position per event shall be deducted from the payment.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2065\" data-end=\"2340\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2065\" data-end=\"2069\" data-col-size=\"sm\">2</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"2069\" data-end=\"2103\" data-col-size=\"md\">Delay in deployment of resource</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"2103\" data-end=\"2234\">Any delay in deployment of the resource against the resource deployment plan mentioned in EOIs issued based on this empanelment.</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"2234\" data-end=\"2340\">1.0% of the person-month rate for the respective position per week shall be deducted from the payment.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"2341\" data-end=\"2446\">\r\n<td data-start=\"2341\" data-end=\"2345\" data-col-size=\"sm\">3</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"2345\" data-end=\"2363\">Other penalties</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"2363\" data-end=\"2410\">As per EOI issued based on this empanelment.</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"2410\" data-end=\"2446\">Maximum 10% of work order value.</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', NULL, '<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"128\" data-end=\"385\">\r\n<p data-start=\"130\" data-end=\"385\">CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest (EOI). No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation or discussion with the Committee.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"386\" data-end=\"579\">\r\n<p data-start=\"388\" data-end=\"579\">A presentation will be made by the bidding companies to demonstrate their understanding of the proposed area of work and to showcase their experience, if any, in similar areas of expertise.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"580\" data-end=\"713\">\r\n<p data-start=\"582\" data-end=\"713\">During the presentation by the companies, the proposed candidates will be interviewed (face-to-face) by the Evaluation Committee.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"714\" data-end=\"1052\">\r\n<p data-start=\"716\" data-end=\"1052\">Any deviation from the proposal and resource CVs submitted as part of the bid response to this EOI will not be considered and will result in rejection. Therefore, bidders are instructed to ensure that the actual resource who will be deployed for the assignment is present for the interview (in person, via Skype, or video conference).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1053\" data-end=\"1210\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1055\" data-end=\"1128\">The marking for the presentation and interview will be done as follows:<br><br></p>\r\n<table style=\"height: 89px; width: 100%;\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr data-start=\"410\" data-end=\"735\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 10.7762%;\" data-start=\"410\" data-end=\"437\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"412\" data-end=\"435\">Bidder Presentation</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 5.80268%;\" data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"437\" data-end=\"452\"><strong data-start=\"439\" data-end=\"451\">50 Marks</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 83.4211%;\" data-col-size=\"xl\" data-start=\"452\" data-end=\"735\">- Approach and Methodology<br>- Understanding of the Project<br>- Quality of proposed methodology for such specific kind of project<br>- Prior exposure to implementing government projects in Bid Management and Exit Management<br>- Understanding of key SLAs for project management</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<table>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr data-start=\"736\" data-end=\"1450\">\r\n<td data-start=\"736\" data-end=\"763\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"738\" data-end=\"761\">Candidate Interview</strong></td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"763\" data-end=\"778\"><strong data-start=\"765\" data-end=\"777\">50 Marks</strong></td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"xl\" data-start=\"778\" data-end=\"1450\">- The CVs of the following positions to be submitted as part of the EoI submission; interviews shall be conducted only for these positions. The rest of the CVs are to be submitted at the time of mobilization of the team at CGHB:<br>1. Project Director<br>2. Team Leader<br>3. Finance Expert<br>4. Procurement Expert<br>5. Technical Expert<br><br><strong data-start=\"1136\" data-end=\"1159\">Interview Criteria:</strong><br>- Suitability of profile<br>- Years of relevant experience<br>- Good understanding of project management best practices framework<br>- Ability to Negotiate / Persuade / Influence<br>- Strong ability to understand, deliberate, and monitor key SLAs<br>- Excellent communication abilities</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p class=\"p1\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to be done after careful</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The last date for submission of response is 21/10/2024,17:00 Hrs. Any response received after the above deadline</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">will be rejected.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">CEO, CHiPS, State Data Centre, Civil Lines,</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Raipur 492001</p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\"><span class=\"s1\">Email ID: </span>ceochips@nic.in empl.chips@cgchips.in</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax:+91 771-4014158</p>', '<ul data-start=\"118\" data-end=\"380\">\r\n<li data-start=\"118\" data-end=\"146\">\r\n<p data-start=\"120\" data-end=\"146\">Signed copy of this EOI.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"147\" data-end=\"201\">\r\n<p data-start=\"149\" data-end=\"201\">Copy of the approach and methodology presentation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"202\" data-end=\"380\">\r\n<p data-start=\"204\" data-end=\"380\">Resumes of resources who will appear for the interview. The format of resumes shall be as per empanelment tender number <strong data-start=\"324\" data-end=\"377\">68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020 dated 31/10/2020</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-29 10:36:29', 4, 1, '2025-10-29 01:29:53', 23, '2025-10-29 10:36:29', NULL, '2025-10-29 10:39:43', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-29', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Selection of Project Support Consultant for CG Housing Board', '2024-10-04', '2024-10-09 17:00:00', '2024-10-21 00:00:00', '2024-10-22 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-11', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/xvZArqxSY422P47P37TiMQ7NlpfQ7gmjlW5fjZVM.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 75504348.39, 0, 0, 13590782.71, 89095131.1, 1, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(6, 85, 31, 'EOI/EMPL/CHiPS/PMU/PMGATISHAKTI/2024', 1, 'PMU for PM GatiShakti', '12', '<p class=\"p1\">The objective of the assignment is to provide assistance to <strong>Department of Commerce &amp; Industries </strong><strong>for </strong>Gati Shakti Initiatives in the State of Chhattisgarh.&nbsp;DGM/CHiPS is inviting all empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No.&nbsp;68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/31-10-2020) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope&nbsp;of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.</p>', 2, 31, '2024-09-24 01:52:31', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 18054000, 902700, 18956700, 0, 18, 5, '<p class=\"p1\">PM GatiShakti National Master Plan (PMGS-NMP) was launched for providing multimodal connectivity&nbsp;infrastructure to various economic zones. PM GatiShakti National Master Plan will encompass the 7 engines&nbsp;for economic transformation, seamless multimodal connectivity and logistics efficiency. It will also include&nbsp;the infrastructure developed by the State Governments, as per the GatiShakti Master Plan. The focus will be&nbsp;on planning, financing including through innovative ways, use of technology and speedier implementation.&nbsp;The PMU shall provide assistance and handholding support to the Department of Commerce and Industries,&nbsp;Chhattisgarh for implementation of various initiatives identified under Gati Shakti including State Master&nbsp;Plan and its integration with National Master Plan.</p>', NULL, NULL, '<p data-start=\"1151\" data-end=\"1263\">The TSU shall support the Department of Commerce and Industries, Chhattisgarh, through the following activities:</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"1265\" data-end=\"1268\">\r\n<h3 data-start=\"1270\" data-end=\"1323\"><strong data-start=\"1274\" data-end=\"1323\">1. Implementation of PM GatiShakti Initiative</strong></h3>\r\n<h4 data-start=\"1325\" data-end=\"1374\"><strong data-start=\"1330\" data-end=\"1374\">a) PM GatiShakti State Level Master Plan</strong></h4>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1376\" data-end=\"2801\">\r\n<li data-start=\"1376\" data-end=\"1475\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1378\" data-end=\"1475\">Assist the Department in identifying critical layers to be integrated on the GatiShakti Portal.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1476\" data-end=\"1642\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1478\" data-end=\"1642\">Map various attributes and layers for implementing the <strong data-start=\"1533\" data-end=\"1554\">State Master Plan</strong> and integrate it with the <strong data-start=\"1581\" data-end=\"1611\">National Master Plan (NMP)</strong> as per <strong data-start=\"1619\" data-end=\"1639\">DPIIT guidelines</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1643\" data-end=\"1824\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1645\" data-end=\"1824\">Coordinate with the <strong data-start=\"1665\" data-end=\"1694\">State Remote Sensing team</strong>, relevant <strong data-start=\"1705\" data-end=\"1720\">departments</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1722\" data-end=\"1735\">districts</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"1741\" data-end=\"1766\">local administrations</strong> for implementation at state, district, and city levels.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1825\" data-end=\"1924\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1827\" data-end=\"1924\">Coordinate with <strong data-start=\"1843\" data-end=\"1854\">BISAG-N</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1856\" data-end=\"1864\">RSAC</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"1870\" data-end=\"1891\">State Departments</strong> for continuous portal updates.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1925\" data-end=\"2020\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1927\" data-end=\"2020\">Facilitate mapping of key infrastructure assets and planned projects up to 2024 and beyond.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2021\" data-end=\"2117\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2023\" data-end=\"2117\">Ensure <strong data-start=\"2030\" data-end=\"2056\">constant data updation</strong> to keep the State Master Plan dynamic and future-relevant.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2118\" data-end=\"2215\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2120\" data-end=\"2215\">Conduct <strong data-start=\"2128\" data-end=\"2159\">infrastructure gap analysis</strong> around key industrial areas/parks and other projects.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2216\" data-end=\"2328\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2218\" data-end=\"2328\">Plan <strong data-start=\"2223\" data-end=\"2249\">integrated development</strong> of economic zones and clusters near DFCs, corridors, expressways, and ports.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2329\" data-end=\"2412\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2331\" data-end=\"2412\">Provide <strong data-start=\"2339\" data-end=\"2359\">decision support</strong> for multimodal logistics planning and integration.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2413\" data-end=\"2562\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2415\" data-end=\"2562\">Perform <strong data-start=\"2423\" data-end=\"2439\">data mapping</strong> of physical assets and assist in <strong data-start=\"2473\" data-end=\"2500\">geospatial data capture</strong>, <strong data-start=\"2502\" data-end=\"2528\">metadata documentation</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"2534\" data-end=\"2559\">SOP-compliant mapping</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2563\" data-end=\"2697\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2565\" data-end=\"2697\">Support project selection based on <strong data-start=\"2600\" data-end=\"2665\">logistics efficiency, resilience, sustainability, reliability</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"2671\" data-end=\"2694\">integrated planning</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2698\" data-end=\"2801\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2700\" data-end=\"2801\">Facilitate <strong data-start=\"2711\" data-end=\"2741\">API-based data integration</strong> between state planning portals and the PM GatiShakti NMP.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4 data-start=\"2803\" data-end=\"2861\"><strong data-start=\"2808\" data-end=\"2861\">b) Mapping of Regulatory Approvals and Clearances</strong></h4>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2863\" data-end=\"3199\">\r\n<li data-start=\"2863\" data-end=\"2948\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2865\" data-end=\"2948\">Coordinate with departments to identify project-related approvals and clearances.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2949\" data-end=\"3047\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2951\" data-end=\"3047\">Map these approvals geographically and institutionally on the PM GatiShakti State Master Plan.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3048\" data-end=\"3100\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3050\" data-end=\"3100\">Adopt a <strong data-start=\"3058\" data-end=\"3085\">district-level approach</strong> for mapping.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3101\" data-end=\"3199\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3103\" data-end=\"3199\">Assist in <strong data-start=\"3113\" data-end=\"3157\">process standardization and digitization</strong> to enhance efficiency and productivity.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4 data-start=\"3201\" data-end=\"3252\"><strong data-start=\"3206\" data-end=\"3252\">c) Assistance in Logistics Sector Projects</strong></h4>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3254\" data-end=\"4014\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3254\" data-end=\"3345\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3256\" data-end=\"3345\">Support the State in identifying and implementing <strong data-start=\"3306\" data-end=\"3342\">multimodal connectivity projects</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3346\" data-end=\"3407\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3348\" data-end=\"3407\">Assist the <strong data-start=\"3359\" data-end=\"3367\">EGoS</strong> in monitoring project implementation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3408\" data-end=\"3500\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3410\" data-end=\"3500\">Facilitate <strong data-start=\"3421\" data-end=\"3447\">grant/loan acquisition</strong> under the <em data-start=\"3458\" data-end=\"3497\">Special Assistance from Centre Scheme</em>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3501\" data-end=\"3593\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3503\" data-end=\"3593\">Prepare a <strong data-start=\"3513\" data-end=\"3547\">logistics optimization roadmap</strong> using analytics for better decision-making.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3594\" data-end=\"3667\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3596\" data-end=\"3667\">Synchronize efforts between <strong data-start=\"3624\" data-end=\"3631\">NPG</strong>, <strong data-start=\"3633\" data-end=\"3641\">EGoS</strong>, and relevant agencies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3668\" data-end=\"3728\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3670\" data-end=\"3728\">Track and monitor <strong data-start=\"3688\" data-end=\"3704\">data updates</strong> from all departments.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3729\" data-end=\"3786\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3731\" data-end=\"3786\">Provide <strong data-start=\"3739\" data-end=\"3783\">technical and project management support</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3787\" data-end=\"3856\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3789\" data-end=\"3856\">Document <strong data-start=\"3798\" data-end=\"3817\">recommendations</strong> and coordinate departmental actions.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3857\" data-end=\"3935\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3859\" data-end=\"3935\">Manage <strong data-start=\"3866\" data-end=\"3932\">events, workshops, stakeholder meetings, and outreach programs</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3936\" data-end=\"4014\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3938\" data-end=\"4014\">Support <strong data-start=\"3946\" data-end=\"3980\">procurement and bid management</strong> for third-party agency selection.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"4016\" data-end=\"4019\">\r\n<h3 data-start=\"4021\" data-end=\"4087\"><strong data-start=\"4025\" data-end=\"4087\">2. Integrated Development of Logistics Sector in the State</strong></h3>\r\n<h4 data-start=\"4089\" data-end=\"4150\"><strong data-start=\"4094\" data-end=\"4150\">d) Implementation of Integrated State Logistics Plan</strong></h4>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4152\" data-end=\"4639\">\r\n<li data-start=\"4152\" data-end=\"4235\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4154\" data-end=\"4235\">Coordinate with departments for <strong data-start=\"4186\" data-end=\"4220\">development and implementation</strong> of the plan.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4236\" data-end=\"4307\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4238\" data-end=\"4307\">Facilitate <strong data-start=\"4249\" data-end=\"4272\">industry engagement</strong> to gather feedback and insights.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4308\" data-end=\"4404\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4310\" data-end=\"4404\">Establish mechanisms for <strong data-start=\"4335\" data-end=\"4370\">inter-departmental coordination</strong> and <strong data-start=\"4375\" data-end=\"4401\">stakeholder engagement</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4405\" data-end=\"4480\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4407\" data-end=\"4480\">Oversee <strong data-start=\"4415\" data-end=\"4441\">project implementation</strong> under the <strong data-start=\"4452\" data-end=\"4477\">Logistics Master Plan</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4481\" data-end=\"4545\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4483\" data-end=\"4545\">Maintain and update the <strong data-start=\"4507\" data-end=\"4522\">Action Plan</strong> to monitor progress.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4546\" data-end=\"4639\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4548\" data-end=\"4639\">Track implementation of identified projects and initiatives through <strong data-start=\"4616\" data-end=\"4636\">periodic reports</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4 data-start=\"4641\" data-end=\"4714\"><strong data-start=\"4646\" data-end=\"4714\">e) Response to Government of India &ndash; GatiShakti and LEADS Survey</strong></h4>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4716\" data-end=\"5301\">\r\n<li data-start=\"4716\" data-end=\"4811\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4718\" data-end=\"4811\">Analyze parameters related to <strong data-start=\"4748\" data-end=\"4808\">logistics infrastructure, connectivity, and nodal points</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4812\" data-end=\"4892\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4814\" data-end=\"4892\">Evaluate <strong data-start=\"4823\" data-end=\"4873\">LEADS (Logistics Ease Across Different States)</strong> survey rankings.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4893\" data-end=\"4963\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4895\" data-end=\"4963\">Coordinate with departments for survey-related inputs and actions.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4964\" data-end=\"5041\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4966\" data-end=\"5041\">Identify short-term and long-term gaps and propose actionable strategies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5042\" data-end=\"5144\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5044\" data-end=\"5144\">Draft the <strong data-start=\"5054\" data-end=\"5098\">Chhattisgarh State Logistics Master Plan</strong> including <strong data-start=\"5109\" data-end=\"5141\">LEADS report recommendations</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5145\" data-end=\"5220\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5147\" data-end=\"5220\">Map departments against <strong data-start=\"5171\" data-end=\"5196\">LEADS recommendations</strong> and monitor progress.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5221\" data-end=\"5301\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5223\" data-end=\"5301\">Assist the Department in implementing the <strong data-start=\"5265\" data-end=\"5298\">Industrial Park Rating System</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5221\" data-end=\"5301\">oordination and Consultation</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5346\" data-end=\"5703\">\r\n<li data-start=\"5346\" data-end=\"5441\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5348\" data-end=\"5441\">Promote <strong data-start=\"5356\" data-end=\"5393\">adoption of the PM GatiShakti NMP</strong> through data uploads and backend integration.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5442\" data-end=\"5556\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5444\" data-end=\"5556\">Coordinate with <strong data-start=\"5460\" data-end=\"5474\">ministries</strong>, <strong data-start=\"5476\" data-end=\"5496\">state government</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"5502\" data-end=\"5531\">inter-agency stakeholders</strong> for project execution.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5557\" data-end=\"5703\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5559\" data-end=\"5703\">Engage with <strong data-start=\"5571\" data-end=\"5602\">Spatial Planning Institutes</strong>, <strong data-start=\"5604\" data-end=\"5630\">Subject Matter Experts</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"5636\" data-end=\"5651\">Think Tanks</strong> to develop customized state-level planning tools.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4 data-start=\"5705\" data-end=\"5746\"><strong data-start=\"5710\" data-end=\"5746\">f) Planning and Tool Development</strong></h4>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5748\" data-end=\"5898\">\r\n<li data-start=\"5748\" data-end=\"5825\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5750\" data-end=\"5825\">Facilitate <strong data-start=\"5761\" data-end=\"5822\">development of state-specific planning tools and datasets</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5826\" data-end=\"5898\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5828\" data-end=\"5898\">Coordinate with <strong data-start=\"5844\" data-end=\"5855\">BISAG-N</strong> for technical and planning tool support.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h4 data-start=\"5900\" data-end=\"5941\"><strong data-start=\"5905\" data-end=\"5941\">g) Identification and Resolution</strong></h4>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5943\" data-end=\"6121\">\r\n<li data-start=\"5943\" data-end=\"6023\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5945\" data-end=\"6023\">Identify challenges faced by Chhattisgarh in adopting the PM GatiShakti SMP.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"6024\" data-end=\"6121\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6026\" data-end=\"6121\">Document issues and provide <strong data-start=\"6054\" data-end=\"6096\">feedback for escalation and resolution</strong> at the Ministry level.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '<h2 data-start=\"155\" data-end=\"178\"><strong data-start=\"158\" data-end=\"178\">Payment Terms</strong></h2>\r\n<p data-start=\"180\" data-end=\"292\">Payment to the selected bidder for the scope of work completed will be released as per the following schedule:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"294\" data-end=\"663\">\r\n<li data-start=\"294\" data-end=\"419\">\r\n<p data-start=\"296\" data-end=\"419\">The successful bidder shall submit the <strong data-start=\"335\" data-end=\"379\">invoice for payment on a man-month basis</strong>, as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"420\" data-end=\"663\">\r\n<p data-start=\"422\" data-end=\"663\">For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or <strong data-start=\"479\" data-end=\"488\">CHiPS</strong>, the selected bidder shall be <strong data-start=\"519\" data-end=\"559\">paid the requisite man-month payment</strong>, provided that the bidder has performed its obligations in compliance with the terms of the contract.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"665\" data-end=\"668\">\r\n<h2 data-start=\"670\" data-end=\"693\"><strong data-start=\"673\" data-end=\"693\">Penalty Terms</strong></h2>\r\n<ul data-start=\"695\" data-end=\"774\">\r\n<li data-start=\"695\" data-end=\"774\">\r\n<p data-start=\"697\" data-end=\"774\">Penalty, if any, shall be <strong data-start=\"723\" data-end=\"771\">governed as per the agreed empanelment terms</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"240\" data-end=\"397\">\r\n<p data-start=\"242\" data-end=\"397\"><strong data-start=\"242\" data-end=\"251\">CHiPS</strong> will constitute an <strong data-start=\"271\" data-end=\"295\">Evaluation Committee</strong>, whose decision shall be <strong data-start=\"321\" data-end=\"330\">final</strong> in evaluating responses to the <strong data-start=\"362\" data-end=\"394\">Expression of Interest (EOI)</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"398\" data-end=\"512\">\r\n<p data-start=\"400\" data-end=\"512\"><strong data-start=\"400\" data-end=\"421\">No correspondence</strong> will be entertained outside the process of negotiation or discussion with the Committee.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"513\" data-end=\"723\">\r\n<p data-start=\"515\" data-end=\"723\">A <strong data-start=\"517\" data-end=\"533\">presentation</strong> shall be made by the bidding company demonstrating their <strong data-start=\"591\" data-end=\"638\">understanding of the proposed scope of work</strong> and their <strong data-start=\"649\" data-end=\"663\">experience</strong> in similar areas of expertise (<strong data-start=\"695\" data-end=\"719\">via Video Conference</strong>).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"724\" data-end=\"883\">\r\n<p data-start=\"726\" data-end=\"883\">During this presentation, the <strong data-start=\"756\" data-end=\"780\">Evaluation Committee</strong> will also <strong data-start=\"791\" data-end=\"828\">interview the proposed candidates</strong> (either <strong data-start=\"837\" data-end=\"851\">physically</strong> or <strong data-start=\"855\" data-end=\"879\">via Video Conference</strong>).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"884\" data-end=\"959\">\r\n<p data-start=\"886\" data-end=\"959\">The <strong data-start=\"890\" data-end=\"932\">marking for Presentation and Interview</strong> will be done as follows:<br><br></p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th><strong>Key Evaluation Criteria</strong></th>\r\n<th><strong>Bidder Presentation</strong><em>(50 Marks)</em></th>\r\n<th><strong>Candidate Interview</strong><em>(50 Marks)</em></th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Criteria Details</strong></td>\r\n<td>&bull; Approach and Methodology &bull; Understanding of the Project Framework &bull; Quality of proposed methodology for such a specific kind of project &bull; Prior experience in project interaction with senior Government officials &bull; Prior exposure to auditing Government projects &bull; Resource deployment at multiple Government offices across multiple locations &bull; Understanding of key SLAs of project management</td>\r\n<td>&bull; Suitability of profile &bull; Years of relevant experience &bull; Good understanding of project management best practices framework &bull; Ability to negotiate, persuade, and influence &bull; Strong ability to deliberate, monitor, and report key SLAs &bull; Excellent communication abilities</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p data-start=\"129\" data-end=\"468\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions, and implications.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"470\" data-end=\"607\">The last date for submission of response is <strong data-start=\"514\" data-end=\"539\">21/10/2024, 17:00 Hrs</strong>. Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"609\" data-end=\"688\">The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"690\" data-end=\"863\"><strong data-start=\"690\" data-end=\"753\">CEO, CHiPS, State Data Centre, Civil Lines, Raipur &ndash; 492001</strong><br data-start=\"753\" data-end=\"756\"><strong data-start=\"759\" data-end=\"778\"><a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"761\" data-end=\"776\">ceochips@nic.in</a></strong>, <strong data-start=\"780\" data-end=\"805\"><a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"782\" data-end=\"803\">empl.chips@cgchips.in</a></strong><br data-start=\"805\" data-end=\"808\"><strong data-start=\"811\" data-end=\"819\">Tel:</strong> +91-771-4014158&emsp;&emsp;<strong data-start=\"837\" data-end=\"845\">Fax:</strong> +91-771-4014158</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"97\" data-end=\"128\">\r\n<p data-start=\"99\" data-end=\"128\"><strong data-start=\"99\" data-end=\"114\">Signed copy</strong> of this EOI</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"129\" data-end=\"234\">\r\n<p data-start=\"131\" data-end=\"234\"><strong data-start=\"131\" data-end=\"153\">Experience details</strong> of the bidding firm along with relevant <strong data-start=\"194\" data-end=\"232\">Work Orders / supporting documents</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"235\" data-end=\"292\">\r\n<p data-start=\"237\" data-end=\"292\"><strong data-start=\"237\" data-end=\"290\">Copy of the Approach and Methodology presentation</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"293\" data-end=\"447\">\r\n<p data-start=\"295\" data-end=\"447\"><strong data-start=\"295\" data-end=\"306\">Resumes</strong> of the resources who will attend the interview, as per the format specified in <strong data-start=\"386\" data-end=\"445\">Empanelment Tender No. 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-29 11:24:41', 4, 1, '2025-10-29 10:04:43', 31, '2025-10-29 11:24:41', NULL, '2025-10-29 11:27:57', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-29', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'For Selection of PMU for Gati Shakti Initiatives in the state of Chhattisgarh', '2024-10-04', '2024-10-09 17:00:00', '2024-10-21 00:00:00', '2024-10-22 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-11', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/FKbRSvDQlBPM9EDLdBbcnnVapeGKMRHoXpmBEyR8.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 5264516.13, 0, 0, 947612.9, 6212129.03, 1, 0, NULL, NULL),
(7, 81, 28, 'CEO/EMPL/PMU/IGRS/CHiPS/2024', 1, 'Design, Development, and Implementation of next generation registration application for Stamps and Registration Department, Govt. of Chhattisgarh', '12', '<p>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS), the nodal agency of Department of Information Technology, Government of Chhattisgarh in the State of Chhattisgarh invites proposal for &ldquo;Selection of System Integrator for design, development, and implementation of next generation of registration application for Stamps and Registration department, Government of Chhattisgarh.&rdquo;<br><br>All empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No- 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020) are invited to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.</p>', 2, 28, '2024-11-25 11:29:35', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 73561200, 3678060, 77239260, 0, 18, 5, '<p><strong>Introduction</strong></p>\r\n<p>In order to establish a uniform process for the registration of deeds and documents across the country, the Government of India is implementing the &ldquo;One Nation One Registration Software,&rdquo; known as the &ldquo;National Generic Document Registration System (NGDRS).&rdquo; NGDRS is a significant initiative by the Government of India, aimed at transforming document registration processes nationwide.</p>\r\n<p>Aligned with the Viksit Bharat 2047 vision for a \"Developed India,\" the NGDRS system is designed as a<br>configurable, user-centric platform supporting sub-registrars, citizens, and departmental users. NGDRS is<br>more than a catchphrase; it represents a common, generic, and adaptable application tailored specifically<br>for use by sub-registrars, citizens, and apex users within registration departments.</p>\r\n<p>NGDRS enables states to create state-specific instances and configure the software according to their unique requirements. It offers a user-friendly interface for property and document registration, allowing citizens to conduct land transactions online. From checking circle rates to calculating property valuations, citizens can make informed decisions about land purchases. NGDRS streamlines the process by allowing property buyers to visit the sub-registrar\'s office only once&mdash;for final signing and registration.</p>\r\n<p>Additionally, NGDRS has significantly boosted departmental productivity. Aligned with the Viksit Bharat vision, it utilizes modern open-source technologies, microservices, enhanced user experience design, Platform as a Service (PaaS), DevOps, and more, empowering citizens, enhancing transparency, and contributing to India\'s journey toward becoming a developed nation by 2047</p>\r\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong></p>\r\n<p>The state of Chhattisgarh aims to develop the next generation of registration application based on current NGDRS application in Chhattisgarh is to modernize, simplify, and enhance the efficiency of property and document registration processes across the state. The state of Chhattisgarh, by implementing next generation of registration application the Chhattisgarh Stamp &amp; Registration Department aims to achieve the following:</p>\r\n<p>a) Improve Accessibility and Convenience for Citizens: Next generation of registration application will offers a digital-first approach, allowing citizens to conduct essential registration tasks&mdash;such as checking circle rates, calculating property valuations, and document registration&mdash;from anywhere with internet access. This reduces the need for multiple physical visits to sub-registrar offices, enabling citizens to visit only once for final signing and verification.</p>\r\n<p>b) Enhance Transparency and Trust: Next generation of registration application promotes transparency by providing citizens with real-time access to land transaction information, valuation rates, and document verification processes. This increases accountability and trust between the registration department and the citizens it serves</p>\r\n<p>c) State-Specific Configurability: Next generation of registration application allows for a customized configuration that aligns with Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s unique regulatory, linguistic, and procedural requirements. This adaptability enables the state to meet its specific needs while adhering to a standardized framework.</p>\r\n<p>d) Increase Efficiency and Productivity: With next generation of registration application, the registration process is streamlined, reducing manual processes, paperwork, and redundancies, thereby improving the overall productivity of the department. Automation and digital workflows also reduce errors and accelerate service deliveryd) Increase Efficiency and Productivity: With next generation of registration application, the registration process is streamlined, reducing manual processes, paperwork, and redundancies, thereby improving the overall productivity of the department. Automation and digital workflows also reduce errors and accelerate service delivery</p>\r\n<p>e) Alignment with the Viksit Bharat 2047 Vision: The next generation of registration application initiative aligns with India&rsquo;s Viksit Bharat 2047 vision, aiming to support the pillars of Yuva (Youth), Garib (Poor), Mahila (Women), and Kisan (Farmers) by providing a more inclusive and accessible registration system that fosters empowerment and development for all segments of society.</p>\r\n<p>f) Leverage Modern Technology for a Scalable Solution: Utilizing open-source technologies, microservices architecture, Platform as a Service (PaaS), and DevOps practices, next generation of registration application provides a scalable and robust platform capable of handling Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s future needs and supporting the state&rsquo;s journey toward digital transformation.</p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">&nbsp;</p>', NULL, NULL, '<p>a. Study the Registration process of department and Current system (NGDRS1.0) <br>Study the Registration and other process of department to understand the requirement of the department. Also study the NGDRS1.0 system to understand its challenges and technological gaps such as gap in design, missing attributes, redesigning the modules or UI/UX improvement, unavailability of required reports &amp; dashboards etc. Conduct an in-depth analysis of the existing NGDRS, including its features, user interface, and workflow, and Identify areas of improvement and potential integration points with other government databases.</p>\r\n<p>b. Requirement gathering &amp; preparation of Functional Requirement Specifications&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>Engage with stakeholders to gather detailed functional requirements, Document the requirements in an FRS, ensuring clarity and completeness for developers and stakeholders.</p>\r\n<p>c. Preparation of SRS, Design Documents, test cases, test plans &amp; DevOps</p>\r\n<p>Develop an SRS that translates the FRS into technical specifications, create SRS wireframes, design<br>documents that outline the system architecture and module interactions, write unit and integration test<br>cases to ensure quality and reliability, Establish a DevOps pipeline for continuous integration and<br>deployment.</p>\r\n<p>d. Development of modules</p>\r\n<p>Define modules such as User Management, Property Valuation, Document Submission, Payment Processing, and Appointment Scheduling based on the current NGDRS structure, consult with department to understand the requirement of new modules. All the modules&rsquo; implementations should be done along with its complete documentation viz. SRS, architecture-design documents, code comments, test cases etc.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '<p>Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the agreed&nbsp;empanelment terms.</li>\r\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed current empanelment terms.</li>\r\n<li>The consultancy firm shall perform its obligations under the agreement in a professional manner.&nbsp;In the event of failure to maintain the SLA or deliverables timelines, the penalty would be levied&nbsp;as per below:&nbsp;\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Go-Live of the next generation registration application (Both Phase I &amp; Phase II): The selected&nbsp;consultancy firm shall be responsible for the delivery of the modules as per the timeline&nbsp;mentioned in the EOI document. For any delay in the Go-Live, a 1% penalty will be applicable&nbsp;of the monthly invoice value for each month\'s delay.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Post Implementation Operation &amp; Maintenance Support Services: The criticality of the required&nbsp;services for next generation registration application including bug fixing, technical support, etc. is&nbsp;categorized under the four categories/ priorities i.e. Critical, High, Medium, and Low. Each of the&nbsp;support categories is associated with a respective response and resolution time as under:&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHIPS/CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/ discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding companies about their understanding of the proposed&nbsp;area of work and their experience if any in similar area of expertise.</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies the proposed candidates may be interviewed (face to&nbsp;face/virtually through video conferencing) by the Evaluation Committee.</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and Interview will be done as follows-</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.036%; border-width: 1px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.3333%;\"></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">Bidder Presentation</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">Candidates Interview</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">50 Marks</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top; text-align: center;\">50 Marks</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">Key&nbsp;Evaluation&nbsp;Criteria</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of theProject</li>\r\n<li>Prior exposure in E-Governance projects</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of the profile</li>\r\n<li>Educational Qualification</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant Experience</li>\r\n<li>Experience of Working in<br>Government Projects</li>\r\n<li>Communication abilities</li>\r\n<li>Strong ability to understand and<br>deliberate and report and monitor<br>the key aspects</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>The bidder receiving highest marking shall be considered for award of work.</p>', '<p>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in&nbsp;response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to&nbsp;have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its&nbsp;terms, conditions and implications.</p>\r\n<p>The last date for submission of response is 09/12/2024 at 05:00 PM. Any response received after the&nbsp;above deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n<p>The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to</p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>CHiPS, State Data Centre, Civil<br>Lines, Raipur 492001.<br>Email: ceochips@nic.in<br>empl.chips@cgchips.in<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-4014158</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EOI</li>\r\n<li>Copy of Approach and methodology presentation</li>\r\n<li>Resumes of the proposed resources. The format of resumes will be as per empanelment tender&nbsp;number 8733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-29 11:39:41', 4, 1, '2025-10-29 11:38:26', 28, '2025-10-29 11:39:41', NULL, '2025-10-29 11:40:16', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-29', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Selection of Consultancy firm for Design, Development, and Implementation of next generation of registration application for IGRS Department, Governme', '2024-11-25', '2024-11-29 17:00:00', '2024-12-09 00:00:00', '2024-12-16 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-11', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/HevL8mfZWFuGGVkqmlnPlcGlRTnP6b7UCzvDyj6Q.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 30304166.67, 0, 0, 5454750, 35758916.67, 1, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(8, 75, 32, 'EOI/EMPL/CHiPS/PMU/EP/2025', 1, 'State Level PMU for Export Promotion', '24', '<p data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"513\">The Director of Industries, Government of Chhattisgarh, is seeking to establish a Program Management Unit (PMU) with professional consultants for the planning, implementation, and monitoring of export promotion&ndash;related works. The scope of work for the PMU will broadly encompass the comprehensive management of projects, activities, and schemes being implemented by the Director of Industries, Government of Chhattisgarh, ensuring alignment with the Government of India guidelines and the Ministry&rsquo;s directives.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"515\" data-end=\"1078\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">The PMU will provide end-to-end consultancy support and handholding to the Director of Industries, Government of Chhattisgarh, in planning, implementation, and monitoring of schemes related to export promotion in the state. This support will include planning, policy formulation, and the monitoring of physical (desk assessment) and financial progress of the projects. Additionally, the PMU will focus on capacity building, knowledge management, Information, Education, and Communication (IEC), and other critical aspects of program management and implementation.</p>', 2, 32, '2025-01-20 12:04:13', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 61737600, 3086880, 64824480, 0, 18, 5, '<p data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"544\">The Government of Chhattisgarh recognizes the critical role of exports in driving economic growth, industrial development, and global competitiveness. To harness the State\'s export potential and align with national objectives, the Directorate of Industries seeks to establish a dedicated Project Management Unit (PMU) for Export Promotion. The PMU will serve as a strategic and operational partner in enhancing the State\'s export ecosystem through targeted interventions, policy formulation, capacity building, and infrastructure development.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"546\" data-end=\"1129\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">This initiative aims to strengthen Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s position in both domestic and international markets by transitioning from raw material exports to high-value finished products, developing district-level export hubs, promoting Champion Service Sectors, and improving the State&rsquo;s performance in national export preparedness indices. By addressing critical gaps in infrastructure, market access, and institutional support&mdash;while leveraging emerging trends in international trade&mdash;the PMU will play a pivotal role in fostering an export-oriented economic framework for sustainable growth.</p>', NULL, NULL, '<p data-start=\"181\" data-end=\"404\">The consultant shall support the Export Cell under the Directorate of Industries, Department of Commerce &amp; Industries, Government of Chhattisgarh across the following major components and component-wise scope of work items:</p>\r\n<h4 data-start=\"406\" data-end=\"500\">1. Support in the formulation of New/Revised Export Promotion Strategy for Chhattisgarh</h4>\r\n<ul data-start=\"501\" data-end=\"1323\">\r\n<li data-start=\"501\" data-end=\"672\">\r\n<p data-start=\"503\" data-end=\"672\">Conduct a comprehensive analysis of Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s existing export performance and trends, including sectoral contributions, export destinations, and emerging markets.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"673\" data-end=\"902\">\r\n<p data-start=\"675\" data-end=\"902\">Assist in preparation of the Export Promotion Strategy and the nuances pertaining to the exercise like data gathering, conduct of stakeholder meets, field work/interaction, data analysis, formulation of research reports, etc.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"903\" data-end=\"1162\">\r\n<p data-start=\"905\" data-end=\"1162\">Develop strategies, in the form of fiscal and non-fiscal initiatives, to boost exports of finished products from the state, in addition to the raw materials. Strategies may focus on transitioning from low-value add exports to high-value finished products.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1163\" data-end=\"1323\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1165\" data-end=\"1323\">Assist in conduct of the said Exporter Interactions Meets, identify and follow up with the right stakeholders/institutions for conduct of such interactions.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1325\" data-end=\"2019\"><strong data-start=\"1325\" data-end=\"1334\">Note:</strong> Currently, Chhattisgarh Industrial Policy 2024&ndash;30 has identified export promotion as a key strategy to bring in industrial development in the State and aims to create favorable environment for promotion of export and to attract foreign investment by encouraging the establishment of Special Economic Zones and development of necessary infrastructure. However, there&rsquo;s a need to develop a separate Export Strategy which accentuates the need to align with contemporary trends and requirements of the overall international trade landscape. Hence the need for formulation of an Export Promotion Strategy for Chhattisgarh in collaboration with the Export Cell, Directorate of Industries.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"2021\" data-end=\"2024\">\r\n<h4 data-start=\"2026\" data-end=\"2114\">2. Export Promotion support to improve market access of Exporters in Chhattisgarh</h4>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2115\" data-end=\"4525\">\r\n<li data-start=\"2115\" data-end=\"2266\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2117\" data-end=\"2266\">Assess export promotion facilitation provided by the state &ndash; key programs and policies, events calendar, target groups, stakeholders involved, etc.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2267\" data-end=\"2385\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2269\" data-end=\"2385\">Assess export ecosystem potential across districts &ndash; identify key products with potential and markets for exports.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2386\" data-end=\"2596\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2388\" data-end=\"2596\">Undertake stakeholder consultations to assess the effectiveness of the existing export promotion activities and evaluate the key gaps in the current institutional export promotion architecture of the state.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2597\" data-end=\"2761\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2599\" data-end=\"2761\">Conceptualize customized activities for selected products with potential including Geographical Indication (GI) tagged products for promotion in target markets.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2762\" data-end=\"3102\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2764\" data-end=\"3102\">Assist in compilation of the content for preparation of knowledge collaterals for export promotion &ndash; trade guide, sector profiles, market profiles, quarterly newsletters, E-books, Coffee table book, etc. The same may be circulated across Embassies/Missions abroad and in India, Central and State Departments, Associations/Chambers, etc.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3103\" data-end=\"3257\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3105\" data-end=\"3257\">Undertake outreach activities with Indian missions and business associations in target markets for generating export leads and scouting market access.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3258\" data-end=\"3435\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3260\" data-end=\"3435\">Assist in undertaking export promotion activities like organizing/participating in bilateral trade events, B2B meetings, BSM, Reverse BSM, organizing trade delegations, etc.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3436\" data-end=\"3579\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3438\" data-end=\"3579\">Identify potential and significant Domestic and International Trade Fairs and Exhibitions to provide a platform to the exporter fraternity.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3580\" data-end=\"3788\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3582\" data-end=\"3788\">Supplement Directorate&rsquo;s ongoing initiatives in this space for successful conduct of varied and significant exhibitions with the objective to provide impetus to market access and exposure to stakeholders.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3789\" data-end=\"3991\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3791\" data-end=\"3991\">Assist in upgradation/updation of contents of Directorate&rsquo;s portal which provides information on Export Market Intelligence, Warehouses, GI products and also is a Grievances and Redressals platform.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3992\" data-end=\"4153\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3994\" data-end=\"4153\">Supplement Directorate of Industries&rsquo; ongoing efforts towards capacity building programs/initiatives across districts like Bhilai, Raipur, Korba and Raigarh.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4154\" data-end=\"4438\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4156\" data-end=\"4438\">Assist in preparation of the export promotion calendar with coverage to maximum districts with identified export potential products &ndash; clearly identifying the events and activities to be undertaken/participated by the client, in order to promote and position the state effectively.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4439\" data-end=\"4525\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4441\" data-end=\"4525\">Assist in organizing events, investment promotion events, seminars, and workshops.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"4527\" data-end=\"4530\">\r\n<h4 data-start=\"4532\" data-end=\"4599\">3. Support in Developing Districts as Export Hubs initiative</h4>\r\n<p data-start=\"4600\" data-end=\"4877\">The initiative pertains to Government of India&rsquo;s vision to develop each district as an export hub in the country and has mandated the Regional Authorities of DGFT to work with respective state governments and district level officers, Lead Bank Managers to implement the same.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4878\" data-end=\"5641\">\r\n<li data-start=\"4878\" data-end=\"5040\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4880\" data-end=\"5040\">Conduct wide range of meetings at State and district level with grass root officers and stakeholders to sensitize on the subject and vision of Govt. of India.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5041\" data-end=\"5173\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5043\" data-end=\"5173\">Organize capacity building and training programs which are appropriate and aligned with upskilling artisans and those concerned.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5174\" data-end=\"5265\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5176\" data-end=\"5265\">Identify export potential in each district and constantly interact with local industry.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5266\" data-end=\"5434\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5268\" data-end=\"5434\">Prepare promotional materials relevant to the district with information pertaining to Government of India and Government of Chhattisgarh schemes to promote exports.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5435\" data-end=\"5536\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5437\" data-end=\"5536\">Identify financial, logistics and other challenges faced in districts for suitable interventions.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5537\" data-end=\"5641\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5539\" data-end=\"5641\">Assist the Directorate in preparation of District Export Action Plans (DEAP)/Export Readiness Plans.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"5643\" data-end=\"5646\">\r\n<h4 data-start=\"5648\" data-end=\"5729\">4. Assistance in developing Champion Service Sectors (CSS) in Chhattisgarh</h4>\r\n<p data-start=\"5730\" data-end=\"5859\">Govt. of India in 2018 announced the Champion Services Sector Scheme with focus to 12 identified sectors in the Indian economy.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5860\" data-end=\"5987\">\r\n<li data-start=\"5860\" data-end=\"5987\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5862\" data-end=\"5987\">Assist Directorate of Industries in the development and implementation of Champion Services Sector Initiative/Action Plans.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"5989\" data-end=\"5992\">\r\n<h4 data-start=\"5994\" data-end=\"6095\">5. Assistance to enhance the scores/ranking of State in Government of India&rsquo;s Indexes like EPI</h4>\r\n<ul data-start=\"6096\" data-end=\"6779\">\r\n<li data-start=\"6096\" data-end=\"6779\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6098\" data-end=\"6256\">NITI Aayog at the behest of DPIIT, Ministry of Commerce &amp; Industry, comes up with the overall ranking of States through its Export Preparedness Index (EPI).</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"6259\" data-end=\"6779\">\r\n<li data-start=\"6259\" data-end=\"6418\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6261\" data-end=\"6418\">Assist in data gathering, field work, coordination with respective departments, for sharing it with Govt. of India for seamless conclusion of the exercise.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"6421\" data-end=\"6509\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6423\" data-end=\"6509\">Lend support in responding to the queries corresponding to assessment questionnaire.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"6512\" data-end=\"6603\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6514\" data-end=\"6603\">Analyze State&rsquo;s performance in the above Indexes to identify critical performance gaps.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"6606\" data-end=\"6779\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6608\" data-end=\"6779\">Support in enhancing State&rsquo;s ranking and performance, identifying strategic initiatives and interventions by concerned departments in the State and oversee the progress.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"6781\" data-end=\"6784\">\r\n<h4 data-start=\"6786\" data-end=\"6852\">6. Export related infrastructure assessment and development</h4>\r\n<ul data-start=\"6853\" data-end=\"8008\">\r\n<li data-start=\"6853\" data-end=\"6970\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6855\" data-end=\"6970\">Evaluate the existing export infrastructure, including logistics, ports, warehouses, and cold storage facilities.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"6971\" data-end=\"7516\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6973\" data-end=\"7516\">Support Directorate in implementation of several initiatives such as Establishment of Export Facilitation cum Convention Centre, air cargo along with Custom Clearance facility in Raipur, Awareness programs for export promotion through coordinated efforts of Export Promotion Council, Export Cell in the Directorate of Industries, additional industrial investment incentives to exports related manufacturing industries, strengthening of Inland Container Depot, upgradation of the Office of the Director General of Foreign Trade at Raipur etc.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"7517\" data-end=\"7751\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7519\" data-end=\"7751\">Support in utilization and implementation of initiatives funded by Central Government such as ASIDE, etc. and Multilateral Funding Institutions such as ADB, USAID, World Bank, etc. for development of export related infrastructure.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"7752\" data-end=\"7879\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7754\" data-end=\"7879\">Identify gaps in trade facilitation infrastructure such as testing labs, certification centers, and export promotion zones.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"7880\" data-end=\"8008\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7882\" data-end=\"8008\">Recommend infrastructure development and modernization projects, with a focus on industrial parks, SEZs, and logistics hubs.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"8010\" data-end=\"8013\">\r\n<h4 data-start=\"8015\" data-end=\"8072\">7. Development of a Web-based Platform &amp; Dashboard</h4>\r\n<ul data-start=\"8073\" data-end=\"8409\">\r\n<li data-start=\"8073\" data-end=\"8186\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8075\" data-end=\"8186\">Assist the Directorate in designing and maintenance of a query-based platform for export related information.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"8187\" data-end=\"8409\">\r\n<p data-start=\"8189\" data-end=\"8409\">The platform may include exporters database, export performance dashboard, trade insights, trade facilitation services, export schemes &amp; incentives, information related to regulations &amp; documentations for exports, etc.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"8411\" data-end=\"8414\">\r\n<h4 data-start=\"8416\" data-end=\"8441\">8. Team Deployment</h4>\r\n<p data-start=\"8442\" data-end=\"9037\">The Successful Agency shall deploy a team of consultants on a full-time/intermittent/part-time/remote-working basis at the office of the Client. Collectively, the team shall demonstrate adequate experience in the field of implementation of government programs to ensure quality service delivery to the client. The PMU team will be responsible for providing comprehensive support to Director Industries, Government of Chhattisgarh, ensuring the successful planning, implementation, and monitoring of all schemes and programs being implemented by Director Industries, Government of Chhattisgarh.</p>', NULL, '<h3 data-start=\"114\" data-end=\"135\">Payment Terms</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"136\" data-end=\"639\">\r\n<li data-start=\"136\" data-end=\"639\">\r\n<p data-start=\"138\" data-end=\"639\">Payment to the selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule:<br data-start=\"243\" data-end=\"246\">&bull; The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on a man-month basis as per the agreed empanelment terms.<br data-start=\"366\" data-end=\"369\">&bull; For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or CHiPS, as the case may be, the selected bidder shall be paid the requisite man-month payment in the event that the selected bidder has performed its obligations in compliance with the terms of this contract.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-start=\"646\" data-end=\"667\">Penalty Terms</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"668\" data-end=\"743\">\r\n<li data-start=\"668\" data-end=\"743\">\r\n<p data-start=\"670\" data-end=\"743\">Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '<ul data-start=\"183\" data-end=\"794\">\r\n<li data-start=\"183\" data-end=\"431\">\r\n<p data-start=\"185\" data-end=\"431\">CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"432\" data-end=\"609\">\r\n<p data-start=\"434\" data-end=\"609\">A presentation will be made by the bidding companies about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their past experience, if any, in similar areas of expertise.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"610\" data-end=\"722\">\r\n<p data-start=\"612\" data-end=\"722\">The Committee shall review the projects and CVs submitted along with the presentation and award the marking.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"723\" data-end=\"794\">\r\n<p data-start=\"725\" data-end=\"794\">The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"796\" data-end=\"799\">\r\n<h4 data-start=\"801\" data-end=\"826\"><strong data-start=\"806\" data-end=\"826\">Evaluation Table</strong></h4>\r\n<div class=\"_tableContainer_1rjym_1\">\r\n<div class=\"group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"828\" data-end=\"1773\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"828\" data-end=\"924\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"828\" data-end=\"924\">\r\n<th data-start=\"828\" data-end=\"853\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"830\" data-end=\"852\">Area of Evaluation</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"853\" data-end=\"879\" data-col-size=\"lg\"><strong data-start=\"855\" data-end=\"878\">Bidder Presentation</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"879\" data-end=\"905\" data-col-size=\"xl\"><strong data-start=\"881\" data-end=\"904\">Candidate Interview</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"905\" data-end=\"924\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"907\" data-end=\"922\">Total Marks</strong></th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"1025\" data-end=\"1773\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"1025\" data-end=\"1072\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1025\" data-end=\"1037\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"1027\" data-end=\"1036\">Marks</strong></td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1037\" data-end=\"1048\">50 Marks</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"xl\" data-start=\"1048\" data-end=\"1059\">50 Marks</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"1059\" data-end=\"1072\">100 Marks</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1073\" data-end=\"1773\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1073\" data-end=\"1103\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><strong data-start=\"1075\" data-end=\"1102\">Key Evaluation Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"lg\" data-start=\"1103\" data-end=\"1249\">- Approach and Methodology<br>- Understanding of the Project Framework<br>- Quality of proposed methodology for such specific kind of a project</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"xl\" data-start=\"1249\" data-end=\"1769\">- Suitability of profile<br>- Educational Qualification<br>- Years of relevant experience<br>- Good understanding of scope of work<br>- Prior experience in providing consulting/advisory services for trade promotion/strategy development<br>- Prior experience of drafting State and National level policies<br>- Prior experience in undertaking large transformation projects<br>- Strong ability to understand, deliberate, and report<br>- Excellent communication abilities<br>- Experience of working in Government Projects</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"1769\" data-end=\"1773\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr data-start=\"1775\" data-end=\"1778\">\r\n<h4 data-start=\"1780\" data-end=\"1794\"><strong data-start=\"1785\" data-end=\"1794\">Note:</strong></h4>\r\n<p data-start=\"1795\" data-end=\"2501\">i. All experience should be in the name of the firm bidding for the project. Experience of sister/associate firms shall not be eligible.<br data-start=\"1931\" data-end=\"1934\">ii. Only assignments where the work order is issued directly by a Government Entity/Donor Agency to the firm bidding for the project shall be eligible. Assignments carried out via any third party/private agency/sub-let shall not be considered for evaluation.<br data-start=\"2192\" data-end=\"2195\">iii. Only assignments undertaken directly by the agency will be considered eligible. Experiences or assignments from sister, associate, or subsidiary firms will not be recognized or considered. Further, to be eligible, the contract signing or work order must be exclusively issued by a Government Entity.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"2503\" data-end=\"2506\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2508\" data-end=\"2589\"><strong>The bidder receiving the highest marking shall be considered for award of work.</strong></p>', '<p data-start=\"82\" data-end=\"421\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions, and implications.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"423\" data-end=\"560\">The last date for submission of response is <strong data-start=\"467\" data-end=\"492\">05/02/2025, 17:00 hrs</strong>. Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"562\" data-end=\"641\">The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"643\" data-end=\"904\"><strong data-start=\"643\" data-end=\"670\">Chief Executive Officer</strong><br data-start=\"670\" data-end=\"673\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS),<br data-start=\"721\" data-end=\"724\">State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room,<br data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"780\">Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh &ndash; 492001<br data-start=\"822\" data-end=\"825\">Tel.: +91-771-4014158<br data-start=\"846\" data-end=\"849\">Email: <strong data-start=\"856\" data-end=\"875\"><a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"858\" data-end=\"873\">ceochips@nic.in</a></strong>, <strong data-start=\"877\" data-end=\"902\"><a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"879\" data-end=\"900\">empl.chips@cgchips.in</a></strong></p>', '<ul data-start=\"84\" data-end=\"299\">\r\n<li data-start=\"84\" data-end=\"112\">\r\n<p data-start=\"86\" data-end=\"112\">Signed copy of this EOI.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"113\" data-end=\"163\">\r\n<p data-start=\"115\" data-end=\"163\">Copy of Approach and Methodology presentation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"164\" data-end=\"299\">\r\n<p data-start=\"166\" data-end=\"299\">Resumes of the proposed resources. The format of resumes will be as per empanelment tender number 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-29 12:13:34', 4, 1, '2025-10-29 12:11:59', 32, '2025-10-29 12:13:34', NULL, '2025-10-29 12:14:06', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-29', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Expression of Interest (EOI) for State Level Project Management Unit (PMU) for Exports Promotion', '2025-01-20', '2025-01-24 17:00:00', '2025-02-05 00:00:00', '2025-02-10 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-11', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/7pMpcPD92hjYop650JsrCUJzsFBTIRPsvGW2mHwv.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 43659774.19, 0, 0, 7858759.35, 51518533.55, 1, 0, NULL, NULL),
(10, 92, 12, 'EOI/EMPL/GST/PMU/2024', 1, 'For Selection of Consultancy Service Firm for PMU support to Commercial Tax- GST Department, Setting up and Operationalization of GST Business Intelli', '24', '<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-alpha;\">\r\n<li>CHiPS is inviting all Tier(I) empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Terms of&nbsp;Reference, Proposed Team, Qualification and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.</li>\r\n</ol>', 2, 12, '2024-02-12 14:00:40', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 177141600, 8857080, 185998680, 0, 18, 5, '<p><strong>About CTD PMU project</strong></p>\r\n<p>Commercial Tax Department is one of the key revenue earning departments in the Government of&nbsp;Chhattisgarh. The Commercial Tax - Goods and Services Tax (GST) Department is responsible for levy&nbsp;and collection of Value Added Tax and Goods and Services Tax in the State through assessment of&nbsp;cases. Commercial Tax - GST forms the largest source of revenue for the State.</p>\r\n<p>The terms of reference defines the requirements to hire a consultant (firm), for PMU support to&nbsp;Commercial Tax- GST Department, Setting up and Operationalization of GST Business Intelligence Unit&nbsp;(GST BIU) and Capacity building of officials for Commercial Tax-GST Department, Government of&nbsp;Chhattisgarh.</p>\r\n<p>The objective of this project is broadly as mentioned below,</p>\r\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-alpha;\">\r\n<li>To set up a GST Business Intelligence Unit (GST BIU) and support the CTD in operationalization&nbsp;of GST BIU unit.</li>\r\n<li>Assist in enhancing the tax data analytical capacity to facilitate the department in detecting&nbsp;tax evasions, increasing tax compliance, resulting in revenue enhancement for the State.</li>\r\n<li>Strengthening the process of GST Audit &amp; capacity building through training on select topics.</li>\r\n<li>Prepare Industry Specific Checklist for Audit</li>\r\n<li>Assist CTD in any other PMU related work</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>Term of Reference along with Team Composition</strong></p>\r\n<p>The Department therefore intends to hire a consultant (firm) who could help in meeting the objectives. The&nbsp;overall scope of work is divided into 3 modules since the segregation of team for various activities are key to&nbsp;this project and each team may be reporting to different units in CTD. The consultant needs to deploy separate&nbsp;team for each of the modules with separate module leaders. Each of these teams and respective module leaders&nbsp;will be working closely with respective sections of the Department that they will be assigned to.&nbsp;Given the diversity of work in the project the consultant needs to deploy a full-time project manager to<br>coordinate all the activities and to interact with the highest level of department for project related matter.</p>\r\n<p>The Modules and the envisaged activities under each of them are as follows</p>\r\n<p><strong>Module 1 &ndash; Setting up and operationalization of GST Business Intelligence Unit (GST BIU)</strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Objective :&nbsp;</strong>The Commercial Tax Department aims to enhance its tax administration capabilities by establishing&nbsp;a GST Business Intelligence Unit (GST BIU). This unit will leverage data analytics to detect fraudulent&nbsp;practices, improve compliance, and optimize revenue collection within the GST system.</p>\r\n<p>Broad objectives of GST BIU are:&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-alpha;\">\r\n<li>Detect potential fraudulent practices through logical analysis and pattern recognition through data&nbsp;analysis.</li>\r\n<li>Support data-based policy decision making</li>\r\n<li>Enable risk-based auditing and enforcement.</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate the expansion of the taxpayer base.</li>\r\n<li>Improve dealer compliances.</li>\r\n<li>Empower the department with information and analytics capabilities.</li>\r\n</ol>', NULL, NULL, '<p>The detailed scope of the consultancy will include following :</p>\r\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-alpha;\">\r\n<li>The consultants will suggest the institutional structure of the GST BIU, the resources required and their&nbsp;Job Description to facilitate establishment of a GST BIU. The consultant will support the Department in&nbsp;following activities-</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><strong>Defining Institutional Structure:&nbsp;</strong>The consultancy firm will work closely with the CTD to recommend a wellorganized institutional structure for the GST Business Intelligence Unit (GST BIU). This involves proposing<br>a clear hierarchy and reporting structure of the unit along with staffing requirements.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Defining Job Roles and Responsibilities:&nbsp;</strong>Consultant should define the specific roles and responsibilities of<br>each proposed resource within the GST BIU. This includes preparing job descriptions for proposed position.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Supporting Operationalization:&nbsp;</strong>In order to operationalize the unit, design a roadmap to integrate the<br>proposed institutional structure with existing units for a smooth transition. The consultants will also<br>suggest the specific skillsets required for functioning of unit which may not be available internally The<br>consultant should assist CTD in configuring a suitable analytics tool (The tool will be provided by CTD) for<br>the use cases to perform GST analytics.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-alpha;\">\r\n<li>The consultant would assist in preparing use cases on emerging scenarios in fraud cases, develop analytics<br>models to detect complex patterns and high- risk scenarios for GST fraud, like circular trade, linear trade<br>etc.</li>\r\n<li>The consultant should assist CTD in data ingestion and extraction as and when required by the GST BIU,&nbsp;identify the gaps in data requirements for deeper analysis, creating a model/build APIs for fetching GST&nbsp;related data from various sources like- GSTN, TINXSYS, NIC and storing the data in structured manner for&nbsp;further analysis.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>The consultant should assist to analyze MIS &amp; analytics reports available at various systems (GSTN, e-way&nbsp;bills, etc.) offered by GSTN , like &ndash;\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Analysis of Non-filers&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Analysis of Nil filers</li>\r\n<li>Analysis of Revised Returns</li>\r\n<li>ITC ledger matching</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>The Consultant should additionally support in performing the following analysis -\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Analysis of revenue from various goods, services</li>\r\n<li>HSN based commodity classification and analysis of data.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Commodity supply chain analysis for each commodity group to identify the degree of value addition&nbsp;in each stage and arrive at a more supply chain centric view.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Perform Risk Analysis of taxpayers based on taxpayers profiling.</li>\r\n<li>Perform verification of ineligible ITC claims, Circular or Linear Trade Analysis, etc.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Analyze available digitized information from external sources like newspaper reports, exhibitions,&nbsp;internet websites, Customs, Income Tax, DRI, DGFT, Other State Commercial Tax Departments etc.</li>\r\n<li>Cash-Credit ratio analysis</li>\r\n<li>Exempt to Taxable ratio analysis</li>\r\n<li>Other reports based on tax-related data as requested by CTD from time to time.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>The consultant should assist in following periodic (Weekly, Fortnightly, Monthly, or as required) analysis<br>based on certain parameter (as decided by CTD) to facilitate preventive measures and enforcement by<br>CTD &ndash;\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Deposit trend (from current a/c, utilization of credit etc.) analysis,</li>\r\n<li>Taxpayers&rsquo; analysis (new registration, registration surrendered, Nil return filers, Composite dealers etc</li>\r\n<li>Registration Data Analysis (including amendments) &amp; Dealer Profiling,</li>\r\n<li>Commodity Analysis (impact of tax exemption, withdrawal of tax exemption, change in rate etc.),</li>\r\n<li>Analysis on mismatch of data in multiple returns of the Taxpayer &amp; Tax Rationalization</li>\r\n<li>Inter-state data analysis etc</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>The consultant should assist in data analysis to categorize GST taxpayers across multiple dimensions&nbsp;(registration, returns, refunds, payments, e-way bills, etc.)</li>\r\n<li>The consultant should develop excel based reports/dashboards and their customization according to the&nbsp;need of the department.</li>\r\n<li>The consultant should assist in creating 360 degree taxpayer profile based on available data for analysis of&nbsp;risk prone dealers, common patterns, etc.</li>\r\n<li>Consultant should build capacity of GST BIU in running the analytics model and creating reports from the&nbsp;available data.</li>\r\n<li>The consultant will provide training in Raipur to the identified officials (2 batches of 25 officials in each&nbsp;batch) on knowledge of data analytics on following areas &ndash;\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Overview of type of Analytics and its application in Tax Function.</li>\r\n<li>Understanding key trend of Analytics in Tax Function.</li>\r\n<li>Understanding Data Ingestion: Integrating data from different agencies for a holistic view</li>\r\n<li>Training on handling sensitive taxpayer information securely and ensuring compliance with data&nbsp;protection regulations.</li>\r\n<li>Basics of Data Preparation and Analytical Modelling</li>\r\n<li>Understanding Data Mining and Warehousing</li>\r\n<li>Advanced statistical methods (Predictive Analysis, regression analysis, clustering, etc. ) for data&nbsp;analysis and to anticipate potentially fraudulent activities and segment taxpayers for targeted&nbsp;interventions.</li>\r\n<li>Understanding Data Visualization - Preparing, Interpreting, and understanding data visualization&nbsp;reports to present complex tax data</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>Deliverables</strong></p>\r\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-alpha;\">\r\n<li>Report on setting up of the GST BIU.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Training of officials within the GST BIU to develop the analytical capability of the officers.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Monthly Progress Report on development of use case and analytical model.</li>\r\n</ol>', NULL, '<p>The payment shall be made on a Monthly basis.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis&nbsp;as per the agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n<li>As per Empanelment Agreement</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the&nbsp;evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will&nbsp;be entertained outside the process of negotiation/ discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company about their understanding of&nbsp;the proposed area of work and their experience if any in similar area of expertise (Via&nbsp;Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview&nbsp;the proposed candidates (Via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and Interview will be done as follows</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.036%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 19.929%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.1536%;\"><col style=\"width: 46.882%;\"></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\">Bidder Presentation</td>\r\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: left;\">\r\n<p>Key Resource Interview (For Team Leader,<br>Module Leaders and Indirect Tax<br>Consultants)</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Team Leader- 15 Marks</li>\r\n<li>2 Module Leaders &ndash; 20 Marks (10<br>marks each)</li>\r\n<li>5 Indirect Tax Consultants &ndash; 15 marks&nbsp;(3 marks each)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\">50 Marks</td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\">50 Marks</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top;\">Key&nbsp;Evaluation&nbsp;Criteria</td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Understanding ofthe Project&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Work Plan</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\">Prior experience of&nbsp;working with<br>Government</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: left;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Educational qualification</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Good understanding of project&nbsp;requirements</li>\r\n<li>Previous work experience</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p><strong>Change Management</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The selected agency needs to give 2 weeks of advance notice to Commissioner, CTD&nbsp;for any change of deployed resource during the course of the assignment.</li>\r\n<li>The selected agency needs to ensure knowledge transfer and handover during&nbsp;change of any resource for smooth transition</li>\r\n<li>The replacement of any resource should be approved by Commissioner, CTD.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting&nbsp;their proposalsin response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to&nbsp;this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination<br>of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.&nbsp;The last date for submission of response is 26/02/2024. Any response received after&nbsp;the above deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n<p>The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email<br>to: - CEO, CHiPS, State Data Centre, Civil Lines, Raipur 492001<br>ceochips@nic.in<br>empl.chips@cgchips.in<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax:+91 771-4014158</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EOI</li>\r\n<li>Copy of Approach and methodology presentation.</li>\r\n<li>Resumes of resources for evaluation.</li>\r\n<li>The format of resumes will be as per empanelment tender number &nbsp;8733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020 and any subsequent extension.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-29 14:12:35', 4, 1, '2025-10-29 14:11:23', 12, '2025-10-29 14:12:35', NULL, '2025-10-29 14:12:57', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-29', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'PMU support to Commercial Tax- GST Department, Setting up and Operationalization of GST Business Intelligence Unit (GST BIU) and Capacity building of ', '2024-02-12', '2024-02-16 17:00:00', '2024-02-26 00:00:00', '2024-02-27 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-11', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/7bNuFGBXSPNBH7ViEMMQ3zTKNZS7IstrDjskyZVT.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 52720714.29, 0, 0, 9489728.57, 62210442.86, 1, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(11, 87, 14, 'EOI/EMPL/CHIPS/PMU/SYWD/NG2028', 1, 'Setting up of Project Management Unit (PMU) for Policy formulation, Infrastructure Gap assessment and assistance in Project Implementation for conduct', '18', '<p>The objective of the assignment is to provide assistance to Sports &amp; Youth Welfare Department, Government of Chhattisgarh (SYWD, CG) for setting up of Project Management Unit (PMU) for Policy formulation, Infrastructure Gap assessment and assistance in Project Implementation for conducting the&nbsp;2028 National Games in the State of Chhattisgarh.</p>\r\n<p>Director, SYWD, Govt of Chhattisgarh is inviting only Tier-1 Firm as per the CHIPS Empanelment (as&nbsp;per the Tender No.&nbsp; 8733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020 dated 31/10/2020) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration&nbsp;as mentioned in this EOI.</p>\r\n<p>Issuer / Address for business query and Correspondence<br>The Director,<br>Sports and Youth Welfare Department, Chhattisgarh<br>Sardar Vallabh Bhai Patel, International Hockey Stadium<br>G. E. Road, Raipur Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492010<br>Tel: +91-771-2262177<br>Email: dir-sportsyw.cg@gov.in</p>', 2, 14, '2024-09-05 15:36:59', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 16142400, 807120, 16949520, 0, 18, 5, '<p><strong>Introduction</strong></p>\r\n<p>The Sports &amp; Youth Welfare Department of Chhattisgarh is dedicated to fostering a vibrant sporting&nbsp;culture and empowering the state\'s youth. Established with a vision to promote physical fitness and&nbsp;sportsmanship, the department works tirelessly to identify and nurture athletic talent, providing robust&nbsp;support through structured programs and state-of-the-art facilities. With a focus on both urban and rural&nbsp;areas, the department ensures that opportunities for excellence in sports are accessible to all. Through&nbsp;initiatives like the Chhattisgarh Sports Development Program and rural sports outreach, the department is&nbsp;committed to elevating athletes to national and international stages.</p>\r\n<p>In addition to its sports initiatives, the department is equally devoted to youth empowerment. It designs&nbsp;and implements programs that enhance leadership skills, promote community engagement, and support&nbsp;personal and professional growth. By offering youth leadership programs and health and fitness&nbsp;campaigns, the department aims to equip young individuals with the necessary skills to contribute&nbsp;positively to society. Overall, the Sports &amp; Youth Welfare Department of Chhattisgarh strives to create a&nbsp;dynamic environment where sports and youth development go hand in hand, fostering a future of&nbsp;excellence, inclusivity, and holistic growth for the state.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Need identification</strong></p>\r\n<p>The Sports &amp; Youth Welfare Department, Government of Chhattisgarh (SYWD, CG) has taken various&nbsp;steps in implementing the State Sports Policy 2017 and have recently created a Chhattisgarh State Sports&nbsp;Authority. As a next step to enhance the sporting activities, to develop state-of-the-art sport infrastructure,&nbsp;to oversee development of various sports facilities, training programs, and talent development initiatives&nbsp;throughout Chhattisgarh, SYWD wishes to engage a strategic consulting firm for setting up a Project&nbsp;Management Unit (PMU) for Policy formulation, Infrastructure Gap assessment and assistance in Project&nbsp;Implementation for conducting the 2028 National Games in the State of Chhattisgarh</p>\r\n<p>The SYWD, CG has been instrumental in nurturing local talent and creating a sports-friendly environment.&nbsp;However, recognizing the need for specialized expertise to elevate the state\'s sporting prowess, the&nbsp;department is now looking to bring in external consultants. This initiative aims to build upon the existing&nbsp;foundation, establish a more robust sports ecosystem, nurture talent more effectively, and significantly&nbsp;elevate Chhattisgarh\'s performance on national and international stages.</p>\r\n<p>The engagement of Strategic Advisors will complement the department\'s ongoing efforts in hosting&nbsp;various sports competitions, augmenting sports infrastructure, and implementing various schemes for&nbsp;athlete support. It will bring in fresh perspectives and global best practices to enhance the department\'s&nbsp;capabilities in areas such as talent identification, high-performance centre establishment, and sports event&nbsp;management. The advisory firm shall assist in connecting with the conglomerates for their CSR&nbsp;investments in Chhattisgarh for development of Sports facilities and to pull in experts in the field for&nbsp;special coaching sessions.</p>\r\n<p>This strategic move aligns with the state government\'s vision to position Chhattisgarh as a leading sports&nbsp;hub in India. By leveraging the expertise of professional consultants, the Sports &amp; Youth Welfare.</p>\r\n<p>Department aims to accelerate its progress towards creating a vibrant sports culture, developing worldclass infrastructure, and producing elite athletes who can compete at the highest levels; furthermore, the&nbsp;Sports &amp; Youth Welfare Department wishes to empower its youth while selecting their field of education,&nbsp;specialization and career counselling.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Purpose</strong></p>\r\n<p>Sports &amp; Youth Welfare Department, Government of Chhattisgarh intends to engage a strategic consulting firm for setting up a Project Management Unit (PMU) for Policy formulation, Infrastructure Gap assessment and assistance in Project Implementation for conducting the 2028&nbsp;National Games in the State of Chhattisgarh, along with the required support in the field of Youth<br>upliftment and empowerment. The PMU shall be comprising a team of well-experienced and&nbsp;qualified professionals in the field of Sports, infrastructure, finance, education, project management,&nbsp;procurement, information technology implementation, IEC and BCC activities, to help in planning&nbsp;and execute the Department&rsquo;s vision to become the leading State in the country having better sports<br>infrastructure and medal winning athletes at both National and International level, along with having&nbsp;youth which are well guided for having a flourishing career.</p>\r\n<p>By establishing this Project Management Unit (PMU), broader long-term vision of the Department&nbsp;will be accelerated, and execution will be done in a planned manner. The Project Management Unit&nbsp;(PMU) will primarily function out of SYWD Directorate office, Raipur with intermittent travel to&nbsp;other locations on requirement basis.</p>\r\n<p>The setting-up of a Project Management Unit (PMU) shall assist in achieving the following</p>\r\n<p><strong>Objectives:</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Building a robust Talent Identification and Development system</li>\r\n<li>Creating a vibrant sports culture in the State</li>\r\n<li>Providing requisite support for sportspersons and other key stakeholders</li>\r\n<li>Development of fundamental infrastructure focusing on Field-of-Plays required for sports.</li>\r\n<li>Ultra-modern training facilities to the players and coaches of the district for enhancing the&nbsp;performance at National and International level.</li>\r\n<li>Setting-up High-Performance centers and providing adequate sports science support to&nbsp;talented athletes</li>\r\n<li>Increasing the no. of medals at National and International level by the sportspersons of the&nbsp;State</li>\r\n<li>Use of technology-enabled platforms for performance enhancement for sportspersons</li>\r\n<li>Provide better career counselling and prospects for youth and athletes.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, NULL, '<p><strong>Terms of reference</strong></p>\r\n<p>The scope of consultancy work shall be comprised of two parts:</p>\r\n<p><strong>Part &ndash; A &ndash; first 6 months:</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Sports Infrastructure Assessment and Planning\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>The Project Management Unit (PMU) will support in conducting gap analysis of the existing&nbsp;sports infrastructure for augmentation / improvement / upgradation including current utilization&nbsp;&amp; operationalization of key sports infrastructure for hosting National Games in the State in a&nbsp;phase-wise manner.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Study infrastructure facilities being developed in other states and countries for specific sports;&nbsp;review their need and suitability with respect to Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Development of a strategic vision/ Policy document\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>Conduct a gap analysis of the vision document vis-&agrave;-vis national and global peers.</li>\r\n<li>Assist SYWD in conducting a Demand &ndash; Supply analysis for identification of focus areas, to&nbsp;be in sync with the National Sports Policy, with special emphasis on Olympic Sports.</li>\r\n<li>Supporting SYWD in preparation of 5-year vision / policy document that may be published by&nbsp;the SYWD as a guideline for sports development in the region.</li>\r\n<li>Align sports and tourism to introduce innovative approaches to the same, along with youth&nbsp;upliftment.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Talent Identification Mechanism\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>Assist SYWD in Identification of best practices for selection of talent at grassroots level.</li>\r\n<li>Preparation of Talent Identification Strategy and Execution Plan in consultation with all the&nbsp;Stakeholders and in conducting talent identification assessments across the State</li>\r\n<li>Assist SYWD in preparation of a comprehensive selection process for immediate talent and&nbsp;potential talent.</li>\r\n<li>Assist SYWD in development of athlete management system, youth development index with&nbsp;data analysis.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Preparation of Comprehensive Sports Events Calendar\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>Assist in developing an online portal for talent identification. Assist SYWD in preparation of&nbsp;Sports Events Calendar for key competitions where athletes can participate.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Capacity Building\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>Assist SYWD in preparation of policy document for athlete centered coach development&nbsp;program.</li>\r\n<li>Assist SYWD in preparing skill development programs for Physical Education Teachers and&nbsp;Community coaches.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>Part &ndash; B &ndash; Post 6 Months &ndash; Continuous Support for National Games 2028:</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Sports Infrastructure Assessment and Planning\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>The Project Management Unit (PMU)shall assist the department in mapping all existing, ongoing &amp; upcoming sports Infrastructure in the State.</li>\r\n<li>The Project Management Unit (PMU)in consultation with department, propose a sustainable&nbsp;plan for utilization of sports infrastructure like leveraging central / state governments policies,&nbsp;induction plan, required manpower, etc.</li>\r\n<li>Develop project-based analysis of existing infrastructure.</li>\r\n<li>Assist in bid process management for preparation of DPRs for mega projects; assist in&nbsp;evaluating viability of financial model</li>\r\n<li>Assistance in conducting the bid process management for onboarding of vendors as needed:\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: circle;\">\r\n<li>Assist in Preparation of Terms of Reference and bid documents for procurement of&nbsp;necessary goods, services, and other allied services.</li>\r\n<li>Conduct meetings to incorporate suggestions in the tender documents from stakeholders.</li>\r\n<li>Assist in issue of EOI/ RFP and in scheduling pre-bid meeting.</li>\r\n<li>Assistance in drafting responses to pre-bid queries and any corrigendum/ addendum</li>\r\n<li>Assist in drafting of contracts and onboarding of service providers/ agencies.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Develop a system or framework for regular review of infrastructure facilities at various levels.</li>\r\n<li>Develop monitoring frameworks and coordinate with service providers for seamless execution&nbsp;of projects.</li>\r\n<li>Support in drafting proposals for infrastructure development to seek grant-in-aid under Central&nbsp;schemes and secure funding from the CSR/ DMF/ securing soft loans from the International&nbsp;Funding Agencies.</li>\r\n<li>Assist in planning and upgrading infrastructure at grassroot level to create a holistic ecosystem.&nbsp;The PMU shall assist the department in managing the relationships and communication with&nbsp;the key stakeholders.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Talent Development Pathway\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>Through proper stakeholder consultation, assist in identification of suitable sports disciplines,&nbsp;talent pockets for the State and prepare a long-term plan for the same.</li>\r\n<li>Through comprehensive consultation process, assist in developing a talent development&nbsp;structure from grassroots to elite level.</li>\r\n<li>The PMU shall assist the department in monitoring the grass-root development plans with&nbsp;progress reports on all activities and initiatives.</li>\r\n<li>Identify an ideal blend of grassroots training centers, intermediate training centers and elite&nbsp;centers.</li>\r\n<li>Assisting in preparing, developing, and implementing a need-based elite athlete support system</li>\r\n<li>Assist in review the gaps in youth development policy, education policy etc. and to&nbsp;recommended policy interventions and amendments to achieve and realize the goals and&nbsp;objectives of the vision document for sports.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Capacity Building\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>The PMU shall assist the department in mapping the existing training programs and schemes,&nbsp;preferably on a digital platform.</li>\r\n<li>Assist in conducting skill development workshops for coaches and trainers.</li>\r\n<li>Assist in enhancing Institutional capacity: recommend changes in current processes, SOPs,&nbsp;training, and refresher workshops, etc.</li>\r\n<li>Assist in developing in-house capacity for conducting State/National/International level events&nbsp;of importance.</li>\r\n<li>Undertaking research to identify and suggest educational courses and possible foreign&nbsp;collaborations in sports education for Colleges/ Universities in the State</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Identify and Leverage State &amp; Central Govt. schemes.\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>The PMU shall assist the Department in identifying the various State &amp; Central Government&nbsp;Schemes like, but not limited to the Khelo India Scheme, Sports Authority of India&rsquo;s funding&nbsp;and plan how all areas of the schemes may be leveraged.</li>\r\n<li>The PMU shall assist the department in preparing, submitting, and following up on DPRs&nbsp;submitted on behalf of the Department.</li>\r\n<li>Additionally, the PMU shall also develop conceptual framework and roadmap to attract funding&nbsp;from corporates/ State PSUs/MPLAD/CSR, etc.</li>\r\n<li>Study and suggest measures for convergence and harmonization of the various Schemes and&nbsp;Programmes for promotion and development of sports being implemented by the Government&nbsp;of India and State Government.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Project Management Support\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>Assistance in preparing Dashboard for online monitoring of projects.</li>\r\n<li>Overall coordination and organizing review meetings with relevant stakeholders.</li>\r\n<li>Preparing the Minutes/ discussion points, Presentations etc. on regular basis&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Support for day-to-day activities undertaken by the Authority</li>\r\n<li>Submission of Monthly Progress Reports</li>\r\n<li>Assistance in preparing Dashboards on implementation of the Central and State Government&nbsp;Schemes for the Youth Development and Upliftment in the State.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Assistance in Setting up Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s first ever Sports University\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>Assist in drafting the policies for setting up the Sports University</li>\r\n<li>Assist in identification of possible areas of tie-ups in India and abroad.</li>\r\n<li>Assist in bid process management for setting up the University</li>\r\n<li>Data collection, project implementation monitoring and provide recommendations.</li>\r\n<li>Stakeholder co-ordination for timely completion of works on site</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Other Tasks as assigned by the Department\r\n<ul style=\"list-style-type: square;\">\r\n<li>The PMU shall assist the Department in analyzing the various proposals received by the&nbsp;Department.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>', NULL, '<p>Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the&nbsp;agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n<li>For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or SYWD/CHiPS, as the case may be&nbsp;selected bidder shall be paid the requisite man month payment in the event that selected bidder&nbsp;has performed on its obligations in compliance with the terms of this contract.</li>\r\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS/SYWD will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation&nbsp;of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the&nbsp;process of negotiation/ discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding companies about their understanding of the proposed&nbsp;area of work and their experience if any in similar area of expertise.</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies the proposed candidates may be interviewed (face to&nbsp;face) by the Evaluation Committee.</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and Interview will be done as follows</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.036%; border-width: 1px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 18.2238%;\"><col style=\"width: 35.7107%;\"><col style=\"width: 46.03%;\"></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top; padding: 5px;\">Bidder Presentation</td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top; padding: 5px;\">Candidates Profile</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top; padding: 5px;\">50 Marks</td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; vertical-align: top; padding: 5px;\">50 Marks</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: left; vertical-align: top; padding: 5px;\">Key&nbsp;Evaluation&nbsp;Criteria</td>\r\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: left; padding: 5px;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of the Project</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such specific kind of&nbsp;a project. (Sports Consulting/Sports Infrastructure&nbsp;Planning &amp; Monitoring/ Sports Events)</li>\r\n<li>Prior exposure in similar government projects related to Sports Consulting/ Sports Infrastructure Planning &amp;&nbsp;Monitoring/ Sports Events along with experience in&nbsp;education sector for youth empowerment.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"vertical-align: top; text-align: left; padding: 5px;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of the profile</li>\r\n<li>Educational Qualification</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant Experience</li>\r\n<li>Experience of Working in&nbsp;Government Projects</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication&nbsp;abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>The bidder receiving highest marking shall be considered for award of work.</p>', '<p>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in&nbsp;response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have&nbsp;been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms,&nbsp;conditions and implications.</p>\r\n<p>The last date for physical submission of response is 16/09/2024; 05:00 PM. Any response received after&nbsp;the above deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n<p>The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to</p>\r\n<p>The Director,<br>Sports and Youth Welfare Department, Chhattisgarh<br>Sardar Vallabh Bhai Patel, International Hockey Stadium<br>G. E. Road, Raipur Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492010, Tel: +91-771-2262177<br>Email: dir-sportsyw.cg@gov.in</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EOI</li>\r\n<li>Copy of Approach and methodology presentation</li>\r\n<li>Resumes of the proposed resources. The format of resumes will be as per empanelment tender number&nbsp; 8733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-29 15:46:01', 4, 1, '2025-10-29 15:43:47', 14, '2025-10-29 15:46:01', NULL, '2025-10-29 15:46:23', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-29', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Project Management Unit (PMU) for Policy formulation, Infrastructure Gap assessment and assistance in Project Implementation for conducting the 2028 N', '2024-09-05', '2024-09-10 17:00:00', '2024-09-16 00:00:00', '2024-09-26 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-11', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/IuxojjEWszbodmvlzZeeU6gus5GSZU24OEUQZlsa.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 6962580.65, 0, 0, 1253264.52, 8215845.16, 1, 0, NULL, NULL),
(12, 77, 31, 'EOI/EMPL/PMU/CSIDC RCB-RRC/2025', 1, 'For selection of PMU for Reducing Compliance Burden (RCB) & Reducing Regulatory Cost (RRC)under CSIDC Chhattisgarh.', '12', '<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The objective of the assignment is to provide assistance to Department of Commerce &amp; Industries/</span><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chhattisgarh State Industrial Development Corporation (CSIDC) for consulting / advisory support as </span><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Project Management Unit (PMU) with the Department for Investment Promotion &amp; Facilitation in </span><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Service Sector.</span></p>\r\n<p><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">CHIPS is inviting all empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No. 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020 </span><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">dated 31/10/2020) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, </span><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.</span></p>\r\n<p><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Issuer / Address for business query and Correspondence</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The CEO,</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Lines, Raipur,</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-4014158</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Email: ceochips@nic.in</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;empl.chips@cgchips.in</span></p>', 2, 31, '2025-01-09 11:08:20', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 22585200, 1129260, 23714460, 0, 18, 5, '<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s economy has grown at a tremendous pace in the last decade. CSIDC has contributed&nbsp;tremendously to the industrial and economic development and growth of Chhattisgarh, which is one of&nbsp;the youngest states in India.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chhattisgarh is rapidly emerging as one of the most preferred destinations for investment in India. It has&nbsp;developed a strong infrastructure, and its location gives it access to vital markets in North, Central and&nbsp;South India. CSIDC has played a pivotal role in driving establishment of industries in the state through&nbsp;its infrastructure projects and has undertaken several initiatives to improve land allotment procedures.&nbsp;CSIDC on behalf of the state government is committed to further strengthening industrial infrastructure</span><br><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">by facilitating ease of doing business and providing complete support to all the industries.&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Government of Chhattisgarh has recently launched Industrial Development Policy 2024-30, which focuses on fostering comprehensive growth across sectors in various development blocks of Chhattisgarh, aligning with the vision of \"Amrit Kaal: Chhattisgarh Vision @ 2047.\" The policy aims to create an investor-friendly environment, streamline administrative processes, and encourage the development of industries based on local resources and advanced technologies.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt; line-height: 98%; font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">State Government has adopted focused approach to further reduce compliance burden and reduce regulatory cost for the State which will particularly support in strengthening industrial environment and streamlining processes in Chhattisgarh.</span></p>', NULL, NULL, '<ol>\r\n<li><strong>Reducing Compliance Burden and Cost for Business and Citizen</strong>\r\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-alpha;\">\r\n<li>Identify and map key stakeholders involved in the regulatory process, including:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Government departments and regulatory bodies.</li>\r\n<li>Industry representatives (businesses, MSMEs, and trade associations).</li>\r\n<li>Intermediaries such as auditors, consultants, and certifying authorities.</li>\r\n<li>Investors and entrepreneurs affected by compliance requirements.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Understand the role of each stakeholder in the regulatory ecosystem to identify pain points and&nbsp;opportunities for&nbsp; improvement.</li>\r\n<li>Organize structured consultations with stakeholders to gather qualitative insights on the compliance&nbsp;burden, cost and impact of regulations.</li>\r\n<li>Conduct surveys targeting businesses across sectors to quantify the costs of compliance, delays, and&nbsp;statutory requirements.</li>\r\n<li>Explore challenges specific to sectors, geographies, and business sizes, particularly MSMEs, Export&nbsp;oriented units, women entrepreneur, entrepreneur of weaker sections of society and startups.</li>\r\n<li>Evaluate the state&rsquo;s regulatory framework across four pillars:\r\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-alpha;\">\r\n<li><strong>Administrative Cost</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Assess the financial burden on businesses for adhering to compliance obligations (e.g.,&nbsp;documentation, filings).</li>\r\n<li>Identify areas where digital platforms and process automation can reduce compliance costs.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><strong>Intermediary Cost</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Examine the cost incurred for obtaining certifications, approvals, and reports from third-party&nbsp;intermediaries.</li>\r\n<li>Propose reforms to simplify processes and reduce reliance on intermediaries</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><strong>Delays</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Analyze the costs businesses face due to delays in obtaining approvals or clearances.</li>\r\n<li>Recommend strategies to streamline approval processes, including single-window systems and&nbsp;time-bound service delivery.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li><strong>Statutory Cost</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Assess statutory fees paid directly to the government for permits, licenses, and other regulatory&nbsp;requirements.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Suggest rationalization of fees to improve affordability for small and medium enterprises.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Collaborate with relevant state departments to collect data on regulatory processes, compliance&nbsp;requirements, and associated costs.</li>\r\n<li>Understand current policies, identify bottlenecks, and collect evidence for proposed reforms.</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate regular meetings with state departments to share findings and align on recommendations.</li>\r\n<li>Assist state departments in calculating the monetary impact of administrative, intermediary, delay, and&nbsp;statutory costs.</li>\r\n<li>Benchmark Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s regulatory processes and costs against other states or global best practices.</li>\r\n<li>Evaluate the direct and indirect impact of regulatory costs on business operations and economic growth.</li>\r\n<li>Prepare detailed reports summarizing the findings, including data insights, stakeholder feedback, and&nbsp;identified cost components.</li>\r\n<li>Provide practical solutions to reduce compliance burden and associated costs, improve regulatory&nbsp;efficiency, and enhance ease of doing business.</li>\r\n<li>Offer guidance to state departments for executing recommended reforms, including process redesign,&nbsp;digital transformation, and capacity building.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</li>\r\n<li style=\"font-weight: bold;\"><strong>Decriminalization</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">Decriminalization of business-related acts and rules is a reformative approach aimed at creating a more&nbsp;business-friendly environment within a state. This process involves converting certain non-compliant&nbsp;behaviors from criminal offenses to civil offenses, reducing the severity of penalties, or eliminating the&nbsp;punitive aspect altogether for minor infractions. The goal is to encourage entrepreneurship and investment by&nbsp;reducing the fear of harsh legal consequences for minor and inadvertent breaches of regulations.</p>\r\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: lower-alpha;\">\r\n<li>Conduct a comprehensive review of current business laws to identify provisions that criminalize minor&nbsp;offenses. This review should prioritize offenses that do not impact public health, safety, or&nbsp;National/State security etc.</li>\r\n<li>Engage with business owners, legal experts, industry associations, and other stakeholders to understand&nbsp;the impact of criminal provisions on business operations and to gather suggestions for reform.</li>\r\n<li>Assess the risks associated with decriminalizing certain offenses, ensuring that the changes do not&nbsp;inadvertently encourage non-compliance or unethical business practices.</li>\r\n<li>Identify criminal provisions which may be eliminated under applicable Acts/ Rules/ Notification&nbsp;whatsoever, applicable in the State</li>\r\n<li>Analyzing the provisions with contemporary Acts in leading States and with the States of similar&nbsp;ecosystem</li>\r\n</ol>', NULL, '<p>Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following&nbsp;schedule.</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the&nbsp;agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n<li>For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or CHiPS, as the case may be selected&nbsp;bidder shall be paid the requisite man month payment in the event that selected bidder has&nbsp;performed on its obligations in compliance with the terms of this contract.</li>\r\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n<li>Important Note: All other terms and conditions of tender 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020&nbsp;shall be applicable to this EOI.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the&nbsp;evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will&nbsp;be entertained outside the process of negotiation/ discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company about their understanding of&nbsp;the proposed area of work and their experience if any in similar area of expertise (Via&nbsp;Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview&nbsp;the proposed candidates (Physically/Via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and Interview will be done as follows-</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.036%; border-width: 1px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 17.9041%;\"><col style=\"width: 41.5682%;\"><col style=\"width: 40.4922%;\"></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\">Bidder Presentation</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\">Candidate Interview</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\">50 Marks</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\">50 Marks</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">Key&nbsp;Evaluation&nbsp;Criteria</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of the Project&nbsp;Framework</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology&nbsp;for such specific kind of a project</li>\r\n<li>Prior experience in project&nbsp;interaction with senior Government&nbsp;officials</li>\r\n<li>Prior exposure to Auditing&nbsp;Government projects</li>\r\n<li>Resource deployment at multiple&nbsp;government officesin multiple locations</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of key SLAs of project&nbsp;management</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Good understanding of&nbsp;project management best&nbsp;practicesframework</li>\r\n<li>Ability to&nbsp;Negotiate/Persuade/Influence</li>\r\n<li>Strong ability to&nbsp;understand&nbsp;and deliberate and report&nbsp;monitor the key SLAs</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication&nbsp;abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<p>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in&nbsp;response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been&nbsp;done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions&nbsp;and implications.</p>\r\n<p>The last date for submission of response is 24/01/2025, 17:00 Hrs; Any response received after the above&nbsp;deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n<p>The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to:</p>\r\n<p>CEO, CHiPS, State Data Centre, Civil Lines,<br>Raipur 492001 ceochips@nic.in<br>empl.chips@cgchips.in<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax:+91 771-4014158</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EOI.</li>\r\n<li>Copy of Approach and methodology presentation.</li>\r\n<li>Resumes of resources that will face the interview. The format of resumes will be as per empanelment tender number 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-30 11:34:31', 4, 1, '2025-10-30 11:23:13', 31, '2025-10-30 11:34:31', NULL, '2025-10-30 11:34:49', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-30', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Selection of Project Management Unit for Reducing Compliance Burden (RCB) and Reducing Regulatory Cost (RRC) under CSIDC Chhattisgarh', '2025-01-09', '2025-01-15 17:00:00', '2025-01-24 00:00:00', '2025-01-30 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-12', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/V6RXXWTZW7iyUrJ8M9hjlfzcsn5zZOEZX65ILS4M.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 11628064.52, 0, 0, 2093051.61, 13721116.13, 1, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(14, 76, 31, 'EOI/EMPL/PMU/CSIDC IP/2025', 1, 'PMU for Investment Promotion and Facilitation in Service Sector under CSIDC Chhattisgarh.', '12', '<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">The objective of the assignment is to provide assistance to Department of Commerce &amp; Industries/Chhattisgarh State Industrial&nbsp; Development Corporation (CSIDC) for consulting / advisory support as Project Management Unit (PMU) with the Department for Investment Promotion &amp; Facilitation in&nbsp;Service Sector.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">CHIPS is inviting all empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No. 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020&nbsp;dated 31/10/2020) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team,&nbsp;Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Issuer / Address for business query and Correspondence</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">The CEO,</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Lines, Raipur,</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-4014158</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">Email: <a href=\"mailto:ceochips@nic.in\">ceochips@nic.in</a></span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif; font-size: 12pt;\">empl.chips@cgchips.in</span></p>', 2, 31, '2025-01-09 13:17:36', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 22585200, 1129260, 23714460, 0, 18, 5, '<p>Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s economy has grown at a tremendous pace in the last decade. CSIDC has contributed&nbsp;tremendously to the industrial and economic development and growth of Chhattisgarh, which is one of&nbsp;the youngest states in India.</p>\r\n<p>Chhattisgarh is rapidly emerging as one of the most preferred destinations for investment in India. It&nbsp;has developed a strong infrastructure, and its location gives it access to vital markets in North, Central&nbsp;and South India. CSIDC has played a pivotal role in driving establishment of industries in the state&nbsp;through its infrastructure projects and has undertaken several initiatives to improve land allotment&nbsp;procedures. CSIDC on behalf of the state government is committed to further strengthening industrial&nbsp;infrastructure by facilitating ease of doing business and providing complete support to all the industries.</p>\r\n<p>Government of Chhattisgarh has recently launched Industrial Development Policy 2024-30, which&nbsp;focuses on fostering comprehensive growth across sectors in various development blocks of&nbsp;Chhattisgarh, aligning with the vision of \"Amrit Kaal: Chhattisgarh Vision @ 2047.\" The policy aims&nbsp;to create an investor-friendly environment, streamline administrative processes, and encourage the&nbsp;development of industries based on local resources and advanced technologies.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, NULL, '<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The PMU is expected to carry out following tasks during the term of engagement &ndash;</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Ideate and implement new strategies, programs for garnering investment across identified&nbsp;service sector identified by Government of India and Government of Chhattisgarh from&nbsp;time to time</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Aid the state in promotion programs/events to create a conducive investment climate and&nbsp;to address the needs of the service sector in the State</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Analyze intelligence on global, national markets in IT, ITeS, AI &amp; Robotics, Tourism,&nbsp;Wellness, etc. and convert into usable knowledge for investment promotion.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Cultivate and manage strategic alliances with industry bodies &ndash; State, National and&nbsp;international.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Follow, analyze and compare State, National landscape for investment promotion in service sector to suggest areas of improvement for State of Chhattisgarh.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Facilitate closure of investments working closely with investors and relevant functionaries&nbsp;within Department of Commerce and Industries, and other State Departments.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Provide marketing, business development support for investment promotion.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Lead efforts independently, coordinating with various stakeholders and partners, in areas&nbsp;relevant to investment promotion or as warranted by Department of Commerce and&nbsp;Industries</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Work with allied, complimentary efforts of Department of Commerce and Industries, State&nbsp;of Chhattisgarh, Government of India and any other agency that will aid investment in&nbsp;Service Sector.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Identify bottlenecks and gap areas in identified service sectors where immediate policy&nbsp;interventions are required</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Identifying benefits of development of the service sector in the state, including estimation&nbsp;of economic growth targets, employment opportunities and incoming investment</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Assist the State in implementation of service Sector provisions</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Define a broad-based Action plan for implementation of Service sector policy provisions&nbsp;procedures &ndash; structures and guidelines/rules etc.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Provide Policy implementation Advocacy in sync with the mission spelled out for service&nbsp;sector</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Develop &amp; Define the means for monitoring &amp; follow up/track progress of compliances&nbsp;under the Policy</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Preparation of event calendar and action plan for participation in Investment Promotion&nbsp;Events organized by Service Industry related Associations</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Preparation of presentations, talking points, speeches, press briefs etc. required for&nbsp;participation in investment promotion events.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Assistance in further development of Financial Model developed by the State for&nbsp;disbursement of incentives for service sector enterprises</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Assistance in conducting cost benefit analysis of the investment proposals applying&nbsp;Financial Model developed by the State for service sector enterprises</span></li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule.</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the&nbsp;agreed empanelment terms.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or CHiPS, as the case may be selected&nbsp;bidder shall be paid the requisite man month payment in the event that selected bidder has&nbsp;performed on its obligations in compliance with the terms of this contract.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Important Note:</strong> All other terms and conditions of tender 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020&nbsp;shall be applicable to this EOI.</span></p>', NULL, '<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the&nbsp;evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will&nbsp;be entertained outside the process of negotiation/ discussion with the Committee.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">A presentation will be made by the bidding company about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their experience if any in similar area of expertise (Via Video Conference).</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (Physically/Via Video Conference).&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The marking for presentation and Interview will be done as follows-</span></p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.036%; border-width: 1px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 18.2345%;\"><col style=\"width: 48.4795%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.357%;\"></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Bidder Presentation</span></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Candidate Interview</span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Key&nbsp;Evaluation&nbsp;Criteria</span></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">50 Marks</span></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">50 Marks</span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top; text-align: left;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Approach and Methodology</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Understanding of the Project Framework</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Quality of proposed methodology for such specific kind of a project</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Prior experience in project interaction with senior Government officials</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Prior exposure to Auditing</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Government projects</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Resource deployment at multiple government officesin multiple locations</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Understanding of key SLAs of project management</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top; text-align: left;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Suitability of profile</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Years of relevant experience</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Good understanding of project management best practicesframework</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Ability to Negotiate / Persuade / Influence</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Strong ability to understand and deliberate and report monitor the key SLAs</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Excellent communication abilities</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in&nbsp;response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been&nbsp;done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions&nbsp;and implications.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The last date for submission of response is 24/01/2025, 17:00 Hrs; Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to:</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">CEO, CHiPS, State Data Centre, Civil Lines,</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Raipur 492001 ceochips@nic.in</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">empl.chips@cgchips.in</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax:+91 771-4014158</span></p>', '<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Signed copy of this EOI.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Experience of the bidding firm along with relevant Work Orders/ documents.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Copy of Approach and methodology presentation.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Resumes of resources that will face the interview. The format of resumes will&nbsp;be as per empanelment tender number 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020.</span></li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-30 13:27:27', 4, 1, '2025-10-30 13:26:38', 31, '2025-10-30 13:27:27', NULL, '2025-10-30 13:27:48', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-30', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Selection of Project Management Unit for Investment Promotion And Facilitation in Service Sector under CSIDC Chhattisgarh', '2025-01-09', '2025-01-15 17:00:00', '2025-01-24 00:00:00', '2025-01-30 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-12', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/HvHUhOBjolAybM3661nV8kQ969dbBtCzZ7YnNG0k.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 11628064.52, 0, 0, 2093051.61, 13721116.13, 1, 0, NULL, NULL),
(15, 72, 26, 'EOI/EMPL/CHiPS/PMU/FD/FPRU/2025', 1, 'Consulting Services for Setting up a Fiscal Policy Research Unit (FPRU) at the Finance Department (FD), Government of Chhattisgarh', '12', '<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS), the nodal agency of Department of Electronics &amp;&nbsp;Information Technology, Government of Chhattisgarh on behalf of Finance Department, Government of&nbsp;Chhattisgarh is planning &ldquo;To deploy 8 resources for Fiscal Policy Research Unit (FPRU)&rdquo; The detailed&nbsp;Scope of Work (SoW) is listed below. CHiPS want to hire experts consulting services who shall be&nbsp;providing support to Finance Department, Government of Chhattisgarh as per scope of work mentioned&nbsp;in subsequent section.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The objective of the assignment is to provide assistance to the Finance Department (FD), Government of&nbsp;Chhattisgarh is to setup Fiscal Policy Research Unit (FPRU) to devise initiatives aimed at enhancing its&nbsp;revenues, minimizing expenditures and overall financial commitments, implementation of IT solutions for&nbsp;data management and transparency, co-ordination within various departments, discovering innovative&nbsp;low-cost funding avenues, promoting Public-Private Partnerships (PPP) in key areas, and assist in priority</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">initiatives and public financial management of the Finance Department, Chhattisgarh.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">CHIPS is inviting all empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No. 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020&nbsp;dated 31/10/2020) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team,&nbsp;Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Issuer / Address for business query and Correspondence</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The CEO,</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-4014158</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Email: ceochips@nic.in</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">empl.chips@cgchips.in</span></p>', 2, 26, '2025-04-04 14:42:28', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 36957600, 1847880, 38805480, 0, 18, 5, '<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chhattisgarh is on a path of strong growth and is emerging as a dynamic state in India. The Finance&nbsp;Department is key in managing public funds, optimizing resource allocation, and aligning financial&nbsp;strategies with the state\'s development objectives. To enhance financial flexibility for future growth,&nbsp;the state aims to increase revenue without raising tariffs, cut costs through government efficiency</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">without compromising outcomes, and find new affordable financing options. Effective budget management is also crucial for the proper allocation of resources to essential services, infrastructure,&nbsp;and social welfare. In the face of a rapidly changing economy, Chhattisgarh is planning to adopt&nbsp;innovative solutions to address challenges and seize opportunities, balancing debt sustainability with</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">wise budgeting to maintain economic growth and prioritize its citizens\' welfare.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The Finance Department, Government of Chhattisgarh, therefore, plans to set up Fiscal Policy&nbsp;Research Unit (FPRU) to devise initiatives aimed at enhancing its revenues, minimizing expenditures&nbsp;and overall financial commitments, implementation of IT solutions for data management and&nbsp;transparency, co-ordination within various departments, discovering innovative low-cost funding&nbsp;avenues, promoting Public-Private Partnerships (PPP) in key areas, and assist in priority initiatives&nbsp;and public financial management of the Finance Department.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Establishing a Fiscal Policy Research Unit (FPRU) within the Finance Department would provide a&nbsp;data-driven, analytical framework to support evidence-based decision-making in key areas of fiscal&nbsp;management. By leveraging advanced fiscal research and economic modelling, the FPRU can help in&nbsp;revenue augmentation through better tax policy design, compliance enhancement, and expansion of</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">the tax base. It would support expenditure rationalization by identifying inefficiencies, optimizing&nbsp;resource allocation, and ensuring outcome-based budgeting. In debt management, the unit can analyze&nbsp;borrowing patterns, assess fiscal risks, and develop sustainable debt strategies. Additionally, the FPRU&nbsp;would enhance the efficiency and effectiveness of financial governance by improving financial</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">forecasting, expenditure tracking, and inter-departmental coordination. The unit could also play a&nbsp;pivotal role in identifying and optimizing Public-Private Partnerships (PPP) and asset monetization&nbsp;opportunities by assessing project viability, structuring transactions, and ensuring financial&nbsp;sustainability. Overall, the FPRU would act as a strategic think tank, enabling the Finance Department&nbsp;to adopt best practices, improve fiscal health, and enhance economic resilience.</span></p>', NULL, NULL, '<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">To unlock budget potential for Chhattisgarh and improve efficiency and effectiveness of the Finance&nbsp;Department, the objective of the FPRU to support on the below mentioned areas:</span></p>\r\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-alpha;\">\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Macro Fiscal Analysis and Revenue mobilization measures</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Expenditure management and rationalization</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Budget Preparation and Management</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Financial Management System</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Inter-departmental Coordination for implementation</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Public-Private Partnerships (PPP)</span></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The scope of work will be divided into the following parallel work-streams, which may be initiated,&nbsp;prioritized, or deprioritized based on the needs of the overall program. The detailed activities within&nbsp;each of these work-streams shall include but not be limited to the following:</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Macro-Fiscal Analysis for Enhancing Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s Revenues</strong></span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Comparative Macro-Fiscal Performance Analysis:</strong> Conduct a state-wise analysis of tax&nbsp;performance metrics such as the tax-GSDP ratio, own tax revenue-GSDP ratio, SGST-GSDP ratio, tax&nbsp;buoyancy estimation, etc.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Correlation with Economic Parameters:</strong> Align state economic indicators with high frequency&nbsp;national and other states\' economic parameters to assess relative fiscal performance.&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Sector-wise Micro &amp; Macro Analysis:</strong> Conduct in-depth analyses of various economic sectors&nbsp;economic indicators such as economic growth, core industry growth, inflation, consumption pattern,&nbsp;employment, supply and demand side economic indicators etc. to identify growth trends and their&nbsp;revenue implications.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Sectoral Growth &amp; Revenue Impact Assessment:</strong> Identify leading sectors with declining or slower&nbsp;growth, assess their historical revenue performance evaluations, industry value chain analysis and&nbsp;impact on state revenue, and suggest corrective measures.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Comprehensive Tax Framework Review:</strong> Assess the existing tax framework and identify potential&nbsp;areas for broadening revenue collection.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Tax Policy &amp; Revenue Collection Benchmarking:</strong> Compare tax collection practices, compliance&nbsp;measures, and tax rates with other states to adopt leading practices and maintain competitive tax&nbsp;structures.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Identifying Revenue Gaps &amp; Compliance Measures:</strong> Analyze gaps in revenue collection, propose&nbsp;measures, and recommend short and medium-term strategies to improve compliance and expand the&nbsp;tax base.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Decision Support System for Fiscal Policy:</strong> Develop and maintain a data-driven decision support&nbsp;process to assist policymakers in making informed, strategic fiscal decisions.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Debt Management Support:</strong> Assist in debt sustainability analysis, debt servicing and repayment&nbsp;planning, and identifying risks related to interest rate fluctuations and foreign currency borrowings (if&nbsp;any).</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Non-tax revenue augmentation support:</strong> Identify sources for improving Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s non-tax&nbsp;revenues with a specific focus on Mining department, Forest department, User fees, and&nbsp;New/innovative sources of non-tax revenues. Compare and benchmark these charges and levies with&nbsp;those implemented in other states, seeking any untapped revenue sources.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Expenditure Management and Rationalization</strong></span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Historical Spending Analysis:</strong> Conduct a detailed baseline assessment of historical expenditures&nbsp;across key departments to identify inefficiencies and areas for cost reduction.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Stakeholder Consultation &amp; Process Mapping:</strong> Engage with Finance Department and major&nbsp;departments to identify challenges, redundancies, and bottlenecks in the existing expenditure&nbsp;processes.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Inter-State Benchmarking:</strong> Compare Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s expenditure management practices with bestperforming states to identify best practices and process improvements.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Expenditure Commitments &amp; Cost-Saving Analysis:</strong> Conduct a comprehensive review of financial&nbsp;commitments and explore areas where outflow reductions and cost-saving measures can be applied.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Data-Driven Cost Reduction Strategies:</strong> Develop evidence-based recommendations supported by&nbsp;financial analysis to streamline outflows.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Performance-Linked Cost-Saving Plan:</strong> Define Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) and cost-saving&nbsp;targets, ensuring a structured and results-driven approach to expenditure management.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Budget Preparation and Management</strong></span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Budget Manual Updation &amp; Process Assistance:</strong> Provide technical support in updation of the Budget&nbsp;Manual to align with leading practices and evolving fiscal policies and in streamlining the budget&nbsp;preparation process and improving procedural efficiency.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>FRBM Compliance &amp; Fiscal Statements:</strong> Assist in adherence to the Fiscal Responsibility and Budget&nbsp;Management (FRBM) Act by supporting in preparation and reviewing key fiscal policy documents,&nbsp;including the Medium-Term Fiscal Policy Statement, Macro-Economic Framework Statement, and&nbsp;Medium-Term Expenditure Framework Statement.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Outcome-Based Budgeting:</strong> Support in preparing a performance-based approach to ensure that public&nbsp;funds are allocated efficiently, linking expenditure to measurable outcomes and impact assessments.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Analytical Budget Report Preparation:</strong> Develop detailed analytical reports on budget performance,&nbsp;expenditure trends, and revenue forecasts to aid decision-making and improve financial planning.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Expenditure Review &amp; Rationalization:</strong> Conduct a detailed analysis of government spending to&nbsp;identify inefficiencies and prioritize high-impact sectors.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Public Financial Management Support</strong></span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Adoption of PFMS &amp; SNA SPARSH:</strong> Assist Finance departments in implementing Public Financial&nbsp;Management System (PFMS) and SNA SPARSH.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Monitoring &amp; Evaluation of SNA Implementation:</strong> Continuously assess and track the progress of&nbsp;the Single Nodal Agency (SNA) implementation across the state.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Financial Management System (FMIS) Revamp:</strong> Conduct a detailed gap analysis of the existing system and support the implementation of an improved Financial Management &amp; Information System&nbsp;(FMIS).</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Inter-departmental Coordination Support</strong></span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Central Fund Release &amp; Expenditure Management:</strong> Provide programmatic support to the&nbsp;Department of Finance in fund allocation, expenditure monitoring, and utilization certificate (UC)&nbsp;submissions.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Tracking Fund Allocation &amp; Utilization:</strong> Develop mechanisms to consistently track fund releases&nbsp;and utilization across departments and schemes to improve financial efficiency.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Assessment of Central Schemes &amp; Grants:</strong> Identify relevant Centrally Sponsored Schemes (CSS),&nbsp;special assistance programs, and grants applicable to the state and assist in leveraging them effectively.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Scheme Performance Monitoring &amp; Issue Resolution:</strong> Define key data requirements, assign&nbsp;responsibilities for data collection, analyze scheme performance, and identify bottlenecks in&nbsp;implementation.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Enhancing Preparedness for Central Grants:</strong> Support in developing checklists, preparing necessary&nbsp;documents, including applications for Central Government grants.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Support on Public Private Partnership (PPP)</strong></span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Project Identification &amp; Feasibility Assessment:</strong> Assist in identifying potential projects and&nbsp;prioritization of projects for suitable for PPP models and conduct feasibility studies, including financial&nbsp;viability and risk assessment.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Benchmarking &amp; Leading Practices:</strong> Conduct an in-depth benchmarking analysis of PPP models that&nbsp;have been successfully adopted globally and within India, emphasizing best practices, governance&nbsp;structures, financing mechanisms, and outcomes.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Transaction Advisory &amp; Structuring:</strong> Support in designing PPP project structures, drafting&nbsp;concession agreements, and defining risk-sharing mechanisms to attract private investment.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Financial Modelling &amp; Risk Analysis:</strong> Develop detailed financial models to assess project&nbsp;sustainability, return on investment (ROI), and potential risks for both public and private stakeholders.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Stakeholder Coordination &amp; Capacity Building:</strong> Support engagement between government&nbsp;agencies, private investors, financial institutions, and regulatory bodies for seamless project execution.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Funding &amp; Financial Assistance Advisory:</strong> Support to identify potential sources of funding,&nbsp;including Viability Gap Funding (VGF), multilateral financing, and state support to enhance project&nbsp;bankability.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 99.9655%; border-width: 1px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 7.99159%;\"><col style=\"width: 27.2675%;\"><col style=\"width: 64.7409%;\"></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; padding: 5px;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>S.No.</strong></span></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Deliverable Milestones</strong></span></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Time/ Month</strong></span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; padding: 5px;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">1</span></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Inception Report</span></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">1 month from date of signing of the contract</span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; padding: 5px;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">2</span></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Monthly Progress Report</span></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">7th day of the month</span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the&nbsp;agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Important Note:</strong> All other terms and conditions of tender 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020&nbsp;shall be applicable to this EOI.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the&nbsp;evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be&nbsp;entertained outside the process of negotiation/ discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company about their understanding of the&nbsp;proposed area of work and their experience if any in similar area of expertise (Via Video&nbsp;Conference).</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the&nbsp;proposed candidates (Physically/Via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and Interview will be done as follows</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100.036%; border-width: 1px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 19.2993%;\"><col style=\"width: 47.4147%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.2504%;\"></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Bidder Presentation</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>Candidate Interview</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>50 Marks</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; text-align: center; vertical-align: top;\"><strong>50 Marks</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">Key Evaluation&nbsp;Criteria</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of the Project</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such specific kind of a project</li>\r\n<li>Prior exposure to implementing government projects in Bid Management and Exit Management</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of key SLAs for the project management</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Good understanding of project management best practices framework</li>\r\n<li>Ability to Negotiate / Persuade / Influence</li>\r\n<li>Strong ability to understand.</li>\r\n<li>and deliberate and report monitor the key SLAs.</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in&nbsp;response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have&nbsp;been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms,&nbsp;conditions and implications.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The last date for submission of response is 21/04/2025; 17:00 hrs. Any response received after the above&nbsp;deadline will be rejected.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to:</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">CEO, CHiPS, State Data Centre, Civil Lines, Raipur 492001</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-4014158</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EOI.</li>\r\n<li>Experience of the bidding firm along with relevant Work Orders/ documents.</li>\r\n<li>Copy of Approach and methodology presentation.</li>\r\n<li>Resumes of resources that will face the interview. The format of resumes will be&nbsp;as per empanelment tender number 68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-30 14:51:42', 4, 1, '2025-10-30 14:50:22', 26, '2025-10-30 14:51:42', NULL, '2025-10-30 14:52:02', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-30', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Selection of Consulting Services for Setting up a Fiscal Policy Research Unit (FPRU) at the Finance Department (FD), Government of Chhattisgarh', '2025-04-04', '2025-04-09 17:00:00', '2025-04-21 00:00:00', '2025-04-26 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-12', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/OcEzo6uKvjF4848qbyAEQzdCb9FSh5dpWWgV2OPD.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 26448000, 0, 0, 4760640, 31208640, 1, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(16, 74, 32, 'EOI/EMPL/CHiPS/PMU/SED/2025', 1, 'Project Management Unit (PMU) for Start-up Ecosystem Development in the State of Chhattisgarh.', '24', '<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The Director Industries, Government of Chhattisgarh is seeking to establish a Program Management Unit&nbsp;(PMU) with professional consultants for the planning, implementation, and monitoring of Start-up Promotion&nbsp;related works. The scope of work for the PMU will broadly encompass the comprehensive management of&nbsp;projects, activities, and scheme being implemented by Director Industries, Government of Chhattisgarh,&nbsp;ensuring alignment with the Government of India guidelines and the Ministry\'s directives.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The PMU will provide end-to-end consultancy support and handholding to Director Industries, Government of&nbsp;Chhattisgarh in planning, implementation and monitoring of schemes related to Start-up Ecosystem&nbsp;Development in the State of Chhattisgarh. This support will include planning, policy formulation, and the&nbsp;monitoring of physical (Desk Assessment) and financial progress of the projects. Additionally, the PMU will focus&nbsp;on capacity building, knowledge management, Information, Education, and Communication (IEC), and other&nbsp;critical aspects of program management and implementation.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">CHiPS is inviting all Tier-1 empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No. 68733 /CEO /CHiPS /Empanelment /2020&nbsp;dated 31/10/2020) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team,&nbsp;Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Issuer / Addressfor business query and Correspondence</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The CEO,</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">State DataCentreBuilding, Near PoliceControlRoom, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-4014158</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Email: ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in</span></p>', 2, 32, '2025-03-13 16:57:37', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 59472000, 2973600, 62445600, 0, 18, 5, '<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Globally, Startups are seen as nation builders as they create positive contribution to the nation&rsquo;s economy and create&nbsp;jobs. Startups are normally identified as a newly emerged, fast-growing business that aims to meet a marketplace&nbsp;need by developing a viable business model around innovative product, service, process or a platform. With their&nbsp;success they also create a sense that indigenous innovations and technologies can bring fruitful economic benefits&nbsp;in the long run. The Startup landscape is growing rapidly in our country.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The Startup India initiative of the Government of India was launched by the Hon&rsquo;ble Prime Minister in January,&nbsp;2016. The initiative envisions building a strong ecosystem for nurturing innovation and entrepreneurship in the&nbsp;country. Driven by a 19-point Action Plan spanning across areas such as &ldquo;Simplification and handholding&rdquo;,&nbsp;&ldquo;Funding support and incentives&rdquo; and &ldquo;Industry academia partnership and incubation&rdquo;, it lays down the roadmap&nbsp;for creation of a conducive ecosystem for the growth of Startups in India. The Department of Industrial Policy and&nbsp;Promotion conceived the States Startup Ranking Framework with the key objective to encourage States and Union&nbsp;Territories to take proactive steps towards strengthening the enabling Startup ecosystems within their jurisdictions.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">In the States\' Startup Ranking 4th Edition 2022 announced by DPIIT, Chhattisgarh was listed in the &ldquo;Emerging&nbsp;Start-up Ecosystems&rdquo; under Category A. The State aims to further improve its Start-up ranking in the SRF 2024 and&nbsp;beyond.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The Government of Chhattisgarh is committed to fostering a vibrant start-up ecosystem to catalyze innovation,&nbsp;entrepreneurship, and economic growth within the State. In line with this vision, the State aims to establish a Project&nbsp;Management Unit (PMU) to provide strategic, operational, and technical support for the holistic development of the&nbsp;start-up ecosystem. The PMU will play a pivotal role in drafting and implementing policies, facilitating stakeholder&nbsp;engagement, building institutional capacities, and enhancing outreach and promotion efforts.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The objective is to create a conducive environment for start-ups by addressing challenges, leveraging opportunities,&nbsp;and ensuring effective coordination between stakeholders, including government departments, industry associations,&nbsp;incubators, and entrepreneurs. Through this initiative, the Government envisions making Chhattisgarh a preferred&nbsp;destination for start-ups, driving innovation and job creation across the State.</span></p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', NULL, NULL, '<p><strong>Policy Support:</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Drafting the Start-up policy of Chhattisgarh:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Understanding the uptake of Chhattisgarh Start-up Policy 2019-2024.</li>\r\n<li>Stakeholder consultation (workshops with industry associations, incubators, start-ups etc.)</li>\r\n<li>Benchmarking the incentives (fiscal and non-fiscal) provided by other States.</li>\r\n<li>Recommending incentives for Chhattisgarh and formulation of draft Start-up policy for 5-year period.</li>\r\n<li>Support in preparation of Rules and policy guidelines on-need basis.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Policy Implementation Support:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Develop SOPs for review of applications/ proposals received from start-ups and incubators as part of the&nbsp;Start-up policy.</li>\r\n<li>Act as a single point of contact for queries and grievances from start-up and incubators.</li>\r\n<li>Procurement support for hiring of vendors for policy implementation.</li>\r\n<li>Designing of a dashboard to monitor all interventions laid down in the Policy.</li>\r\n<li>Support in designing a Start-up challenge across districts in the State based on the Start-up India Ranking&nbsp;framework and support in evaluation of proposals.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Ecosystem and Stakeholder Analysis\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Preparation of a centralized database for start-ups, incubators, investors etc.</li>\r\n<li>Conducting data analysis for informed decision making (in line with BHASKAR portal)</li>\r\n<li>Mapping of mentors/ incubators for guiding start-ups.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Capacity Building Support:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Designing incubation and training programs for start-ups in partnership with stakeholders and qualified external&nbsp;agencies.</li>\r\n<li>Preparing training materials and organizing capacity building training programs highlighting global best practices&nbsp;for managing and operating start-up infrastructure in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Trainings of officials of Departments/ nodal agency for engaging with start-ups and onboarding of partners for&nbsp;supporting the Department</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Helpdesk Support\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Prepare startup and incubator handbook, FAQs for guiding the incubators, and online training content, etc. for&nbsp;guiding the startups.</li>\r\n<li>Resolve day-to-day issues for applicants related to application processing.</li>\r\n<li>Understand needs of startups and coordinate with incubators and institutes to plug those gaps through knowledge&nbsp;sessions.</li>\r\n<li>Designing of a start-up grievance redressal mechanism in the Department&rsquo;s website for timely redressal of queries&nbsp;from start-ups and incubators.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Marketing &amp; Promotion:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Assistance in preparation of promotion material and content writing for various collaterals (including website),&nbsp;social media, presentations &amp; speeches.</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate in regular investment promotion and facilitation including reaching out to incubators, mentors, various&nbsp;stakeholders from academia, industry, VC, corporates, public institutions (through email, voice call &amp; other modes<br>of communication) and marketing through state-wide and nationwide workshops, hackathons, bootcamps, epromotion etc.</li>\r\n<li>Support in conducting startup events and outreach programs across regions to spread awareness about&nbsp;entrepreneurship and innovation among youth. The consulting firm shall submit their detailed recommendations&nbsp;for all necessary meetings/ events to be held for start-up/ incubator/ events.</li>\r\n<li>Assist in organizing events, investment promotion events, seminars and workshops.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Team Deployment\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The Successful Agency shall deploy a team of consultants on a full-time/Intermittent/ part-time/remoteworking basis at office of Client. Collectively, the team shall demonstrate adequate experience in the field&nbsp;of implementation of government programs to ensure quality service delivery to the client. The PMU team&nbsp;will be responsible for providing comprehensive support to Department of Commerce &amp; Industries,&nbsp;Government of Chhattisgarh, ensuring the successful planning, implementation, and monitoring of all&nbsp;schemes and programs being implemented by in the Start-up Promotion ecosystem.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per&nbsp;the agreed empanelment terms.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or CHiPS, as the case may be&nbsp;selected bidder shall be paid the requisite man month payment in the event that selected&nbsp;bidder has performed on its obligations in compliance with the terms of this contract.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</span></li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses&nbsp;to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation /&nbsp;discussion with the Committee.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">A presentation will be made by the bidding companies about their understanding of the proposed area of work&nbsp;and their past experience if any in similar area of expertise.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The committee shall review the projects and CV submitted along with the presentation and award the marking.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The marking for presentation and Interview will be done as follows-</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%; border-width: 1px;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 18.2303%;\"><col style=\"width: 41.8977%;\"><col style=\"width: 39.8721%;\"></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Area of&nbsp;Evaluation</strong></span></td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Bidder Presentation</strong></span></td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Candidate Interview</strong></span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>Total&nbsp;Marks</strong></span></td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>50 Marks</strong></span></td>\r\n<td style=\"text-align: center; padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><strong>50 Marks</strong></span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Key&nbsp;Evaluation&nbsp;Criteria</span></td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Approach and Methodology</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Understanding of the Project Framework</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Qualityofproposed methodology for such specific kind of a project</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Prior experience in Start-up/ Investment Promotion, investment / business facilitation</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Prior experience of drafting State and National level policies</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Prior experience in undertaking large transformation projects</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Suitability of profile</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Educational Qualification</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Years of relevant experience</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Good understanding of scope of work</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Strong ability to understand and deliberate and report</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Excellent communication abilities</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Experience of Working in Government Projects</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"padding: 5px; vertical-align: top;\" colspan=\"3\">\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Note:</span></p>\r\n<ol style=\"list-style-type: upper-roman;\">\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">All experience should be in the name of the firm bidding for the project. Experience of sister / associate firms shall not be eligible.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Only assignments where work order is issued directly by a govt. entity/ Donor Agency to the firm bidding for the project shall be eligible. Assignments which are carried out via any third party/ private agency/ Sub-let shall not be considered for evaluation.</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Only assignments undertaken directly by the agency will be considered eligible. Experiences or assignments from sister, associate or subsidiary firms will not be recognized or considered. Further, to be eligible, the contract signing or work order must be exclusively issued by a Government Entity.</span></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The bidder receiving highest marking shall be considered for award of work.</span></p>', '<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to&nbsp;this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after&nbsp;careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.&nbsp;The last date for submission of response is 05/02/2025; 17:00 hrs Any response received after the above deadline&nbsp;will be rejected.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">The preferred mode of communication for query resolution isthrough email to</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chief Executive Officer</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS), State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001, Tel.: +91-771-4014158</span><br><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Email: ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in</span></p>', '<ul>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Signed copy of this EOI</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Copy of Approach and methodology presentation</span></li>\r\n<li style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\"><span style=\"font-family: arial, helvetica, sans-serif;\">Resumes of the proposed resources. The format of resumes will be as per empanelment tender number&nbsp;68733/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/2020.</span></li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-30 17:08:19', 4, 1, '2025-10-30 17:07:28', 32, '2025-10-30 17:08:19', NULL, '2025-10-30 17:09:14', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-30', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Expression of Interest (EOI) Setting up of Project Management Unit (PMU) for Start-up Ecosystem Development in the State of Chhattisgarh', '2025-01-20', '2025-01-24 17:00:00', '2025-02-05 00:00:00', '2025-02-10 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-12', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/hl0PNMPi7X74AAUGLU0kvSjox8YGGZrOSCig15Tp.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 42057580.65, 0, 0, 7570364.52, 49627945.16, 1, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(17, 70, 89, 'EOI/EMPL/CHiPS/PMU/eDistrict2.0/2025', 1, 'PMU E-District 2.0', '24', '<article class=\"text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto [content-visibility:auto] supports-[content-visibility:auto]:[contain-intrinsic-size:auto_100lvh] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]\" dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-turn-id=\"a316b0a4-c8b2-4aaa-ba2c-95ffb55af912\" data-testid=\"conversation-turn-62\" data-scroll-anchor=\"true\" data-turn=\"assistant\">\r\n<div class=\"text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)\">\r\n<div class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col grow\">\r\n<div class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\" dir=\"auto\" data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"98788df7-f708-484f-8949-424eb073b43f\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-5\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]\">\r\n<div class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling\">\r\n<p data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"764\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">The objective of appointing a Project Management Unit (PMU) for the e-District Project 2.0 is to ensure the successful and efficient implementation of the project, which focuses on enhancing the delivery of government services to citizens through the use of Information and Communication Technology (ICT). The PMU will play a vital role in overseeing, coordinating, and managing the project, including Service Level Agreement (SLA) monitoring during the Operations and Maintenance (O&amp;M) phase of the e-District 2.0 initiative. CHiPS invites all empaneled agencies to submit a proposal based on the Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualifications, Terms of Reference (TOR), and Deployment Duration as outlined in this Expression of Interest (EOI).</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"mt-3 w-full empty:hidden\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</article>', 2, 34, '2025-04-23 19:44:13', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 21523200, 1076160, 22599360, 0, 18, 5, '<article class=\"text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto [content-visibility:auto] supports-[content-visibility:auto]:[contain-intrinsic-size:auto_100lvh] scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]\" dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"-1\" data-turn-id=\"request-69012463-b720-8321-a14e-45abf0080357-12\" data-testid=\"conversation-turn-64\" data-scroll-anchor=\"true\" data-turn=\"assistant\">\r\n<div class=\"text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:--spacing(4)] thread-sm:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(6)] thread-lg:[--thread-content-margin:--spacing(16)] px-(--thread-content-margin)\">\r\n<div class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] thread-lg:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col grow\">\r\n<div class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\" dir=\"auto\" data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"683e0cbe-c791-4336-a3b7-6704a6746a7a\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-5\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden first:pt-[1px]\">\r\n<div class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full break-words dark markdown-new-styling\">\r\n<p data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"924\"><strong data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"16\">Introduction</strong><br data-start=\"16\" data-end=\"19\">The Government of Chhattisgarh (GoC) has been implementing e-Governance in the State of Chhattisgarh with a view to enhance transparency, efficiency, and provide quality &amp; prompt services to its citizens. The Chhattisgarh e-District 1.0 project went live on 27th February 2015. Presently, the e-District portal is delivering more than 117 G2C services online, clocking over 3 lakh transactions per month with a total of 2.82 crore transactions to date. A total of 4,176 Lok Sewa Kendras, Common Service Centers, and Choice Centers are providing services across the state. Citizens can also apply directly online through the e-District portal. Services are accessible from Citizen Kiosks (CSC/Lok Sewa Kendra), the Web Portal, and the Mobile App. There is scope for onboarding new departmental services on this portal along with managing operational day-to-day activities of departments across the state.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"926\" data-end=\"1186\"><strong data-start=\"926\" data-end=\"937\">Mission</strong><br data-start=\"937\" data-end=\"940\">The mission of the e-District project is <em data-start=\"981\" data-end=\"1184\">&ldquo;Strengthening the District administration to deliver government services in a simplified, transparent, and convenient manner to the citizens leveraging Information &amp; Communication Technologies (ICT).&rdquo;</em></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1188\" data-end=\"1405\"><strong data-start=\"1188\" data-end=\"1200\">Approach</strong><br data-start=\"1200\" data-end=\"1203\">The approach for engaging a Project Management Unit (PMU) for the existing e-District portal involves several key steps to ensure the successful integration, enhancement, and management of the portal.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1407\" data-end=\"1996\"><strong data-start=\"1407\" data-end=\"1459\">Purpose and Objective of Project Management Unit</strong><br data-start=\"1459\" data-end=\"1462\">The PMU will be engaged in coordinating with departments to identify challenges in online service delivery. It will be responsible for understanding the workflow of services for service delivery and transforming offline/semi-online services into complete online services in coordination with the current System Integrator (SI). The PMU is expected to bring enhancements in the current application (functional, technical, UI/UX architecture, etc.). The selected PMU will monitor the SLA of the SI as per the RFP terms and conditions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1998\" data-end=\"2032\">The specific objectives include:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2034\" data-end=\"2086\"><strong data-start=\"2034\" data-end=\"2084\">QGR Payment Verification for System Integrator</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2087\" data-end=\"2856\">\r\n<li data-start=\"2087\" data-end=\"2120\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2089\" data-end=\"2120\">Reviewing the contract terms.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2121\" data-end=\"2163\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2123\" data-end=\"2163\">Confirming the agreed-upon QGR amount.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2164\" data-end=\"2239\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2166\" data-end=\"2239\">Checking for conditions or performance metrics required before payment.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2240\" data-end=\"2305\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2242\" data-end=\"2305\">Identifying the payment schedule (e.g., end of each quarter).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2306\" data-end=\"2377\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2308\" data-end=\"2377\">Verifying that the invoiced amount matches the QGR in the contract.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2378\" data-end=\"2441\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2380\" data-end=\"2441\">Checking for any deductions, penalties, or additional fees.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2442\" data-end=\"2496\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2444\" data-end=\"2496\">Comparing payments received with expected revenue.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2497\" data-end=\"2577\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2499\" data-end=\"2577\">Ensuring internal approvals are in place before finalizing QGR verification.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2578\" data-end=\"2633\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2580\" data-end=\"2633\">Conducting internal or external audits if required.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2634\" data-end=\"2695\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2636\" data-end=\"2695\">Documenting findings for compliance and future reference.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2696\" data-end=\"2744\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2698\" data-end=\"2744\">Identifying any missing or delayed payments.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2745\" data-end=\"2810\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2747\" data-end=\"2810\">Contacting the payer for clarification or dispute resolution.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2811\" data-end=\"2856\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2813\" data-end=\"2856\">Adjusting financial records if necessary.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2858\" data-end=\"2894\"><strong data-start=\"2858\" data-end=\"2892\">Project Planning and Execution</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2895\" data-end=\"3371\">\r\n<li data-start=\"2895\" data-end=\"2951\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2897\" data-end=\"2951\">Re-engineering existing services of the application.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2952\" data-end=\"3040\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2954\" data-end=\"3040\">Preparing detailed project plans, timelines, and milestones to onboard new services.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3041\" data-end=\"3162\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3043\" data-end=\"3162\">Overseeing the implementation of project activities according to defined scope, objectives, and timelines in the RFP.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3163\" data-end=\"3254\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3165\" data-end=\"3254\">Planning the transformation of offline/semi-online services into fully online services.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3255\" data-end=\"3371\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3257\" data-end=\"3371\">Reviewing the LSG Act and working with respective departments to onboard new services and enhance existing ones.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3373\" data-end=\"3406\"><strong data-start=\"3373\" data-end=\"3404\">Coordination and Monitoring</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3407\" data-end=\"3674\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3407\" data-end=\"3517\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3409\" data-end=\"3517\">Coordinating between government departments, stakeholders, and vendors involved in the e-District project.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3518\" data-end=\"3602\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3520\" data-end=\"3602\">Monitoring progress to ensure deliverables meet quality standards and timelines.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3603\" data-end=\"3674\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3605\" data-end=\"3674\">Tracking and resolving issues or bottlenecks during implementation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3676\" data-end=\"3699\"><strong data-start=\"3676\" data-end=\"3697\">Quality Assurance</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3700\" data-end=\"3907\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3700\" data-end=\"3804\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3702\" data-end=\"3804\">Ensuring adherence to standards like MMPs and maintaining desired quality and performance standards.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3805\" data-end=\"3907\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3807\" data-end=\"3907\">Implementing procedures for regular testing, evaluation, and review of the system&rsquo;s functionality.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3909\" data-end=\"3945\"><strong data-start=\"3909\" data-end=\"3943\">Capacity Building and Training</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3946\" data-end=\"4146\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3946\" data-end=\"4041\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3948\" data-end=\"4041\">Conducting training for government employees and stakeholders involved in service delivery.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4042\" data-end=\"4146\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4044\" data-end=\"4146\">Strengthening the capacity of local bodies and authorities to use the e-District system effectively.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4148\" data-end=\"4171\"><strong data-start=\"4148\" data-end=\"4169\">Change Management</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4172\" data-end=\"4419\">\r\n<li data-start=\"4172\" data-end=\"4242\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4174\" data-end=\"4242\">Managing the transition from manual to digital processes smoothly.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4243\" data-end=\"4337\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4245\" data-end=\"4337\">Promoting the adoption of e-Government services among citizens and ensuring accessibility.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4338\" data-end=\"4419\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4340\" data-end=\"4419\">Making necessary changes in existing services based on evolving requirements.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4421\" data-end=\"4465\"><strong data-start=\"4421\" data-end=\"4463\">Risk Management and Problem Resolution</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4466\" data-end=\"4628\">\r\n<li data-start=\"4466\" data-end=\"4537\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4468\" data-end=\"4537\">Identifying potential risks and implementing mitigation strategies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4538\" data-end=\"4628\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4540\" data-end=\"4628\">Resolving operational and functional challenges promptly to keep the project on track.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4630\" data-end=\"4658\"><strong data-start=\"4630\" data-end=\"4656\">Performance Evaluation</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4659\" data-end=\"4901\">\r\n<li data-start=\"4659\" data-end=\"4752\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4661\" data-end=\"4752\">Establishing Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) to evaluate project progress and outcomes.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4753\" data-end=\"4840\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4755\" data-end=\"4840\">Providing regular reports to CHiPS on project status, achievements, and challenges.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4841\" data-end=\"4901\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4843\" data-end=\"4901\">Designing department-wise dashboards with relevant KPIs.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4903\" data-end=\"4923\"><strong data-start=\"4903\" data-end=\"4921\">Sustainability</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4924\" data-end=\"5131\">\r\n<li data-start=\"4924\" data-end=\"5046\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4926\" data-end=\"5046\">Ensuring the long-term sustainability of the e-District project through ongoing maintenance, updates, and scalability.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5047\" data-end=\"5131\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5049\" data-end=\"5131\">Developing strategies for continuous improvement in e-District service delivery.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5133\" data-end=\"5148\"><strong data-start=\"5133\" data-end=\"5146\">Reporting</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5149\" data-end=\"5320\">\r\n<li data-start=\"5149\" data-end=\"5224\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5151\" data-end=\"5224\">Monitoring and delivering various reports generated by the application.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5225\" data-end=\"5320\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5227\" data-end=\"5320\">Suggesting different report formats and information extraction methods for better insights.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5322\" data-end=\"5347\"><strong data-start=\"5322\" data-end=\"5345\">Emerging Technology</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5348\" data-end=\"5677\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-start=\"5348\" data-end=\"5444\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5350\" data-end=\"5444\">Analyzing the current application and suggesting enhancements through emerging technologies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5445\" data-end=\"5508\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5447\" data-end=\"5508\">Leveraging Data Analytics and Artificial Intelligence (AI).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5509\" data-end=\"5585\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5511\" data-end=\"5585\">Implementing data-driven decision-making processes and service delivery.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5586\" data-end=\"5677\" data-is-last-node=\"\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5588\" data-end=\"5677\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Using predictive analytics to optimize resource allocation and improve service timelines.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"mt-3 w-full empty:hidden\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</article>', NULL, NULL, '<p data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"19\"><strong data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"17\">Scope of Work</strong></p>\r\n<ol data-start=\"21\" data-end=\"492\">\r\n<li data-start=\"21\" data-end=\"492\">\r\n<p data-start=\"24\" data-end=\"492\">Senior Consultant/Associate Consultant in the IT sector working on projects like e-District, the scope of work is crucial in ensuring the successful implementation of the technology solutions required for e-Government service delivery. The e-District Project aims to streamline government services to citizens through a digital platform, and the Senior IT Consultant\'s role encompasses strategic guidance, technical design, project management, and capacity building.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p data-start=\"514\" data-end=\"619\">Detailed breakdown of the scope of work for a Senior Consultant/Associate Consultant in such a project:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"620\" data-end=\"4094\">\r\n<li data-start=\"620\" data-end=\"843\">\r\n<p data-start=\"622\" data-end=\"843\"><strong data-start=\"622\" data-end=\"661\">Strategic, advisory and assessment:</strong> Strategic on technology uses, advisory on best practices, assessment of current IT infrastructure and create roadmap to add 500 online service rule book knowledge for the project.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"844\" data-end=\"1036\">\r\n<p data-start=\"846\" data-end=\"1036\"><strong data-start=\"846\" data-end=\"871\">Integration Strategy:</strong> Develop a strategy for integrating the e-District platform with other government applications and databases, ensuring seamless data exchange and interoperability.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1037\" data-end=\"1370\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1039\" data-end=\"1370\"><strong data-start=\"1039\" data-end=\"1082\">Solution Development and Customization:</strong> Oversee and guide the customization of e-District software solutions to meet the specific needs of government services and citizens and Stakeholder Coordination with third-party vendors and service providers for software development, infrastructure provisioning, and technical support.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1371\" data-end=\"1571\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1373\" data-end=\"1571\"><strong data-start=\"1373\" data-end=\"1414\">Project Implementation and Oversight:</strong> Manage the execution of e-district services, ensuring that the design and solutions are being implemented as per the project&rsquo;s requirements and timelines.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1572\" data-end=\"1777\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1574\" data-end=\"1777\"><strong data-start=\"1574\" data-end=\"1608\">Quality Assurance and Testing:</strong> Prepare a comprehensive testing plan, including unit tests, integration tests, system tests, user acceptance tests (UAT), performance tests and its issues resolution.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1778\" data-end=\"1930\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1780\" data-end=\"1930\"><strong data-start=\"1780\" data-end=\"1815\">Capacity Building and Training:</strong> Prepare &amp; Design training programs for government officials, administrators, and users of the e-District system.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1931\" data-end=\"2265\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1933\" data-end=\"2265\"><strong data-start=\"1933\" data-end=\"1968\">Risk Management and Compliance:</strong> Identify technical, operational and security risks during implementation and advise on mitigation strategies and also ensure that the e-District platform complies with relevant national laws, data protection regulations, government policies on security and advise on the cybersecurity measures.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2266\" data-end=\"2483\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2268\" data-end=\"2483\"><strong data-start=\"2268\" data-end=\"2321\">Monitoring, Evaluation, and Performance Tracking:</strong> monitoring the performance of the e-District platform, including uptime, service reliability, and user feedback and advise on continuous improvement processes.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2484\" data-end=\"2783\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2486\" data-end=\"2783\"><strong data-start=\"2486\" data-end=\"2530\">Stakeholder Communication and Reporting:</strong> Serve as a key liaison between technical teams, government officials, vendors, and other stakeholders, ensuring clear and consistent communication and reporting on key stakeholders, highlighting achievements, challenges, and any changes to timelines.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2784\" data-end=\"3062\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2786\" data-end=\"3062\"><strong data-start=\"2786\" data-end=\"2808\">Change Management:</strong> Help government entities manage the transition to the new e-District system, addressing resistance and encouraging acceptance of the new processes and end-user support, ensuring the citizens and government employees can easily use e-district services.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3063\" data-end=\"3309\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3065\" data-end=\"3309\"><strong data-start=\"3065\" data-end=\"3098\">Coordination with department:</strong> Coordinate directly with concerned departments to enable integration of departmental applications and services, ensure necessary technical configurations, and adhere to state-level interoperability standards.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3311\" data-end=\"3611\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3313\" data-end=\"3341\"><strong data-start=\"3313\" data-end=\"3339\">Payment verifications:</strong></p>\r\n<ol data-start=\"3344\" data-end=\"3611\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3344\" data-end=\"3430\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3347\" data-end=\"3430\">Scrutiny and validation of payment claims or bills raised by SI and other vendors</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3433\" data-end=\"3546\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3436\" data-end=\"3546\">Ensuring that supporting documents (invoices, work order, attendance sheets, etc.) are complete and correct.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3549\" data-end=\"3611\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3552\" data-end=\"3611\">Verifying compliance with RFP and fund utilization norms.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3613\" data-end=\"4094\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3615\" data-end=\"3636\"><strong data-start=\"3615\" data-end=\"3634\">SLA monitoring:</strong></p>\r\n<ol data-start=\"3639\" data-end=\"4094\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3639\" data-end=\"3723\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3642\" data-end=\"3723\">Identify measurable KPIs (e.g., response time, resolution time, system uptime).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3726\" data-end=\"3784\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3729\" data-end=\"3784\">Set acceptable thresholds and penalties for breaches.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3787\" data-end=\"3875\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3790\" data-end=\"3875\">Use dashboards, automated monitoring systems, or MIS tools to track SLA compliance.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3878\" data-end=\"3960\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3881\" data-end=\"3960\">Data might come from service providers, IT systems, or field-level reporting.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3963\" data-end=\"3995\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3966\" data-end=\"3995\">Weekly/monthly SLA reports.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3998\" data-end=\"4055\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4001\" data-end=\"4055\">Exception reports for escalations or non-compliance.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4058\" data-end=\"4094\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4061\" data-end=\"4094\">Inform departments of breaches.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4118\" data-end=\"4181\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4121\" data-end=\"4181\">Trigger escalation mechanisms for critical SLA violations.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4184\" data-end=\"4253\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4187\" data-end=\"4253\">Recommend or enforce penalties or performance improvement plans.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4256\" data-end=\"4294\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4260\" data-end=\"4294\">Reporting to Higher Authorities:</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4297\" data-end=\"4366\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4301\" data-end=\"4366\">Share SLA performance reports with State/National level bodies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4369\" data-end=\"4420\" data-is-last-node=\"\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4373\" data-end=\"4420\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Highlight trends, risks, and recommendations.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '<h3 data-start=\"132\" data-end=\"156\"><strong data-start=\"136\" data-end=\"156\">Payment Terms</strong></h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"158\" data-end=\"365\">Payment to the selected agency (PMU) for the scope of work executed will be released as per the <strong data-start=\"254\" data-end=\"313\">terms and conditions of the CHiPS Empanelment Agreement</strong>.<br data-start=\"314\" data-end=\"317\">The payment terms and conditions are as follows:</p>\r\n<ol data-start=\"367\" data-end=\"832\">\r\n<li data-start=\"367\" data-end=\"424\">\r\n<p data-start=\"370\" data-end=\"424\"><strong data-start=\"370\" data-end=\"388\">Payment Terms:</strong> As per the Empanelment Agreement.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"425\" data-end=\"498\">\r\n<p data-start=\"428\" data-end=\"498\"><strong data-start=\"428\" data-end=\"468\">Milestone Fixation and Verification:</strong> To be carried out by CHiPS.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"499\" data-end=\"714\">\r\n<p data-start=\"502\" data-end=\"714\"><strong data-start=\"502\" data-end=\"527\">Invoice Verification:</strong> Payment (invoice) verification and recommendation for release of payment to the consulting firm will be done by CHiPS based on the <strong data-start=\"659\" data-end=\"692\">Monthly Progress Report (MPR)</strong> and <strong data-start=\"697\" data-end=\"711\">Attendance</strong>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"715\" data-end=\"832\">\r\n<p data-start=\"718\" data-end=\"832\"><strong data-start=\"718\" data-end=\"737\">Man-Month Rate:</strong> Applicable as per the new empanelment rate effective from the date of issue of the work order.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h3 data-start=\"839\" data-end=\"863\"><strong data-start=\"843\" data-end=\"863\">Penalty Terms</strong></h3>\r\n<div class=\"_tableContainer_1rjym_1\">\r\n<div class=\"group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"865\" data-end=\"1396\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"865\" data-end=\"911\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"865\" data-end=\"911\">\r\n<th data-start=\"865\" data-end=\"878\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"867\" data-end=\"877\">Reason</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"878\" data-end=\"896\" data-col-size=\"lg\"><strong data-start=\"880\" data-end=\"895\">Description</strong></th>\r\n<th data-start=\"896\" data-end=\"911\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"898\" data-end=\"909\">Penalty</strong></th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"961\" data-end=\"1396\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"961\" data-end=\"1159\">\r\n<td data-start=\"961\" data-end=\"1016\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"963\" data-end=\"1015\">Change of selected resources as part of this EOI</strong></td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1016\" data-end=\"1082\" data-col-size=\"lg\">Any change of resource within 2 months from the deployment date</td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1082\" data-end=\"1159\" data-col-size=\"md\">2.0% of the work order value per event shall be deducted from the payment</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"1160\" data-end=\"1396\">\r\n<td data-start=\"1160\" data-end=\"1198\" data-col-size=\"md\"><strong data-start=\"1162\" data-end=\"1197\">Delay in deployment of resource</strong></td>\r\n<td data-start=\"1198\" data-end=\"1320\" data-col-size=\"lg\">Any delay in deployment of the resource against the resource deployment plan as mentioned in Section 4 of this document</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"1320\" data-end=\"1396\">2.0% of the work order value per week shall be deducted from the payment</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>', NULL, '<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"477\" data-end=\"654\">CHiPS will constitute an <strong data-start=\"250\" data-end=\"274\">Evaluation Committee</strong> whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"477\" data-end=\"654\">\r\n<p data-start=\"479\" data-end=\"654\">A&nbsp;<strong data-start=\"481\" data-end=\"497\">presentation</strong> will be made by the bidding companies about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their experience, if any, in a similar area of expertise.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"655\" data-end=\"792\">\r\n<p data-start=\"657\" data-end=\"792\">During the presentation by the companies, the <strong data-start=\"703\" data-end=\"761\">proposed candidates will be interviewed (face to face)</strong> by the Evaluation Committee.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"793\" data-end=\"1103\">\r\n<p data-start=\"795\" data-end=\"1103\">Further, any deviation from proposal and resource CV submitted as bid response to this EOI would not be considered and would be duly ruled as rejection. Therefore, it is instructed to bidders that the actual resource who will be deployed for assignment should be present for interview (in person/Skype/VC).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"793\" data-end=\"1103\">\r\n<h3 data-start=\"183\" data-end=\"253\">The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows</h3>\r\n<table style=\"width: 100%; height: 156.789px;\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 22.3984px;\">\r\n<th style=\"width: 12.8109%; height: 22.3984px;\">&nbsp;</th>\r\n<th style=\"width: 42.6574%; height: 22.3984px;\"><strong>Bidder Presentation (50 Marks)</strong></th>\r\n<th style=\"width: 44.5318%; height: 22.3984px;\"><strong>Candidate Interview (50 Marks)</strong></th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 134.391px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8109%; height: 134.391px;\"><strong>Key Evaluation Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 42.6574%; height: 134.391px;\">&bull; Approach and Methodology <br>&bull; Understanding of the Project <br>&bull; Quality of proposed methodology for such specific kind of a project <br>&bull; Prior exposure to implementing government projects in Bid Management and Exit Management <br>&bull; Understanding of key SLAs for the project management</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 44.5318%; height: 134.391px;\">&bull; Suitability of profile <br>&bull; Years of relevant experience <br>&bull; Good understanding of project management best practices framework&nbsp;<br>&bull; Ability to Negotiate / Persuade / Influence <br>&bull; Strong ability to understand, deliberate and report / monitor the key SLAs <br>&bull; Excellent communication abiliti</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p data-start=\"148\" data-end=\"703\">Agencies (PMU) are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.<br data-start=\"483\" data-end=\"486\">The last date for submission of response is <strong data-start=\"530\" data-end=\"556\">08/05/2025; 17:00 hrs.</strong> Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.<br data-start=\"621\" data-end=\"624\">The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"705\" data-end=\"853\"><strong data-start=\"705\" data-end=\"770\">CEO, CHiPS, State Data Centre, Civil Lines,<br data-start=\"750\" data-end=\"753\">Raipur &ndash; 492001</strong><br data-start=\"770\" data-end=\"773\"><strong data-start=\"776\" data-end=\"795\"><a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"778\" data-end=\"793\">ceochips@nic.in</a></strong><br data-start=\"795\" data-end=\"798\"><strong data-start=\"801\" data-end=\"809\">Tel:</strong> +91-771-4014158&emsp;&emsp;<strong data-start=\"827\" data-end=\"835\">Fax:</strong> +91-771-4014158</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"220\" data-end=\"251\">\r\n<p data-start=\"222\" data-end=\"251\"><strong data-start=\"222\" data-end=\"249\">Signed copy of this EOI</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"252\" data-end=\"305\">\r\n<p data-start=\"254\" data-end=\"305\"><strong data-start=\"254\" data-end=\"303\">Copy of Approach and Methodology Presentation</strong></p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"306\" data-end=\"433\">\r\n<p data-start=\"308\" data-end=\"433\"><strong data-start=\"308\" data-end=\"332\">Resumes of resources</strong> who will appear for the interview (the format of resumes shall be as per the <em data-start=\"410\" data-end=\"430\">Empanelment Tender</em>)</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2025-10-30 20:40:22', 4, 1, '2025-10-30 20:38:38', 34, '2025-10-30 20:40:22', NULL, '2025-10-30 20:41:01', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2025-10-30', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Expression of Interest (EOI) for Setting up of Project Management Unit (PMU) for e-District 2.0 Project', '2025-04-23', '2025-04-28 17:00:00', '2025-05-08 00:00:00', '2025-05-14 00:00:00', NULL, NULL, 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2026-06-12', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/6EhgjXcDryEBZrK0WxHXk7hoYyW1i1AiXF5B7No5.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 17711800, 0, 0, 3188124, 20899924, 1, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(18, 65, 69, 'EOI/EMPL/CHiPS/TPA/CGSWAN/2025', 1, 'TPA under CGSWAN', '12', '<p data-start=\"152\" data-end=\"1016\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS), the nodal agency of Department of Electronics &amp; Information Technology, Government of Chhattisgarh, implemented the \"CGSWAN Project\", and has envisaged appointing a Third-Party Audit Team (TPA) for CGSWAN Project.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"152\" data-end=\"1016\">This section provides general information about the Issuer, important dates and addresses, and the overall eligibility criteria for the parties.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"152\" data-end=\"1016\">The objective of the assignment is to carry out an independent third-party Audit for CGSWAN Operator performance for the CGSWAN 3.0 Project.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"152\" data-end=\"1016\">CHiPS is inviting all empaneled agencies Tier 1 and Tier 2 (as per the Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025 Raipur dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.</p>', 2, 34, '2025-06-06 21:05:32', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 12956400, 647820, 13604220, 0, 18, 5, '<p data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"1128\">The Government has approved the Scheme for establishing State Wide Area Networks (SWANs) across the country in March 2005. SWAN has been identified as a core infrastructure project for supporting e-Governance initiatives and has been undertaken by respective State Governments.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"1128\">The Government of Chhattisgarh (GoCG) has nominated CHiPS as the nodal agency for the implementation of SWAN in the state.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"1128\">The Chhattisgarh State Wide Area Network (CG-SWAN) is a project aimed at providing an information technology backbone. It supports the transmission of voice, data, and video traffic, facilitating interdepartmental communication and data sharing within the state. CG-SWAN is designed to provide a network that connects all blocks of the state through a hybrid infrastructure comprising RF, leased lines, MPLS connectivity, etc.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"119\" data-end=\"1128\">In September 2022, CHiPS awarded the CGSWAN project to M/s. Akshara Enterprise Pvt. Ltd. for a period of five years, extendable by up to two more years as per the agreement.</p>', NULL, NULL, '<p data-start=\"340\" data-end=\"517\">The scope will encompass the <strong data-start=\"369\" data-end=\"404\">audit of the CGSWAN 3.0 Project</strong> as well as <strong data-start=\"416\" data-end=\"471\">periodic audits of bandwidth connectivity locations</strong> (as listed below) on a <strong data-start=\"495\" data-end=\"514\">quarterly basis</strong>.</p>\n<p data-start=\"519\" data-end=\"594\">The scope shall include, but not be limited to, the following activities:</p>\n<ol data-start=\"596\" data-end=\"1617\">\n<li data-start=\"596\" data-end=\"683\">\n<p data-start=\"599\" data-end=\"683\">Regular review of uptime reports, bandwidth utilization, latency, and packet loss.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"684\" data-end=\"758\">\n<p data-start=\"687\" data-end=\"758\">Verification of <strong data-start=\"703\" data-end=\"721\">SLA compliance</strong> by the Operator/System Integrator.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"759\" data-end=\"873\">\n<p data-start=\"762\" data-end=\"873\">Periodic <strong data-start=\"771\" data-end=\"786\">site visits</strong> to randomly selected PoPs to ensure operational readiness and infrastructure upkeep.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"874\" data-end=\"920\">\n<p data-start=\"877\" data-end=\"920\">Conducting an <strong data-start=\"891\" data-end=\"917\">Annual Inventory Audit</strong>.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"921\" data-end=\"1067\">\n<p data-start=\"924\" data-end=\"1067\">Checking the functioning of <strong data-start=\"952\" data-end=\"1000\">Helpdesk and Network Operations Centre (NOC)</strong> &mdash; including call logging, escalation, and resolution mechanisms.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1068\" data-end=\"1180\">\n<p data-start=\"1071\" data-end=\"1180\">Preparation of <strong data-start=\"1086\" data-end=\"1113\">Quarterly Audit Reports</strong>, <strong data-start=\"1115\" data-end=\"1136\">Deviation Reports</strong>, and <strong data-start=\"1142\" data-end=\"1161\">Recommendations</strong> for improvement.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1181\" data-end=\"1272\">\n<p data-start=\"1184\" data-end=\"1272\">Validation of <strong data-start=\"1198\" data-end=\"1216\">SLA compliance</strong> for release of payment to the System Integrator (SI).</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1273\" data-end=\"1380\">\n<p data-start=\"1276\" data-end=\"1380\"><strong data-start=\"1276\" data-end=\"1304\">Verification of invoices</strong> raised by the SI/operator against actual performance and delivered scope.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1381\" data-end=\"1463\">\n<p data-start=\"1384\" data-end=\"1463\">Determination of <strong data-start=\"1401\" data-end=\"1414\">penalties</strong> for SLA breaches as per the contractual terms.</p>\n</li>\n<li data-start=\"1464\" data-end=\"1617\">\n<p data-start=\"1468\" data-end=\"1617\">Recommendation of necessary <strong data-start=\"1496\" data-end=\"1519\">compliance measures</strong> to ensure secure and uninterrupted operation of the network in line with applicable guidelines.</p>\n</li>\n</ol>\n<hr data-start=\"1619\" data-end=\"1622\">\n<h2 data-start=\"1624\" data-end=\"1672\"><strong data-start=\"1627\" data-end=\"1672\">Bandwidth Connectivity Audit Locations</strong></h2>\n<div class=\"_tableContainer_1rjym_1\">\n<div class=\"group _tableWrapper_1rjym_13 flex w-fit flex-col-reverse\" tabindex=\"-1\">\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"1674\" data-end=\"4369\">\n<thead data-start=\"1674\" data-end=\"1808\">\n<tr data-start=\"1674\" data-end=\"1808\">\n<th data-start=\"1674\" data-end=\"1687\" data-col-size=\"sm\"><