(169, 21, 448, 'EOI/CHiPS/PMU/Khanij/Geology/2026', 1, 'Additional Domain Experts in the areas of Geology, Mining, GIS and IT Systems.', '12', '<p>Additional domain expertise in the areas of Geology, Mining , GIS and IT Sysystems</p>', 2, 448, '2026-05-29 12:52:53', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, '<ol>\r\n<li>Factsheet</li>\r\n<li>Project Objective&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Scope of Work&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Team Requirements&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Evaulation Process</li>\r\n<li>Payment &amp; Penalty Terms&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Critical Information&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Document required to participate in the EoI.</li>\r\n</ol>', '<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>CHIPS is inviting Tier-1 empaneled agencies (as per Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">1.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">GIS-based mapping of mining lease areas, auctioned blocks, and proposed future blocks for auction.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">2.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Enabling end-to-end visibility and regulatory compliance through IT-enabled interventions, including real-time vehicle movement intelligence through Vehicle Tracking System, precision volumetric analytics, and automated grade and quantity verification.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">3.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Enhancement of the State DMF Portal in alignment with the National DMF Portal, prevailing rules and guidelines, and full compliance with PMKKKY guidelines and DMF Rules.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">4.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Development of a cloud-based Central Query Management System for DGM, including digitization of geological reports, district maps, and resource maps.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">5.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-IN\" style=\"font-size: 14.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Digital expert for coordination in STG</span></p>', NULL, '<p><strong>Payment Terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on a monthly basis.</li>\r\n<li>Each payment will be made only after the delivery of the corresponding deliverable and its acceptance by CHiPS.</li>\r\n<li>Taxes will be applicable as per prevailing government norms.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Penalty terms<br></strong></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Penalty, if any, shall be governed&nbsp;<span class=\"s1\">as per&nbsp;</span>the agreed&nbsp;<span class=\"s2\">empanelment&nbsp;</span>terms.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>Important Note:</strong> All other terms and conditions of tender 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025 shall be applicable to this EOI.</p>', 5, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company regarding their understanding of the proposed scope of work and their experience, if any, in similar areas of expertise (Physical Mode / Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (Physical Mode / Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table style=\"height: 238px;\" border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 42px;\">\r\n<th style=\"height: 42px;\">Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 42px;\">Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 42px;\">Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 196px;\">\r\n<td style=\"height: 196px;\"><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 196px;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of the Project Framework</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such a specific kind of project</li>\r\n<li>Prior exposure to implementing government projects in Bid Management and Exit Management</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of key SLAs of project management</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 196px;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Good understanding of project management best practices framework</li>\r\n<li>Ability to Negotiate / Persuade / Influence</li>\r\n<li>Strong ability to understand, deliberate, and report / monitor the key SLAs</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.&nbsp;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The last date for submission of response is <strong>19/06/2026, 17:00 Hrs</strong><strong>.</strong>&nbsp;Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Pre-bid submissions, proposal submissions, presentation and interview details, and any query resolution shall be accepted only via the Empanelment Portal (<a class=\"decorated-link\" href=\"../../../\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"261\" data-end=\"288\">https://empl.cgstate.gov.in</a>). For any other enquiries, please contact via&nbsp;<a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"335\" data-end=\"356\">empl.chips@cgchips.in,</a>&nbsp;<a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"360\" data-end=\"382\">empl_portal@cgchips.in</a>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul data-start=\"50\" data-end=\"195\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1y1a14t\" data-start=\"50\" data-end=\"78\">Signed copy of this EoI.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1drwwid\" data-start=\"79\" data-end=\"133\">Copy of the approach and methodology presentation.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1iowcl3\" data-start=\"134\" data-end=\"195\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Resumes of the resources who will appear for the interview.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '299572', '2026-05-29 13:47:13', 4, 1, '2026-05-29 13:29:06', 448, '2026-05-29 13:47:13', NULL, '2026-05-30 00:52:08', 1, NULL, 0, 1, '2026-05-30', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Selection of Additional domain expertise in the areas of Geology, Mining, GIS and IT Systems', '2026-05-29', '2026-06-03 17:00:00', '2026-06-19 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Presentation and interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-01-09', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/3mGjVvctbXGNlLYfp7ZgFwwwpWi97aysUFSuIN3A.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 1, 0, '1,2,3,4,5', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/sy29uBvsvOvzzYbjPwX4MbZarKFYtsAO3Pct2SQC.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 17129419.35, 0, 0, 3083295.48, 20212714.84, 1, 0, NULL, NULL),
(170, 20, 24, 'EoI/CHiPS/CSF/PMU/Agriculture/2026', 1, 'Program Management Unit (PMU) – Directorate of Agriculture, Government of Chhattisgarh', '12', '<p>The Agriculture Department is implementing multiple schemes to strengthen value chains, enhance farmer incomes, and build institutional capacity, including support for high-value crop clusters and FPOs strengthening.</p>\r\n<p>However, Implementation effectiveness is affected by limited real-time data visibility and weak feedback mechanisms, constraining outcome realisation. Systematic scheme monitoring is essential to track physical and financial progress, assess outcomes, and identify implementation gaps in a timely manner. An integrated MIS and structured review framework, supported through dedicated technical assistance, will enable evidence-based decision-making, strengthen accountability, and facilitate course correction across schemes. It is proposed to setup a Programme Management Unit (PMU) to support the Directorate of Agriculture.</p>', 2, 24, '2026-06-10 11:38:52', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, NULL, '<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>CHIPS is inviting Tier-1 empaneled agencies (as per Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/ Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Team Requirement, Qualification, and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p>The scope of work for the Programme Management Unit (PMU) is outlined below &ndash;</p>\r\n<p><strong>1) Market-Linked Agri-Business Development for FPOs:</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Facilitate market linkages for cluster-linked FPOs through:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Buyer meetings and linkages, and exposure visits</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate support for market linkage MoUs / alliances</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate value chain advisory support with a focus on leveraging convergence across government departments, relevant schemes, and institutions.</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate enhancement of product quality and marketability of prioritized crops</li>\r\n<li>Conduct a rapid assessment of the status of FPOs across the state</li>\r\n<li>Develop a comprehensive framework for strengthening FPOs, incorporating modules on governance and compliance, capacity building, business planning, digital enablement, and modules alignment with government schemes.</li>\r\n<li>Develop monitoring frameworks for assessing the progress of FPOs in the State</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>2) Scheme Monitoring and optimization</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Develop a robust Monitoring and Evaluation (M&amp;E) framework incorporating benchmarking indicators, aligned with key outcome indicators to measure the effectiveness of interventions.</li>\r\n<li>Develop a repository of scheme data, performance visualization presentations, and facilitate systematic review and implementation red-flagging to aid in achievement of physical / financial achievements against schemes</li>\r\n<li>Conduct data analysis to identify implementation challenges, conduct stakeholder connect, take up field truthing visits and suggest plans for improving implementation efficiency</li>\r\n<li>Documentations of success stories etc adopted by farmers in the state to enable cross-learning.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>3) Process Governance</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Monitor and facilitate progress of activities including SOP specialized input- output related activities to ensure timely completion and alignment with process guidelines.\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Maintain structured records of approvals and process steps to support governance and review readiness.</li>\r\n<li>Assist in coordinating and guiding external entities through approved digital systems, ensuring adherence to established protocols.</li>\r\n<li>Identify delays or gaps in workflows and recommend improvements for efficiency and transparency.</li>\r\n<li>Conduct training sessions for stakeholders on effective adherence to workflows and governance standards.</li>\r\n<li>Develop periodic reports on workflow progress, turnaround timelines, and compliance indicators for senior management reviews</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p><strong>Duration of the assignment</strong></p>\r\n<p>The consultancy team shall be engaged for an initial period of twelve (12) months. Further the extension of engagement shall be considered on a yearly basis subject to satisfactory performance of the deployed team. The consultants will be onboarded through the CHiPS empanelment process.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Payment Terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Payment to selected bidder for technical and operational support be released on person month basis, post submission of the invoice for payment.</li>\r\n<li>The payment will be as per current resources person month rates applicable under empanelment and payment terms will be governed terms and conditions of Empanelment agreement</li>\r\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Deliverables:</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Convergence roadmap</li>\r\n<li>Market Linkage Plan Document</li>\r\n<li>Branding &amp; Certification Toolkit for FPO products</li>\r\n<li>Market interactions, and connect for facilitating partnerships of buyers sellers</li>\r\n<li>FPO Baseline Assessment Report covering operational status and gaps.</li>\r\n<li>Training Modules for FPO Strengthening</li>\r\n<li>Governance Framework and training modules</li>\r\n<li>Half-yearly and Annual Performance Reports summarizing scheme achievements and gaps.</li>\r\n<li>Scheme performance delta reports</li>\r\n<li>Repository of scheme data</li>\r\n<li>Monitoring and evaluation of key Central Sponsored Schemes and State Sponsored Schemes across the state.</li>\r\n<li>Compendium of Success Stories &amp; Best Practices for cross-learning dissemination.<strong><br></strong></li>\r\n</ul>', '<p><strong>Payment Terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on a monthly basis.</li>\r\n<li>Each payment will be made only after the delivery of the corresponding deliverable and its acceptance by CHiPS.</li>\r\n<li>Taxes will be applicable as per prevailing government norms.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Penalty Terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the terms and conditions mentioned in Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025, Raipur dated 20/02/2025.</li>\r\n</ul>', 5, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company regarding their understanding of the proposed scope of work and their experience, if any, in similar areas of expertise (Physical Mode / Video Conference)</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (Physical Mode / Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th>Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th>Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of the Project Framework</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such a specific kind of project</li>\r\n<li>Prior experience in project interaction with senior Government officials</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Good understanding of project management best practices framework</li>\r\n<li>Ability to Negotiate / Persuade / Influence</li>\r\n<li>Strong ability to understand, deliberate, and report / monitor the key SLAs</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\r\n<li class=\"p1\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The last date for submission of response is&nbsp;<strong>dd/mm/yyyy 17:00 Hrs.</strong>&nbsp;Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Pre-bid submissions, proposal submissions, presentation and interview details, and any query resolution shall be accepted only via the Empanelment Portal (<a class=\"decorated-link\" href=\"../../../\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"261\" data-end=\"288\">https://empl.cgstate.gov.in</a>). For any other enquiries, please contact via&nbsp;<a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"335\" data-end=\"356\">empl.chips@cgchips.in,</a>&nbsp;<a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"360\" data-end=\"382\">empl_portal@cgchips.in</a>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul data-start=\"50\" data-end=\"195\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1y1a14t\" data-start=\"50\" data-end=\"78\">Signed copy of this EoI.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1drwwid\" data-start=\"79\" data-end=\"133\">Copy of the approach and methodology presentation.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1iowcl3\" data-start=\"134\" data-end=\"195\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Resumes of the resources who will appear for the interview.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2026-06-14 10:48:47', 4, 1, '2026-06-14 10:44:58', 24, '2026-06-14 10:48:47', NULL, '2026-06-20 04:43:15', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-06-20', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Program Management Unit PMU Directorate of Agriculture, Government of Chhattisgarh', '2026-06-19', '2026-06-24 17:00:00', '2026-07-10 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Presentation & interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-01-25', 1, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/APK5A3alFn9vmxa36rIsjm1bEjMBiyk3i1o8BL7C.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 1, 0, '1,2,3,4,5', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/JwG6K0snuynFkR31RsR2sNfvsK3irYPjCRdY9sk1.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(171, 19, 623, 'EoI/DMFT/BIJAPUR/CSF/PMU/2026', 1, 'Project Management Unit DMF, Bijapur', '24', '<h1 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">1. Introduction</span></h1>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The District Mineral Foundation (DMF), Bijapur, is a statutory trust established for the welfare of communities and regions affected by mining activities in the district. Bijapur is characterized by a predominantly tribal population, difficult geographical terrain, dispersed habitations, and Left Wing Extremism (LWE)-affected areas that require focused development interventions and effective service delivery mechanisms.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">DMFT Bijapur undertakes developmental interventions across sectors such as health, nutrition, education, skill development, livelihoods, drinking water, sanitation, women and child development, tribal development, infrastructure, and other priority areas identified by the District Administration.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">To strengthen planning, implementation, monitoring, evaluation, governance, and effective utilization of DMF resources, DMFT Bijapur intends to establish a Project Management Unit (PMU) through a Tier-II empanelled consultancy firm. The PMU shall provide technical, managerial, analytical, monitoring, and field-level support to DMFT Bijapur and the District Administration.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The PMU shall function as a strategic support unit for project identification, project design, appraisal, implementation support, monitoring, evaluation, infrastructure verification, digital governance, knowledge management, and institutional strengthening.</p>\r\n<h1 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">2. Objectives</span></h1>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The key objectives of the assignment are:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Strengthen planning, implementation, monitoring, and governance mechanisms under DMFT Bijapur.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support effective utilization of DMF resources in accordance with PMKKKY Guidelines, State DMF Rules, and Government directives.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Provide technical and managerial assistance for project formulation, appraisal, implementation, monitoring, and evaluation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Strengthen institutional capacity of DMFT through innovation, best practices, knowledge management, stakeholder engagement, and data-driven decision making.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Facilitate convergence of DMF projects with Government schemes, CSR initiatives, and other developmental programs.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Improve transparency, accountability, and outcome-oriented implementation of DMF-supported interventions.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Strengthen evidence-based planning and monitoring through digital tools, dashboards, MIS systems, and AI-enabled analytics.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', 2, 623, '2026-06-11 17:24:35', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, NULL, '<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>CHIPS is inviting Tier-2 empaneled agencies (as per Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/ Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Team Requirement, Qualification, and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p dir=\"ltr\">The selected agency shall function as a \"DMF Resource and Project Management Support Unit\" and shall be responsible for the following activities:</p>\r\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">A. Programme Management and Governance Support</span></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Provide managerial and technical support to DMFT Bijapur in accordance with State DMF Rules, PMKKKY Guidelines, and applicable Government instructions.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support effective allocation and utilization of DMF resources.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Assist DMFT in project planning, implementation, monitoring, review, and reporting.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Provide technical and facilitation support to the DMF Trust Board, Governing Council, Managing Committee, and Executive Committee.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support preparation of agenda notes, presentations, policy briefs, concept notes, and review documents.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Facilitate coordination between district administration, line departments, implementing agencies, community institutions, and other stakeholders.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">B. Project Identification, Design and Appraisal</span></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Identify development gaps and priority interventions in mining-affected areas.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support preparation of concept notes, project proposals, Detailed Project Reports (DPRs), implementation frameworks, and operational plans.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Review and technically appraise DPRs and project proposals submitted by departments and agencies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Assess feasibility, sustainability, scalability, and expected outcomes of proposed interventions.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support project prioritization based on impact, need, feasibility, and alignment with district priorities.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Develop project-specific monitoring frameworks and implementation roadmaps.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">C. Infrastructure Planning, Verification and Technical Assessment</span></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Conduct technical assessment of infrastructure projects supported through DMF.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Undertake physical verification of assets and infrastructure projects through field inspections.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Assess quality, functionality, utilization, and maintenance requirements of infrastructure created under DMF.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Verify project progress through field visits, geotagged documentation, photographs, beneficiary interactions, and physical observations.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support quality assurance and quality control measures.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Identify implementation bottlenecks and recommend corrective actions.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Assist in preparation, review, and validation of technical reports and progress assessments.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">D. Monitoring, Evaluation and Learning (MEL)</span></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Develop monitoring and evaluation frameworks for DMF projects.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Define key performance indicators (KPIs), outputs, outcomes, and impact indicators.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Conduct periodic monitoring of projects and schemes.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Undertake impact assessment studies, beneficiary assessments, and outcome evaluations.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Conduct social audits and independent verification exercises whenever required.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Develop feedback mechanisms for beneficiaries and stakeholders.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Document lessons learned, innovations, success stories, and best practices.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support preparation of annual performance assessments and outcome reports.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">E. Digital Governance, MIS and Data Management</span></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Design and manage digital survey tools and data collection systems.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Develop and maintain project databases, dashboards, and management information systems.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Facilitate digitization of project records, reports, and documentation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Develop geotagged asset inventories and project tracking systems.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support data analytics, visualization, and evidence-based decision making.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Promote adoption of AI-enabled tools for analytics, reporting, monitoring, and knowledge management.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Generate periodic MIS reports for review by DMFT and District Administration.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">F. Sectoral Support</span></h2>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The PMU shall provide technical, managerial, analytical, and field-level support across all sectors permissible under DMF and PMKKKY guidelines including but not limited to:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Health and Nutrition</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Education</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Skill Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Livelihood Promotion</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Tribal Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Women and Child Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Agriculture and Allied Sectors</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Drinking Water Supply</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Sanitation</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Rural and Urban Infrastructure</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Renewable Energy</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Digital Governance</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Environmental Sustainability</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Sports and Youth Development</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Culture and Heritage</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Any other sector identified by the District Administration.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">G. Convergence and Resource Optimization</span></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Identify opportunities for convergence with Central and State Government schemes.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Facilitate convergence with CSR initiatives, development partners, and external agencies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support integration of departmental programs for maximizing developmental outcomes.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Develop frameworks for coordinated implementation across departments.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">H. Procurement, Financial and Compliance Support</span></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support procurement-related activities associated with DMF projects.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Assist in maintaining compliance with DMF Rules, PMKKKY Guidelines, and statutory requirements.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support documentation for audits, inspections, and reviews.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Assist in strengthening internal controls, financial discipline, and reporting systems.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">I. Knowledge Management and Capacity Building</span></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Organize workshops, trainings, consultations, and stakeholder engagements.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Develop knowledge products, manuals, SOPs, and guidance documents.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Facilitate dissemination of best practices and cross-learning initiatives.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Build capacities of implementing agencies and stakeholders.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">J. Other Responsibilities</span></h2>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Undertake any strategic, technical, analytical, monitoring, evaluation, documentation, coordination, capacity building, field verification, project management, or governance support activity assigned by the District Collector, Governing Council, Managing Committee, Chief Executive Officer, or any authorized officer of DMFT Bijapur from time to time.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '<p><strong>Payment Terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on a monthly basis.</li>\r\n<li>Each payment will be made only after the delivery of the corresponding deliverable and its acceptance by CHiPS.</li>\r\n<li>Taxes will be applicable as per prevailing government norms.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Penalty Terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the terms and conditions mentioned in Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025, Raipur dated 20/02/2025.</li>\r\n</ul>', 5, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company regarding their understanding of the proposed scope of work and their experience, if any, in similar areas of expertise (Physical Mode / Video Conference)</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (Physical Mode / Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th>Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th>Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of the Project Framework</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such a specific kind of project</li>\r\n<li>Prior experience in project interaction with senior Government officials</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Good understanding of project management best practices framework</li>\r\n<li>Ability to Negotiate / Persuade / Influence</li>\r\n<li>Strong ability to understand, deliberate, and report / monitor the key SLAs</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\r\n<li class=\"p1\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The last date for submission of response is&nbsp;<strong>22/07/2026 17:00 Hrs.</strong>&nbsp;Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Pre-bid submissions, proposal submissions, presentation and interview details, and any query resolution shall be accepted only via the Empanelment Portal (<a class=\"decorated-link\" href=\"../../../\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"261\" data-end=\"288\">https://empl.cgstate.gov.in</a>). For any other enquiries, please contact via&nbsp;<a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"335\" data-end=\"356\">empl.chips@cgchips.in,</a>&nbsp;<a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"360\" data-end=\"382\">empl_portal@cgchips.in</a>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul data-start=\"50\" data-end=\"195\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1y1a14t\" data-start=\"50\" data-end=\"78\">Signed copy of this EoI.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1drwwid\" data-start=\"79\" data-end=\"133\">Copy of the approach and methodology presentation.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1iowcl3\" data-start=\"134\" data-end=\"195\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Resumes of the resources who will appear for the interview.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '528758', '2026-06-15 11:41:07', 4, 1, '2026-06-14 10:59:16', 623, '2026-06-15 11:41:07', NULL, '2026-07-01 11:57:14', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-07-01', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Selection of Project Management Unit DMF, Bijapur', '2026-07-01', '2026-07-06 17:00:00', '2026-07-22 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Presentation & Interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-01-25', 1, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/5yyvRuCjkNAoie67AOaHjIlcQRTH5iBPSDX15jkL.pdf', NULL, 0, 2, 1, 0, '7,8', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/J7PIhnnfwwSIIevzUi4fyj8zFIleltyd0bCCpB9C.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 7865473.62, 0, 0, 1415785.25, 9281258.87, 1, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(172, 18, 94, 'EoI/CHiPS/PMU/AVIATION2/2026', 1, 'Program Management Unit (PMU) for Technical Support and Transaction Advisory Support for Directorate of Aviation, Government of Chhattisgarh', '24', '<p><strong>1. Introduction</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS), the nodal agency of the Department of Electronics &amp; Information Technology, Government of Chhattisgarh, invites Expression of Interest (EoI) from empanelled consulting firms for setting up an onsite Transaction Advisory Project Management Unit (PMU) for the Directorate of Aviation, Government of Chhattisgarh.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The Directorate of Aviation is responsible for overseeing and promoting civil aviation activities within the State, including airport and airstrip development, regulatory compliance, sectoral growth, and aviation skill development. With the expansion of regional air connectivity and the growth of aviation-related services and infrastructure in the State, the Directorate requires a dedicated multi-disciplinary team to provide end-to-end transaction advisory and bid process management support.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The selected firm shall deploy a Transaction Advisory PMU on a full-time, onsite basis for following broad scope. The team shall support in structuring, procuring, and managing the appointment of service providers across the aviation value chain, and in developing policy, schemes, and skill development frameworks for the sector and other.</p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li3\">The Directorate of Aviation is required to procure a range of specialised aviation services and infrastructure, including ground handling agencies, helicopter services, safety and security equipment, and the development of airstrips. Each of these procurements requires structured bid process management, technical and financial structuring, and compliance with applicable procurement rules.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li3\">Procurement of aviation services and infrastructure involves multi-stage transactions, contract structuring, and risk allocation that demand dedicated transaction advisory expertise not available within the Directorate on a full-time basis.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li3\">The State requires the development of an enabling aviation policy, sector schemes, and structured training modules to promote aviation-related skill development and employment among local youth, including pilot training, cabin crew training, and allied aviation trades.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li4\">There is a need to augment the institutional capacity of the Directorate through a dedicated PMU that can provide specialized, full-time transaction advisory, bid process management, and project management support across the aviation sector.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class=\"p5\"><strong>2. Purpose</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The key objective of engaging the Transaction Advisory PMU is to strengthen the institutional capacity of the Directorate of Aviation in the following areas:</p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li3\">End-to-end bid process management and transaction advisory for procurement of aviation services, infrastructure, and equipment.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li3\">Development of aviation policy, sector schemes, and facilitate in preparing training modules for skill development of local youth in aviation and allied trades.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li3\">Strengthening project management, monitoring, and reporting of aviation infrastructure and service delivery projects of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Coordination with national-level aviation institutions, regulatory authorities, and industry stakeholders for capacity building and sectoral development.</li>\r\n</ul>', 2, 94, '2026-06-14 11:49:34', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, NULL, '<p class=\"p1\"><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The objective of the assignment is to provide assistance to Directorate of Aviation for Program Management Unit (PMU) for Technical Support and Transaction Advisory Support.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p4\">CHiPS is inviting all Tier-I empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/ Empanelment/Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur Dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p>The deployed team shall carry out the following tasks during the term of the engagement:</p>\r\n<p><strong>1. Transaction Advisory and Bid Process Management</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Provide end-to-end transaction advisory and bid process management support for procurement of goods, services, and works across the aviation sector, covering the full bid cycle from need assessment to contract award and contract management.</li>\r\n<li>Techno-commercial assessment for proposed aviation procurements and advise on appropriate procurement and contracting strategies.</li>\r\n<li>Prepare, review, and finalise procurement documents including Expressions of Interest (EoIs), Requests for Proposal (RFPs), Requests for Qualification (RFQs), bid documents, draft contracts, concession agreements, Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs), and related documentation.</li>\r\n<li>Design qualification criteria, evaluation frameworks, and bid evaluation methodologies in alignment with the General Financial Rules (GFR) 2017, Central Vigilance Commission (CVC) guidelines, and applicable State of Chhattisgarh procurement rules.</li>\r\n<li>Manage the complete bid process, including pre-bid meetings, issuance of clarifications and corrigendum, bid opening, evaluation support, and preparation of evaluation reports and recommendations for the competent authority.</li>\r\n<li>Provide transaction advisory and bid process management support for empanelment of, and tendering for, the following primary aviation services and infrastructure but not limited to:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Ground handling agencies for airports and airstrips in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Helicopter services, including charter, regional connectivity, and emergency / medical evacuation services.</li>\r\n<li>Agencies for capacity building and training of aviation sector personnel and for institutional strengthening of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li>Suppliers of safety, security, and firefighting equipment for aviation facilities.</li>\r\n<li>Agencies for the development, upgradation, and maintenance of airstrips and allied aviation infrastructure.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Prepare empanelment frameworks, eligibility criteria, and rate-contract or panel-based selection structures for recurring aviation service requirements of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li>Support the Directorate in tender publication, bidder coordination, evaluation, award, and onboarding of empanelled service providers.</li>\r\n<li>Develop contract management and performance monitoring frameworks for empanelled agencies and selected service providers.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>2. Policy, Schemes, and Skill Development</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Support in the formulation of the State Aviation Policy, including policy research, benchmarking with national and global practices, stakeholder consultations, and drafting.</li>\r\n<li>Support the Directorate in the design and development of aviation sector schemes for promotion of air connectivity, aviation services, infrastructure, and investment in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate and assist the Directorate in the selection of specialised agencies for the development of training modules and curricula for skill development of local youth in aviation and allied trades, including pilot training, cabin crew training, aircraft maintenance engineering (AME), air traffic control (ATC), and ground handling.</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate partnerships and coordination with Flying Training Organisations (FTOs), national aviation academies, DGCA-approved institutions, and skill development agencies for establishment of training centres and skilling initiatives in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Suggestion on initiatives to promote aviation-related employment opportunities for local youth and to strengthen the aviation skilling ecosystem in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Conduct a comparative study of aviation services, schemes, and best practices implemented by other States, including regional connectivity, helicopter services, aviation infrastructure, aviation skilling, investment promotion, and allied aviation services. Identify replicable practices and prepare recommendations for adoption and contextual adaptation in Chhattisgarh, including implementation roadmaps and institutional arrangements required for roll-out.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>3. Project Monitoring, Reporting, and Departmental Handholding</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Provide project management support for aviation infrastructure and service delivery projects, including activities under the Regional Connectivity Scheme (RCS), airport and airstrip development, and operationalisation of State aviation assets.</li>\r\n<li>PMU shall support for monitoring of all ongoing projects and track upcoming and future projects, including their onboarding, progress, timelines, and overall implementation status.</li>\r\n<li>Establish and maintain a structured project monitoring framework covering all aviation projects, procurements, and empanelment processes, including project timelines, milestones, deliverables, and physical and financial progress against approved targets.</li>\r\n<li>Track the implementation status of selected and empanelled service providers, contractors, and agencies, and prepare progress reviews highlighting delays, bottlenecks, deviations from approved scope, and corrective actions required.</li>\r\n<li>Prepare periodic monitoring and progress reports, including weekly status updates, monthly progress reports, and quarterly review reports, in formats approved by the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li>Verify bills and invoices submitted by selected agencies, contractors, and service providers against the terms and conditions of the tender, work order, and contract. Recommend approval or rejection of bills with supporting verification notes.</li>\r\n<li>Support the Directorate in compilation of data and preparation of replies, status notes, and information sought by the State Government, the Legislative Assembly, audit authorities, and other competent forums.</li>\r\n<li>Coordinate with regulatory authorities, national aviation institutions, and industry stakeholders, and support stakeholder communication, meeting coordination, and follow-up actions.</li>\r\n<li>Carry out any other task assigned by the Directorate of Aviation related to aviation sector development, transaction advisory, bid process management, and routine departmental work.</li>\r\n</ol>', '<p><strong>1. Change Management</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">Any change in the scope of work, team composition, or duration shall be subject to mutual agreement between Directorate of Aviation/CHiPS and the selected consultant and shall be documented through a formal amendment to the Work Order. In case of unavoidable substitution, the replacement personnel must possess qualifications and experience equivalent to or higher than those specified in the original team requirement.</p>\r\n<p><strong>2. Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p6\">The envisaged duration of the assigned is 24 calendar months, extendable as required. The resource may be extended as per requirement of project need. Deployment timelines will be governed as per the approved Resource Deployment Plan to be submitted by the selected consultant within 30 working days of issuance of the Work Order.</p>', '<p><strong>Payment terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li class=\"p3\">Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule.</li>\r\n<li class=\"p3\">The successful bidder shall submit&nbsp;<span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">the </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">invoice for payment on man month basis</span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\"> as per </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">the agreed </span><span class=\"s3\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">empanelment </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">terms.</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"p3\">For&nbsp;<span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">reasons beyond </span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">the </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">control </span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">of </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">the selected bidder </span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">or </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">CHiPS, </span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">as the </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">case </span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">may be </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">selected bidder shall </span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">be </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">paid </span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">the </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">requisite man month payment </span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">in </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">the event that selected bidder </span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">has </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">performed </span><span style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">on </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">its obligations </span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">in </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">compliance with </span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">the </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">terms</span><span style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\"> of </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">this</span><span style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\"> </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">contract.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Penalty terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li9\"><span class=\"s1\">Penalty, if any, shall be governed </span><span class=\"s2\">as per </span><span class=\"s1\">the agreed </span><span class=\"s3\">empanelment </span><span class=\"s1\">terms.</span></li>\r\n</ul>', 5, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding companies about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their experience if any in similar area of expertise</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies the proposed candidates may be interviewed (face to face) by the Evaluation Committee.</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and Interview will be done as follows-</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th style=\"width: 16.8511%;\">Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th style=\"width: 35.8431%;\">Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th style=\"width: 47.2756%;\">Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 16.8511%;\"><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 35.8431%;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Work Plan, Activity Schedule, and Staffing Schedule</li>\r\n<li>Quality&nbsp;<span class=\"s3\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">of </span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">proposed methodology for such </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">specific kind </span><span style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">of a </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">project.</span></li>\r\n<li>Prior&nbsp;<span class=\"s3\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">exposure </span><span style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">in similar government projects</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 47.2756%;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Educational Qualification</li>\r\n<li>Suitability&nbsp;<span style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">of </span><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">profile</span></li>\r\n<li>Years&nbsp;<span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">of </span><span class=\"s3\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">relevant</span><span style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\"> </span><span class=\"s3\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">experience</span></li>\r\n<li>Experience of working in Government Projects</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\r\n<li class=\"p1\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The last date for submission of response is&nbsp;<strong>06/07/2026 17:00 Hrs.</strong>&nbsp;Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Pre-bid submissions, proposal submissions, presentation and interview details, and any query resolution shall be accepted only via the Empanelment Portal (<a class=\"decorated-link\" href=\"../../../\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"261\" data-end=\"288\">https://empl.cgstate.gov.in</a>). For any other enquiries, please contact via&nbsp;<a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"335\" data-end=\"356\">empl.chips@cgchips.in,</a>&nbsp;<a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"360\" data-end=\"382\">empl_portal@cgchips.in</a>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Signed copy of this EOI</li>\r\n<li class=\"li2\">Copy of Approach and methodology presentation</li>\r\n<li class=\"li3\">Resumes of resources proposed for the evaluation. The format of resumes will be as per empanelment tender number<span class=\"s1\">.</span></li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2026-06-14 15:28:24', 3, 1, '2026-06-14 13:54:57', 94, '2026-06-14 15:28:24', NULL, '2026-06-14 15:46:30', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-06-14', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Program Management Unit (PMU) for Technical Support and Transaction Advisory Support for Directorate of Aviation, Government of Chhattisgarh', '2026-06-14', '2026-06-19 17:00:00', '2026-07-06 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Technical Score and Presentation', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-01-25', 0, 0, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/ZNRz8iqaiJHw7GOv7O8HXt2BtN5UsIRXkeamrwQB.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 0, 0, '1,2,3,4,5', 1, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/1C4xClp7Snuw73jD2CTSkWOfSKKq8hvUiBljey6S.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(173, 0, 59, 'EOI/CHiPS/EMPL/AWD/CGCOG/2026', 1, 'for Selection of Technical Resources under\nChhattisgarh Center of Geo-Informatics\n(CGCOG) Project of CHiPS', '9', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; line-height: 150%;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-ansi-language: EN-IN;\">CHiPS</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-ansi-language: EN-IN;\">, a Registered Society promoted by the Government of Chhattisgarh, is the nodal agency and prime mover for propelling IT growth and implementation of IT plans in the State. The Hon&rsquo;ble Chief Minister heads the High Powered Governing Council of <strong>CHiPS</strong>. It includes Minister for Finance &amp; Commercial Taxes, Minister for Commerce &amp; Industry, Minister for Education, and Minister for Panchayat &amp; Rural Development, Chief Secretary, representative from the Ministry of Electronics &amp; Information Technology in Government of India and eminent persons from IT industry. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; line-height: 150%;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-ansi-language: EN-IN;\">The objective of Chhattisgarh Center of Geoinformatics (CGCOG) is insertion of GIS/Geospatial technology in Chhattisgarh State for effective planning, monitoring, management of natural resources, efforts optimization, GIS capacity building among Departments and Development of Geo-Ecosystem. It will help to optimize collection, collation, compilation and centralization of spatial data. This project will facilitate Spatial Data Infrastructure (SDI) of Chhattisgarh State.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; line-height: 150%;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif;\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS) intends to on-board an agency for CGCOG a period initially for One (1) year which is extendable.</span></p>', 1, 59, '2026-06-30 17:39:31', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>CHIPS is inviting Tier-II empanelled agencies (as per tender no 160137/CEO/CHIPS/EMPL/Application &amp; Website Development, Dated 18/10/2024) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p><!-- [if !supportLists]--></p>\r\n<h1 style=\"text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 150%; mso-pagination: widow-orphan; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; mso-hyphenate: none; margin: 0cm 0cm .0001pt 18.0pt;\"><a name=\"_Toc229132960\"></a><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">1.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Scope of Work</span></h1>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif;\">Development of Chhattisgarh Center of Geoinformatics (CGCOG) at State </span></p>\r\n<p><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif;\">Development of an open and interoperable architecture approach for implementing a &ldquo;Spatial Data Infrastructure (SDI)&rdquo; accessible to all authorized users.</span></p>\r\n<p><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif;\">Establishment of &ldquo;Geo Portals&rdquo; for State Government Departments. </span></p>\r\n<p><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif;\">Develop of data management, data visualization, and data dissemination strategies and techniques, with a particular focus on the needs of state.</span></p>\r\n<p><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif;\">Centralization of geospatial data of various departments with standard schema designing and cataloging. </span></p>\r\n<p><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif;\">Define Distributed SDI requirements by undertaking a technology workshop in Chhattisgarh; the focus of workshop will be at exchanging ideas and approaches on specific requirements, specifications, technology and products required.</span></p>\r\n<p><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-ansi-language: EN-IN;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif;\">Development of an Architecture document describing key architectural elements of Geo Portal prototype.</span></p>\r\n<p><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-ansi-language: EN-IN;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif;\">PM Gati-Shakti Project.</span></p>\r\n<h1 style=\"text-indent: -18pt; line-height: normal; margin: 0cm 0cm 0.0001pt 18pt; text-align: left;\"><a name=\"_Toc229132961\"></a><a name=\"_Toc86169715\"></a><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc229132961;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">2.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Resources Requirement</span></span><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc229132961;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">, Responsibility:</span></span></h1>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; line-height: 150%;\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Web GIS application development involve various tasks that require a team of skilled professionals with wide-ranging skill sets. A spatial data infrastructure &amp; Web GIS solution development, Server &amp; Geodatabase Management project need a skilled team made up of specialists &amp; well-versed in GIS field. Following are the required skill that brought together to develop &ldquo;Chhattisgarh Center of Geoinformatics&rdquo;-</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 150%; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo2; margin: 0cm 0cm 6.0pt 18.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">1)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong></span><!--[endif]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Manager- GIS</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: 18.0pt; line-height: 150%;\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">A Manager GIS will be required to manage geographical information system and associated vector datasets under project. He/she will have responsibility of monitoring of Geoprocessing, Geoanalytics, Spatial Analysis, Network Analysis operations and Geodatabase management from an executive level. This individual has responsibility of management of team members and allocated resources. Further, Managers will be responsible for planning, development and execution of project activities. Their work tasks will include- </span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 150%; mso-list: l2 level2 lfo3; margin: 0cm 0cm 0cm 36.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">a)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Communication with departments and understand its key requirements and accordingly preparation of SRS, FRS and TRS,</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 150%; mso-list: l2 level2 lfo3; margin: 0cm 0cm 0cm 36.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">b)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Efforts and Cost estimation,</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 150%; mso-list: l2 level2 lfo3; margin: 0cm 0cm 0cm 36.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">c)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Scheduling the project timelines,</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 150%; mso-list: l2 level2 lfo3; margin: 0cm 0cm 0cm 36.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">d)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Planning for work allocation to human resources, </span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 150%; mso-list: l2 level2 lfo3; margin: 0cm 0cm 0cm 36.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">e)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Coordination management among team members for timely completion of tasks.</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 150%; mso-list: l2 level2 lfo3; margin: 0cm 0cm 0cm 36.0pt;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 150%; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo2; margin: 0cm 0cm 6.0pt 18.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">2)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong></span><!--[endif]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Assistant Manager - (Geodatabase, Network Analysis, Image Processing, Geoprocessing, R&amp;D)</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: 18.0pt; line-height: 150%;\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">A GIS expert will be required to handle GIS datasets and associated vector datasets under project. He/she will have responsibility of execution of Geoprocessing, Geoanalytics, Spatial Analysis, Network Analysis operations, Cartography and Geodatabase management. This individual has responsibility of management of allocated resources.</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-bottom: 0cm; text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: 18.0pt; line-height: 150%;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 150%; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo2; margin: 0cm 0cm 6.0pt 18.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">3)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong></span><!--[endif]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Programmer </span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; line-height: 150%;\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Programmers will be required for the development of World Wide Web applications using a client-server model and handling \"HTML, CSS and JavaScript (in client side) and PHP, ASP.NET (C#) or Java (in the server) and HTTP for communications between client and server. Further, they will be responsible for mobile technology, such as building apps for Google&rsquo;s Android, Apple&rsquo;s iOS and Microsoft&rsquo;s Windows Phone platforms. They will also be responsible for creating and implementing databases required for the website and mobile applications. They will be responsible for testing entire application efficiency, performance and troubleshoot and to correct problems.</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 150%; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo2; margin: 0cm 0cm 6.0pt 18.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">4)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong></span><!--[endif]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">GIS Associates</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: 18.0pt; line-height: 150%;\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">GIS associates will be required for execution of various GIS activities, handling of GIS vector datasets under project. He/she will have responsibility of generation of various GIS datasets, digitisation, and map updation, execution of Geoprocessing, Geoanalytics, Spatial Analysis, Network Analysis operations, Cartography and Geodatabase preparation. This individual will provide assistance to GIS Experts on various GIS activities under project.</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-justify: inter-ideograph; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 150%; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo2; margin: 0cm 0cm 6.0pt 18.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; color: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">5)<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong></span><!--[endif]--><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong style=\"mso-bidi-font-weight: normal;\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; color: windowtext;\">Assistant Programmer</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 150%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif;\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',serif; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-fareast; color: windowtext; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: HI;\">Assistant Programmers will be required for the development of World Wide Web applications using a client-server model and handling \"HTML, CSS and JavaScript (in client side) and PHP, ASP.NET (C#) or Java (in the server) and HTTP for communications between client and server. Further, they will be responsible for mobile technology, such as building apps for Google&rsquo;s Android, Apple&rsquo;s iOS and Microsoft&rsquo;s Windows Phone platforms. They will also be responsible for creating and implementing databases required for the website and mobile applications. They will be responsible for testing entire application efficiency, performance and troubleshoot and to correct problems. Further, they will provide assistance to Programmer for the completion of project objectives.</span></span></span></p>', NULL, '<p><strong>Penalty terms </strong><br>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Important Note: </strong>All other terms and conditions as per tender no 160137/CEO/CHIPS/EMPL/Application &amp; Website Development, Dated 18/10/2024</p>', 6, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/ discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the Empaneled companies about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their past experience if any in similar area of expertise.</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies the proposed candidates will be interviewed through Online by the Evaluation Committee.</li>\r\n<li>The marking of candidates Interview will be done as follows -<br>&nbsp;<br>\r\n<table style=\"width: 95.6625%;\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th style=\"width: 4.54101%; text-align: center;\" align=\"right\">#</th>\r\n<th style=\"width: 82.5877%;\">Candidate Interview</th>\r\n<th style=\"width: 12.8713%;\" align=\"right\">Max Marks</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.54101%; text-align: center;\" align=\"right\">1</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82.5877%;\">Suitability of profile</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8713%;\" align=\"right\">15</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.54101%; text-align: center;\" align=\"right\">2</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82.5877%;\">Your relevant experience</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8713%;\" align=\"right\">15</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.54101%; text-align: center;\" align=\"right\">3</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82.5877%;\">Good understanding of Design Development best practices framework</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8713%;\" align=\"right\">25</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.54101%; text-align: center;\" align=\"right\">4</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82.5877%;\">Excellent communication abilities</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8713%;\" align=\"right\">20</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.54101%; text-align: center;\" align=\"right\">5</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82.5877%;\">Strong ability to understand, deliberate and report</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8713%;\" align=\"right\">25</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 4.54101%; text-align: center;\" align=\"right\"><strong>Total</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 82.5877%;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 12.8713%;\" align=\"right\"><strong>100</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.<br><br></li>\r\n<li>The last date for submission of response is 24/07/2026; 17:00 Hrs. Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.<br><br></li>\r\n<li>Pre-bid submissions, proposal submissions, presentation and interview details, and any query resolution shall be accepted only via the Empanelment Portal (https://empl.cgstate.gov.in). For any other enquiries, please contact via empl.chips@cgchips.in, empl_portal@cgchips.in.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EoI</li>\r\n<li>Resumes of the resources who will appear for the interview.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '728816', '2026-07-02 17:33:39', 3, 1, '2026-07-02 17:28:59', 59, '2026-07-02 17:33:39', NULL, '2026-07-03 16:40:39', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-07-03', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Selection of resources from Manpower Service Provider Firm for Chhattisgarh Center of Geo-Informatics Project of CHIPS', '2026-07-03', '2026-07-08 17:00:00', '2026-07-24 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Presentation & Interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-02-12', 0, 0, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/FPWyzwc6d95DNe2Ii3uKmOAiVsIOkKj7S2xnp0Uw.pdf', NULL, 0, 2, 0, 0, '14,15,16', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/JlHUx2gaf8eezkG7SxqNauceZxjHeEtQ45DEfi95.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(174, 1, 90, 'EOI/CHIPS/EMPL/Aadhaar & AUA/KUAProject/2026', 1, 'For Selection of Resource for Aadhaar (EA) & AUA/KUA Project of CHiPS', '12', '<p class=\"p1\">CHiPS, a Registered Society promoted by the Government of Chhattisgarh, is the nodal agency and prime mover for propelling IT growth and implementation of IT plans in the State. TheHon&rsquo;b1e Chief Minister heads the High Powered Governing Council of CHiPS. It includes Minister for Finance &amp; Commercial Taxes, Minister for Commerce &amp; Industry, Minister for Education, and Minister for Panchayat &amp; Rural Development, Chief Secretary, representative from the Ministry of Electronics &amp; Information Technology in Government of India and eminent persons from IT industry.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">CHiPS is involved as State Designated Agency (SDA) in NeGPMMP&rsquo;s implementation ofsome mega IT Projects like CHOiCE, e-Procurement, SDC, SWAN, Wi-Fi, Digital Secretariat,SLCM, GIS and CSCs. A professional approach is being adopted for the implementation of ITProjects using the services of e-governance experts and consultants from corporate and academia.Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS) intends to on-board an agency for a period ofThree (3) year to assist and support Various State Government Departments in order toImplement IT Services/ E- Governance Services through Empanelment Project of CHiPS.</p>', 1, 90, '2026-07-07 11:42:58', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 10, 18, 0, NULL, '<ol>\r\n<li>Factsheet&nbsp; &nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Introduction&nbsp; &nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Scope of Work&nbsp; &nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Team Composition&nbsp; &nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Resource Replacement&nbsp; &nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Duration of the assignment&nbsp; &nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Critical Information and Last Date for Response&nbsp; &nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Evaluation Process&nbsp; &nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Penalty terms&nbsp; &nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Documents required as response to this EoI&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ol>', '<p class=\"p1\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS) intends to on-board a Manpower Service provider Firms fora period of One year to assist and support Various State Government Departments for IT Services/E- Governance Services through Empanelment Project of CHiPS. The detailed Scope of Work (SoW)is listed below. CHiPS want to appoint 1 resource under Aadhaar (EA) &amp; AUA-KUA Project (Level<span class=\"s1\"> &ndash; 10).</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">This section provides general information about the issuer, important dates, relevant addresses and the overall eligibility criteria for the bidders.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">CHiPSis inviting all Tier II empanelled agencies (as per the Tender No.<strong>160137/CEO/CHiPS/EMPL/Application &amp; Website Development/ dated 18/10/2024) </strong>to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p class=\"p1\"><strong>Assistant Technical Manager (AUA/KUA &amp; ADV Project)</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The Solution Architect for the AUA (Authentication User Agency) and KUA (e-KYC User Agency) at CHiPS (Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society) plays a pivotal role in designing and implementing robust solutions that ensure seamless integration with Aadhaar services. This position requires in-depth technical expertise and a strong understanding of Aadhaar authentication and KYC processes. The Solution Architect is responsible for collaborating with the Sub-AUA/Sub-KUA, Authentication Service Agency (ASA/KSA) and the Unique Identification Authority of India (UIDAI) to ensure compliance with regulatory standards and to facilitate efficient communication and data exchange. Key responsibilities include analyzing system requirements, designing scalable and secure architecture, and overseeing the implementation of solutions. The role demands a proactive approach to problem-solving, ensuring high availability and performance of Aadhaar and Project Related services, and maintaining comprehensive documentation of all architectural designs and changes. The Solution Architect must also stay updated with the latest technologies and UIDAI guidelines to ensure the continuous improvement of the system. Effective coordination of AUA/KUA with standard hierarchy wise channel such asSub-AUA/Sub-KUA, ASA/KSA, and UIDAI is crucial to address any technical issues promptly and to ensure that all integrations and updates are executed smoothly and efficiently.</p>\r\n<p><strong>A. Job Description:-</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">System Design and Architecture:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Design and develop scalable, secure, and high-performance solutions for Authentication User Agency (AUA) and Electronic Know Your Customer User Agency (KUA) services.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Create detailed architectural blueprints and technical specifications.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Integration Management:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Ensure seamless integration of AUA/KUA systems with the Authentication Service Agency (ASA) and UIDAI infrastructure.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Develop APIs and middleware to facilitate communication between systems.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Compliance and Security:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Ensure solutions comply with UIDAI guidelines, data privacy regulations, and security standards.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Implement robust security measures to protect sensitive data and prevent unauthorized access.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Technical Coordination:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Act as the primary point of contact for technical coordination with ASA and UIDAI.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Facilitate regular meetings and communication to address technical issues and updates.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Project Management:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Lead and manage end-to-end implementation of AUA/KUA projects.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Coordinate with project managers to ensure projects are completed on time, within scope, and within budget.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Documentation and Reporting:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Maintain comprehensive documentation of system architecture, design decisions, and integration processes.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Prepare and present regular reports on project status, risks, and mitigation strategies.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Performance Optimization:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Monitor and optimize the performance of AUA/KUA systems to ensure high availability and efficiency.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Implement best practices for system maintenance and upgrades.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Stakeholder Collaboration:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Collaborate with internal teams, including developers, analysts, and IT support, to ensure alignment and successful project execution.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Work with external stakeholders (Sub-AUA / Sub-KUA), such as ASA and UIDAI, to ensure compliance and successful integration.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Risk Management:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Identify potential risks and develop mitigation strategies to address them.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Ensure contingency plans are in place for critical system failures or breaches.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Continuous Improvement:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Stay updated with the latest technologies, UIDAI guidelines, and industry best practices.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Implement continuous improvement processes to enhance system functionality and user experience.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Training and Support:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Provide training and support to internal teams and stakeholders on new systems and processes.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Ensure users are well-equipped to handle new functionalities and system changes.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Problem Resolution:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Troubleshoot and resolve technical issues promptly to minimize downtime and service disruption.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Coordinate with ASA and UIDAI technical teams for issue resolution and system updates.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Experience:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Work closely with IT and technical teams to ensure alignment between technology implementations and change management activities.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Support the integration of new systems and technologies with existing workflows and processes.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Understanding of data privacy regulations and compliance requirements related to Authentication System.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Familiarity with government policies and procedures.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Technical Skills:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Proficiency in system architecture design, software development, and integration methodologies.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Strong knowledge of API development, web services, and middleware technologies.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Expertise in security protocols and data protection measures.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Soft Skills:</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Excellent communication, interpersonal, and stakeholder management skills.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Strong analytical and problem-solving abilities.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Ability to work collaboratively in a team environment and lead cross-functional teams.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class=\"p6\">This job description outlines the essential responsibilities and qualifications for a Solution Architect for AUA/KUA at CHiPS, emphasizing the critical role of coordination with ASA and UIDAI to deliver comprehensive and compliant solutions.</p>\r\n<p><strong>B. Requirements</strong></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li7\">At least Minimum of 10 years of experience in solution architecture, system integration, and project management.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Experience with Aadhaar authentication and KYC processes is highly desirable.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Experience of project management for state &ndash;wide e-Governance delivery project.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Should have a knowledge and experience of IT service delivery and project execution.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Knowledge of executing IT Projects Min 10 Years</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Strong programming skills in languages such as Java, or similar.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Experience with integration platforms and middleware technologies.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Ability to integrate diverse systems, applications, and services seamlessly.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Deep understanding of cybersecurity principles and best practices.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Experience implementing security protocols and compliance measures.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Knowledge of database management systems (e.g., SQL, NoSQL).</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Strong leadership and team management capabilities.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Exceptional analytical and problem-solving skills.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Ability to diagnose issues quickly and propose effective solutions.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Experience in project management, including planning, execution, and monitoring.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Familiarity with project management tools and methodologies.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Flexibility to adapt to changing project requirements and priorities.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li7\">Ability to align technical solutions with organizational goals.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>C. Desirable</strong></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li6\">Communication skills: Proficient in both written and oral communication in English and Hindi.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p><strong>1. Resource Replacement</strong></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li2\">The selected agency needs to give 1 (One) Month of advance notice to CHiPS for any change of deployed resource during the course of the assignment.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li3\">The selected agency needs to ensure knowledge transfer and handover during change of any resource for smooth transition.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li4\">The replacement of any resource should be approved by <span class=\"s1\">CHiPS.</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>2. Duration of the assignment</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">Government of Chhattisgarh intends to on-board manpower resource for a period of 01 year at least to assist, support State Government and may be extended as per project need &amp; contract.</p>\r\n<p><strong>3. Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p4\">The envisaged duration of the assigned is 12 calendar months. The resources may be extended as per the project need.</p>\r\n<p><strong>4. HR Policy</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p4\">The selected candidate shall work on the payroll of the empanelled agency. The empanelled agency shall manage the HR {Salary, PF, leaves (as per CHiPS Policy) and other compliances of the selected resources (As per Empanelment of Manpower Service Provider Firms for Government of Chhattisgarh for a period of 3 years RFP &amp;Agreement).</p>\r\n<p><strong>5. Termination Clause</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p4\">Termination will be done as per Empanelment of Manpower Service Provider Firms for Government of Chhattisgarh for a period of 3 years RFP &amp;Agreement.</p>', '<p><strong>1. Penalty terms</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">Important Note: All other terms and conditions as per tender no 160137/CEO/CHIPS/EMPL/Application &amp; Website Development, Dated 18/10/2024</p>', 11, '<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/ discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">A presentation will be made by the Empanelled companies about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their past experience if any in similar area of expertise.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">During the presentation by the companies the proposed candidates will be interviewed through Online (WebEx Link) by the Evaluation Committee.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The marking of candidates Interview will be done as follows-<br><br>\r\n<table style=\"width: 94.164%; height: 347px;\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"0\">\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 32px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1.57017%; height: 32px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\">#</span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.2002%; height: 32px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Candidate Interview</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2296%; height: 32px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Max Marks</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 52px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1.57017%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>1</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.2002%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Suitability of profile </strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2296%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>15</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 52px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1.57017%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>2</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.2002%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Your relevant experience</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2296%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>20</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 55px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1.57017%; height: 55px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>3</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.2002%; height: 55px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Good understanding of Design Development best practices framework </strong></span><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Management</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2296%; height: 55px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>25</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 52px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1.57017%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>4</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.2002%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Excellent communication abilities</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2296%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>15</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 52px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1.57017%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>5</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.2002%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Strong ability to understand, deliberate and report </strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2296%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>25</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 52px;\">\r\n<td style=\"width: 1.57017%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 84.2002%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>Total</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 14.2296%; height: 52px;\" valign=\"middle\">\r\n<p align=\"center\"><span style=\"color: #000000; font-family: Times New Roman; font-size: medium;\"><strong>100</strong></span></p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p class=\"p1\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The last date for submission of response is <strong>Dated 28/07/2026, 17:00 Hrs</strong>. Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">Pre-bid submission, proposal submission, presentation and interview details and any query resolution will be accepted only via the Empanelment Portal (<a href=\"../../../\">https://empl.cgstate.gov.in</a>) in the specific section respectively. For any other enquiries, contact via <a href=\"mailto:empl.chips@cgchips.in\">empl.chips@cgchips.in</a>, <a href=\"mailto:empl_portal@cgchips.in\">empl_portal@cgchips.in</a></p>', '<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Signed copy of this EoI</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Resumes of resources that will face the interview.<strong>&nbsp;</strong></li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '976990', '2026-07-07 11:57:20', 4, 1, '2026-07-07 11:47:54', 90, '2026-07-07 11:57:20', NULL, '2026-07-07 11:59:05', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-07-07', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Selection of resource for  Aadhaar & AUA-m KUA Project of CHiPS', '2026-07-07', '2026-07-13 17:00:00', '2026-07-28 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-02-17', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/Pwnsfgwowdohdu7V5Kxwtx8X8rfWmfc5p79wvwpZ.pdf', NULL, 0, 2, 1, 0, '14,15,16', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/WNizwAHk9dZtkcArFWfrh1yfxKdFd4af76ZEY5Ld.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(175, 0, 78, 'EoI/EMPL/CHiPS/PMU/GoodGov&Con/2026', 1, 'For Providing PMU Services for Good Governance and Convergence Department', '12', '<p>The Government of Chhattisgarh is committed to strengthening public service delivery, enhancing administrative efficiency, and deepening citizen-centric governance. The State continues to prioritise ease of living, transparency, digital transformation, capacity building, and stronger accountability across public systems.<br><br>The Department of Good Governance leads this agenda by supporting departments in modernising administrative processes, re-designing service delivery, building institutional capacities, and driving evidence-based innovations to enable a responsive, transparent, and efficient government.<br><br>While Chhattisgarh has undertaken several good governance reforms, there remains an opportunity to further streamline processes, strengthen service delivery, enhance communication and stakeholder alignment, and embed structured operating models and best practices across departments. There is also scope to accelerate adoption of service-level improvements, performance monitoring mechanisms, and innovation-driven approaches. To support these efforts and ensure coordinated, statewide implementation of good governance practices, the Department proposes to establish a dedicated PMU.</p>', 2, 78, '2026-01-02 12:25:35', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, '<ol>\r\n<li>Objective</li>\r\n<li>Factsheet</li>\r\n<li>Introduction</li>\r\n<li>Scope of Work</li>\r\n<li>Team Requirement</li>\r\n<li>Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment</li>\r\n<li>Critical Information and Last Date for Response</li>\r\n<li>Evaluation Process</li>\r\n<li>Payment terms</li>\r\n<li>Penalty terms Reason Description Penalty</li>\r\n<li>Documents required as response to this EoI<br>ANNEXURE &ndash; I</li>\r\n</ol>', '<p>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS) intends to onboard a Tier -I Consultancy Firm for a period of twelve (12) months to provide specialized consultancy support for the implementation of Good Governance and Convergence initiatives across various State Government departments. This initiative is being undertaken to meet the objective of Good Governance, emphasizing process simplification, digital transformation, and enhanced interdepartmental coordination to improve citizen service delivery. Under this engagement, CHiPS plans to deploy a team of three (3) specialized professionals who will work as a Project Management Unit (PMU) for Department of Good Governance and Convergence Department, Government of Chhattisgarh.<br><br>This Expression of Interest (EoI) outlines the scope of work, eligibility criteria, timelines, and other relevant details for empanelled consultancy firms interested in supplying qualified professionals to support this transformative initiative.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>CHiPS invites proposals exclusively from Tier-I empaneled Consultancy firms (as per the Tender No165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/ Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on the Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Candidates, Qualifications, Terms of Reference (ToR), and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI for providing Strategic Support for Good Governance and Convergence Department, Government of Chhattisgarh.<br><br>To provide program management and advisory support to strengthen good governance reforms across departments through:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Development of governance frameworks, operating models, and service-delivery standards</li>\r\n<li>Process improvements, SOPs, and adoption of best practices</li>\r\n<li>Structured rollout of governance reforms and pilot initiatives</li>\r\n<li>Enhanced performance monitoring, communication, and stakeholder engagement</li>\r\n<li>Capacity buildingand continuous learning mechanisms</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p>Through the course of the engagement, the PMU is expected to undertake the following:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Develop a clear vision, mission, and governance principles, and convert them into practical priorities, communication tools, and performance measures to guide day-to-day operations.</li>\r\n<li>Create and roll out scalable operating models for good governance, including SOPs, process maps, and role definitions to ensure consistent delivery across departments.</li>\r\n<li>Build a simple and consistent branding and communication approach, supported by toolkits, templates, and training for effective messaging and stakeholder engagement.</li>\r\n<li>Define core building blocks of good governance suited to Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s context, with clear milestones, responsibilities, and resource plans for smooth adoption.</li>\r\n<li>Benchmark leading governance models from other states and adapt relevant insights into operational tools, templates, and guidelines for Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li>Support implementation of identified governance improvements, including pilots and structured initiatives to build momentum and sustain long-term reforms.</li>\r\n<li>Strengthen Lok Seva Guarantee through service diagnostics, process improvements, performance reviews, and stronger compliance for timely and citizen-focused delivery.</li>\r\n<li>Create platforms for innovation&mdash;such as hackathons, podcasts, talks, and knowledge repositories&mdash; to encourage collaboration and continuous learning.</li>\r\n<li>Assist departments in preparing and delivering annual capacity-building plans, covering curriculum design, training, and monitoring of outcomes.</li>\r\n<li>Work with Rajya NITI Aayog, CHiPS, and the Academy of Administration to support policy execution, technology-enabled governance, and expanded capacity-building efforts.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p><strong>Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment </strong><br>The envisaged duration of the assignment is 1 year (12 months) from the date of work order and will be extendable for another 2 years (24 months) as required.</p>', '<p><strong>Payment Terms<br><br></strong>Payment to selected bidder for technical and operational support to the Department of Good Governance and Convergence, Government of Chhattisgarh be released on person month basis, post submission of the invoice for payment. The payment will be as per current resources person month rates applicable under empanelment and payment terms will be governed terms and conditions of Empanelment agreement.<strong><br></strong></p>\r\n<p><strong>Penalty terms Reason Description Penalty</strong></p>\r\n<p>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms. Important Note: All other terms and conditions of tender 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025 shall be applicable to this EOI.</p>', 6, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/ discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding companies about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their experience if any in similar area of expertise.</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies the proposed candidates will be interviewed (face to face) by the Evaluation Committee.</li>\r\n<li>Further, any deviation from proposal and resource CV submitted as bid response to this EOI would not be considered and would be duly ruled as rejection. Therefore, it instructed to bidders that the actual resource who will be deployed for assignment should be present for interview (in person/Skype/VC). instructed to bidders that the actual resource who will be deployed for assignment should be present for interview (in person/Skype/VC).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and Interview will be done as follows -</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th>Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th>Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of the Project</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such specific kind of a project</li>\r\n<li>Prior exposure to implementing government projects in Bid Management and Exit Management</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of key SLAs for the project management&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Good understanding of project management best practices framework</li>\r\n<li>Ability to Negotiate / Persuade / Influence</li>\r\n<li>Strong ability to understand, deliberate, and report / monitor the key SLAs</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<p>Agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.<br><br>The last date for submission of response is 23/01/2026; 17:00 hrs. Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.<br><br>The preferred mode of communication for query resolution is through email to:&nbsp;<br><br><strong>CEO, CHiPS</strong><br>State Data Centre, Civil Lines,<br>Raipur &ndash; 492001<br>Email: ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158 | Fax: +91-771-4014158</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EoI</li>\r\n<li>Copy of Approach and methodology presentation</li>\r\n<li>Resumes of resources that will face the interview as per annexure</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2026-07-13 12:38:17', 4, 1, '2026-07-13 12:33:44', 78, '2026-07-13 12:38:17', NULL, '2026-07-13 12:39:07', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-07-13', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Expression of Interest (EoI) for Providing PMU Services for Good Governance and Convergence Department', '2026-01-02', '2026-01-09 17:00:00', '2026-01-23 17:00:00', '2026-01-30 15:00:00', 'To be informed later', 'To be informed later', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-02-23', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/IUIWH3sSfUor3N6Zhfyiq51m1r0ahBMMQmarkpuf.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 1, 0, '1,2,3,4,5', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/ZlOvD3jTAKnPSiV3YqxVGgmksMZrO0mA0kA7td7b.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 24252391.94, 0, 0, 4365430.55, 28617822.48, 1, 0, NULL, NULL),
(176, 98, 719, 'EoI/EMPL/CHiPS/CGRDC/2026', 1, 'For Engagement of a Consulting Firm for Deployment of Technical to Support CGRDC in Infrastructure Projects', '12', '<p>Chhattisgarh Road Development Corporation (CGRDC) is the nodal agency of the Government of Chhattisgarh responsible for planning, development, and implementation of road, highway, bridge, and allied infrastructure projects across the State, working closely with the Public Works Department (PWD) and other line departments.<br><br>CGRDC\'s project pipeline spans road and highway construction, bridges and Road Over Bridges (ROBs), Hybrid Annuity Model (HAM) and other PPP-mode projects, asset monetization initiatives, and large-scale building infrastructure. Effective execution requires dedicated technical, financial, and IT/MIS capacity that is not always available within the existing sanctioned strength of CGRDC and PWD.</p>', 2, 719, '2026-07-13 15:26:51', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, '<ol>\r\n<li>Factsheet</li>\r\n<li>Introduction</li>\r\n<li>Scope of Work</li>\r\n<li>Team Requirement</li>\r\n<li>Change Management</li>\r\n<li>Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment</li>\r\n<li>Critical Information and Last Date for Response</li>\r\n<li>Evaluation Process</li>\r\n<li>Payment terms</li>\r\n<li>Penalty terms</li>\r\n<li>Documents required as response to this EoI</li>\r\n</ol>', '<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\n<p>CHIPS is inviting Tier-I empaneled agencies (as per Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/ Consultancy&nbsp;Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Team&nbsp;Requirement, Qualification, and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.</p>\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p>CGRDC therefore intends to engage a reputed Consulting Firm to depute a team of 3 (three) domain specialists to support CGRDC and PWD on an ongoing basis in project implementation, contract and concession management, IT-enabled process automation, and monetization advisory. The deputed team shall, under the direction of CGRDC, provide the following support (illustrative, not exhaustive; CGRDC may modify scope during the engagement period):</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Support planning, implementation, monitoring, and progress review of infrastructure projects of CGRDC, including roads, highways, bridges, ROBs, and building infrastructure.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Support automation and process re-engineering of the Work Management System (WMS) &ndash; requirement gathering, workflow mapping, vendor/system coordination, User Acceptance Testing, rollout, and field-level training.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Support automation and digitisation of the electronic Measurement Book (eMB) system &ndash; process mapping, integration with WMS/financial systems, field validation protocols, and capacity building of site engineers.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Draft, review, and vet project proposals, DPRs, RFPs/RFQs/tender documents, and support end-to-end bid process management including pre-bid clarifications, technical and financial evaluation, and comparative statements.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Support structuring, drafting, vetting, and negotiation of concession agreements and other PPP contractual instruments, and provide ongoing contract management support during the concession/construction period.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Draft, evaluate, and support approval processing of project proposals structured under EPC, Hybrid Annuity Model (HAM), and Toll-Operate-Transfer (TOT) modes, including financial structuring inputs and compliance with MoRTH/State guidelines.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Support preparation, appraisal, and processing of Road Over Bridge (ROB) proposals, including coordination with Railways and other stakeholder agencies.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Support CGRDC\'s asset monetisation initiatives (e.g. Toll-Operate-Transfer, or comparable structures), including asset identification, valuation inputs, transaction structuring support, and investor/stakeholder coordination.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Prepare periodic MIS reports, dashboards, and review-meeting briefs for CGRDC/PWD leadership and, as required, for State Government reviews.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Any other task, assignment, or advisory support as may be entrusted by CGRDC from time to time, within the broad domain expertise of the deputed team.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\"><strong>Change Management:</strong></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<ol class=\"ol1\">\r\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\r\n<ol class=\"ol2\">\r\n<li class=\"li2\">The selected agency will have to give 2 weeks of advance notice to CGRDC for any change of deployed resource/s during the course of the assignment.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li2\">The selected agency will have to ensure that the knowledge transfer and handover during change of any resource/s for smooth transition.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li2\">The replacement of any resource/s should be approved by CGRDC in writing.<br><br></li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\"><strong>Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment<br></strong>01 year from the date of issuance of the Work Order (WO).</li>\r\n</ol>', '<p><strong>Payment Terms</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule.</li>\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the agreed empanelment<br>terms.</li>\n<li>For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or CHiPS, as the case may be selected bidder shall be paid<br>the requisite man month payment in the event that selected bidder has performed on its obligations in compliance<br>with the terms of this contract.</li>\n</ul>\n<p><strong>PENALTY TERMS</strong></p>\n<ul>\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the terms and conditions mentioned in Tender No.165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025, Raipur dated 20/02/2025.</li>\n</ul>', 6, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their experience, if any, in a similar area of expertise (via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th>Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th>Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of the Project</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such specific kind of a project</li>\r\n<li>Prior exposure to implementing government projects in Bid Management and Exit Management</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of key SLAs for the project management</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Good understanding of project management best practices framework</li>\r\n<li>Ability to Negotiate / Persuade / Influence</li>\r\n<li>Strong ability to understand, deliberate, and report / monitor the key SLAs</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\n<li>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful&nbsp;study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.</li>\n<li>The last date for submission of response is <strong>05/08/2026 17:00 Hrs</strong>. Any response received after the above deadline&nbsp;will be rejected.</li>\n<li>All pre-bid queries and proposal submissions shall be submitted through the Empanelment Portal&nbsp;(https://empl.cgstate.gov.in) only. Any submission or communication received through e-mail, messages, or any&nbsp;mode other than the Empanelment Portal shall not be accepted or considered. For any other enquiries, please&nbsp;contact empl.chips@cgchips.in and empl_portal@cgchips.in.</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EoI.</li>\r\n<li>Copy of the approach and methodology presentation.</li>\r\n<li>Resumes of the resources who will appear for the interview.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2026-07-15 16:47:49', 4, 1, '2026-07-13 15:36:42', 719, '2026-07-15 16:47:49', NULL, '2026-07-15 17:22:03', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-07-15', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Expression of Interest (EOI) For Engagement of a Consulting Firm for Deployment of Technical to Support CGRDC in Infrastructure Projects', '2026-07-15', '2026-07-20 17:00:00', '2026-08-05 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Presentation & Interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-02-23', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/EIKTTCmi8NIksDqLj7YRmVuPAFKqwtNZCFxcZ6Mn.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 1, 0, '1,2,3,4,5', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/qBRTmg90IhS2R29DmKiXx3kYxlDVfCBzJIx6aQUR.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 13690306.45, 0, 0, 2464255.16, 16154561.61, 1, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(177, 97, 720, 'EoI/DMFT/SURAJPUR/CSF/PMU/2026', 1, 'Selection of PMU Consultants for Preparation of Vision Document/ Project Plan for Sustainable Development of Mining-Affected Areas, Surajpur District', '12', '<p><strong>1. Background</strong><br><br>Surajpur intends to engage a Project Management Unit (PMU) comprising three domain experts to provide technical, strategic and implementation support for preparation of a Vision Document/Project Plan for sustainable development of operational, suspended and closed mining areas.<br><br><strong>2. Objectives</strong> <br><br>The primary objective of this assignment is to provide technical and implementation support to the District Administration, Surajpur, in preparation of a comprehensive Perspective Plan/Vision Document/Project Plan for the sustainable and inclusive development of operational, suspended, and abandoned mining-affected areas in District. <br><br>The specific objectives of the assignment are to: <br><br><strong>1. Prepare a Comprehensive Vision Document</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Conduct a detailed assessment of the existing socio-economic, environmental, and infrastructure conditions in the mining-affected areas.</li>\r\n<li>Develop a long-term Vision Document outlining sustainable development strategies, sector-wise priorities, and actionable recommendations aligned with the objectives and applicable Government policies.&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>2. Identify Priority Development Interventions</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Assess the development needs of mining-affected communities through field visits, stakeholder consultations, and data analysis.</li>\r\n<li>Identify and prioritize interventions across key sectors including environmental sustainability, social and community development, skill development and employment generation, livelihood promotion, education, healthcare, water resource management, agriculture, Sanitation, Animal husbandry, Infrastructure, Energy &amp; Watershed development, Drinking water supply, Irrigation, welfare of women &amp; child and welfare of aged &amp; disabled and irrigation</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>3. Develop an Implementation Roadmap and Monitoring Framework</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Prepare a phased implementation plan with clearly defined activities, timelines, responsibilities, estimated financial requirements, and measurable outcomes.</li>\r\n<li>Develop a robust monitoring and evaluation framework, including Key Performance Indicators (KPIs), reporting mechanisms, and review processes to ensure effective implementation and periodic assessment of project outcomes.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>4. Provide Technical and Implementation Support to the District Administration</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Asist the District Administration in project planning, formulation, and prioritization of development initiatives.</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate stakeholder consultations with Government departments, local bodies, mining agencies, community representatives, and other relevant stakeholders.</li>\r\n<li>Provide technical inputs during project appraisal, review meetings, and decision-making processes to support effective implementation of the proposed interventions.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>5. Promote Sustainable and Inclusive Development</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Recommend innovative, technology-enabled, and community-centric solutions for enhancing the socio-economic well-being of mining-affected populations.</li>\r\n<li>Ensure that the proposed interventions are environmentally sustainable, financially viable, and aligned with the long-term development goals of the district.</li>\r\n</ul>', 2, 720, '2026-07-15 16:05:37', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, '<ol>\r\n<li>Factsheet</li>\r\n<li>Project Objective&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Scope of Work</li>\r\n</ol>', '<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>CHiPS is inviting all Tier-I empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/ Empanelment/Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur Dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p>The selected consultancy firm shall provide technical, strategic, and implementation support to the District Administration, Surajpur for preparation of a comprehensive Vision Document/Project Plan for the sustainable development of operational, abandoned, and closed mining areas. The scope of work shall include, but not be limited to, the following:-<br><br><strong>1. Baseline Assessment </strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Conduct a comprehensive baseline assessment of mining-affected areas, including demographic, socio-economic, environmental, infrastructural, institutional, and resource mapping.</li>\r\n<li>Collect, compile, validate, and analyse primary and secondary data from relevant departments and stakeholders.</li>\r\n<li>Assess the current status of development interventions implemented and identify existing gaps and challenges.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>2. Field Assessment and Stakeholder Consultation</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Conduct field visits to operational, abandoned, and closed mining areas.</li>\r\n<li>Organize consultations with District Administration, line departments, Panchayati Raj Institutions, mining agencies, community representatives, Self Help Groups (SHGs), NGOs, and other stakeholders.</li>\r\n<li>Document stakeholder expectations, challenges, and recommendations for sustainable development.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>3. Preparation of Vision Document</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Develop a comprehensive Vision Document outlining the long-term development strategy for mining-affected areas.</li>\r\n<li>Define sector-wise development goals, priorities, implementation strategies, and expected outcomes.</li>\r\n<li>Ensure alignment with Guidelines, Sustainable Development Goals (SDGs), Government of India and Government of Chhattisgarh policies, and other applicable schemes.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>4. Project Planning and DPR Preparation</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Identify and prioritize development projects based on need assessment.</li>\r\n<li>Prepare sector-wise project proposals, Detailed Project Reports (DPRs), implementation strategies, cost estimates, and resource requirements.</li>\r\n<li>Recommend innovative and sustainable development models suitable for the district.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>5. Implementation Roadmap</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Develop a phased implementation roadmap with timelines, milestones, responsibilities, and financial requirements.</li>\r\n<li>Recommend institutional arrangements and governance mechanisms for effective execution.</li>\r\n<li>Identify convergence opportunities with Central and State Government schemes.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>6. Monitoring and Evaluation Framework</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Develop Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) for monitoring project implementation.</li>\r\n<li>Design monitoring, reporting, and evaluation mechanisms.</li>\r\n<li>Recommend digital tools and dashboards for project monitoring and performance tracking.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>7. Technical Support</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Provide technical support during review meetings, presentations, workshops, and consultations.</li>\r\n<li>Assist the District Administration in incorporating observations and finalizing the Vision Document.</li>\r\n<li>Provide implementation support during the initial phase of project execution, if required.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p><strong>4. Engagement Period&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n<p>The envisaged duration of the assignment is 12 calendar months (1 year). The duration may be extended further as per the project need.</p>\r\n<p><strong>5. Key Deliverables&nbsp;</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Inception Report</li>\r\n<li>Baseline Assessment Report</li>\r\n<li>Stakeholder Consultation Report</li>\r\n<li>Draft Vision Document</li>\r\n<li>Final Vision Document</li>\r\n<li>Implementation Roadmap</li>\r\n<li>Presentations and Review Notes</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>6. KPIs</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Timely submission of deliverables.</li>\r\n<li>Quality of reports.</li>\r\n<li>Stakeholder consultation coverage.</li>\r\n<li>Acceptance of Vision Document by District Administration.</li>\r\n<li>Support during implementation planning.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p><strong>Payment Terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on a monthly basis.</li>\r\n<li>Each payment will be made only after the delivery of the corresponding deliverable and its acceptance by CHiPS.</li>\r\n<li>Taxes will be applicable as per prevailing government norms.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Penalty Terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the terms and conditions mentioned in Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025, Raipur dated 20/02/2025.</li>\r\n</ul>', 7, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company regarding their understanding of the proposed scope of work and their experience, if any, in similar areas of expertise (Physical Mode / Video Conference)</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (Physical Mode / Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th>Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th>Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of the Project Framework</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such a specific kind of project</li>\r\n<li>Prior experience in project interaction with senior Government officials</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Good understanding of project management best practices framework</li>\r\n<li>Ability to Negotiate / Persuade / Influence</li>\r\n<li>Strong ability to understand, deliberate, and report / monitor the key SLAs</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\r\n<li class=\"p1\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The last date for submission of response is&nbsp;<strong>07/08/2026 17:00 Hrs.</strong>&nbsp;Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Pre-bid submissions, proposal submissions, presentation and interview details, and any query resolution shall be accepted only via the Empanelment Portal (<a class=\"decorated-link\" href=\"../../../\" target=\"_new\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"261\" data-end=\"288\">https://empl.cgstate.gov.in</a>). For any other enquiries, please contact via&nbsp;<a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"335\" data-end=\"356\">empl.chips@cgchips.in,</a>&nbsp;<a class=\"decorated-link cursor-pointer\" rel=\"noopener\" data-start=\"360\" data-end=\"382\">empl_portal@cgchips.in</a>.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul data-start=\"50\" data-end=\"195\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1y1a14t\" data-start=\"50\" data-end=\"78\">Signed copy of this EoI.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1drwwid\" data-start=\"79\" data-end=\"133\">Copy of the approach and methodology presentation.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1iowcl3\" data-start=\"134\" data-end=\"195\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Resumes of the resources who will appear for the interview.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2026-07-16 21:43:50', 4, 1, '2026-07-15 16:13:22', 720, '2026-07-16 21:43:50', NULL, '2026-07-17 17:44:40', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-07-17', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Expression of Interest for Selection of PMU Consultants for Preparation of Vision Document Project Plan for Sustainable Development of Mining-Affected Areas, Surajpur Distric', '2026-07-17', '2026-07-22 17:00:00', '2026-08-17 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Presentation & Interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-02-25', 1, 0, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/ijMG87FD550Y4SjpLboBvt56aWH2DM5CqwfIsgLq.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 1, 0, '2,3,4,5', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/gCwm7sCfO85TT1khpetVJmuLm9bVWKknptL6nmy6.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(179, 96, 90, 'EoI/EMPL/CHiPS/PMU/M-SOC/2026', 1, 'Setting up of Project Management Unit (PMU) for Managed Security Operations Center (M-SOC) Services in Chhattisgarh', '12', '<p dir=\"ltr\">The Government of Chhattisgarh, through Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHIPS), intends to establish a State-wide Managed Security Operations Centre (Managed SOC) to strengthen the cybersecurity posture of the State\'s digital infrastructure, including the State Data Centre (SDC), Disaster Recovery (DR) site, cloud-hosted applications, departmental IT systems, networks, endpoints, and citizen-centric digital services.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">To ensure transparent procurement, robust solution design, timely implementation, and effective governance of this strategic initiative, CHIPS proposes to engage a competent and experienced Project Management Unit (PMU).&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The PMU shall provide end-to-end consultancy and project management support encompassing bid process management, technical advisory, implementation oversight, vendor performance monitoring, SLA management, security governance, compliance with applicable Government of India guidelines (including CERT-In and MeitY), and successful operationalization of the Managed SOC in line with industry best practices and the cybersecurity objectives of the Government of Chhattisgarh.&nbsp;</p>', 2, 90, '2026-07-27 16:44:57', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, NULL, '<h1 dir=\"ltr\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">1. Background</span></h1>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The core objective of the Security Operations Center (SOC) for the State of Chhattisgarh is to focus on establishing a proactive cybersecurity posture that anticipates and mitigates threats before they materialize. This proactive approach is essential for enhancing incident response capabilities by reducing Mean Time to Detect (MTTD) and Mean Time to Respond (MTTR).&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">To achieve these objectives, CHiPS intends to procure Managed SOC services on an outcome-based model, wherein the Service Provider is responsible for design, operation, tooling, and continuous improvement of SOC capabilities, subject to governance, audit, and performance requirements defined in RFP.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Further, CG SOC will operate on a Managed SOC (Subscription-based) model while deploying a cybersecurity team within Chhattisgarh. CG SOC will implement automated processes and predefined incident response playbooks, fostering a culture of rapid response and recovery to minimize the impact of cyber incidents.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">In addition to proactive threat management, CG SOC will prioritize remediation efforts based on risk exposure. This initiative will be supported by the development of comprehensive risk management framework that aligns with national and international standards. Collaboration and information sharing will be integral to the SOC&rsquo;s mission, serving as a central hub for cooperation among various government departments. This collaborative approach will facilitate real-time information exchange and joint exercises, thereby enhancing collective cybersecurity capabilities.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Managed SOC major scope include:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM)&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Application Security Monitoring&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Database Activity Monitoring (DAM)&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Web Application Firewall Monitoring&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">API Security Monitoring&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">SIEM + SOAR&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Threat Intelligence Integration&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">CERT-In reporting support&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Compliance with MeitY, CERT-In directions, ISO 27001 and State Cyber Security Policy</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">For implementation of a Managed Security Operations Centre (Managed SOC) for the Government of Chhattisgarh, a 3-member Project Management Unit (PMU) will be engaged, the PMU will be responsible for:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">End-to-end bid process management (RFP preparation to contract award)&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Project implementation and governance&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Vendor performance monitoring&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">SLA management&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Coordination with departments and OEMs&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Compliance with CERT-In, MeitY, ISO 27001, and State Cyber Security Policy</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">&nbsp;2. Objective of the EoI</span></strong></p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The primary objective of this EOI is to empanel/select a competent and experienced Project Management Unit (PMU) to provide end-to-end consultancy and project management support to the Government of Chhattisgarh/CHIPS for the successful procurement, implementation, and operationalization of a Managed Security Operations Centre (Managed SOC).</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The specific objectives are:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Provide Strategic Advisory Services&nbsp;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Assist CHIPS in defining the vision, implementation strategy, governance framework, and roadmap for establishing a state-wide Managed SOC.&nbsp;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support Bid Process Management&nbsp;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Prepare and finalize the RFP, technical specifications, Bill of Quantities (BoQ), eligibility criteria, service level agreements (SLAs), evaluation methodology, and other procurement documents in accordance with applicable Government procurement guidelines.&nbsp;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ensure Transparent and Competitive Procurement&nbsp;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Facilitate the complete procurement lifecycle, including pre-bid meetings, clarification management, bid evaluation support, contract finalization, and award recommendations, ensuring transparency, fairness, and competitiveness.&nbsp;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Provide Technical Expertise&nbsp;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Validate the proposed Managed SOC architecture, technology stack, security controls, integration requirements, SIEM sizing, log onboarding strategy, and monitoring use cases based on industry best practices and Government cybersecurity requirements.&nbsp;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Support Project Implementation&nbsp;</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Assist CHIPS in planning, monitoring, coordinating, and supervising the implementation of the Managed SOC, ensuring timely delivery of project milestones and adherence to approved timelines.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"78\" data-end=\"127\">The PMU shall undertake the following activities:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"129\" data-end=\"427\">The selected PMU shall provide end-to-end consultancy, technical advisory, project management, procurement support, implementation monitoring, and governance support for establishment and operationalization of the Managed Security Operations Centre (Managed SOC) for the Government of Chhattisgarh.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"429\" data-end=\"508\">The detailed scope of work shall include, but not be limited to, the following:</p>\r\n<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"209\" data-end=\"233\"><strong data-start=\"209\" data-end=\"233\">3.1 Project Planning</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"235\" data-end=\"473\">Understand the existing cybersecurity ecosystem of the State, including State Data Centre (SDC), Disaster Recovery (DR), Cloud infrastructure, departmental data centres, network infrastructure, security devices, and critical applications.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"475\" data-end=\"567\">Conduct stakeholder consultations with CHIPS, user departments, and other relevant agencies.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"569\" data-end=\"723\">Prepare a Report detailing the project approach, implementation methodology, timelines, governance structure, deliverables, and risk management framework.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"725\" data-end=\"823\">Prepare a comprehensive implementation roadmap for establishment and operation of the Managed SOC.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"825\" data-end=\"855\"><strong data-start=\"825\" data-end=\"855\">3.2 Bid Process Management</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"857\" data-end=\"938\">The PMU shall provide complete support during the procurement process, including:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"940\" data-end=\"970\"><strong data-start=\"940\" data-end=\"970\">3.2.1 Procurement Strategy</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"972\" data-end=\"1033\">Develop the procurement strategy and implementation approach.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1035\" data-end=\"1125\">Recommend appropriate contracting methodology (e.g., EPC, Managed Services, Output-based).</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1127\" data-end=\"1171\">Define project scope and service boundaries.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1173\" data-end=\"1214\"><strong data-start=\"1173\" data-end=\"1214\">3.2.2 Preparation of Tender Documents</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1216\" data-end=\"1316\">Prepare RFP, technical specifications, BoQ, SLAs, KPIs, payment milestones, and contract conditions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1318\" data-end=\"1325\">Define:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1327\" data-end=\"1591\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1rjbw5h\" data-start=\"1327\" data-end=\"1359\">Technical Eligibility Criteria</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"sxcum7\" data-start=\"1360\" data-end=\"1392\">Financial Eligibility Criteria</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"vr0183\" data-start=\"1393\" data-end=\"1417\">Evaluation Methodology</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jqp40o\" data-start=\"1418\" data-end=\"1470\">Bid Security and Performance Security requirements</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1rpyg8q\" data-start=\"1471\" data-end=\"1504\">Service Level Agreements (SLAs)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1qflqnl\" data-start=\"1505\" data-end=\"1539\">Penalty and incentive mechanisms</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1dcc10o\" data-start=\"1540\" data-end=\"1562\">Exit Management Plan</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1n4umf\" data-start=\"1563\" data-end=\"1591\">Transition Management Plan</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1593\" data-end=\"1617\"><strong data-start=\"1593\" data-end=\"1617\">3.2.3 Bid Management</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"1619\" data-end=\"1661\">Publish and manage bid-related activities.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1663\" data-end=\"1699\">Prepare responses to bidder queries.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1701\" data-end=\"1727\">Organize pre-bid meetings.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1729\" data-end=\"1758\">Issue corrigenda and addenda.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1760\" data-end=\"1792\">Assist CHIPS during bid opening.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1794\" data-end=\"1818\"><strong data-start=\"1794\" data-end=\"1818\">3.2.4 Bid Evaluation</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"1820\" data-end=\"1849\">Develop evaluation templates.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1851\" data-end=\"1880\">Support technical evaluation.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1882\" data-end=\"1930\">Review compliance with technical specifications.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1932\" data-end=\"2016\">Support Proof of Concept (PoC), presentations, and demonstrations, where applicable.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2018\" data-end=\"2087\">Assist in financial evaluation and preparation of evaluation reports.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2089\" data-end=\"2145\">Support contract negotiations and award recommendations.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2147\" data-end=\"2182\"><strong data-start=\"2147\" data-end=\"2182\">3.3 Technical Advisory Services</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2184\" data-end=\"2235\">The PMU shall provide expert technical guidance on:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2237\" data-end=\"2271\"><strong data-start=\"2237\" data-end=\"2271\">3.3.1 Managed SOC Architecture</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2273\" data-end=\"2499\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"7m8pcr\" data-start=\"2273\" data-end=\"2302\">SOC architecture and design</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"tz5tq0\" data-start=\"2303\" data-end=\"2342\">SIEM sizing (Events Per Second - EPS)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11y1582\" data-start=\"2343\" data-end=\"2362\">SOAR architecture</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"d716aq\" data-start=\"2363\" data-end=\"2405\">Threat Intelligence Platform integration</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jbzjd1\" data-start=\"2406\" data-end=\"2430\">Security orchestration</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"13ipio3\" data-start=\"2431\" data-end=\"2455\">Log retention strategy</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1tve4w9\" data-start=\"2456\" data-end=\"2499\">Disaster Recovery and Business Continuity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2501\" data-end=\"2532\"><strong data-start=\"2501\" data-end=\"2532\">3.3.2 Technology Validation</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2534\" data-end=\"2595\">Review and validate the proposed technology stack, including:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2597\" data-end=\"2927\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1j4cn22\" data-start=\"2597\" data-end=\"2603\">SIEM</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1j4crvr\" data-start=\"2604\" data-end=\"2610\">SOAR</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"sc8zcq\" data-start=\"2611\" data-end=\"2620\">XDR/EDR</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1o4cq8\" data-start=\"2621\" data-end=\"2626\">NDR</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"gfz6v0\" data-start=\"2627\" data-end=\"2657\">Threat Intelligence Platform</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1arwir3\" data-start=\"2658\" data-end=\"2684\">Vulnerability Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"pjyecd\" data-start=\"2685\" data-end=\"2717\">Web Application Firewall (WAF)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zgo1c5\" data-start=\"2718\" data-end=\"2754\">Database Activity Monitoring (DAM)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"a1vmxl\" data-start=\"2755\" data-end=\"2791\">Privileged Access Management (PAM)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1in70ob\" data-start=\"2792\" data-end=\"2828\">Identity &amp; Access Management (IAM)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"2e8fii\" data-start=\"2829\" data-end=\"2871\">Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hix7lp\" data-start=\"2872\" data-end=\"2891\">Endpoint Security</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"741tma\" data-start=\"2892\" data-end=\"2908\">Email Security</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4lsko0\" data-start=\"2909\" data-end=\"2927\">Network Security</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2929\" data-end=\"2957\"><strong data-start=\"2929\" data-end=\"2957\">3.3.3 Security Use Cases</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2959\" data-end=\"3014\">Review and recommend security monitoring use cases for:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3016\" data-end=\"3251\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1sfcvwk\" data-start=\"3016\" data-end=\"3035\">State Data Centre</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"dkwybz\" data-start=\"3036\" data-end=\"3060\">Disaster Recovery Site</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1i9cx24\" data-start=\"3061\" data-end=\"3088\">Cloud-hosted applications</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"89w5qg\" data-start=\"3089\" data-end=\"3116\">Departmental applications</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15bmvfs\" data-start=\"3117\" data-end=\"3130\">API Gateway</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1w57mf2\" data-start=\"3131\" data-end=\"3142\">Databases</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17nhjod\" data-start=\"3143\" data-end=\"3160\">Network devices</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cirl79\" data-start=\"3161\" data-end=\"3172\">Firewalls</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1o4wkg\" data-start=\"3173\" data-end=\"3178\">VPN</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12m8zvz\" data-start=\"3179\" data-end=\"3195\">Email gateways</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"del5vx\" data-start=\"3196\" data-end=\"3214\">Active Directory</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1bwdg9k\" data-start=\"3215\" data-end=\"3226\">Endpoints</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"601tsw\" data-start=\"3227\" data-end=\"3251\">Citizen-facing portals</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3253\" data-end=\"3283\"><strong data-start=\"3253\" data-end=\"3283\">3.4 Implementation Support</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3285\" data-end=\"3359\">The PMU shall monitor and facilitate implementation activities, including:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3361\" data-end=\"3806\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"srosz2\" data-start=\"3361\" data-end=\"3391\">Review implementation plans.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"s8zxz0\" data-start=\"3392\" data-end=\"3434\">Validate detailed solution architecture.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15s5d9l\" data-start=\"3435\" data-end=\"3463\">Monitor project schedules.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"3wtnqr\" data-start=\"3464\" data-end=\"3499\">Review implementation milestones.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zwcdnw\" data-start=\"3500\" data-end=\"3545\">Facilitate coordination among stakeholders.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1rjfms2\" data-start=\"3546\" data-end=\"3582\">Monitor onboarding of log sources.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6vim3g\" data-start=\"3583\" data-end=\"3658\">Validate integration of all identified security devices and applications.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12y8zsi\" data-start=\"3659\" data-end=\"3708\">Review configuration of SIEM correlation rules.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"e0inbu\" data-start=\"3709\" data-end=\"3745\">Monitor testing and commissioning.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l0p7z3\" data-start=\"3746\" data-end=\"3776\">Validate acceptance testing.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6rf9nq\" data-start=\"3777\" data-end=\"3806\">Recommend Go-Live approval.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3808\" data-end=\"3834\"><strong data-start=\"3808\" data-end=\"3834\">3.5 Project Governance</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3836\" data-end=\"3892\">The PMU shall establish a governance framework covering:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3894\" data-end=\"4096\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1w6erb6\" data-start=\"3894\" data-end=\"3930\">Project Steering Committee support</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"rdfhmn\" data-start=\"3931\" data-end=\"3967\">Weekly and Monthly Review Meetings</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1vk5fqw\" data-start=\"3968\" data-end=\"3985\">Risk Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zp9k9u\" data-start=\"3986\" data-end=\"4004\">Issue Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"nvbezw\" data-start=\"4005\" data-end=\"4032\">Change Request Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6dus1j\" data-start=\"4033\" data-end=\"4052\">Decision Tracking</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9kh0zi\" data-start=\"4053\" data-end=\"4076\">Escalation Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"10rdtii\" data-start=\"4077\" data-end=\"4096\">Quality Assurance</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4098\" data-end=\"4120\">The PMU shall prepare:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4122\" data-end=\"4286\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"jpej29\" data-start=\"4122\" data-end=\"4147\">Weekly Progress Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17ieril\" data-start=\"4148\" data-end=\"4174\">Monthly Progress Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cciiez\" data-start=\"4175\" data-end=\"4201\">Steering Committee Notes</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"10fmsrj\" data-start=\"4202\" data-end=\"4224\">Executive Dashboards</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15pbqsi\" data-start=\"4225\" data-end=\"4240\">Risk Register</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ymim48\" data-start=\"4241\" data-end=\"4257\">Issue Register</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17ufy8o\" data-start=\"4258\" data-end=\"4286\">Action Taken Reports (ATR)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4288\" data-end=\"4333\"><strong data-start=\"4288\" data-end=\"4333\">3.6 SLA and Vendor Performance Monitoring</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4335\" data-end=\"4357\">The PMU shall monitor:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4359\" data-end=\"4619\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"blrg23\" data-start=\"4359\" data-end=\"4375\">SLA compliance</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1h5eyi0\" data-start=\"4376\" data-end=\"4400\">Incident Response Time</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"yu8qyb\" data-start=\"4401\" data-end=\"4418\">Resolution Time</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"rzv5g9\" data-start=\"4419\" data-end=\"4433\">Availability</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"80023\" data-start=\"4434\" data-end=\"4453\">Device onboarding</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1romid8\" data-start=\"4454\" data-end=\"4475\">False Positive Rate</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"njnmry\" data-start=\"4476\" data-end=\"4504\">Mean Time to Detect (MTTD)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"vf1ydq\" data-start=\"4505\" data-end=\"4534\">Mean Time to Respond (MTTR)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"fu5pdm\" data-start=\"4535\" data-end=\"4562\">Threat Hunting activities</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"jjxazf\" data-start=\"4563\" data-end=\"4600\">Vulnerability remediation timelines</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1mhu0pn\" data-start=\"4601\" data-end=\"4619\">Patch compliance</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4621\" data-end=\"4699\">The PMU shall recommend penalties and service credits in case of SLA breaches.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4701\" data-end=\"4746\"><strong data-start=\"4701\" data-end=\"4746\">3.7 Security Compliance and Audit Support</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4748\" data-end=\"4785\">The PMU shall ensure compliance with:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4787\" data-end=\"5080\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6ax1o4\" data-start=\"4787\" data-end=\"4807\">CERT-In Directions</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1xx7diy\" data-start=\"4808\" data-end=\"4841\">MeitY Cyber Security Guidelines</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"pxzgpb\" data-start=\"4842\" data-end=\"4874\">National Cyber Security Policy</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"oy9tqh\" data-start=\"4875\" data-end=\"4890\">ISO/IEC 27001</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"gmjszz\" data-start=\"4891\" data-end=\"4921\">ISO 27701 (where applicable)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9cjism\" data-start=\"4922\" data-end=\"4951\">State Cyber Security Policy</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"hku4dc\" data-start=\"4952\" data-end=\"5022\">Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act, 2023 (where applicable)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1djvd21\" data-start=\"5023\" data-end=\"5080\">Cloud Security Guidelines issued by Government of India</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5082\" data-end=\"5104\">The PMU shall support:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5106\" data-end=\"5205\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1rp35ev\" data-start=\"5106\" data-end=\"5132\">Internal Security Audits</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"xmiac6\" data-start=\"5133\" data-end=\"5153\">Third-party Audits</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"113f02m\" data-start=\"5154\" data-end=\"5182\">CERT-In Audit observations</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"qq66xn\" data-start=\"5183\" data-end=\"5205\">Compliance reporting</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5207\" data-end=\"5248\"><strong data-start=\"5207\" data-end=\"5248\">3.8 Cloud Security Monitoring Support</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5250\" data-end=\"5310\">The PMU shall ensure that the Managed SOC adequately covers:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5312\" data-end=\"5615\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"w9a0ji\" data-start=\"5312\" data-end=\"5356\">State Government cloud-hosted applications</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"tt2l8z\" data-start=\"5357\" data-end=\"5387\">Private cloud infrastructure</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4f9bdp\" data-start=\"5388\" data-end=\"5399\">NIC Cloud</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"10krw2b\" data-start=\"5400\" data-end=\"5427\">Hybrid cloud environments</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"7325jw\" data-start=\"5428\" data-end=\"5452\">APIs and microservices</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1cdz1zt\" data-start=\"5453\" data-end=\"5490\">Containers and Kubernetes platforms</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"tz4wbj\" data-start=\"5491\" data-end=\"5509\">Virtual Machines</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"sa8m2j\" data-start=\"5510\" data-end=\"5533\">Cloud-native services</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ftj8r4\" data-start=\"5534\" data-end=\"5553\">Identity services</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"s98lj7\" data-start=\"5554\" data-end=\"5572\">Cloud audit logs</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"2e8fii\" data-start=\"5573\" data-end=\"5615\">Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5617\" data-end=\"5665\"><strong data-start=\"5617\" data-end=\"5665\">3.9 Capacity Building and Knowledge Transfer</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5667\" data-end=\"5681\">The PMU shall:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5683\" data-end=\"5954\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"eu9dm4\" data-start=\"5683\" data-end=\"5732\">Conduct awareness sessions for CHIPS officials.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1brff9y\" data-start=\"5733\" data-end=\"5787\">Train departmental nodal officers on SOC governance.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1kgy1tt\" data-start=\"5788\" data-end=\"5835\">Develop Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs).</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"151n93g\" data-start=\"5836\" data-end=\"5874\">Prepare incident response playbooks.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"78fw0m\" data-start=\"5875\" data-end=\"5905\">Prepare operational manuals.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"gce0e8\" data-start=\"5906\" data-end=\"5954\">Support transition to BAU (Business as Usual).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5956\" data-end=\"5992\"><strong data-start=\"5956\" data-end=\"5992\">3.10 Reporting and Documentation</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5994\" data-end=\"6029\">The PMU shall prepare and maintain:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\r\n<ul data-start=\"6031\" data-end=\"6343\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"bkdyff\" data-start=\"6031\" data-end=\"6049\">Inception Report</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"iol0ot\" data-start=\"6050\" data-end=\"6075\">Project Management Plan</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cxhoej\" data-start=\"6076\" data-end=\"6098\">Risk Management Plan</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1030aju\" data-start=\"6099\" data-end=\"6122\">Procurement Documents</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"a9f42r\" data-start=\"6123\" data-end=\"6143\">Evaluation Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17ieril\" data-start=\"6144\" data-end=\"6170\">Monthly Progress Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"10fmsrj\" data-start=\"6171\" data-end=\"6193\">Executive Dashboards</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1pxmqmz\" data-start=\"6194\" data-end=\"6214\">Governance Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1i9grvr\" data-start=\"6215\" data-end=\"6239\">SLA Monitoring Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hvvf0q\" data-start=\"6240\" data-end=\"6264\">Incident Trend Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"14hmr21\" data-start=\"6265\" data-end=\"6291\">Security Posture Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"g3k6g5\" data-start=\"6292\" data-end=\"6318\">Go-Live Readiness Report</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"begc5e\" data-start=\"6319\" data-end=\"6343\">Project Closure Report</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', '<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"39\" data-end=\"61\"><strong data-start=\"39\" data-end=\"61\">1. Team Deployment</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"63\" data-end=\"364\">The Successful Agency shall deploy a team of consultants on a full-time/Intermittent/part-time/remote-working basis at office of Client. Collectively, the team shall demonstrate adequate experience in the field of implementation of government programs to ensure quality service delivery to the client.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"366\" data-end=\"429\"><strong data-start=\"366\" data-end=\"429\">2. Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"431\" data-end=\"743\">Initial Contract Period for the project shall be 12 months which is extendable for next 12 Months on mutual consent. However, based on the performance of the consultant and approval form the competent authority, the contract duration may be extended further for 12 months or beyond based on the mutual agreement.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"775\"><strong data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"775\">3. Human Resource Policies</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1yogdgn\" data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"801\">3.1 Employment Terms</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"803\" data-end=\"1180\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hxzp9v\" data-start=\"803\" data-end=\"931\">All resources will be engaged on a full-time/part-time/remote basis (as per the need and approval of the competent authority).</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1p9ssd9\" data-start=\"932\" data-end=\"1180\"><strong data-start=\"934\" data-end=\"964\">Mobilization/ Replacement:</strong> RFP No. -165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025 Dated 20 Feb 2025. Issued by Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society for &ldquo;Empanelment of Consultancy Firms for a period of 3 years&rdquo; and amendments thereof.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"us5gs\" data-start=\"1182\" data-end=\"1206\">3.2 Team Composition</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1208\" data-end=\"1539\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1vnc9qf\" data-start=\"1208\" data-end=\"1278\">The PMU team will include resources as mentioned in the table above.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"r74kls\" data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1539\">The Department may seek for additional resources/ Subject Matter Experts during the project implementation as per its requirement. Consultant shall be given sufficient time (minimum 60 days) for deployment of the additional resources/ Subject Matter Experts.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1541\" data-end=\"1575\"><strong data-start=\"1541\" data-end=\"1575\">4. Leave and Other HR Policies</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"18f6cly\" data-start=\"1577\" data-end=\"1597\">4.1 Leave Policy</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1599\" data-end=\"2414\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cw84ku\" data-start=\"1599\" data-end=\"1736\">Each position shall be eligible for the entitlement of 2 leave in a month which can be carry forward for the next month if not availed.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9qb3s8\" data-start=\"1737\" data-end=\"1908\">Each position can avail maximum of 3 leaves in a month (if cumulated/carried forward) without deductions, subsequently amount would be deducted as per the approved rate.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12bcd5c\" data-start=\"1909\" data-end=\"1999\">Unused leave can be carried forward to the next year/ till the end of contract duration.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4a82xc\" data-start=\"2000\" data-end=\"2102\">The proposed team must follow the working hours, working days and Holidays of State of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11t5u05\" data-start=\"2103\" data-end=\"2310\">In case of Travel/ Boarding/ Lodging/ Communication and printing and stationery for any official travel for Authority related work or to cover the work as per scope of work would be borne by the Authority.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1lyokhv\" data-start=\"2311\" data-end=\"2414\">The PMU team will follow the work schedule and timing of client as per the norms of Government of CG.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1up6e70\" data-start=\"2416\" data-end=\"2437\">4.2 Working Hours</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2439\" data-end=\"2717\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"xmltiq\" data-start=\"2439\" data-end=\"2580\">Consultants are expected to work as per calendar and office hours of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh and complete the given task on time.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1vmhbb6\" data-start=\"2581\" data-end=\"2717\">Flexibility in working hours may be allowed based on the project requirements and approval from the CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"vhvewx\" data-start=\"2719\" data-end=\"2749\">4.3 Performance Evaluation</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2751\" data-end=\"3078\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4b9cgf\" data-start=\"2751\" data-end=\"2899\">Regular performance evaluations will be conducted to ensure consultants meet their targets and contribute effectively to the mission\'s objectives.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"wt2lra\" data-start=\"2900\" data-end=\"2993\">Evaluations will be based on predefined key performance indicators (KPIs) and deliverables.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ghrrd1\" data-start=\"2994\" data-end=\"3078\">Continuous performance below expectations may lead to termination of the contract.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3080\" data-end=\"3122\"><strong data-start=\"3080\" data-end=\"3122\">5. Data Management and Confidentiality</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"pvrkun\" data-start=\"3124\" data-end=\"3147\">5.1 Data Management</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3149\" data-end=\"3392\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"f767sz\" data-start=\"3149\" data-end=\"3250\">Consultants are responsible for maintaining accurate and up-to-date records related to their tasks.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12k64xy\" data-start=\"3251\" data-end=\"3392\">All data must be stored securely and managed in compliance with the data protection policies outlined by CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"q8v6u1\" data-start=\"3394\" data-end=\"3417\">5.2 Confidentiality</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3419\" data-end=\"3715\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"iyhvmg\" data-start=\"3419\" data-end=\"3544\">Consultant must maintain the confidentiality of all sensitive information related to the CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"nrzosc\" data-start=\"3545\" data-end=\"3715\">Disclosure of any confidential information to unauthorized persons is strictly prohibited and will result in disciplinary action, including termination of the contract.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1l8qwid\" data-start=\"3717\" data-end=\"3746\">5.3 Intellectual Property</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3748\" data-end=\"3989\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1fss1at\" data-start=\"3748\" data-end=\"3867\">Any intellectual property created during the course of employment will be owned by CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1awxvpf\" data-start=\"3868\" data-end=\"3989\">Consultants must agree to transfer all intellectual property rights to CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh upon creation.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3991\" data-end=\"4020\"><strong data-start=\"3991\" data-end=\"4020\">6. Operational Guidelines</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1q25ol4\" data-start=\"4022\" data-end=\"4057\">6.1 Reporting and Documentation</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4059\" data-end=\"4351\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17fet12\" data-start=\"4059\" data-end=\"4198\">Consultants are required to submit regular progress reports, including monthly, quarterly, and annual reports, as specified in their ToR.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"s63p6x\" data-start=\"4199\" data-end=\"4351\">All reports must be submitted to the CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh and relevant Dept. of E&amp;IT, Government of Chhattisgarh for review and approval.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"t6yanu\" data-start=\"4353\" data-end=\"4382\">6.2 Compliance and Ethics</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4384\" data-end=\"4651\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1fzmj1t\" data-start=\"4384\" data-end=\"4512\">Consultants must adhere to the ethical guidelines and professional standards established by CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l3rhbk\" data-start=\"4513\" data-end=\"4651\">Any form of misconduct, including fraud, corruption, or harassment, will be dealt with severely and may result in immediate termination.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"u45o84\" data-start=\"4653\" data-end=\"4691\">6.3 Capacity Building and Training</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4693\" data-end=\"4950\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"93bcgt\" data-start=\"4693\" data-end=\"4833\">Consultants are expected to participate in ongoing capacity-building programs and training sessions to enhance their skills and knowledge.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1mfh3x3\" data-start=\"4834\" data-end=\"4950\">CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh will provide necessary resources and opportunities for professional development.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1dgylj8\" data-start=\"4952\" data-end=\"4990\">6.4 Coordination with Stakeholders</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4992\" data-end=\"5264\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1nthaq1\" data-start=\"4992\" data-end=\"5147\">Consultants must coordinate effectively with stakeholders to ensure seamless implementation of schemes and programs of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1bbdsi8\" data-start=\"5148\" data-end=\"5264\">Regular meetings and consultations with stakeholders are mandatory to discuss progress, challenges, and solutions.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5266\" data-end=\"5306\"><strong data-start=\"5266\" data-end=\"5306\">7. Travel and Reimbursement Policies</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"x98ipi\" data-start=\"5308\" data-end=\"5322\">7.1 Travel</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5324\" data-end=\"5595\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"j2jy7a\" data-start=\"5324\" data-end=\"5450\">Consultants shall be required to travel within the state and to other locations as necessary for project-related activities.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1nn26ht\" data-start=\"5451\" data-end=\"5595\">Travel arrangements and itineraries must be approved in advance by the Project Manager or representative of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"pmaha7\" data-start=\"5597\" data-end=\"5618\">7.2 Reimbursement</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5620\" data-end=\"6418\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15u8tlu\" data-start=\"5620\" data-end=\"5814\">The inter-city/state conveyance charges for any official travel for Authority related work or to cover the work as per scope of RFP would be borne by the Authority subjected to prior approval.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1q8mt64\" data-start=\"5815\" data-end=\"6137\">The entitlement for reimbursement of visits would be as per the provisions of the RFP Issued by CHiPS, for RFP No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025 Dated 20 Feb 2025 issued by Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society for &ldquo;Empanelment of Consultancy Firms for a period of 3 years&rdquo; and amendments thereof.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"3ofl17\" data-start=\"6138\" data-end=\"6307\">Consultants will be reimbursed for any other travel and other expenses incurred during the course of their duties as per policies of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"5f4wz9\" data-start=\"6308\" data-end=\"6418\">All reimbursement claims must be supported by valid receipts and submitted within the stipulated time frame.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"6420\" data-end=\"6454\"><strong data-start=\"6420\" data-end=\"6454\">8. Additional Responsibilities</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"6456\" data-end=\"6679\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"bmf1ve\" data-start=\"6456\" data-end=\"6573\">Consultants may be assigned additional responsibilities related to day-to-day operations as required by the client.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"x62hbz\" data-start=\"6574\" data-end=\"6679\">Flexibility and adaptability in handling diverse tasks and projects are essential for all team members.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"6681\" data-end=\"6871\">By adhering to these terms and conditions, the PMU will ensure a high standard of professionalism, efficiency, and accountability in achieving the goals of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6873\" data-end=\"7380\">The client is expected to provide the consultants with available data, information, maps or drawings relevant to the task at no cost to the consultant as per availability. The DPRs/Reports/Documents will be shared with the consultant for their review. In case any additional information is needed, the client will arrange for access to all relevant information and to key officials in the local government and agencies concerned with subjects related to the project. No survey is required by the consultant.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7382\" data-end=\"7473\">The client will also help consultants in obtaining permission/data from other stakeholders.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7475\" data-end=\"7938\">The consultants shall verify the correctness of the data/information provided by the client and satisfy them about the accuracy of data/information/material before these are used. Data/information/material provided to the consultants shall remain the property of the originating agency and shall be provided solely for the purpose of the work to be done under this contract. All such borrowed material shall be returned to the client upon completion of the study.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7940\" data-end=\"8201\">Client shall provide sitting space, office furniture and wifi access to the consultants, however, arranging the IT assets like the Laptop/computer and auxiliary hardware and software required for performing the services shall be arranged by the consulting firm.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8203\" data-end=\"8227\"><strong data-start=\"8203\" data-end=\"8227\">9. Change Management</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"8229\" data-end=\"8853\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1n9sz1q\" data-start=\"8229\" data-end=\"8376\">The selected consulting firm shall preferably give 2 weeks of advance notice to client for any change in deployed resource during the assignment.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1aqze4q\" data-start=\"8377\" data-end=\"8519\">The selected consulting firm needs to ensure that the knowledge transfer and handover during change of any resource for a smooth transition.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ulup6\" data-start=\"8520\" data-end=\"8587\">The replacement of any resource should be approved by the client.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"qapg81\" data-start=\"8588\" data-end=\"8853\" data-is-last-node=\"\">The change of resource should be in accordance to RFP No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025 Dated 20 Feb 2025 issued by Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society for &ldquo;Empanelment of Consultancy Firms for a period of 3 years&rdquo; and amendments thereof.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Note:</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">The CVs of all Key Experts needs to be submitted.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">CV of candidates submitted against respective positions must fulfil all the qualification requirements.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Apart from the above-mentioned personnel, Client may ask, at any time during execution of the Contract, for any additional personnel that it deems necessary for carrying the scope of work under this Contract. Upon such request by the Client, the Consultant shall submit to the Client for review and approval a copy of the Curriculum Vitae (CVs) of the proposed Expert. The remuneration payable towards the services of additional personnel shall be payable on the basis of the man month rate approved as per RFP No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025 Dated 20 Feb 2025 issued by Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society for &ldquo;Empanelment of Consultancy Firms for a period of 3 years&rdquo; and amendments thereof. The payment shall be on actual number of man days spent under this Consultancy Agreement.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">The Consultant proposed team shall be deployed within 90 days of the issuance of the Letter of Award/ Work Order.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>', '<h1 dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Payment terms</span></h1>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"2\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or CHiPS, as the case may be selected bidder shall be paid the requisite man month payment in the event that selected bidder has performed on its obligations in compliance with the terms of this contract.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h1 dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\">Penalty terms</span></h1>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', 6, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their experience, if any, in a similar area of expertise (via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th>Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th>Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Understanding of the Project Framework</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Quality of proposed methodology for such specific kind of a project</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Prior experience of Consultancy/ Advisory with Central or State government in for AI-led governance and innovation, Startup ecosystem development as per TOR.</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Prior experience in undertaking large digital transformation projects at Central or State level.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Educational Qualification</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Good understanding of scope of work</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Strong ability to understand and deliberate and report</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Experience of Working in Government in similar kind of Projects&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<strong id=\"docs-internal-guid-2357740c-7fff-6a16-5989-4033e028306c\"></strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.<br><br></li>\r\n<li>The last date for submission of response is <strong>17/08/2026 17:00 Hrs.</strong> Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.<br><br></li>\r\n<li>All pre-bid queries and proposal submissions shall be submitted through the Empanelment Portal (https://empl.cgstate.gov.in) only. Submissions through e-mail, portal messages, or any other mode shall not be accepted. Only submissions made through the respective provisions of the Empanelment Portal shall be considered. For any other enquiries, please contact empl.chips@cgchips.in and empl_portal@cgchips.in.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EoI</li>\r\n<li>Presentation showing strategy and action plan for conducting Impact Assessment</li>\r\n<li>Resumes of the resources who will appear for the interview&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '919336', NULL, 4, 1, '2026-07-27 17:03:04', 0, NULL, NULL, '2026-07-28 14:21:21', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-07-28', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Expression of Interest (EoI) Setting up of Project Management Unit (PMU) for Managed Security Operations Center (M-SOC) Services in Chhattisgarh).', '2026-07-27', '2026-08-03 17:00:00', '2026-08-17 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Presentation and interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-03-09', 1, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/QRvh0Z1lLFwfmyuGMCa4pihQit8XdsFpksFzEozC.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 1, 0, '1,2,3,4,5', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/JboXTqEtNTJujpz0ZAUYADh8025ra17IGQUCZb5D.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 12125188.31, 0, 0, 2182533.9, 14307722.2, 1, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(180, 18, 94, 'EoI/CHiPS/PMU/2ndCall AVIATION2/2026', 1, '2nd Call for Program Management Unit (PMU) for Technical Support and Transaction Advisory Support for Directorate of Aviation, Government of Chhattisgarh', '24', '<h1 class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-section-id=\"1cno33t\" data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"17\">1. Introduction</h1>\r\n<p data-start=\"19\" data-end=\"378\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS), the nodal agency of the Department of Electronics &amp; Information Technology, Government of Chhattisgarh, invites Expression of Interest (EoI) from empanelled consulting firms for setting up an onsite Transaction Advisory Project Management Unit (PMU) for the Directorate of Aviation, Government of Chhattisgarh.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"380\" data-end=\"876\">The Directorate of Aviation is responsible for overseeing and promoting civil aviation activities within the State, including airport and airstrip development, regulatory compliance, sectoral growth, and aviation skill development. With the expansion of regional air connectivity and the growth of aviation-related services and infrastructure in the State, the Directorate requires a dedicated multi-disciplinary team to provide end-to-end transaction advisory and bid process management support.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"878\" data-end=\"1218\">The selected firm shall deploy a Transaction Advisory PMU on a full-time, onsite basis for following broad scope. The team shall support in structuring, procuring, and managing the appointment of service providers across the aviation value chain, and in developing policy, schemes, and skill development frameworks for the sector and other.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1220\" data-end=\"2372\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zx5vbd\" data-start=\"1220\" data-end=\"1613\">The Directorate of Aviation is required to procure a range of specialised aviation services and infrastructure, including ground handling agencies, helicopter services, safety and security equipment, and the development of airstrips. Each of these procurements requires structured bid process management, technical and financial structuring, and compliance with applicable procurement rules.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"znlkmr\" data-start=\"1614\" data-end=\"1856\">Procurement of aviation services and infrastructure involves multi-stage transactions, contract structuring, and risk allocation that demand dedicated transaction advisory expertise not available within the Directorate on a full-time basis.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15hqlcq\" data-start=\"1857\" data-end=\"2128\">The State requires the development of an enabling aviation policy, sector schemes, and structured training modules to promote aviation-related skill development and employment among local youth, including pilot training, cabin crew training, and allied aviation trades.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1w6qcq1\" data-start=\"2129\" data-end=\"2372\">There is a need to augment the institutional capacity of the Directorate through a dedicated PMU that can provide specialized, full-time transaction advisory, bid process management, and project management support across the aviation sector.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h1 data-section-id=\"3h2xtw\" data-start=\"2374\" data-end=\"2386\">2. Purpose</h1>\r\n<p data-start=\"2388\" data-end=\"2545\">The key objective of engaging the Transaction Advisory PMU is to strengthen the institutional capacity of the Directorate of Aviation in the following areas:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2547\" data-end=\"3134\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1wvrfgv\" data-start=\"2547\" data-end=\"2676\">End-to-end bid process management and transaction advisory for procurement of aviation services, infrastructure, and equipment.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1a7to55\" data-start=\"2677\" data-end=\"2839\">Development of aviation policy, sector schemes, and facilitate in preparing training modules for skill development of local youth in aviation and allied trades.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17yfmra\" data-start=\"2840\" data-end=\"2978\">Strengthening project management, monitoring, and reporting of aviation infrastructure and service delivery projects of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"368k2v\" data-start=\"2979\" data-end=\"3134\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Coordination with national-level aviation institutions, regulatory authorities, and industry stakeholders for capacity building and sectoral development.</li>\r\n</ul>', 2, 94, '2026-07-28 11:38:24', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, NULL, '<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>The objective of the assignment is to provide assistance to Directorate of Aviation for Program Management Unit (PMU) for Technical Support and Transaction Advisory Support. <br><br>CHiPS is inviting all empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/ Empanelment/Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur Dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"92\"><strong data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"92\">The deployed team shall carry out the following tasks during the term of the engagement:</strong></p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"41ekof\" data-start=\"94\" data-end=\"147\">1. Transaction Advisory and Bid Process Management</h2>\r\n<ol data-start=\"149\" data-end=\"2434\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"yizp3c\" data-start=\"149\" data-end=\"392\">Provide end-to-end transaction advisory and bid process management support for procurement of goods, services, and works across the aviation sector, covering the full bid cycle from need assessment to contract award and contract management.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"q81y5h\" data-start=\"394\" data-end=\"526\">Techno-commercial assessment for proposed aviation procurements and advise on appropriate procurement and contracting strategies.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"k9mmkj\" data-start=\"528\" data-end=\"806\">Prepare, review, and finalise procurement documents including Expressions of Interest (EoIs), Requests for Proposal (RFPs), Requests for Qualification (RFQs), bid documents, draft contracts, concession agreements, Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs), and related documentation.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"hqa1v\" data-start=\"808\" data-end=\"1058\">Design qualification criteria, evaluation frameworks, and bid evaluation methodologies in alignment with the General Financial Rules (GFR) 2017, Central Vigilance Commission (CVC) guidelines, and applicable State of Chhattisgarh procurement rules.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1481o2t\" data-start=\"1060\" data-end=\"1287\">Manage the complete bid process, including pre-bid meetings, issuance of clarifications and corrigendum, bid opening, evaluation support, and preparation of evaluation reports and recommendations for the competent authority.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"8fohhg\" data-start=\"1289\" data-end=\"1993\">Provide transaction advisory and bid process management support for empanelment of, and tendering for, the following primary aviation services and infrastructure but not limited to:\r\n<ul data-start=\"1478\" data-end=\"1993\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"way9xt\" data-start=\"1478\" data-end=\"1545\">Ground handling agencies for airports and airstrips in the State.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1pwyuwg\" data-start=\"1549\" data-end=\"1658\">Helicopter services, including charter, regional connectivity, and emergency / medical evacuation services.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"csdv3q\" data-start=\"1662\" data-end=\"1792\">Agencies for capacity building and training of aviation sector personnel and for institutional strengthening of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1qrjhro\" data-start=\"1796\" data-end=\"1880\">Suppliers of safety, security, and firefighting equipment for aviation facilities.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1g4fu8i\" data-start=\"1884\" data-end=\"1993\">Agencies for the development, upgradation, and maintenance of airstrips and allied aviation infrastructure.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"pqxu29\" data-start=\"1995\" data-end=\"2169\">Prepare empanelment frameworks, eligibility criteria, and rate-contract or panel-based selection structures for recurring aviation service requirements of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"26cezh\" data-start=\"2171\" data-end=\"2308\">Support the Directorate in tender publication, bidder coordination, evaluation, award, and onboarding of empanelled service providers.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"f4p8c8\" data-start=\"2310\" data-end=\"2434\">Develop contract management and performance monitoring frameworks for empanelled agencies and selected service providers.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"d2lj4m\" data-start=\"2436\" data-end=\"2480\">2. Policy, Schemes, and Skill Development</h2>\r\n<ol data-start=\"2482\" data-end=\"4061\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1p4ik8s\" data-start=\"2482\" data-end=\"2658\">Support in the formulation of the State Aviation Policy, including policy research, benchmarking with national and global practices, stakeholder consultations, and drafting.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"hb9zq6\" data-start=\"2660\" data-end=\"2842\">Support the Directorate in the design and development of aviation sector schemes for promotion of air connectivity, aviation services, infrastructure, and investment in the State.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"facqm1\" data-start=\"2844\" data-end=\"3182\">Facilitate and assist the Directorate in the selection of specialised agencies for the development of training modules and curricula for skill development of local youth in aviation and allied trades, including pilot training, cabin crew training, aircraft maintenance engineering (AME), air traffic control (ATC), and ground handling.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"hwbb2z\" data-start=\"3184\" data-end=\"3435\">Facilitate partnerships and coordination with Flying Training Organisations (FTOs), national aviation academies, DGCA-approved institutions, and skill development agencies for establishment of training centres and skilling initiatives in the State.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1kdxhi8\" data-start=\"3437\" data-end=\"3598\">Suggestion on initiatives to promote aviation-related employment opportunities for local youth and to strengthen the aviation skilling ecosystem in the State.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"135f72m\" data-start=\"3600\" data-end=\"4061\">Conduct a comparative study of aviation services, schemes, and best practices implemented by other States, including regional connectivity, helicopter services, aviation infrastructure, aviation skilling, investment promotion, and allied aviation services. Identify replicable practices and prepare recommendations for adoption and contextual adaptation in Chhattisgarh, including implementation roadmaps and institutional arrangements required for roll-out.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1ngv8xt\" data-start=\"4063\" data-end=\"4128\">3. Project Monitoring, Reporting, and Departmental Handholding</h2>\r\n<ol data-start=\"4130\" data-end=\"6075\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ne924z\" data-start=\"4130\" data-end=\"4376\">Provide project management support for aviation infrastructure and service delivery projects, including activities under the Regional Connectivity Scheme (RCS), airport and airstrip development, and operationalisation of State aviation assets.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"19e4zc5\" data-start=\"4378\" data-end=\"4561\">PMU shall support for monitoring of all ongoing projects and track upcoming and future projects, including their onboarding, progress, timelines, and overall implementation status.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11myey\" data-start=\"4563\" data-end=\"4820\">Establish and maintain a structured project monitoring framework covering all aviation projects, procurements, and empanelment processes, including project timelines, milestones, deliverables, and physical and financial progress against approved targets.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"138d1c0\" data-start=\"4822\" data-end=\"5057\">Track the implementation status of selected and empanelled service providers, contractors, and agencies, and prepare progress reviews highlighting delays, bottlenecks, deviations from approved scope, and corrective actions required.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"18puw6h\" data-start=\"5059\" data-end=\"5240\">Prepare periodic monitoring and progress reports, including weekly status updates, monthly progress reports, and quarterly review reports, in formats approved by the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"szoqmk\" data-start=\"5242\" data-end=\"5488\">Verify bills and invoices submitted by selected agencies, contractors, and service providers against the terms and conditions of the tender, work order, and contract. Recommend approval or rejection of bills with supporting verification notes.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"y9r2oo\" data-start=\"5490\" data-end=\"5702\">Support the Directorate in compilation of data and preparation of replies, status notes, and information sought by the State Government, the Legislative Assembly, audit authorities, and other competent forums.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"n6h4ej\" data-start=\"5704\" data-end=\"5889\">Coordinate with regulatory authorities, national aviation institutions, and industry stakeholders, and support stakeholder communication, meeting coordination, and follow-up actions.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"fwf1nt\" data-start=\"5891\" data-end=\"6075\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Carry out any other task assigned by the Directorate of Aviation related to aviation sector development, transaction advisory, bid process management, and routine departmental work.</li>\r\n</ol>', '<p><strong>Change Management</strong><br><br>Any change in the scope of work, team composition, or duration shall be subject to mutual agreement between Directorate of Aviation/CHiPS and the selected consultant and shall be documented through a formal amendment to the Work Order. In case of unavoidable substitution, the replacement personnel must possess qualifications and experience equivalent to or higher than those specified in the original team requirement.<br><br><strong>Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment<br><br></strong>The envisaged duration of the assigned is 24 calendar months, extendable as required. The resource may be extended as per requirement of project need. Deployment timelines will be governed as per the approved Resource Deployment Plan to be submitted by the selected consultant within 30 working days of issuance of the Work Order.</p>', '<p><strong>Payment terms </strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule.</li>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n<li>For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or CHiPS, as the case may be selected bidder shall be paid the requisite man month payment in the event that selected bidder has performed on its obligations in compliance with the terms of this contract</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Penalty terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n</ul>', 8, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their experience, if any, in a similar area of expertise (via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th>Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th>Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Work Plan, Activity Schedule, and Staffing Schedule</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such specific kind of a project</li>\r\n<li>Prior exposure in similar government projects</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Educational Qualification</li>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Experience of working in Government Projects</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.</li>\r\n<li>The last date for submission of response is 11/08/2026 17:00 Hrs. Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</li>\r\n<li>All pre-bid queries and proposal submissions shall be submitted through the Empanelment Portal (https://empl.cgstate.gov.in) only. Submissions through e-mail, portal messages, or any other mode shall not be accepted. Only submissions made through the respective provisions of the Empanelment Portal shall be considered.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EoI</li>\r\n<li>Copy of Approach and methodology presentation</li>\r\n<li>Resumes of resources proposed for the evaluation.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2026-07-28 11:45:27', 4, 1, '2026-07-28 11:44:45', 94, '2026-07-28 11:45:27', NULL, '2026-07-28 11:54:02', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-07-28', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', '2nd Call Program Management Unit (PMU) for Technical Support and Transaction Advisory Support for Directorate of Aviation, Government of Chhattisgarh', '2026-07-27', NULL, '2026-08-11 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Technical Score and Presentation', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-03-10', 0, 1, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/B5ZmCXHPGZzu53BlfgImV9u9Q6WzCXkoKTLmp76k.pdf', NULL, 0, 3, 1, 0, '1,2,3,4,5,7,8', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/xZidbJBcDr7CRKDSXdaQVFad7vm0qtFbLL07qyo7.pdf', 0, 1, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 1, 0, 0, 1, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 17534717.58, 0, 0, 3156249.16, 20690966.74, 1, 0, NULL, NULL),
(181, 95, 33, 'EoI/EMPL/CHiPS/CGSPC/ANJOR/2026', 1, 'Project Monitoring Unit under \'Chhattisgarh Anjor Vision 2047\'', '12', '<p>The primary objectives of the assignment shall include, but not be limited to:&nbsp;</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Providing technical and professional support.</li>\r\n<li>Strengthening project planning and implementation.</li>\r\n<li>Supporting monitoring, evaluation, and reporting mechanisms.</li>\r\n<li>Facilitating data analysis and evidence-based decision-making.</li>\r\n<li>Enhancing institutional capacity through technical assistance.</li>\r\n</ul>', 2, 33, '2026-08-14 12:25:38', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, NULL, '<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>CHiPS is inviting Tier-I empaneled agencies (as per Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/ Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Team Requirement, Qualification, and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p>The team of consultants shall be responsible to provide technical, analytical, and operational support for the implementation and monitoring of Chhattisgarh Anjor Vision @2047. The scope of work shall include, but not be limited to, the&nbsp; following:&nbsp;<br>I. Provide strategic and technical support for the implementation of&nbsp; Chhattisgarh Anjor Vision @2047.&nbsp;<br>II.&nbsp; Coordinate with Departments to facilitate effective planning, implementation, and convergence of Vision initiatives.&nbsp;<br>III. Monitor departmental KPIs, targets, milestones, and project progress through the Anjor Vision Monitoring Portal.&nbsp;<br>IV. Collect, validate, analyse, and maintain project data, ensuring data quality&nbsp; and timely reporting.&nbsp;<br>V. Prepare periodic progress reports, dashboards, presentations, policy briefs, and review notes for senior management.&nbsp;<br>VI. Support the development and refinement of KPIs, monitoring frameworks,&nbsp; and performance assessment mechanisms.&nbsp;<br>VII. Undertake research, policy analysis, benchmarking, and documentation of best practices.&nbsp;<br>VIII. Organise review meetings, workshops, and capacity-building programmes&nbsp; for stakeholders.&nbsp;<br>IX. Provide technical support for the enhancement and maintenance of digital monitoring systems and dashboards.&nbsp;<br>X. Perform any other tasks assigned by the Government of Chhattisgarh in furtherance of the objectives of Chhattisgarh Anjor Vision @2047.&nbsp;</p>', NULL, '<p><strong>Payment Terms<br></strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on a monthly basis.</li>\r\n<li>Each payment will be made only after the delivery of the corresponding deliverable and its acceptance by CHiPS.</li>\r\n<li>Taxes will be applicable as per prevailing government norms.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>PENALTY TERMS</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Important Note: All other terms and conditions of tender 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025 shall be applicable to this EoI.</p>', 5, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company regarding their understanding of the proposed scope of work and their experience, if any, in similar areas of expertise (Physical Mode / Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (Physical Mode / Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th>Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th>Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of the Project Framework</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such a specific kind of project</li>\r\n<li>Prior experience in project interaction with senior Government officials</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of key SLAs of project management</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Good understanding of project management best practices framework</li>\r\n<li>Ability to Negotiate / Persuade / Influence</li>\r\n<li>Strong ability to understand, deliberate, and report / monitor the key SLAs</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1.5;\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.</li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 2;\">The last date for submission of response is <strong>22/09/2026 17:00 Hrs.</strong> Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</li>\n<li style=\"line-height: 1.5;\">All pre-bid queries and proposal submissions shall be submitted through the Empanelment Portal (https://empl.cgstate.gov.in) only. Any submission or communication received through e-mail, messages, or any mode other than the Empanelment Portal shall not be accepted or considered. For any other enquiries, please contact <span style=\"text-decoration: underline;\">empl.chips@cgchips.</span>in and <a href=\"mailto:empl_portal@cgchips.in\">empl_portal@cgchips.in</a>.</li>\n</ul>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EoI.</li>\r\n<li>Copy of the approach and methodology presentation.</li>\r\n<li>CVs of the resources who will appear for the interview.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '554272', '2026-08-14 16:38:30', 4, 1, '2026-08-14 16:32:26', 33, '2026-08-14 16:38:30', NULL, '2026-09-01 11:59:44', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-09-01', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Expression of Interest For Project Monitoring Unit under Chhattisgarh Anjor Vision 2047', '2026-09-01', '2026-09-07 17:00:00', '2026-09-23 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Technical Presentation and Interview', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-03-27', 1, 0, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/1C744DNrqW1UPpyHDH5RRXFPE4DUTxkMTFTnq2Bm.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 1, 0, '2,3,4,5', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/NMq9fHp1TgsXDarysRkCkZrqPyQyjZ3C6BbfoHaT.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(182, 0, 60, 'EoI/CHiPS/EMPL/CGStatePortal/2026', 1, 'CG State Portal Project', '14', '<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; margin: 0cm 5.65pt .0001pt 5.5pt;\">CHiPS, a Registered Society promoted by the Government of Chhattisgarh, is the nodal agency and prime mover for propelling IT growth and implementation of IT plans in the State. The Hon&rsquo;b1e Chief Minister heads the High-Powered Governing Council of CHiPS. It includes Minister for Finance &amp; Commercial Taxes, Minister for Commerce &amp; Industry, Minister for Education, and Minister for Panchayat &amp; Rural Development, Chief Secretary, representative from the Ministry of Electronics &amp; Information Technology in Government of India and eminent persons from IT industry.<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; margin: 0cm 5.65pt .0001pt 5.5pt;\">CHiPS is involved as State Designated Agency (SDA) in NeGPMMP&rsquo;s implementation of some mega IT Projects like CHOiCE, e-Procurement, SDC, SWAN, Wi-Fi, e-distict, aadhar, GIS and CSCs. A professional approach is being adopted for the implementation of IT Projects using the services of e-governance experts and consultants from corporate and academia. Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS) intends to on-board an agency for a period of Three (3) year to assist and support Various State Government Departments in order to Implement IT Services/ E- Governance Services through Empanelment Project of CHiPS.<a name=\"_TOC_250003\"></a></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; margin: 0cm 5.65pt .0001pt 5.5pt;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; line-height: 115%; margin: 0cm 5.65pt .0001pt 5.5pt;\">The Chhattisgarh State Portal (https://cgstate.gov.in) has been developed as a unified platform to provide citizens, departments with centralized access to important information related to the Government of Chhattisgarh. The portal serves as a single-window interface for accessing government notifications, tenders, departmental information, and links to various e-Governance services.</p>', 1, 60, '2026-08-21 12:36:09', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '<p>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS) intends to on-board a Manpower Service Provider Firms to assist and support Various State Government Departments for IT Services/E- Governance Services through the Empanelment Project of CHiPS. The State Portal functions as a single-window gateway for disseminating authentic government information and providing seamless access to various citizen-centric services, schemes, notifications, tenders, circulars, departmental contacts, downloadable forms, and links to online applications. The detailed Scope of Work (SoW) is listed below. CHiPS want to appoint 03 resources under State portal Project as given below: -</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Database Admin Asst.</li>\r\n<li>Graphic Designer.</li>\r\n<li>Assistant Manager.<br><br>This section provides general information about the issuer, important dates, relevant addresses and the overall eligibility criteria for the bidders.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>CHiPS is inviting Tier-II empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No-160137/CEO/ CHiPS/ EMPL/Application &amp; Website Development/2024 dated 18/10/2024 to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Candidates, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<h1 style=\"margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933835\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt;\">3.1 Database Admin &ndash;Level 7</span></strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"isselectedend\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The <strong>Database Administrator (DBA)</strong> will be responsible for the installation, configuration, administration, monitoring, performance optimization, backup, recovery, security, and maintenance of enterprise databases supporting the State Portal Project. This role is suitable for experienced professionals who can independently manage production databases, ensure high availability, optimize database performance, and maintain data integrity and security.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933836\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.1.1 Key Responsibilities</span></h2>\r\n<ul data-assistant-stream-block=\"\" data-assistant-stream-block-index=\"0\">\r\n<li><strong>Database Administration:</strong>&nbsp;Install, configure, administer, and maintain MySQL/PostgreSQL/MariaDB databases&nbsp;across development, testing, and production environments.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Database Performance &amp; Optimization:</strong> Monitor database performance, optimize queries, indexes, stored procedures, and&nbsp;database structures to&nbsp;ensure efficient system&nbsp;performance.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Backup &amp; Recovery:</strong> Plan, implement, monitor, and&nbsp;periodically test database&nbsp;backup, restoration, disaster&nbsp;recovery, and business&nbsp;continuity procedures.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Database&nbsp;Security:</strong> Implement database&nbsp;security measures including&nbsp;user access control, privilege management,&nbsp;encryption, auditing, and&nbsp;compliance with security&nbsp;best practices.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Database Monitoring &amp; Troubleshooting:</strong> Monitor database health, identify performance bottlenecks, troubleshoot database-related issues, and&nbsp;ensure maximum uptime.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Database Migration &amp; Deployment:</strong> Perform database installation, migration, upgrades, patch&nbsp;management, replication setup, and&nbsp;deployment activities with&nbsp;minimal downtime.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Documentation: </strong>Prepare and&nbsp;maintain database architecture&nbsp;documents, configuration&nbsp;details, backup procedures, recovery plans, and&nbsp;operational documentation.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Work closely&nbsp;with application developers, system administrators,&nbsp;DevOps engineers, and&nbsp;project managers for&nbsp;database design, deployment, and support.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Security &amp; Compliance:</strong> Ensure data integrity, database availability, and compliance with organizational policies and Government security standards.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933837\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.1.2 Requirements</span></h2>\r\n<ul data-assistant-stream-block=\"\" data-assistant-stream-block-index=\"0\">\r\n<li>Bachelor\'s/Master\'s degree&nbsp;in Computer Science, Information Technology, MCA, or related&nbsp;field.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 6 years&nbsp;of professional experience.</li>\r\n<li>Strong knowledge of&nbsp;MySQL, PostgreSQL, MariaDB, SQL, PL/SQL, database design, indexing, query optimization, replication, backup &amp; recovery, performance&nbsp;tuning, and database&nbsp;security.</li>\r\n<li>Experience in database&nbsp;installation, configuration, migration, clustering,&nbsp;high availability, and&nbsp;disaster recovery solutions.</li>\r\n<li>Ability&nbsp;to work independently&nbsp;and manage enterprise&nbsp;database environments.</li>\r\n<li>The candidate will&nbsp;not be required&nbsp;to work exclusively&nbsp;on a single&nbsp;database platform; however, basic knowledge of&nbsp;other database technologies&nbsp;and readiness to&nbsp;learn emerging database&nbsp;platforms as per&nbsp;project requirements is&nbsp;essential.</li>\r\n<li>The candidate should&nbsp;also have working&nbsp;knowledge of server-related activities including&nbsp;database deployment, configuration, monitoring, and troubleshooting.</li>\r\n<li>Preference will be given to experienced candidates who have worked in Government Organizations.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933838\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.1.3 Desirable</span></h2>\r\n<ul data-assistant-stream-block=\"\" data-assistant-stream-block-index=\"0\">\r\n<li>Familiarity with cloud&nbsp;database platforms&nbsp;and containerization technologies.</li>\r\n<li>Knowledge of Linux/Windows server administration&nbsp;and database deployment&nbsp;environments.</li>\r\n<li>Experience with Git, GitLab, Bitbucket, and&nbsp;database automation tools.</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of High&nbsp;Availability, replication, clustering, and disaster recovery&nbsp;architecture.</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of Agile/Scrum methodologies.</li>\r\n<li>Strong communication skills in English and Hindi.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h1 style=\"margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933839\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt;\">3.2 Graphic Designer&ndash;Level 6</span></strong></h1>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left;\">The <strong>Graphic Designer</strong> will be&nbsp;responsible for creating intuitive, user-centered design solutions that enhance the usability and user experience of web and mobile applications. The role involves collaborating closely with UI designers, developers, project managers, and stakeholders to gather requirements, conduct user research, and translate insights into wireframes, prototypes, and user flows.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\">The ideal candidate is creative, detail-oriented, and passionate about improving user experience through thoughtful design and usability practices.</span></p>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><a name=\"_Toc195092065\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.2.1 Key Responsibilities</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<ul data-assistant-stream-block=\"\" data-assistant-stream-block-index=\"0\">\r\n<li><strong>User Research:</strong> Conduct&nbsp;user research, interviews, surveys, and usability&nbsp;tests&nbsp;to understand user&nbsp;needs and behaviours.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Wire framing &amp; Prototyping:</strong> Create wireframes, mockups, and interactive prototypes&nbsp;using tools like&nbsp;Figma, Adobe XD, or&nbsp;Sketch.</li>\r\n<li><strong>User Journey Mapping:</strong> Develop user personas, journey maps, and&nbsp;user flows to&nbsp;guide design decisions.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Work closely&nbsp;with UI designers, developers, and project&nbsp;teams to ensure&nbsp;seamless user experience&nbsp;integration.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Feedback &amp; Testing: </strong>Incorporate&nbsp;feedback from stakeholders&nbsp;and users to&nbsp;refine designs; conduct&nbsp;A/B testing&nbsp;where applicable.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Design Documentation: </strong>Prepare&nbsp;design specifications and&nbsp;documentation to support&nbsp;development teams.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><a name=\"_Toc195092066\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.2.2 Requirements</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<ul data-assistant-stream-block=\"\" data-assistant-stream-block-index=\"0\">\r\n<li>Bachelor\'s or Master&rsquo;s&nbsp;Degree in&nbsp;Computer Science or&nbsp;Bacorhelor&rsquo;s/Master&rsquo;s Degree&nbsp;in Design, Computer&nbsp;Science, or a&nbsp;related field.</li>\r\n<li>5 years&nbsp;of experience in&nbsp;UX/UI design&nbsp;or a similar&nbsp;role.</li>\r\n<li>Preference will be&nbsp;given to experienced&nbsp;candidates of work&nbsp;in Govt. Organization.</li>\r\n<li>Proficient in UX/UI tools such&nbsp;as Figma, Adobe&nbsp;XD, Sketch, InVision, or Balsamiq.</li>\r\n<li>Understanding&nbsp;of design principles, responsive design, accessibility, and user-centered&nbsp;methodologies.</li>\r\n<li>Familiarity with HTML/CSS is a&nbsp;plus (for effective&nbsp;developer communication).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><a name=\"_Toc195092067\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.2.3 Desirable</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<ul data-assistant-stream-block=\"\" data-assistant-stream-block-index=\"0\">\r\n<li>Basic understanding of&nbsp;UX/UI design and&nbsp;visual design principles.</li>\r\n<li>Experience working on&nbsp;government, enterprise, or public-facing applications.</li>\r\n<li>Strong communication and presentation skills in English and Hindi.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class=\"isselectedend\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt;\">3.3 Assistant Manager &ndash; Level 4</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"isselectedend\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Assistant Manager will be responsible for assisting in the overall coordination, monitoring, documentation, and administrative management of the State Portal Project. The role involves maintaining project records and files, preparing official correspondence and reports, monitoring project progress, and ensuring timely execution of project activities in accordance with Government procedures. This role is suitable for experienced professionals who can independently handle project coordination, documentation, stakeholder communication, and administrative functions while supporting the successful implementation of the State Portal Project.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933844\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.3.1 Key Responsibilities</span></h2>\r\n<ul data-assistant-stream-block=\"\" data-assistant-stream-block-index=\"0\">\r\n<li><strong>Project Coordination:</strong> Coordinate&nbsp;with Government Departments, District Administrations, vendors, and technical&nbsp;teams for implementation, maintenance, and enhancement&nbsp;of the State&nbsp;Portal.</li>\r\n<li><strong>File Management:</strong> Process&nbsp;and maintain project&nbsp;files, official records, correspondence, approvals, office notes, and&nbsp;related documentation in&nbsp;accordance with Government&nbsp;procedures.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Documentation:</strong> Prepare and&nbsp;maintain DPRs, TORs, proposals, meeting minutes, technical notes, project&nbsp;reports, presentations,&nbsp;utilization reports, and&nbsp;other project-related&nbsp;documents.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Administrative Support:</strong>&nbsp;Assist in processing&nbsp;administrative and financial&nbsp;proposals, manpower deployment, contract-related documents, and other official&nbsp;matters pertaining to&nbsp;the project.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Monitoring &amp; Reporting:</strong>&nbsp;Monitor project progress, timelines, milestones,&nbsp;resource&nbsp;deployment, and deliverables, and prepare periodic&nbsp;progress reports for&nbsp;higher authorities.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Compliance:</strong> Ensure project&nbsp;documentation and activities&nbsp;comply with Government&nbsp;rules, departmental guidelines&nbsp;and applicable standards.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Meeting Coordination:</strong> Organize&nbsp;meetings, prepare agendas, record minutes of&nbsp;meetings (MoMs), and follow&nbsp;up on action&nbsp;points.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Support to Management:</strong> Provide administrative and coordination support to senior officers in project planning, review meetings, and decision-making processes.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933845\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.3.2 Requirements</span></h2>\r\n<ul data-assistant-stream-block=\"\" data-assistant-stream-block-index=\"0\">\r\n<li>Bachelor\'s/Master\'s degree&nbsp;in Engineering (B.E./B.Tech.) in&nbsp;any discipline, MBA, Management, or any&nbsp;other&nbsp;equivalent professional&nbsp;qualification from a&nbsp;recognized University/Institution.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 4 years&nbsp;of professional experience.</li>\r\n<li>Experience in project&nbsp;coordination, Government&nbsp;correspondence, file processing, documentation, report&nbsp;preparation.</li>\r\n<li>Working knowledge of&nbsp;MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), project&nbsp;documentation, and office&nbsp;management practices.</li>\r\n<li>Ability&nbsp;to independently handle&nbsp;official correspondence, prepare reports, maintain&nbsp;project records, and&nbsp;coordinate with team.</li>\r\n<li>Basic understanding of&nbsp;e-Governance projects, website management will&nbsp;be preferred.</li>\r\n<li>Preference will be given to candidates having experience of working in Government Organizations or Government IT/e-Governance projects.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933846\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.3.3 Desirable</span></h2>\r\n<ul style=\"margin-top: 0cm;\" type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 1.5;\">Experience in handling Government files, official noting and drafting, DPR preparation, and procurement-related documentation.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 1.5;\">Knowledge of Government administrative procedures, project monitoring.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 1.5;\">Familiarity with project management and documentation tools.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 1.5;\">Understanding of e-Governance initiatives and digital service delivery frameworks.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 1.5;\">Strong communication, drafting, presentation, and interpersonal skills in English and Hindi.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<h3 style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.1pt; line-height: 15.3pt; mso-line-height-rule: exactly; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: 23.65pt; margin: 0cm 0cm .0001pt 23.6pt;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933848\"></a><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; position: relative; top: -.5pt; mso-text-raise: .5pt; mso-font-width: 109%; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\"><span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;</span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Resource Replacement</span><u><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><br></span></u></strong></h3>\r\n<ul data-assistant-stream-block=\"\" data-assistant-stream-block-index=\"0\">\r\n<li>The selected agency&nbsp;needs to give&nbsp;1 (One) Month of advance&nbsp;notice to CHiPS&nbsp;for any change&nbsp;of deployed resource&nbsp;during the course&nbsp;of the assignment.</li>\r\n<li>The selected agency&nbsp;needs to ensure&nbsp;knowledge&nbsp;transfer and handover&nbsp;during change of&nbsp;any resource for&nbsp;smooth transition.</li>\r\n<li>The replacement of any resource should be approved by CHiPS.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<h1 dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">1. Penalty terms</span></h1>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms. Important Note: All other terms and conditions as per tender no 160137/CEO/CHIPS/EMPL/Application &amp; Website Development, Dated 18/10/2024</p>', 6, '<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/ discussion with the Committee.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">A presentation will be made by the Empanelled companies about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their past experience if any in similar area of expertise.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">During the presentation by the companies the proposed candidates will be interviewed through Online (WebEx Link) by the Evaluation Committee.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">The marking of candidates Interview will be done as follows-</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\" align=\"left\">\r\n<table style=\"width: 91.3249%; height: 304px;\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 5.39084%;\" width=\"33\"><col style=\"width: 71.6981%;\" width=\"440\"><col style=\"width: 23.0009%;\" width=\"141\"></colgroup>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">#</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Candidate Interview</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Max Marks</p>\r\n</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">1</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Suitability of profile</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">15</p>\r\n</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">2</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Your relevant experience</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">15</p>\r\n</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">3</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Good understanding of Design Development best practices framework Management</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">25</p>\r\n</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">4</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Excellent communication abilities</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">20</p>\r\n</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">5</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Strong ability to understand, deliberate and report</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 49px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">25</p>\r\n</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 10px;\">\r\n<th style=\"height: 10px;\" scope=\"col\">&nbsp;</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 10px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Total</p>\r\n</th>\r\n<th style=\"height: 10px;\" scope=\"col\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">100</p>\r\n</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.</li>\r\n<li>The last date for submission of response is Dated <strong>05/10/2026, 12:00 Hrs.</strong> Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</li>\r\n<li>All pre-bid queries and proposal submissions shall be submitted through the Empanelment Portal (https://empl.cgstate.gov.in) only. Any submission or communication received through e-mail, messages, or any mode other than the Empanelment Portal shall not be accepted or considered. For any other enquiries, please contact empl.chips@cgchips.in and empl_portal@cgchips.in.empl.chips@cgchips.in and empl_portal@cgchips.in.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EoI.</li>\r\n<li>Resumes of the resources who will appear for the interview.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '888054', '2026-09-11 12:46:24', 3, 1, '2026-09-03 17:55:05', 60, '2026-09-11 12:46:24', NULL, '2026-09-11 14:08:09', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-09-11', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Expression of Interest (EoI) for CG State Portal Project', '2026-09-11', '2026-09-16 17:00:00', '2026-10-05 12:00:00', NULL, 'To be decided later', 'Interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-04-16', 0, 0, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/tKnjc8yGqFyUOvagRQtAOMX242n7pqLatdYM05J2.pdf', NULL, 0, 2, 0, 0, '14,15,16', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/5HGs8qtZwixuQZvKdZ2KwyUoSsPiabwU0EIr0iLd.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, 'uploads/notesheet_files/sASEjGfhwxXRL0SRgY4ALSmjbq990BaFEKL94CO6.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(183, 0, 59, 'EoI/CHiPS/EMPL/AWD/2nd Call CGCOG/2026', 1, '2nd Call For Selection of Technical Resources under Chhattisgarh Center of Geo-Informatics (CGCOG) Project of CHiPS', '7', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><strong>CHiPS</strong>, a Registered Society promoted by the Government of Chhattisgarh, is the nodal agency and prime mover for propelling IT growth and implementation of IT plans in the State. The Hon&rsquo;ble Chief Minister heads the High Powered Governing Council of&nbsp;<strong>CHiPS</strong>. It includes Minister for Finance &amp; Commercial Taxes, Minister for Commerce &amp; Industry, Minister for Education, and Minister for Panchayat &amp; Rural Development, Chief Secretary, representative from the Ministry of Electronics &amp; Information Technology in Government of India and eminent persons from IT industry.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">The objective of Chhattisgarh Center of Geoinformatics (CGCOG) is insertion of GIS/Geospatial technology in Chhattisgarh State for effective planning, monitoring, management of natural resources, efforts optimization, GIS capacity building among Departments and Development of Geo-Ecosystem. It will help to optimize collection, collation, compilation and centralization of spatial data. This project will facilitate Spatial Data Infrastructure (SDI) of Chhattisgarh State.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS) intends to on-board an agency for CGCOG a period initially for One (1) year which is extendable.</span></p>', 1, 59, '2026-09-09 15:39:08', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, '<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>CHiPS &nbsp;is &nbsp;inviting &nbsp;Tier-II &nbsp;empaneled &nbsp;agencies &nbsp;(as &nbsp;per &nbsp;tender &nbsp;no &nbsp;160137/CEO/CHiPS /EMPL/Application &amp; Website Development, dated 18/10/2024) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<h1><span lang=\"EN-US\">1.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Scope of Work</span></h1>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Development of Chhattisgarh Center of Geoinformatics (CGCOG) at State</span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Development of an open and interoperable architecture approach for implementing a &ldquo;Spatial Data Infrastructure (SDI)&rdquo; accessible to all authorized users.</span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Establishment of &ldquo;Geo Portals&rdquo; for State Government Departments.</span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Develop of data management, data visualization, and data dissemination strategies and techniques, with a particular focus on the needs of state.</span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Centralization of geospatial data of various departments with standard schema designing and cataloging.</span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Define Distributed SDI requirements by undertaking a technology workshop in Chhattisgarh; the focus of workshop will be at exchanging ideas and approaches on specific requirements, specifications, technology and products required.</span></p>\r\n<p>&bull;&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\">Development of an Architecture document describing key architectural elements of Geo Portal prototype.</span></p>\r\n<p>&bull;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\">PM Gati-Shakti Project.</span></p>\r\n<h1><a name=\"_Toc229132961\"></a><a name=\"_Toc86169715\"></a><span lang=\"EN-US\">2.&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Resources Requirement</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">, Responsibility:</span></h1>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Web GIS application development involve various tasks that require a team of skilled professionals with wide-ranging skill sets. A spatial data infrastructure &amp; Web GIS solution development, Server &amp; Geodatabase Management project need a skilled team made up of specialists &amp; well-versed in GIS field. Following are the required skill that brought together to develop &ldquo;Chhattisgarh Center of Geoinformatics&rdquo;-</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">1)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></strong></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Manager- GIS</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">A Manager GIS will be required to manage geographical information system and associated vector datasets under project. He/she will have responsibility of monitoring of Geoprocessing, Geoanalytics, Spatial Analysis, Network Analysis operations and Geodatabase management from an executive level. This individual has responsibility of management of team members and allocated resources. Further, Managers will be responsible for planning, development and execution of project activities. Their work tasks will include-</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">a)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Communication with departments and understand its key requirements and accordingly preparation of SRS, FRS and TRS,</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">b)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Efforts and Cost estimation,</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">c)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Scheduling the project timelines,</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">d)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Planning for work allocation to human resources,</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">e)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Coordination management among team members for timely completion of tasks.</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">2)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></strong></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Assistant Manager - (Geodatabase, Network Analysis, Image Processing, Geoprocessing, R&amp;D)</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">A GIS expert will be required to handle GIS datasets and associated vector datasets under project. He/she will have responsibility of execution of Geoprocessing, Geoanalytics, Spatial Analysis, Network Analysis operations, Cartography and Geodatabase management. This individual has responsibility of management of allocated resources.</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">3)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></strong></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Programmer</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">Programmers will be required for the development of World Wide Web applications using a client-server model and handling \"HTML, CSS and JavaScript (in client side) and PHP, ASP.NET (C#) or Java (in the server) and HTTP for communications between client and server. Further, they will be responsible for mobile technology, such as building apps for Google&rsquo;s Android, Apple&rsquo;s iOS and Microsoft&rsquo;s Windows Phone platforms. They will also be responsible for creating and implementing databases required for the website and mobile applications. They will be responsible for testing entire application efficiency, performance and troubleshoot and to correct problems.</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">4)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></strong></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">GIS Associates</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><span lang=\"EN-US\">GIS associates will be required for execution of various GIS activities, handling of GIS vector datasets under project. He/she will have responsibility of generation of various GIS datasets, digitisation, and map updation, execution of Geoprocessing, Geoanalytics, Spatial Analysis, Network Analysis operations, Cartography and Geodatabase preparation. This individual will provide assistance to GIS Experts on various GIS activities under project.</span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">5)&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></strong></span><span class=\"fontstyle01\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Assistant Programmer</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\"><span class=\"fontstyle01\">Assistant Programmers will be required for the development of World Wide Web applications using a client-server model and handling \"HTML, CSS and JavaScript (in client side) and PHP, ASP.NET (C#) or Java (in the server) and HTTP for communications between client and server. Further, they will be responsible for mobile technology, such as building apps for Google&rsquo;s Android, Apple&rsquo;s iOS and Microsoft&rsquo;s Windows Phone platforms. They will also be responsible for creating and implementing databases required for the website and mobile applications. They will be responsible for testing entire application efficiency, performance and troubleshoot and to correct problems. Further, they will provide assistance to Programmer for the completion of project objectives.</span></span></p>', NULL, '<ol>\r\n<li>Penalty terms</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Important Note: All other terms and conditions as per tender no 160137/CEO/CHIPS/EMPL/Application &amp; Website Development, Dated 18/10/2024</p>', 6, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their experience, if any, in a similar area of expertise (via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<div dir=\"ltr\" align=\"left\">\r\n<table style=\"width: 96.9419%; height: 339px;\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 5.37459%;\" width=\"33\"><col style=\"width: 71.6612%;\" width=\"440\"><col style=\"width: 22.9642%;\" width=\"141\"></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">#</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Candidate Interview</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Max Marks</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">1</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Suitability of profile</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">15</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">2</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Your relevant experience</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">15</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 84px;\">\r\n<td style=\"height: 84px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">3</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 84px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Good understanding of Design Development best practices</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">framework</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 84px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">25</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">4</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Excellent communication abilities</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">20</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">5</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Strong ability to understand, deliberate and report</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 49px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">25</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr style=\"height: 10px;\">\r\n<td style=\"height: 10px;\">&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 10px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Total</p>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"height: 10px;\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">100</p>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n</div>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>', '<p dir=\"ltr\">Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">The last date for submission of response is Dated 24/09/2026, 17:00 Hrs. Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</p>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\">Pre-bid submission, proposal submission, presentation and interview details and any query resolution will be accepted only via the Empanelment Portal <a href=\"../../../\">(https://empl.cgstate.gov.in)</a>. For any other enquiries, contact via <a href=\"about:blank\">empl.chips@cgchips.in ,</a> <a href=\"mailto:empl_portal@cgchips.in\">empl_portal@cgchips.in</a></p>', '<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Signed copy of this EoI</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Resumes of resources who will face the interview.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '825919', '2026-09-09 17:08:50', 4, 1, '2026-09-09 17:02:19', 59, '2026-09-09 17:08:50', NULL, '2026-09-09 17:18:40', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-09-09', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', '2nd Call for Selection of Technical Resources under Chhattisgarh Center of Geo-Informatics (CGCOG) Project of CHiPS', '2026-09-09', '2026-09-15 17:00:00', '2026-09-24 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-04-22', 0, 0, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/TPT4tlozFNYY2Q3d9LqfbNaC1s9OQyg41UTlPfK8.pdf', NULL, 0, 2, 1, 0, '14,15,16', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/QXSgNRuSVLeRnh4mVqU7Ar5VIcbFBQDEkeCCi2Vt.pdf', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'uploads/notesheet_files/yPCktw78QbIqGR7K28UNNXXBZZCaaMK0FXW9Rhow.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(184, 26, 78, 'EoI/EMPL/CHiPS/GG/TPA1/2026', 1, 'Selection of Third-Party Auditor (TPA) For CM Helpline Call Center implemented by Department of Good Governance and Convergence', '12', '<p>Department of Good Governance and Convergence (GG&amp;C) establishing a dedicated CM Helpline Call Center for the Chhattisgarh State Government. This CM helpline will provide a streamlined platform for citizens of Chhattisgarh to raise grievances, ensuring their issues are addressed in a timely and transparent manner. CM Helpline project will be a key tool in improving citizen-government interaction, fostering trust, and ensuring the administration is responsive to public needs.</p>', 2, 78, '2026-09-11 11:53:55', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, '<ol>\r\n<li>Factsheet</li>\r\n<li>Project Objective</li>\r\n<li>Scope of Work</li>\r\n<li>Team Composition</li>\r\n<li>Team Requirement</li>\r\n<li>Additional Information&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Evaluation Process</li>\r\n<li>Payment &amp; Penalty Terms</li>\r\n<li>Critical Information&nbsp;</li>\r\n<li>Documents Required to Participate in this EoI</li>\r\n</ol>', '<p>The Department of Good Governance and Convergence (GG&amp;C), Government of Chhattisgarh, is implementing the &ldquo;CM Helpline&rdquo; project. This initiative provides a digital platform for citizens to raise grievances, ensuring timely, transparent, and responsive administration. This section provides general information about the issuer, important dates, relevant addresses and the overall eligibility criteria for the bidders.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>CHiPS is inviting Tier-I empaneled agencies (as per Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/ Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Team Requirement, Qualification, and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p>The broad scope of work (Implementation Phase &amp; Operation Phase) of the Third-Party Auditor (TPA) in the CM Helpline project will be as follows:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li><strong>Implementation Phase:</strong>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Audit of deliverables submitted with respect to actual work done as part of implementation phase and submitting report to GG&amp;C\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Indicated deliverables but not limited to FRS, SRS, CMS application, Infrastructure deployment, Data Security, and Compliance audits.</li>\r\n<li>Infrastructure (Hardware and software) Inventory Audit, Connectivity</li>\r\n<li>Audit of Testing (UAT, FAT, Security, Load) and Training</li>\r\n<li>Go-Live report</li>\r\n<li>Operational Support and Rollout</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>The TPA is responsible for the systematic assessment and certification of the CM Helpline solution across all phases. The selected TPA is required to submit final recommendation for each of the milestone listed in CM helpline RFP (Implementation and O&amp;M phases). In addition to this, TPA may also be required to submit report and their recommendation as required by GG&amp;C on the CM helpline project.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Operation Phase:<br>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Audit of Call Center SLA, Operation and Performance and submit report on, any other SLA mentioned in the CM helpline RFP for the call center service provider. Selected TPA needs to submit monthly, quarterly reports/recommendation based on the reports generated by the system and/or shared by TPA\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Overall compliance and KPIs of the RFP/agreement signed with the SP.</li>\r\n<li>Monitoring security compliances of Complaint Management System, web portal, Mobile App</li>\r\n<li>Conduct daily inbound &amp; outbound call audits as mandated (20 inbound + 20 outbound per day minimum) and submit monthly reports to GG&amp;C</li>\r\n<li>Grading performance for Agents, Team Leads, and Trainers.</li>\r\n<li>Observation and Recommendations based on the audit.</li>\r\n<li>Create a framework for effective monitoring of the call center.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>', '<p><strong>1. Change Management:</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left; padding-left: 40px;\">a) The selected agency will have to give 2 weeks of advance notice to GG&amp;C for any change of deployed resource/s during the course of the assignment.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left; padding-left: 40px;\">b) The selected agency will have to ensure that the knowledge transfer and handover during change of any resource/s for smooth transition.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: left; padding-left: 40px;\">c) The replacement of any resource/s should be approved by Department of Good Governance &amp; Convergence in writing.</p>\r\n<p><strong>2. Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment</strong></p>\r\n<p style=\"padding-left: 40px;\">This EoI is raised with an intention to hire management experts for setting up a Third-Party Auditor (TPA) for a period of 01 year from the date of issuance of the Work Order (WO).</p>', '<p>Payment Terms</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the agreed empanelment terms. Selected TPA needs to get MPR and attendance verified by the GG&amp;C.</li>\r\n<li>For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or CHiPS, as the case may be, selected bidder shall be paid the requisite man month payment in the event that selected bidder has performed on its obligation in compliance with the terms of this contract.</li>\r\n<li>The payment shall be payable after receiving approval from GG&amp;C.</li>\r\n<li>Man Month Rate will be as per the new empanelment rate effective from issued of work order.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Penalty Terms</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>Important Note: All other terms and conditions of tender 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025 shall be applicable to this EoI.</p>', 7, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their experience, if any, in a similar area of expertise (in person/VC).</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (in person/VC).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th style=\"width: 11.5532%;\">Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th style=\"width: 49.8892%;\">Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th style=\"width: 38.4812%;\">Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td style=\"width: 11.5532%; text-align: center;\"><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 49.8892%;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of the Project Framework</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such a specific kind of project</li>\r\n<li>Prior involvement in implementing or auditing government projects within CM Helpline, Contact Center, or Exit Management domains.</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of key SLAs</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td style=\"width: 38.4812%;\">\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Good understanding of CM Helpline project best practices framework.</li>\r\n<li>Strong ability to understand and deliberate and report monitor the key SLAs.</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.</li>\r\n<li>The last date for submission of response is <strong>05/10/2026 12:00 Hrs.</strong> Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</li>\r\n<li>All pre-bid queries and proposal submissions shall be submitted through the Empanelment Portal (https://empl.cgstate.gov.in) only. Any submission or communication received through e-mail, messages, or any mode other than the Empanelment Portal shall not be accepted or considered. For any other enquiries, please contact empl.chips@cgchips.in and empl_portal@cgchips.in.empl.chips@cgchips.in and empl_portal@cgchips.in.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EoI.</li>\r\n<li>Copy of the Approach and Methodology Presentation.</li>\r\n<li>CVs of the resources who will appear for the interview.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2026-09-11 13:29:16', 4, 1, '2026-09-11 12:09:43', 78, '2026-09-11 13:29:16', NULL, '2026-09-11 13:52:21', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-09-11', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Expression of Interest (EoI) for Selection of Third-Party Auditor for CM Helpline Call Center implemented by Department of Good Governance & Convergence', '2026-09-11', '2026-09-18 00:00:00', '2026-10-05 12:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Presentation and interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-04-24', 1, 0, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/sz49ZGc1KOQ7d3NknyHilQJTRxj5CzUfw9oukpcm.pdf', NULL, 0, 1, 1, 0, '1,2,3,4,5', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/J6htfOH9CHsAfmefsXzI8k3rG1f09LKncNbgVRNE.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(185, 0, 94, 'EoI/CHiPS/PMU/3rdCall AVIATION2/2026', 1, '3rd Call for Program Management Unit (PMU) for Technical Support and Transaction Advisory Support for Directorate of Aviation, Government of Chhattisgarh', '24', '<h1 class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-section-id=\"1cno33t\" data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"17\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">1. Introduction</span></h1>\r\n<p data-start=\"19\" data-end=\"378\">Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS), the nodal agency of the Department of Electronics &amp; Information Technology, Government of Chhattisgarh, invites Expression of Interest (EoI) from empanelled consulting firms for setting up an onsite Transaction Advisory Project Management Unit (PMU) for the Directorate of Aviation, Government of Chhattisgarh.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"380\" data-end=\"876\">The Directorate of Aviation is responsible for overseeing and promoting civil aviation activities within the State, including airport and airstrip development, regulatory compliance, sectoral growth, and aviation skill development. With the expansion of regional air connectivity and the growth of aviation-related services and infrastructure in the State, the Directorate requires a dedicated multi-disciplinary team to provide end-to-end transaction advisory and bid process management support.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"878\" data-end=\"1218\">The selected firm shall deploy a Transaction Advisory PMU on a full-time, onsite basis for following broad scope. The team shall support in structuring, procuring, and managing the appointment of service providers across the aviation value chain, and in developing policy, schemes, and skill development frameworks for the sector and other.</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1220\" data-end=\"2372\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zx5vbd\" data-start=\"1220\" data-end=\"1613\">The Directorate of Aviation is required to procure a range of specialised aviation services and infrastructure, including ground handling agencies, helicopter services, safety and security equipment, and the development of airstrips. Each of these procurements requires structured bid process management, technical and financial structuring, and compliance with applicable procurement rules.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"znlkmr\" data-start=\"1614\" data-end=\"1856\">Procurement of aviation services and infrastructure involves multi-stage transactions, contract structuring, and risk allocation that demand dedicated transaction advisory expertise not available within the Directorate on a full-time basis.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15hqlcq\" data-start=\"1857\" data-end=\"2128\">The State requires the development of an enabling aviation policy, sector schemes, and structured training modules to promote aviation-related skill development and employment among local youth, including pilot training, cabin crew training, and allied aviation trades.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1w6qcq1\" data-start=\"2129\" data-end=\"2372\">There is a need to augment the institutional capacity of the Directorate through a dedicated PMU that can provide specialized, full-time transaction advisory, bid process management, and project management support across the aviation sector.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h1 data-section-id=\"3h2xtw\" data-start=\"2374\" data-end=\"2386\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">2. Purpose</span></h1>\r\n<p data-start=\"2388\" data-end=\"2545\">The key objective of engaging the Transaction Advisory PMU is to strengthen the institutional capacity of the Directorate of Aviation in the following areas:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2547\" data-end=\"3134\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1wvrfgv\" data-start=\"2547\" data-end=\"2676\">End-to-end bid process management and transaction advisory for procurement of aviation services, infrastructure, and equipment.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1a7to55\" data-start=\"2677\" data-end=\"2839\">Development of aviation policy, sector schemes, and facilitate in preparing training modules for skill development of local youth in aviation and allied trades.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17yfmra\" data-start=\"2840\" data-end=\"2978\">Strengthening project management, monitoring, and reporting of aviation infrastructure and service delivery projects of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"368k2v\" data-start=\"2979\" data-end=\"3134\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Coordination with national-level aviation institutions, regulatory authorities, and industry stakeholders for capacity building and sectoral development.</li>\r\n</ul>', 2, 94, '2026-10-01 21:20:11', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, '<p>1. Factsheet <br>2. Project Objective <br>3. Scope of Work <br>4. Team Composition <br>5. Team Requirements <br>6. Change Management <br>7. Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment <br>8. Evaluation Process <br>9. Payment &amp; Penalty Terms <br>10. Critical Information <br>11. Documents Required as response to this EoI</p>', '<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>The objective of the assignment is to provide assistance to Directorate of Aviation for Program Management Unit (PMU) for Technical Support and Transaction Advisory Support. <br><br>CHiPS is inviting all empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/ Empanelment/Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur Dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"92\"><strong data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"92\">The deployed team shall carry out the following tasks during the term of the engagement:</strong></p>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"41ekof\" data-start=\"94\" data-end=\"147\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">1. Transaction Advisory and Bid Process Management</span></h2>\r\n<ol data-start=\"149\" data-end=\"2434\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"yizp3c\" data-start=\"149\" data-end=\"392\">Provide end-to-end transaction advisory and bid process management support for procurement of goods, services, and works across the aviation sector, covering the full bid cycle from need assessment to contract award and contract management.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"q81y5h\" data-start=\"394\" data-end=\"526\">Techno-commercial assessment for proposed aviation procurements and advise on appropriate procurement and contracting strategies.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"k9mmkj\" data-start=\"528\" data-end=\"806\">Prepare, review, and finalise procurement documents including Expressions of Interest (EoIs), Requests for Proposal (RFPs), Requests for Qualification (RFQs), bid documents, draft contracts, concession agreements, Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs), and related documentation.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"hqa1v\" data-start=\"808\" data-end=\"1058\">Design qualification criteria, evaluation frameworks, and bid evaluation methodologies in alignment with the General Financial Rules (GFR) 2017, Central Vigilance Commission (CVC) guidelines, and applicable State of Chhattisgarh procurement rules.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1481o2t\" data-start=\"1060\" data-end=\"1287\">Manage the complete bid process, including pre-bid meetings, issuance of clarifications and corrigendum, bid opening, evaluation support, and preparation of evaluation reports and recommendations for the competent authority.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"8fohhg\" data-start=\"1289\" data-end=\"1993\">Provide transaction advisory and bid process management support for empanelment of, and tendering for, the following primary aviation services and infrastructure but not limited to:\r\n<ul data-start=\"1478\" data-end=\"1993\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"way9xt\" data-start=\"1478\" data-end=\"1545\">Ground handling agencies for airports and airstrips in the State.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1pwyuwg\" data-start=\"1549\" data-end=\"1658\">Helicopter services, including charter, regional connectivity, and emergency / medical evacuation services.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"csdv3q\" data-start=\"1662\" data-end=\"1792\">Agencies for capacity building and training of aviation sector personnel and for institutional strengthening of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1qrjhro\" data-start=\"1796\" data-end=\"1880\">Suppliers of safety, security, and firefighting equipment for aviation facilities.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1g4fu8i\" data-start=\"1884\" data-end=\"1993\">Agencies for the development, upgradation, and maintenance of airstrips and allied aviation infrastructure.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"pqxu29\" data-start=\"1995\" data-end=\"2169\">Prepare empanelment frameworks, eligibility criteria, and rate-contract or panel-based selection structures for recurring aviation service requirements of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"26cezh\" data-start=\"2171\" data-end=\"2308\">Support the Directorate in tender publication, bidder coordination, evaluation, award, and onboarding of empanelled service providers.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"f4p8c8\" data-start=\"2310\" data-end=\"2434\">Develop contract management and performance monitoring frameworks for empanelled agencies and selected service providers.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"d2lj4m\" data-start=\"2436\" data-end=\"2480\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">2. Policy, Schemes, and Skill Development</span></h2>\r\n<ol data-start=\"2482\" data-end=\"4061\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1p4ik8s\" data-start=\"2482\" data-end=\"2658\">Support in the formulation of the State Aviation Policy, including policy research, benchmarking with national and global practices, stakeholder consultations, and drafting.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"hb9zq6\" data-start=\"2660\" data-end=\"2842\">Support the Directorate in the design and development of aviation sector schemes for promotion of air connectivity, aviation services, infrastructure, and investment in the State.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"facqm1\" data-start=\"2844\" data-end=\"3182\">Facilitate and assist the Directorate in the selection of specialised agencies for the development of training modules and curricula for skill development of local youth in aviation and allied trades, including pilot training, cabin crew training, aircraft maintenance engineering (AME), air traffic control (ATC), and ground handling.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"hwbb2z\" data-start=\"3184\" data-end=\"3435\">Facilitate partnerships and coordination with Flying Training Organisations (FTOs), national aviation academies, DGCA-approved institutions, and skill development agencies for establishment of training centres and skilling initiatives in the State.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1kdxhi8\" data-start=\"3437\" data-end=\"3598\">Suggestion on initiatives to promote aviation-related employment opportunities for local youth and to strengthen the aviation skilling ecosystem in the State.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"135f72m\" data-start=\"3600\" data-end=\"4061\">Conduct a comparative study of aviation services, schemes, and best practices implemented by other States, including regional connectivity, helicopter services, aviation infrastructure, aviation skilling, investment promotion, and allied aviation services. Identify replicable practices and prepare recommendations for adoption and contextual adaptation in Chhattisgarh, including implementation roadmaps and institutional arrangements required for roll-out.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<h2 data-section-id=\"1ngv8xt\" data-start=\"4063\" data-end=\"4128\"><span style=\"font-size: 14pt;\">3. Project Monitoring, Reporting, and Departmental Handholding</span></h2>\r\n<ol data-start=\"4130\" data-end=\"6075\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ne924z\" data-start=\"4130\" data-end=\"4376\">Provide project management support for aviation infrastructure and service delivery projects, including activities under the Regional Connectivity Scheme (RCS), airport and airstrip development, and operationalisation of State aviation assets.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"19e4zc5\" data-start=\"4378\" data-end=\"4561\">PMU shall support for monitoring of all ongoing projects and track upcoming and future projects, including their onboarding, progress, timelines, and overall implementation status.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11myey\" data-start=\"4563\" data-end=\"4820\">Establish and maintain a structured project monitoring framework covering all aviation projects, procurements, and empanelment processes, including project timelines, milestones, deliverables, and physical and financial progress against approved targets.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"138d1c0\" data-start=\"4822\" data-end=\"5057\">Track the implementation status of selected and empanelled service providers, contractors, and agencies, and prepare progress reviews highlighting delays, bottlenecks, deviations from approved scope, and corrective actions required.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"18puw6h\" data-start=\"5059\" data-end=\"5240\">Prepare periodic monitoring and progress reports, including weekly status updates, monthly progress reports, and quarterly review reports, in formats approved by the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"szoqmk\" data-start=\"5242\" data-end=\"5488\">Verify bills and invoices submitted by selected agencies, contractors, and service providers against the terms and conditions of the tender, work order, and contract. Recommend approval or rejection of bills with supporting verification notes.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"y9r2oo\" data-start=\"5490\" data-end=\"5702\">Support the Directorate in compilation of data and preparation of replies, status notes, and information sought by the State Government, the Legislative Assembly, audit authorities, and other competent forums.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"n6h4ej\" data-start=\"5704\" data-end=\"5889\">Coordinate with regulatory authorities, national aviation institutions, and industry stakeholders, and support stakeholder communication, meeting coordination, and follow-up actions.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"fwf1nt\" data-start=\"5891\" data-end=\"6075\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Carry out any other task assigned by the Directorate of Aviation related to aviation sector development, transaction advisory, bid process management, and routine departmental work.</li>\r\n</ol>', '<p><strong>Change Management</strong><br><br>Any change in the scope of work, team composition, or duration shall be subject to mutual agreement between Directorate of Aviation/CHiPS and the selected consultant and shall be documented through a formal amendment to the Work Order. In case of unavoidable substitution, the replacement personnel must possess qualifications and experience equivalent to or higher than those specified in the original team requirement.<br><br><strong>Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment<br><br></strong>The envisaged duration of the assigned is 24 calendar months, extendable as required. The resource may be extended as per requirement of project need. Deployment timelines will be governed as per the approved Resource Deployment Plan to be submitted by the selected consultant within 30 working days of issuance of the Work Order.</p>', '<ul>\r\n<li>\r\n<p><strong>Payment terms </strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Payment to selected bidder for the scope of work done will be released as per the following schedule.</li>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on man month basis as per the agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n<li>For reasons beyond the control of the selected bidder or CHiPS, as the case may be selected bidder shall be paid the requisite man month payment in the event that selected bidder has performed on its obligations in compliance with the terms of this contract</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Penalty terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>', 8, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their experience, if any, in a similar area of expertise (via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th>Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th>Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Work Plan, Activity Schedule, and Staffing Schedule</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such specific kind of a project</li>\r\n<li>Prior exposure in similar government projects</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Educational Qualification</li>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Experience of working in Government Projects</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.</li>\r\n<li>The last date for submission of response is <strong>08/10/2026 17:00</strong> Hrs. Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</li>\r\n<li>All pre-bid queries and proposal submissions shall be submitted through the Empanelment Portal (https://empl.cgstate.gov.in) only. Submissions through e-mail, portal messages, or any other mode shall not be accepted. Only submissions made through the respective provisions of the Empanelment Portal shall be considered.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EoI</li>\r\n<li>Copy of Approach and methodology presentation</li>\r\n<li>Resumes of resources proposed for the evaluation.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '555555', '2026-10-01 21:29:49', 3, 1, '2026-10-01 21:28:23', 94, '2026-10-01 21:29:49', NULL, '2026-10-01 21:39:24', 1, NULL, 0, 0, '2026-10-01', NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', '3rd Call Program Management Unit (PMU) for Technical Support and Transaction Advisory Support for Directorate of Aviation, Government of Chhattisgarh', '2026-10-01', NULL, '2026-10-08 17:00:00', NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Presentation and Interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-05-14', 0, 0, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/tyPItFCCOFIQGi8u5PAPWQE5kPVoFxpcBk4wOU2f.pdf', NULL, 0, 3, 0, 0, '1,2,3,4,5,7,8', 0, 0, 1, NULL, 'uploads/floated_eois/yEF4G7c8NTT9XPnuyLAkBNY6tbJEc08vRyjQWANr.pdf', 0, 1, 0, 0, 'uploads/notesheet_files/EQhKpxImgyxjpz1Ri0s6pyMXnmnSlde7OpGuZUl3.pdf', 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL),
(186, 0, 82, '', 0, 'ECONOMIC SURVEY', '10', '<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; letter-spacing: -.05pt; mso-font-width: 105%;\">The objective of the assignment is to provide assistance to Directorate of Economics &amp; Statistics under Chhattisgarh State Economic Survey Scheme.</span><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; letter-spacing: -.05pt; mso-font-width: 105%;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; letter-spacing: -.05pt; mso-font-width: 105%;\">CHiPS is inviting all empaneled agencies (as per the Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/ Empanelment/Consultancy Firms/2025RaipurDated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, ToR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; letter-spacing: -.05pt; mso-font-width: 105%;\">&nbsp;</span></p>', 2, 82, '2026-10-08 15:30:43', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, NULL, NULL, '<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">The team will undertake the following tasks, with the scope:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">a.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Report Writing and Documentation</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 1.25in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Development of methodology / compilation of IIP, CP! at state and sub state level and formulation and field work report on CPI and IIP For Report Writing and Data analysis.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 1.25in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Development of methodology/compilation/analysis/report generation of Annual Survey of Industries (ASI) at state and substate level and use it in the estimation of DDP (District Domestic Product), formulation and field work report on ASI. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt 1.25in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Formulation and field work report on Capital formation and saving by devising methodology, compilation analysis and report generation of Capital formation 4. Fulfill the gap between Data collection and Data processing at DES level with trust by analysis and preparation of NSS reports of district wise /subdistrict wise estimates of various parameters, Analysis and report preparation.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">b.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Study and Review</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo3; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 1.25in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Assess current schemes and programs implemented by DES, focusing on methods of data collection, validation, compilation, and analysis, including IT aspects. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo3; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt 1.25in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Evaluate data flow mechanisms from districts to DES and between DES and various line departments, preparing detailed reports.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">c.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">DES Portal and Data Dissemination</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt .75in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Review the DES portal and the data dissemination process, including the content, layout, design, visualization techniques, and release periodicity of various reports and publications.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">d.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Best Practices</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt .75in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Gather insights from national and international best practices and prepare improvements, considering emerging needs and standards report for further.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">e.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Liaison and Coordination</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt .75in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Maintain close communication with DES officers. District officials and other related departments for context understanding and development. Coordinate with implementing agencies, departments, and stakeholders, organizing periodic meetings and workshops. Suggest measures to remove bottlenecks and constraints for smooth implementation.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">f.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Training and Capacity Building</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt .75in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Support training programs for DES officers and officials as part of the capacity-building component.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">g.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Additional tasks</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Perform any additional work required to meet team objectives.</span></p>', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/W3Y3UnsFVEAUKhqSjzf6EzonafZUf53X8qLzNSpA.pdf', NULL, 0, 2, 0, 0, NULL, 1, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
INSERT INTO `eoi_request` (`requestid`, `projectid`, `userid`, `eoinumber`, `isgenerated`, `projecttitle`, `projectduration`, `projectobjective`, `categoryid`, `createdby`, `creationdate`, `isapproved`, `approvedby`, `approvedon`, `approvalremark`, `totalbudget`, `totaladmincharge`, `totalamount`, `operatingmargin`, `tax`, `admincharge`, `aboutproject`, `page_indexing`, `chips_objective`, `scopeofwork`, `anyother`, `termsandcondition`, `evaluation_index`, `evaluationprocess`, `criticalinformation`, `documentrequired`, `replywithremark`, `acceptanceotp`, `acceptancedatetime`, `eoistatus`, `sentby`, `senton`, `confirmedby`, `confirmedon`, `authletter`, `eoifloatdate`, `floatedby`, `presentationfile1`, `isfileuploaded1`, `iscommittee`, `floatdate`, `expirydate`, `issuername`, `engagementname`, `releasedate`, `prebidlastdate`, `deadlinedate`, `interviewdate`, `interview_place`, `selection_method`, `communicationaddress`, `eoiexpirydate`, `isinprebid`, `isordered`, `isupdated`, `authorizationletter`, `draftedeoi`, `isUpdateRequired`, `tier_choice`, `isInterviewSet`, `project_type`, `vendorids`, `iscancelled`, `approvalStatus`, `approvalClosed`, `approvalOtp`, `eoi_file`, `isExtended`, `isSecondCall`, `hasOldPreBid`, `oldRequestId`, `notesheet_file`, `isInterviewDone`, `isMomReceived`, `isDemandNoteRaised`, `isPaymentReceoved`, `isOrderFileReceived`, `corrigendum_file`, `corrigendum_date`, `corrigendum_remark`, `isClosed`, `closedOn`, `closure_file`, `eoi_resource_value`, `eoi_admincharge`, `eoi_operatingcost`, `eoi_tax`, `eoi_total_value`, `isCalculated`, `allowResourceAdd`, `addition_resource_letter`, `upload_time`) VALUES
(187, 0, 82, 'EoI/EMPL/CHiPS/DES/Advisory/2026', 1, 'Selection of Expert Advisory Services under Chhattisgarh State Economic Survey Scheme, Directorate of Economics & Statistics', '9', '<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -61.15pt; mso-text-indent-alt: -.25in; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 61.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\"><span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>I.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">About the Directorate of Economics &amp; Statistics</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt 61.15pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">The Directorate of Economics and Statistics was established on 1st November 2000 with the formation of the State Chhattisgarh after separation from Madhya Pradesh. The Directorate of Economics and Statistics is designated as a nodal agency for the State\'s various statistical activities. At the Districts level all districts have \"Districts Planning and Statistical Office\" working under DES and Block Level Investigators are working under districts offices. The various statistical activities co-ordination, area survey, and data collection/analysis on different subjects, tabulation and the representation of compiled data.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -61.15pt; mso-text-indent-alt: -.25in; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 61.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\"><span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span>II.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Major Responsibilities of DES</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 61.15pt;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Some of the major works of DES are as follows:<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">a.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">State Income: The primary job under State Income Division is of four folds ie, estimation of State Income, Capital. Formation and Public Finance and District Domestic Product. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">b.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">National Sample Survey (NSS): The National Statistical Office (NSO), Ministry of Statistics and Programme Implementation, Government of India, New Delhi conducts nation-wide sample surveys relating to various Socio-economic topics to collect data for planning and policy formulation 1958-59.Chhattisgarh state participated in the survey from 2001.<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">c.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Economic Survey: The Economic Survey is an evaluation of annual performance and initiative of Government and way forward for development prospective of the State which is placed in the Chhattisgarh Legislative Assembly on the eve of the Budget Session. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">d.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Economic Census: Economic Census is a Central Sector Scheme to count all entrepreneurial units located in the geographical boundaries of the country, to provide a frame for future follow up survey. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">e.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Vital Statistics: According to the birth-death registration Act 1969. Director of DES is designated as a Chief Registrar for Birth-death registration. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">f.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Annual Survey of Industries (ASI): Annual Survey of Industries (ASI) provides information to assess and evaluate, objectively and realistically, the changes in the growth, composition and structure of the organized manufacturing sector includes processes, repair services, gas and water supply and cold storage. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">g.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Index of Industrial Production (IIP): IIP is a macro-economic indicator of industrial growth that measures the short-term growth of the industrial sector of an economy as compared to a reference period. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">h.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">District Statistical Handbook: This is an annual publication of the districts which covers many sectors across the districts as well as blocks. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">i.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Census of Employees: The objective is to develop database of Civilian employees in Govt. and State PSUs and study growth of employment for manpower planning. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">j.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Publications Division: There are few statistical publications brought out by the DES regularly which may be seen at the DES website. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">k.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Basic Statistics for Local Level Development (BSLLD):<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span>The objective is to develop database on village level statistics on different parameters to aid local-level planning from all the revenue villages of the State through: </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Compilation of different development indicators. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">After Collection, Compilation, Survey, analysis, testing-give the actual socio-economic condition of the State. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Co-ordination among statistical activities of different departments. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 97.15pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Provide data/statistics to Government, Scholars, planners and researchers.</span></p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Arial MT\'; mso-font-width: 105%; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\">Provid</span></p>', 2, 82, '2026-10-09 16:56:56', 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 18, 5, NULL, '<p>1. Factsheet <br>2. Project Objective <br>3. Scope of Work <br>4. Team Composition <br>5. Team Requirements <br>6. Evaluation Process <br>7. Payment &amp; Penalty Terms <br>8. Critical Information <br>9. Documents Required To Participate In This EoI</p>', '<p><strong>Objective</strong></p>\r\n<p>CHiPS is inviting Tier-II empaneled agencies (as per Tender No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/ Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Team Requirement, Qualification, and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EoI.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Issuer/Address for business query and Correspondence</strong></p>\r\n<p>The CEO,<br>Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society, Raipur<br>State Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur,<br>Chhattisgarh&ndash;492001<br>Tel: +91-771-4014158; Fax: +91 771-40141581<br>Email: Empl.chips@cgchips.in, ceochips@nic.in</p>', '<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .5in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">1.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Objectives of the Assignment:</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">a.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">To initiate the Digital Reformation of DES</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">b.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">To strengthen the Data Robustness</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">c.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Addressing Data deficiencies</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">d.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Augmenting User Engagement</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo2; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">e.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Developing Organizational Competence</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo1; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .5in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">2.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Scope of Services</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">The team will undertake the following tasks, with the scope:</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">a.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Report Writing and Documentation</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo4; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 1.25in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Development of methodology / compilation of IIP, CP! at state and sub state level and formulation and field work report on CPI and IIP For Report Writing and Data analysis.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo4; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 1.25in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Development of methodology/compilation/analysis/report generation of Annual Survey of Industries (ASI) at state and substate level and use it in the estimation of DDP (District Domestic Product), formulation and field work report on ASI. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo4; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt 1.25in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Formulation and field work report on Capital formation and saving by devising methodology, compilation analysis and report generation of Capital formation 4. Fulfill the gap between Data collection and Data processing at DES level with trust by analysis and preparation of NSS reports of district wise /subdistrict wise estimates of various parameters, Analysis and report preparation.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">b.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Study and Review</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo5; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt 1.25in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Assess current schemes and programs implemented by DES, focusing on methods of data collection, validation, compilation, and analysis, including IT aspects. </span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo5; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt 1.25in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&bull;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Evaluate data flow mechanisms from districts to DES and between DES and various line departments, preparing detailed reports.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">c.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">DES Portal and Data Dissemination</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt .75in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Review the DES portal and the data dissemination process, including the content, layout, design, visualization techniques, and release periodicity of various reports and publications.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">d.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Best Practices</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt .75in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Gather insights from national and international best practices and prepare improvements, considering emerging needs and standards report for further.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">e.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Liaison and Coordination</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt .75in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Maintain close communication with DES officers. District officials and other related departments for context understanding and development. Coordinate with implementing agencies, departments, and stakeholders, organizing periodic meetings and workshops. Suggest measures to remove bottlenecks and constraints for smooth implementation.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">f.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Training and Capacity Building</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; margin: 0in -24.25pt 12.0pt .75in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Support training programs for DES officers and officials as part of the capacity-building component.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo3; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-fareast-font-family: \'Times New Roman\';\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">g.<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span></strong><!--[endif]--><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Additional tasks</span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: 0in; margin: 0in -24.25pt .0001pt .75in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\';\">Perform any additional work required to meet team objectives.</span></p>', '<h2 style=\"text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 2.0pt -24.25pt .0001pt .5in;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; color: black; mso-themecolor: text1; mso-font-width: 105%;\">Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment:</span></strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\"> </span></h2>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: -.25in; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; margin: 2.0pt -24.25pt .0001pt .5in;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: \'Times New Roman\',\'serif\'; mso-font-width: 105%;\">The envisaged duration of the assignment is till 20-08-2027 from the date of work order and will be extended if required.</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"margin-right: -24.25pt; text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">&nbsp;</span></p>', '<p><strong>Payment Terms</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The successful bidder shall submit the invoice for payment on a monthly basis.</li>\r\n<li>Each payment will be made only after the delivery of the corresponding deliverable and its acceptance by CHiPS.</li>\r\n<li>Taxes will be applicable as per prevailing government norms.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong>Penalty Terms&nbsp;</strong><br>Penalty, if any, shall be governed as per the agreed empanelment terms. <br><br>Important Note: All other terms and conditions of tender 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025 shall be applicable to this EoI.</p>', 7, '<ul>\r\n<li>CHiPS will constitute an Evaluation Committee whose decision will be final in the evaluation of the responses to the Expression of Interest. No correspondence will be entertained outside the process of negotiation/discussion with the Committee.</li>\r\n<li>A presentation will be made by the bidding company about their understanding of the proposed area of work and their experience, if any, in a similar area of expertise (via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>During the presentation by the companies, the Evaluation Committee will interview the proposed candidates (via Video Conference).</li>\r\n<li>The marking for presentation and interview will be done as follows:</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<table border=\"1\" width=\"100%\" cellspacing=\"0\" cellpadding=\"8\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th>Key Evaluation Criteria</th>\r\n<th>Bidder Presentation<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n<th>Candidate Interview<br>(50 Marks)</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Criteria</strong></td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Approach and Methodology</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of the Project Framework</li>\r\n<li>Quality of proposed methodology for such a specific kind of project</li>\r\n<li>Prior experience in project interaction with senior Government officials</li>\r\n<li>Prior exposure to Auditing Government projects</li>\r\n<li>Resource deployment at multiple government offices in multiple locations</li>\r\n<li>Understanding of key SLAs of project management</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n<td>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Suitability of profile</li>\r\n<li>Years of relevant experience</li>\r\n<li>Good understanding of project management best practices framework</li>\r\n<li>Ability to Negotiate / Persuade / Influence</li>\r\n<li>Strong ability to understand, deliberate, and report / monitor the key SLAs</li>\r\n<li>Excellent communication abilities</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Bidder agencies are advised to study this EoI document carefully before submitting their proposals in response to this EoI notice. Submission of a proposal in response to this notice shall be deemed to have been done after careful study and examination of this document with full understanding of its terms, conditions and implications.</li>\r\n<li>The last date for submission of response is dd/mm/yyyy 17:00 Hrs. Any response received after the above deadline will be rejected.</li>\r\n<li>All pre-bid queries and proposal submissions shall be submitted through the Empanelment Portal (https://empl.cgstate.gov.in) only. Any submission or communication received through e-mail, messages, or any mode other than the Empanelment Portal shall not be accepted or considered. For any other enquiries, please contact empl.chips@cgchips.in and empl_portal@cgchips.in.empl.chips@cgchips.in and empl_portal@cgchips.in.</li>\r\n</ul>', '<ul>\r\n<li>Signed copy of this EoI</li>\r\n<li>Copy of the Approach and Methodology Presentation.</li>\r\n<li>CVs of the resources who will appear for the interview.</li>\r\n</ul>', NULL, '348699', '2026-10-12 12:20:40', 2, 1, '2026-10-09 17:27:49', 82, '2026-10-12 12:20:40', NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, 'Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)', 'Expression of Interest (EoI) for Selection of Expert Advisory Services under Chhattisgarh State Economic Survey Scheme, Directorate of Economics & Statistics', NULL, NULL, NULL, NULL, 'To be informed later', 'Presentation and Interview of the candidates', 'Chief Executive Officer\r\nChhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS)\r\nState Data Centre Building, Near Police Control Room, Civil Lines, Raipur, Chhattisgarh-492001\r\nTel : 91771-404158\r\nEmail : ceochips@nic.in, empl.chips@cgchips.in', '2027-05-22', 0, 0, 0, 'uploads/authorizationletters/gXO5xPXi3q4LT0I5Q6OCMbnaO3t2FTDetZ4N9OX7.pdf', NULL, 0, 2, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 1, NULL, '', 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL, NULL, 0, NULL, NULL, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, 0, NULL, NULL);
