(42, 125, 'Special condition of contract changed from  to <p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>1. Change Management<br></strong></span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>The selected agency needs to give 2 weeks of advance notice to Chairman, DMFT, Balod for any change of deployed resource during the course of the assignment.</li>\r\n<li>The selected agency needs to ensure knowledge transfer and handover during change of any resource for smooth transition.</li>\r\n<li>The replacement of any resource should be approved by Chairman, DMFT, Balod</li>\r\n<li>Number of resources may be added based on project requirements.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>2. Duration of the Assignment</strong></span></p>\r\n<p>Government of Chhattisgarh intends to onboard an agency for an initial period of three (3) years, which may be extended further up to two (2) years based on performance and requirements.</p>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong>3. Deliverables</strong></span></p>\r\n<p>The Bidder should submit below mentioned key deliverables.</p>\r\n<table style=\"border-collapse: collapse; width: 100%;\" border=\"1\"><colgroup><col style=\"width: 33.3077%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.3077%;\"><col style=\"width: 33.3077%;\"></colgroup>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>S. No&nbsp; &nbsp;&nbsp;</td>\r\n<td>Deliverable</td>\r\n<td>Timeline</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td>1</td>\r\n<td>Monthly Progress Reports</td>\r\n<td>Monthly</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p><span style=\"font-size: 12pt;\"><strong><br>4. Deliverables</strong></span></p>\r\n<p>The envisaged duration of the assignment is 36 calendar months (3 year). The duration may be extended for another 24 months (2 year) as per the project need.</p><br>', '2026-03-06 13:44:14', 71, 1, '2026-03-06 13:44:37', 1),
(43, 126, 'Scope of work changed from <p><strong>Baseline Survey</strong><br>&bull; Conduct a comprehensive socio-economic and infrastructure baseline survey in<br>mining-affected areas of Korba.<br>&bull; Identify critical gaps in health, education, water, sanitation, livelihoods, and<br>infrastructure.<br>&bull; Map existing resources, community needs, and opportunities for sustainable<br>development.</p>\r\n<p><strong>Perspective &amp; Action Plans</strong><br>&bull; Prepare a 5-Year Perspective Plan for Korba district based on baseline findings and<br>consultations with tribal communities, local governance bodies, and sectoral<br>experts.<br>&bull; Develop Annual Action Plans aligned with DMF guidelines, PMKKKY objectives,<br>and district-level development priorities.<br>&bull; Ensure plans are inclusive, gender-sensitive, and responsive to the unique<br>challenges of mining-affected tribal populations</p>\r\n<p><strong>Programme Management Unit (PMU)</strong><br>&bull; Providing managerial support to the DMFT in sync with State DMF Rules and<br>Guidelines for implementing and monitoring projects/schemes under DMF Trust.<br>&bull; Providing assistance to DMF for efficient and effective allocation of resources for<br>development and welfare schemes for the mining-affected areas and people.<br>&bull; Sectoral support in major priority sectors such as (not limited to):<br>o Health and Nutrition: Strengthening PHCs, mobile health units, child health.<br>o Education: Infrastructure, digital learning, tribal education support</p>\r\n<p>o Drinking Water and Sanitation: Safe water access, sanitation coverage.<br>o Livelihoods: Skill development, SHG strengthening, agro-based enterprises.<br>o Infrastructure: Roads, electrification, housing, digital connectivity.<br>&bull; Providing guidance for project formulation, project designing, tender structuring,<br>and reporting.<br>&bull; Ensuring compliance with State DMF Rules, PMKKKY Guidelines, CGSPR, GFR<br>and other applicable statutory and administrative regulations, including<br>contractual compliance.<br>&bull; Providing strategic direction and innovative ideas for effective utilization of DMF<br>for comprehensive development of people in mining-affected areas.<br>&bull; Acting as an interface between Administrative (Line) Department/State and<br>District level Agencies for facilitating and expediting field-level implementation.<br>&bull; Acting as an interface between district administration and common public for<br>outreach of government schemes.<br>&bull; Collection of credible data from District level, Line Departments and other<br>stakeholders for convergence planning and fund optimization.<br>&bull; Support in bringing financial discipline in the DMFT including internal control,<br>procurement compliance, documentation, support in audit and statutory reviews.<br>&bull; Lead procurement management for DMF projects including preparation of Annual<br>Procurement Plan, drafting of RFPs/NITs, technical specifications, bid evaluation<br>support, contract finalization and monitoring of contractual obligations.<br>&bull; Ensuring transparent, competitive and value-for-money procurement processes<br>in accordance with applicable procurement rules and policies.<br>&bull; Facilitating generation of periodic MIS reports for concurrent monitoring of project<br>formulation, approvals, implementation progress, outputs and outcomes.<br>&bull; Documentation of best practices and creation of a data repository for crosslearning among implementing agencies.<br>&bull; Designing performance assessment frameworks to monitor convergence<br>activities undertaken by Line Departments.<br>&bull; Conducting periodic monitoring and evaluation of programmatic interventions,<br>quality control, ensuring value for money and financial accountability.<br>&bull; Support in management and maintenance of centralized web-based MIS on<br>convergence, and enhancement of the existing DMF Portal for real-time<br>monitoring.<br>&bull; Provide guidance in preparation of Annual Plan and Perspective Plan aligned with<br>the Comprehensive District Plan.<br>&bull; Conduct social audit/impact assessment studies of beneficiary villages.<br>&bull; Overall assessment of schemes &amp; benefits, identification of implementation gaps<br>and proposing corrective measures.<br>&bull; Any other task assigned by the District Collector.<br>Page 5 of 10<br>&bull; Provide technical and facilitation support to the DMF Trust Board and Executive<br>Committee for informed governance and oversight.<br>&bull; Develop and implement a comprehensive IEC strategy including target audience<br>segmentation, key messaging, communication channels, and annual<br>communication calendar aligned with the DMF Action Plan.<br>&bull; Maintain records of IEC activities and generate periodic reports on outreach<br>coverage and effectiveness.</p> to <ul>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: left;\"><strong>Baseline Survey</strong><br>&bull; Conduct a comprehensive socio-economic and infrastructure baseline survey in<br>mining-affected areas of Korba.<br>&bull; Identify critical gaps in health, education, water, sanitation, livelihoods, and<br>infrastructure.<br>&bull; Map existing resources, community needs, and opportunities for sustainable<br>development.</li>\r\n<li><strong>Perspective &amp; Action Plans</strong><br>&bull; Prepare a 5-Year Perspective Plan for Korba district based on baseline findings and<br>consultations with tribal communities, local governance bodies, and sectoral<br>experts.<br>&bull; Develope Annual Action Plans aligned with DMF guidelines, PMKKKY objectives,<br>and district-level development priorities.<br>&bull; Ensure plans are inclusive, gender-sensitive, and responsive to the unique<br>challenges of mining-affected tribal populations</li>\r\n<li><strong>Programme Management Unit (PMU)</strong><br>&bull; Providing managerial support to the DMFT in sync with State DMF Rules and<br>&nbsp; Guidelines for implementing and monitoring projects/schemes under DMF Trust.<br>&bull; Providing assistance to DMF for efficient and effective allocation of resources for<br>development and welfare schemes for the mining-affected areas and people.<br>&bull; Sectoral support in major priority sectors such as (not limited to):<br>o Health and Nutrition: Strengthening PHCs, mobile health units, child health.<br>o Education: Infrastructure, digital learning, tribal education support</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Drinking Water and Sanitation: Safe water access, sanitation coverage.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>o Livelihoods: Skill development, SHG strengthening, agro-based enterprises.<br>o Infrastructure: Roads, electrification, housing, digital connectivity.<br>&bull; Providing guidance for project formulation, project designing, tender structuring,<br>and reporting.<br>&bull; Ensuring compliance with State DMF Rules, PMKKKY Guidelines, CGSPR, GFR<br>and other applicable statutory and administrative regulations, including<br>contractual compliance.<br>&bull; Providing strategic direction and innovative ideas for effective utilization of DMF<br>for comprehensive development of people in mining-affected areas.<br>&bull; Acting as an interface between Administrative (Line) Department/State and<br>District level Agencies for facilitating and expediting field-level implementation.<br>&bull; Acting as an interface between district administration and common public for<br>outreach of government schemes.<br>&bull; Collection of credible data from District level, Line Departments and other<br>stakeholders for convergence planning and fund optimization.<br>&bull; Support in bringing financial discipline in the DMFT including internal control,<br>procurement compliance, documentation, support in audit and statutory reviews.<br>&bull; Lead procurement management for DMF projects including preparation of Annual<br>Procurement Plan, drafting of RFPs/NITs, technical specifications, bid evaluation<br>support, contract finalization and monitoring of contractual obligations.<br>&bull; Ensuring transparent, competitive and value-for-money procurement processes<br>in accordance with applicable procurement rules and policies.<br>&bull; Facilitating generation of periodic MIS reports for concurrent monitoring of project<br>formulation, approvals, implementation progress, outputs and outcomes.<br>&bull; Documentation of best practices and creation of a data repository for crosslearning among implementing agencies.<br>&bull; Designing performance assessment frameworks to monitor convergence<br>activities undertaken by Line Departments.<br>&bull; Conducting periodic monitoring and evaluation of programmatic interventions,<br>quality control, ensuring value for money and financial accountability.<br>&bull; Support in management and maintenance of centralized web-based MIS on<br>convergence, and enhancement of the existing DMF Portal for real-time<br>monitoring.<br>&bull; Provide guidance in preparation of Annual Plan and Perspective Plan aligned with<br>the Comprehensive District Plan.<br>&bull; Conduct social audit/impact assessment studies of beneficiary villages.<br>&bull; Overall assessment of schemes &amp; benefits, identification of implementation gaps<br>and proposing corrective measures.<br>&bull; Any other task assigned by the District Collector.<br>&bull; Provide technical and facilitation support to the DMF Trust Board and Executive<br>Committee for informed governance and oversight.<br>&bull; Develop and implement a comprehensive IEC strategy including target audience<br>segmentation, key messaging, communication channels, and annual<br>communication calendar aligned with the DMF Action Plan.<br>&bull; Maintain records of IEC activities and generate periodic reports on outreach<br>coverage and effectiveness.</p><br>', '2026-03-06 15:25:09', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 00:11:47', 1),
