 with applicable procurement rules and policies.<br>&bull; Facilitating generation of periodic MIS reports for concurrent monitoring of project<br>formulation, approvals, implementation progress, outputs and outcomes.<br>&bull; Documentation of best practices and creation of a data repository for crosslearning among implementing agencies.<br>&bull; Designing performance assessment frameworks to monitor convergence<br>activities undertaken by Line Departments.<br>&bull; Conducting periodic monitoring and evaluation of programmatic interventions,<br>quality control, ensuring value for money and financial accountability.<br>&bull; Support in management and maintenance of centralized web-based MIS on<br>convergence, and enhancement of the existing DMF Portal for real-time<br>monitoring.<br>&bull; Provide guidance in preparation of Annual Plan and Perspective Plan aligned with<br>the Comprehensive District Plan.<br>&bull; Conduct social audit/impact assessment studies of beneficiary villages.<br>&bull; Overall assessment of schemes &amp; benefits, identification of implementation gaps<br>and proposing corrective measures.<br>&bull; Any other task assigned by the District Collector.<br>&bull; Provide technical and facilitation support to the DMF Trust Board and Executive<br>Committee for informed governance and oversight.<br>&bull; Develop and implement a comprehensive IEC strategy including target audience<br>segmentation, key messaging, communication channels, and annual<br>communication calendar aligned with the DMF Action Plan.<br>&bull; Maintain records of IEC activities and generate periodic reports on outreach<br>coverage and effectiveness.</p><br>', '2026-03-06 15:49:11', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 00:11:34', 1),
(45, 127, 'Project objective changed from <p><strong>1. Background<br></strong>Chhattisgarh is actively strengthening its public health initiatives to improve health outcomes throughout the state. According to the fourth edition of NITI Aayog\'s Health Index for 2019- 20, Chhattisgarh has secured the 10th position among large states, underscoring its commitment to advancing healthcare accessibility, affordability and overall performance. Achieving the top position requires a strategic emphasis on critical areas, such as enhancing accessibility and affordability of essential services like preventive and diagnostic care. Ensuring health screening and doctor consultations in remote areas is essential for comprehensive healthcare coverage. Affordability of medicines is a key consideration, given the significant out-of-pocket expenses on drugs. Expanding the coverage of PMJAY to a larger population is crucial for achieving comprehensive healthcare goals. Given Chhattisgarh\'s substantial tribal population, a focused mission to eliminate sickle cell anaemia by also 2027 necessitates proper screening, counselling, and treatment measures.<br><br>Government of Chhattisgarh is looking for a suitable agency to provide strategic support to help realize the vision of a healthy state through a targeted approach encompassing access, and affordability of preventive and curative medical services through increasing reach and access to health services through setting up of Mobile clinics (for care), Jan Aushadhi Kendra (for medicine), access to affordable and quality medicine and OPD services, sickle cell anaemia screening (in line with National Sickle Cell Anaemia Elimination Mission (NSCEM) which aims to eliminate Sickle Cell Anaemia by 2047, dialysis centres, health screening for population and expansion of PMJAY to 1 crore eligible beneficiaries. This multifaceted approach aims to address various aspects of healthcare delivery and make significant strides in improving the overall health of the state.<br><br><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;1.1)</strong> Bidders are encouraged to inform themselves fully about the assignments and the conditions before submitting the Application by visiting Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s office, sending&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; written queries to Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh, and attending a pre-proposal conference on the date and time specified in this RFP Please note that no cost of any such visit is&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; reimbursable by Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh.&nbsp;<br><br><strong>&nbsp; &nbsp;1.2</strong> Bidders must read carefully the eligibility criteria (the &ldquo;Eligibility&rdquo;) provided in RFP and must meet these requirements.<br><br><br><strong>2. Brief description of the Selection Process<br></strong>The Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh has adopted a Single stage two envelope bid process (&ldquo;Selection Process&rdquo;) in evaluating the bids comprising Technical Bid (envelope -1) and financial bid (envelope- 2). In the firststage, a technical check would be carried out as specified in RFP and a list of shortlisted (qualifying bidders) will be made. Financial Bid of only shortlisted bidders will be opened and evaluated as specified in RFP. The selection of the bidder would be done on quality cum cost-based selection (QCBS).<br><br><strong>3. JV/Consortium<br></strong>Not Allowed<br><br><strong>4. Accessing/ Purchasing of Bid Documents<br>a)</strong> RFP documents can be seen on the website <strong>https://gem.gov.in</strong> If downloaded, then the bid processing fee has to be submitted along with the proposal as in RFP<br><strong>b)</strong> The RFP can be postponed or cancelled at any time due to administrative reasons and no claim shall be entertained on this account. Modifications/Amendments/Corrigendum, if any shall not be advertised in the newspaper but shall be published in the departmental website portal only. Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh reserves the right to change the terms and conditions, select/reject any application without assigning any reason thereof.<br><strong>c)</strong> Tender shall be submitted as per &ldquo;Instructions to Tenderers&rdquo; forming a part of the tender document.<br><strong>d)</strong> Any tender received without Earnest Money shall not be considered and shall be summarily rejected.<br><strong>e)</strong> The bidder may note that they are liable to be disqualified at any time during qualification process in case any of the information furnished by them is not found to be true. The decision of Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh in this regard shall be final and binding.<br><br><strong>5. Modification/Substitution/Withdrawal of Applications:<br></strong>Only applicable before the last date and time of submission of bid as per the data sheet. Any request received after that shall not be entertained and might lead to forfeiture of bid security along with other provisions applicable in the RFP.<strong><br></strong></p> to <p><strong>1. Background<br></strong>Chhattisgarh is actively strengthening its public health initiatives to improve health outcomes throughout the state. According to the fourth edition of NITI Aayog\'s Health Index for 2019- 20, Chhattisgarh has secured the 10th position among large states, underscoring its commitment to advancing healthcare accessibility, affordability and overall performance. Achieving the top position requires a strategic emphasis on critical areas, such as enhancing accessibility and affordability of essential services like preventive and diagnostic care. Ensuring health screening and doctor consultations in remote areas is essential for comprehensive healthcare coverage. Affordability of medicines is a key consideration, given the significant out-of-pocket expenses on drugs. Expanding the coverage of PMJAY to a larger population is crucial for achieving comprehensive healthcare goals. Given Chhattisgarh\'s substantial tribal population, a focused mission to eliminate sickle cell anaemia by also 2027 necessitates proper screening, counselling, and treatment measures.<br><br>Government of Chhattisgarh is looking for a suitable agency to provide strategic support to help realize the vision of a healthy state through a targeted approach encompassing access, and affordability of preventive and curative medical services through increasing reach and access to health services through setting up of Mobile clinics (for care), Jan Aushadhi Kendra (for medicine), access to affordable and quality medicine and OPD services, sickle cell anaemia screening (in line with National Sickle Cell Anaemia Elimination Mission (NSCEM) which aims to eliminate Sickle Cell Anaemia by 2047, dialysis centres, health screening for population and expansion of PMJAY to 1 crore eligible beneficiaries. This multifaceted approach aims to address various aspects of healthcare delivery and make significant strides in improving the overall health of the state.<br><br><strong>1.1)</strong> Bidders are encouraged to inform themselves fully about the assignments and the conditions before submitting the Application by visiting Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s office, sending written queries to Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh, and attending a pre-proposal conference on the date and time specified in this RFP Please note that no cost of any such visit is reimbursable by Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh. <br><br><strong>1.2</strong> Bidders must read carefully the eligibility criteria (the &ldquo;Eligibility&rdquo;) provided in RFP and must meet these requirements.<br><br><br><strong>2. Brief description of the Selection Process<br></strong>The Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh has adopted a Single stage two envelope bid process (&ldquo;Selection Process&rdquo;) in evaluating the bids comprising Technical Bid (envelope -1) and financial bid (envelope- 2). In the firststage, a technical check would be carried out as specified in RFP and a list of shortlisted (qualifying bidders) will be made. Financial Bid of only shortlisted bidders will be opened and evaluated as specified in RFP. The selection of the bidder would be done on quality cum cost-based selection (QCBS).<br><br><strong>3. JV/Consortium<br></strong>Not Allowed<br><br><strong>4. Accessing/ Purchasing of Bid Documents<br>a)</strong> RFP documents can be seen on the website <strong>https://gem.gov.in</strong> If downloaded, then the bid processing fee has to be submitted along with the proposal as in RFP<br><strong>b)</strong> The RFP can be postponed or cancelled at any time due to administrative reasons and no claim shall be entertained on this account. Modifications/Amendments/Corrigendum, if any shall not be advertised in the newspaper but shall be published in the departmental website portal only. Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh reserves the right to change the terms and conditions, select/reject any application without assigning any reason thereof.<br><strong>c)</strong> Tender shall be submitted as per &ldquo;Instructions to Tenderers&rdquo; forming a part of the tender document.<br><strong>d)</strong> Any tender received without Earnest Money shall not be considered and shall be summarily rejected.<br><strong>e)</strong> The bidder may note that they are liable to be disqualified at any time during qualification process in case any of the information furnished by them is not found to be true. The decision of Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh in this regard shall be final and binding.<br><br><strong>5. Modification/Substitution/Withdrawal of Applications:<br></strong>Only applicable before the last date and time of submission of bid as per the data sheet. Any request received after that shall not be entertained and might lead to forfeiture of bid security along with other provisions applicable in the RFP.<strong><br></strong></p><br>', '2026-03-07 13:52:58', 380, 1, '2026-03-10 14:16:24', 1),
(46, 127, 'Scope of work changed from <p><strong>1)</strong> Detailed description of the objectives, Scope of Services, Deliverables and other requirements relating to this Consultancy are specified in this RFP. In case a Bidder firm fulfils the condition of the RFP it can participate in the Selection Process. The term Bidder (the &ldquo;Bidder&rdquo;) means the firms applying under this RFP. The manner in which the Proposal is required to be submitted, evaluated and accepted is explained in this RFP. <br><br><strong>2)</strong> Bidders are advised that the pre-qualification of consultants shall be on the basis of an evaluation by the Authority through the Selection Process specified in this RFP. Bidders shall be deemed to have understood and agreed that no explanation or justification for any aspect of the Selection Process will be given and that the Authority&rsquo;s decisions are without any right of appeal whatsoever. <br><br><strong>3)</strong> The Bidder shall submit its Proposal in the form and manner specified in this Section of the RFP. The Technical and Financial proposals shall be submitted in the form as prescribed in the RFP. Upon selection, the Bidder shall be required to enter into an agreement with the Authority.<br><br><strong>Note: The resources shall be responsible for supporting and managing all National Programmes as well as State-specific programmes. </strong><strong>Any additional instructions or work assigned by the Director of Health Services shall be complied with.</strong></p> to <p><strong>1)</strong> Detailed description of the objectives, Scope of Services, Deliverables and other requirements relating to this Consultancy are specified in this RFP. In case a Bidder firm fulfils the condition of the RFP it can participate in the Selection Process. The term Bidder (the &ldquo;Bidder&rdquo;) means the firms applying under this RFP. The manner in which the Proposal is required to be submitted, evaluated and accepted is explained in this RFP. <br><br><strong>2)</strong> Bidders are advised that the pre-qualification of consultants shall be on the basis of an evaluation by the Authority through the Selection Process specified in this RFP. Bidders shall be deemed to have understood and agreed that no explanation or justification for any aspect of the Selection Process will be given and that the Authority&rsquo;s decisions are without any right of appeal whatsoever. <br><br><strong>3)</strong> The Bidder shall submit its Proposal in the form and manner specified in this Section of the RFP. The Technical and Financial proposals shall be submitted in the form as prescribed in the RFP. Upon selection, the Bidder shall be required to enter into an agreement with the Authority.<br><br><strong>Note: The resources shall be responsible for supporting and managing all National Programmes as well as State-specific programmes. </strong><strong>Any additional instructions or work assigned by the Director of Health Services shall also be complied with.</strong></p><br>', '2026-03-07 13:54:58', 380, 1, '2026-03-10 14:16:07', 1),
(47, 126, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Master&rsquo;s Degree (or<br>equivalent) in Management,<br>Development<br>Studies/Practice, Social<br>Work, or related field(s) from<br>a reputed<br>National/International<br>University/Institution.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum of 5 years of total<br>work experience related to<br>project management in<br>private/public/not-for-profit<br>sector.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum of 5 years of<br>experience in<br>implementation of<br>government<br>schemes/projects</li>\r\n</ul> to <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Master&rsquo;s Degree (or<br>equivalent) in Management,<br>Development<br>Studies/Practice, Social<br>Work, or related field(s) from<br>a reputed<br>National/International<br>University/Institution.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum of 7&nbsp; years of total<br>work experience related to<br>project management in<br>private/public/not-for-profit<br>sector.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum of 7 years of<br>experience in<br>implementation of<br>government<br>schemes/projects</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 09-03-2026, 11:21 AM', '2026-03-09 11:21:01', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 00:11:22', 1),
