(49, 126, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Master&rsquo;s Degree (or<br>equivalent) in Management,<br>Development<br>Studies/Practice, Social<br>Work, or related field(s).</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 3 years experience<br>in Social &amp; Livelihood<br>management.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 3 years experience<br>in implementation of<br>government<br>schemes/projects. &bull;<br>Expertise in Livelihood, Skill<br>Development, Education,<br>Environment Conservation,<br>Alternate/Renewable Energy<br>Development.</li>\r\n<li>Experience in ST dominated<br>areas.</li>\r\n</ul> to <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Master&rsquo;s Degree (or<br>equivalent) in Management,<br>Development<br>Studies/Practice, Social<br>Work, or related field(s).</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 5&nbsp; years experience<br>in Social &amp; Livelihood<br>management.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 5&nbsp; years experience<br>in implementation of<br>government<br>schemes/projects. &bull;<br>Expertise in Livelihood, Skill<br>Development, Education,<br>Environment Conservation,<br>Alternate/Renewable Energy<br>Development.</li>\r\n<li>Experience in ST dominated<br>areas.</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 09-03-2026, 11:22 AM', '2026-03-09 11:22:14', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 00:11:04', 1),
(50, 126, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <ul>\r\n<li>B.E./B.Tech in Civil<br>Engineering / B.Arch from<br>recognized<br>University/Institute.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 3 years experience<br>in design, estimation,<br>execution and supervision<br>of civil engineering projects.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 3 years experience<br>in government infrastructure<br>projects.</li>\r\n<li>Proficient in AutoCAD.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Expertise in Environment<br>Conservation, Watershed &amp;<br>Natural Resource<br>Management, Infrastructure<br>Development, Urban &amp; Town<br>Planning, Irrigation, Water<br>Harvestin</li>\r\n</ul> to <ul>\r\n<li>B.E./B.Tech in Civil<br>Engineering / B.Arch from<br>recognized<br>University/Institute.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 5&nbsp; years experience<br>in design, estimation,<br>execution and supervision<br>of civil engineering projects.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 5&nbsp; years experience<br>in government infrastructure<br>projects.</li>\r\n<li>Proficient in AutoCAD.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Expertise in Environment<br>Conservation, Watershed &amp;<br>Natural Resource<br>Management, Infrastructure<br>Development, Urban &amp; Town<br>Planning, Irrigation, Water<br>Harvestin</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 09-03-2026, 11:22 AM', '2026-03-09 11:22:41', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 00:10:57', 1),
(51, 126, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <ul>\r\n<li>Postgraduate degree in<br>Mass Communication,<br>Journalism, Social Work,<br>Development Studies or<br>related fields.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 5 years experience<br>in large-scale IEC<br>programmes for<br>Government/International<br>organizations.</li>\r\n</ul> to <ul>\r\n<li>Postgraduate degree in<br>Mass Communication,<br>Journalism, Social Work,<br>Development Studies or<br>related fields.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 3&nbsp; years experience<br>in large-scale IEC<br>programmes for<br>Government/International<br>organizations.</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 09-03-2026, 11:23 AM', '2026-03-09 11:23:09', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 00:10:50', 1),
(52, 126, 'Project objective changed from <p>&bull;<strong> As per Section 5 of PMKKKY Guidelines</strong>: Conduct a comprehensive baseline<br>survey in mining-affected areas and prepare a 5-Year Perspective Plan along with<br>Annual Action Plans to ensure systematic and need-based development<br>interventions.<br>&bull; <strong>As per PMKKKY Guideline, Section 2 </strong>- General Guidelines, Subsection (b): Since<br>DMF Korba has an annual collection exceeding INR 50 Crores, establish and<br>operate a Programme Management Unit (PMU) to provide planning, technical, and<br>monitoring support for effective implementation of DMF projects.<br>Strengthening institutional capacity through innovation, best practices, stakeholder<br>training, knowledge management, and technical support to the DMF Trust Board and<br>Executive Committee.<br><br></p> to <p>&bull; As per Section 5 of PMKKKY Guidelines: Conduct a comprehensive baseline survey in mining-affected areas and prepare a 5-Year Perspective Plan along with Annual Action Plans to ensure systematic and need-based development interventions.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; As per PMKKKY Guideline, Section 2 - General Guidelines, Subsection (b): Since DMF Korba has an annual collection exceeding INR 50 Crores, establish and operate a Programme Management Unit (PMU) to provide planning, technical, and monitoring support for effective implementation of DMF projects. Strengthening institutional capacity through innovation, best practices, stakeholder training, knowledge management, and technical support to the DMF Trust Board and Executive Committee.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p><br>Scope of work changed from <ul>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Baseline Survey</strong><br>&bull; Conduct a comprehensive socio-economic and infrastructure baseline survey in<br>mining-affected areas of Korba.<br>&bull; Identify critical gaps in health, education, water, sanitation, livelihoods, and<br>infrastructure.<br>&bull; Map existing resources, community needs, and opportunities for sustainable<br>development.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Perspective &amp; Action Plans</strong><br>&bull; Prepare a 5-Year Perspective Plan for Korba district based on baseline findings and<br>consultations with tribal communities, local governance bodies, and sectoral<br>experts.<br>&bull; Develope Annual Action Plans aligned with DMF guidelines, PMKKKY objectives,<br>and district-level development priorities.<br>&bull; Ensure plans are inclusive, gender-sensitive, and responsive to the unique<br>challenges of mining-affected tribal populations</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\"><strong>Programme Management Unit (PMU)</strong><br>&bull; Providing managerial support to the DMFT in sync with State DMF Rules and<br>&nbsp; Guidelines for implementing and monitoring projects/schemes under DMF Trust.<br>&bull; Providing assistance to DMF for efficient and effective allocation of resources for<br>development and welfare schemes for the mining-affected areas and people.<br>&bull; Sectoral support in major priority sectors such as (not limited to):&nbsp;<br>o Health and Nutrition: Strengthening PHCs, mobile health units, child health.<br>o Education: Infrastructure, digital learning, tribal education support.<br>o Drinking Water and Sanitation: Safe water access, sanitation coverage.<br>o Livelihoods: Skill development, SHG strengthening, agro-based enterprises.<br>o Infrastructure: Roads, electrification, housing, digital connectivity.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify; padding-left: 40px;\">&bull; Providing guidance for project formulation, project designing, tender structuring,<br>and reporting.<br>&bull; Ensuring compliance with State DMF Rules, PMKKKY Guidelines, CGSPR, GFR<br>and other applicable statutory and administrative regulations, including<br>contractual compliance.<br>&bull; Providing strategic direction and innovative ideas for effective utilization of DMF<br>for comprehensive development of people in mining-affected areas.<br>&bull; Acting as an interface between Administrative (Line) Department/State and<br>District level Agencies for facilitating and expediting field-level implementation.<br>&bull; Acting as an interface between district administration and common public for<br>outreach of government schemes.<br>&bull; Collection of credible data from District level, Line Departments and other<br>stakeholders for convergence planning and fund optimization.<br>&bull; Support in bringing financial discipline in the DMFT including internal control,<br>procurement compliance, documentation, support in audit and statutory reviews.<br>&bull; Lead procurement management for DMF projects including preparation of Annual<br>Procurement Plan, drafting of RFPs/NITs, technical specifications, bid evaluation<br>support, contract finalization and monitoring of contractual obligations.<br>&bull; Ensuring transparent, competitive and value-for-money procurement processes<br>in accordance with applicable procurement rules and policies.<br>&bull; Facilitating generation of periodic MIS reports for concurrent monitoring of project<br>formulation, approvals, implementation progress, outputs and outcomes.<br>&bull; Documentation of best practices and creation of a data repository for crosslearning among implementing agencies.<br>&bull; Designing performance assessment frameworks to monitor convergence<br>activities undertaken by Line Departments.<br>&bull; Conducting periodic monitoring and evaluation of programmatic interventions,<br>quality control, ensuring value for money and financial accountability.<br>&bull; Support in management and maintenance of centralized web-based MIS on<br>convergence, and enhancement of the existing DMF Portal for real-time<br>monitoring.<br>&bull; Provide guidance in preparation of Annual Plan and Perspective Plan aligned with<br>the Comprehensive District Plan.<br>&bull; Conduct social audit/impact assessment studies of beneficiary villages.<br>&bull; Overall assessment of schemes &amp; benefits, identification of implementation gaps<br>and proposing corrective measures.<br>&bull; Any other task assigned by the District Collector.<br>&bull; Provide technical and facilitation support to the DMF Trust Board and Executive<br>Committee for informed governance and oversight.<br>&bull; Develop and implement a comprehensive IEC strategy including target audience<br>segmentation, key messaging, communication channels, and annual<br>communication calendar aligned with the DMF Action Plan.<br>&bull; Maintain records of IEC activities and generate periodic reports on outreach<br>coverage and effectiveness.</p> to <p>Baseline Survey</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Conduct a comprehensive socio-economic and infrastructure baseline survey in mining-affected areas of Korba.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Identify critical gaps in health, education, water, sanitation, livelihoods, and infrastructure.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Map existing resources, community needs, and opportunities for sustainable development.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Perspective &amp; Action Plans</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Prepare a 5-Year Perspective Plan for Korba district based on baseline findings and consultations with tribal communities, local governance bodies, and sectoral experts.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Develope Annual Action Plans aligned with DMF guidelines, PMKKKY objectives, and district-level development priorities.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Ensure plans are inclusive, gender-sensitive, and responsive to the unique challenges of mining-affected tribal populations</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Programme Management Unit (PMU)</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Providing managerial support to the DMFT in sync with State DMF Rules and Guidelines for implementing and monitoring projects/schemes under DMF Trust.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Providing assistance to DMF for efficient and effective allocation of resources for development and welfare schemes for the mining-affected areas and people.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">Sectoral support in major priority sectors such as (not limited to):</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">o Health and Nutrition: Strengthening PHCs, mobile health units, child health.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">o Education: Infrastructure, digital learning, tribal education support.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">o Drinking Water and Sanitation: Safe water access, sanitation coverage.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">o Livelihoods: Skill development, SHG strengthening, agro-based enterprises.</li>\r\n<li style=\"text-align: justify;\">o Infrastructure: Roads, electrification, housing, digital connectivity.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Providing guidance for project formulation, project designing, tender structuring,&nbsp;and reporting.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Ensuring compliance with State DMF Rules, PMKKKY Guidelines, CGSPR, GFR&nbsp;and other applicable statutory and administrative regulations, including&nbsp;contractual compliance.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Providing strategic direction and innovative ideas for effective utilization of DMF&nbsp;for comprehensive development of people in mining-affected areas.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Acting as an interface between Administrative (Line) Department/State and&nbsp;District level Agencies for facilitating and expediting field-level implementation.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Acting as an interface between district administration and common public for&nbsp;outreach of government schemes.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Collection of credible data from District level, Line Departments and other&nbsp;stakeholders for convergence planning and fund optimization.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Support in bringing financial discipline in the DMFT including internal control,&nbsp;procurement compliance, documentation, support in audit and statutory reviews.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Lead procurement management for DMF projects including preparation of Annual&nbsp;Procurement Plan, drafting of RFPs/NITs, technical specifications, bid evaluation&nbsp;support, contract finalization and monitoring of contractual obligations.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Ensuring transparent, competitive and value-for-money procurement processes&nbsp;in accordance with applicable procurement rules and policies.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Facilitating generation of periodic MIS reports for concurrent monitoring of project&nbsp;formulation, approvals, implementation progress, outputs and outcomes.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Documentation of best practices and creation of a data repository for crosslearning among implementing agencies.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Designing performance assessment frameworks to monitor convergence&nbsp;activities undertaken by Line Departments.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Conducting periodic monitoring and evaluation of programmatic interventions,&nbsp;quality control, ensuring value for money and financial accountability.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Support in management and maintenance of centralized web-based MIS on&nbsp;convergence, and enhancement of the existing DMF Portal for real-time&nbsp;monitoring.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Provide guidance in preparation of Annual Plan and Perspective Plan aligned with&nbsp;the Comprehensive District Plan.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Conduct social audit/impact assessment studies of beneficiary villages.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Overall assessment of schemes &amp; benefits, identification of implementation gaps&nbsp;and proposing corrective measures.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Any other task assigned by the District Collector.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Provide technical and facilitation support to the DMF Trust Board and Executive&nbsp;Committee for informed governance and oversight.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Develop and implement a comprehensive IEC strategy including target audience&nbsp;segmentation, key messaging, communication channels, and annual&nbsp;communication calendar aligned with the DMF Action Plan.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">&bull; Maintain records of IEC activities and generate periodic reports on outreach coverage and effectiveness.</p><br>', '2026-03-10 12:16:44', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 14:03:20', 1),
(53, 127, 'Project name changed from Selection of Consulting firm for setting up of a Strategic Project Management Team for (SPMT) Directorate of Health Services, GoV of Chhattisgarh to For Providing PMU Services for Directorate of Health Services, Chhattisgarh<br>Project objective changed from <p><strong>1. Background<br></strong>Chhattisgarh is actively strengthening its public health initiatives to improve health outcomes throughout the state. According to the fourth edition of NITI Aayog\'s Health Index for 2019- 20, Chhattisgarh has secured the 10th position among large states, underscoring its commitment to advancing healthcare accessibility, affordability and overall performance. Achieving the top position requires a strategic emphasis on critical areas, such as enhancing accessibility and affordability of essential services like preventive and diagnostic care. Ensuring health screening and doctor consultations in remote areas is essential for comprehensive healthcare coverage. Affordability of medicines is a key consideration, given the significant out-of-pocket expenses on drugs. Expanding the coverage of PMJAY to a larger population is crucial for achieving comprehensive healthcare goals. Given Chhattisgarh\'s substantial tribal population, a focused mission to eliminate sickle cell anaemia by also 2027 necessitates proper screening, counselling, and treatment measures.<br><br>Government of Chhattisgarh is looking for a suitable agency to provide strategic support to help realize the vision of a healthy state through a targeted approach encompassing access, and affordability of preventive and curative medical services through increasing reach and access to health services through setting up of Mobile clinics (for care), Jan Aushadhi Kendra (for medicine), access to affordable and quality medicine and OPD services, sickle cell anaemia screening (in line with National Sickle Cell Anaemia Elimination Mission (NSCEM) which aims to eliminate Sickle Cell Anaemia by 2047, dialysis centres, health screening for population and expansion of PMJAY to 1 crore eligible beneficiaries. This multifaceted approach aims to address various aspects of healthcare delivery and make significant strides in improving the overall health of the state.<br><br><strong>1.1)</strong> Bidders are encouraged to inform themselves fully about the assignments and the conditions before submitting the Application by visiting Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s office, sending written queries to Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh, and attending a pre-proposal conference on the date and time specified in this RFP Please note that no cost of any such visit is reimbursable by Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh. <br><br><strong>1.2</strong> Bidders must read carefully the eligibility criteria (the &ldquo;Eligibility&rdquo;) provided in RFP and must meet these requirements.<br><br><br><strong>2. Brief description of the Selection Process<br></strong>The Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh has adopted a Single stage two envelope bid process (&ldquo;Selection Process&rdquo;) in evaluating the bids comprising Technical Bid (envelope -1) and financial bid (envelope- 2). In the firststage, a technical check would be carried out as specified in RFP and a list of shortlisted (qualifying bidders) will be made. Financial Bid of only shortlisted bidders will be opened and evaluated as specified in RFP. The selection of the bidder would be done on quality cum cost-based selection (QCBS).<br><br><strong>3. JV/Consortium<br></strong>Not Allowed<br><br><strong>4. Accessing/ Purchasing of Bid Documents<br>a)</strong> RFP documents can be seen on the website <strong>https://gem.gov.in</strong> If downloaded, then the bid processing fee has to be submitted along with the proposal as in RFP<br><strong>b)</strong> The RFP can be postponed or cancelled at any time due to administrative reasons and no claim shall be entertained on this account. Modifications/Amendments/Corrigendum, if any shall not be advertised in the newspaper but shall be published in the departmental website portal only. Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh reserves the right to change the terms and conditions, select/reject any application without assigning any reason thereof.<br><strong>c)</strong> Tender shall be submitted as per &ldquo;Instructions to Tenderers&rdquo; forming a part of the tender document.<br><strong>d)</strong> Any tender received without Earnest Money shall not be considered and shall be summarily rejected.<br><strong>e)</strong> The bidder may note that they are liable to be disqualified at any time during qualification process in case any of the information furnished by them is not found to be true. The decision of Director Health Services, Chhattisgarh in this regard shall be final and binding.<br><br><strong>5. Modification/Substitution/Withdrawal of Applications:<br></strong>Only applicable before the last date and time of submission of bid as per the data sheet. Any request received after that shall not be entertained and might lead to forfeiture of bid security along with other provisions applicable in the RFP.<strong><br></strong></p> to <p>In line with the state&rsquo;s aspirations and priority focus areas, the proposed SPMU will foster the health agenda in Chhattisgarh by providing strategic support to help realise the vision of a healthy state through a multi-pronged approach encompassing access and affordability of preventive and curative medical services through the under mentioned identified priority focus areas. The SPMU will work to achieve the following vision laid out by the State, for the Health Services / Infrastructure.</p><br>Scope of work changed from <p><strong>1)</strong> Detailed description of the objectives, Scope of Services, Deliverables and other requirements relating to this Consultancy are specified in this RFP. In case a Bidder firm fulfils the condition of the RFP it can participate in the Selection Process. The term Bidder (the &ldquo;Bidder&rdquo;) means the firms applying under this RFP. The manner in which the Proposal is required to be submitted, evaluated and accepted is explained in this RFP. <br><br><strong>2)</strong> Bidders are advised that the pre-qualification of consultants shall be on the basis of an evaluation by the Authority through the Selection Process specified in this RFP. Bidders shall be deemed to have understood and agreed that no explanation or justification for any aspect of the Selection Process will be given and that the Authority&rsquo;s decisions are without any right of appeal whatsoever. <br><br><strong>3)</strong> The Bidder shall submit its Proposal in the form and manner specified in this Section of the RFP. The Technical and Financial proposals shall be submitted in the form as prescribed in the RFP. Upon selection, the Bidder shall be required to enter into an agreement with the Authority.<br><br><strong>Note: The resources shall be responsible for supporting and managing all National Programmes as well as State-specific programmes. </strong><strong>Any additional instructions or work assigned by the Director of Health Services shall also be complied with.</strong></p> to <p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">1. Support for Ayushman Bharat Yojana and ancillary schemes</strong></strong><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">A. Fraud Detection and Management</strong></strong><br><br>&bull; Assist the Health Department in selecting an optimal tool/software solution. This will be through a comprehensive fraud software solution to detect fraud proactively, develop algorithms that can be used on a large volume of data to identify suspect transactions and entities for checking and validating claims (a zero-tolerance approach to any kind of fraud viz. suspect/non-genuine medical treatment claims, impersonation and upcoding of treatment packages/procedures etc.)<br>&bull; Ensure that the chosen software tool/software aligns with the program\'s requirements and objectives to prevent, detect, mitigate associated risks and deter fraud. Provision of strategic guidance to the Department in selecting appropriate tools and technologies for fraud management.<br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">B. SOP Development</strong></strong><br><br>&bull; Technical inputs for preparation of robust Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) tailored to the specific needs of fraud detection within Ayushman Bharat for overall monitoring and implementation.<br>&bull; Ensuring SOPs are comprehensive, efficient, and in compliance with industry standards.<br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">C. Training and Supervision</strong></strong><br><br>&bull; Technical inputs for development and delivery of structured training programs for department staff involved in fraud detection and control.<br>&bull; Oversee implementation of a supervision framework with robust monitoring mechanisms to ensure continuous feedback and support.<br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">D. Feedback Loop Implementation</strong></strong><br><br>&bull; Establishment of a continuous feedback loop to address evolving challenges and adapt strategies for efficient fraud detection.<br>&bull; Enable ongoing support to the department for refining and optimizing fraud control measures.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">2. Project Report and Infrastructure Planning</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">A. Project Report Preparation</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Monitoring of the implementation plan and providing monthly Progress reports within the 2-year initial contract of the SPMU</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">In order to undertake the above, the SPMU will prepare the following deliverables:</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Initial Project Concept Notes (Seven)</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Detailed Report for operationalization of the approved projects including the business and operational model (including PPP where applicable)</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Request for Proposals &ndash; Bid Management</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Response Evaluation Report including draft agreements</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Implementation Roadmap</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Monthly Progress Reports</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">B. Infrastructure Planning</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; To assist the State/Department to establish in every Division a Chhattisgarh Institute of Medical Science (CIMS), on the lines of All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS) leveraging aspects like PMJAY as well as CGHS pricing.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Provide an enabling environment to set up 500 new Jan Aushadhi Kendras in the State to provide affordable and quality medicines.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; In line with National Sickle Cell Anaemia Elimination Mission (NSCEM) which aims to eliminate Sickle Cell Anaemia by 2047, provide technical guidance to establish a &ldquo;Sickle Cell Screening Centre&rdquo; in every Block (in a phased manner) of the State to eradicate the problem from its root and issue a Sickle Cell Anaemia Card to every citizen in the State.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Provide strategic directions to establish in every Division a Chhattisgarh Institute of Medical Science (CIMS), on the lines of All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS) and to operationalize a Dialysis Centre across the State.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Strategic planning and design of the required infrastructure to support the successful implementation of the project.<br>&bull; Detailed proposals for the necessary physical and technological infrastructure, ensuring alignment with project goals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Assist the State to launch 150 Mobile Clinics, in which there will be a volunteer from a tribal community for public awareness. This will ensure health services are accessible to the last mile via efficient Mobile clinics in state in a phased manner ensuring accessibility and affordability to remote and tribal areas.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Any other program, as decided by Director Health Services.<br><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">3. Public Private Partnership (PPP)</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Preparation and Submission of Detailed Project Report for securing budgetary support as well as PPP model &ndash; where applicable as well as VGF financing, as applicable by GoI/MoF</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Evaluation and incorporation of Public-Private Partnership (PPP) elements where applicable, ensuring alignment with project goals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Comprehensive analysis of potential partnerships, risk assessments, and recommended structures for successful PPP implementation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Development of a detailed business and operational model for the approved projects, outlining key processes and strategies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Integration of best practices and industry standards to ensure optimal project functionality.<br><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">4. Project Management and Key Performance Indicator (KPI)</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">A. Project Management</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; To facilitate expansion of PMJAY to expand to 100% beneficiaries in State. Generate evidence to facilitate the State and to create and enabling environment to increase efficiency of schemes.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; To bring into force the Chhattisgarh Medical Establishments Act to reduce the compliance burden on less than 50-bed hospitals and nursing homes in the State.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; To make a provision for annual free comprehensive physical health check-ups of all senior citizens in the State ensuring efficient primary health care delivery.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Assist the State/Department to effectively plan to double the Budget allocation of the Health Department.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Preparation of an Initial Project Concept Notes (PCN) for operationalization of the Project objective (the objectives are expected to be converted into seven project reports).</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Preparation of the Procurement Roadmap and execution of the same including pre-bid, RFP, and model concession/contract agreements for implementing the projects.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Supporting the Selection of the Implementation Agency and preparing a detailed plan for its implementation with the selected agency.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Develop and implement a comprehensive project management plan outlining key milestones, timelines, and deliverables.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Establish efficient communication channels and protocols to facilitate seamless coordination among project stakeholders.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Provide ongoing monitoring and reporting on project progress, identifying and mitigating potential risks.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Any other project, as decided by Director Health Services.<br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">B. Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) and Coordination with the Central Government</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Preparation of an operational and business plan for implementing the approved concept notes that would also include coordination and discussion with GoI and institutions like CGHS, ESIC, and NHA.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Facilitate seamless coordination and communication with relevant authorities within the central government.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Coordination for Budgetary approval for agencies outside of the State Government</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Ensure compliance with central government policies and guidelines governing the project.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Oversee and maintain detailed documentation to track and analyse project performance against established KPIs.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Collaborate with stakeholders to define clear and measurable KPIs aligned with project objectives.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Design and implement a robust KPI tracking system to measure project performance against established benchmarks.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Regularly assess and report on KPI outcomes, making data-driven recommendations for continuous improvement.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">C. Other Responsibilities</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; The PMU is typically a team responsible for overseeing and managing various aspects of the project. They are expected to handle any extra work or adjustments that arise during the project\'s execution.<br><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">5. Key Indicators/Deliverables (KPIs)</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of persons with Ayushman cards.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of families with atleast one Ayushman card.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of active Public hospitals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of active Private hospitals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; No. of claim, paid, pending and rejected.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Amount of claim, paid, pending and rejected.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of complaints resolved (as received in SNA or 104).</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of complaints resolved (as received in CGRMS and CPGRAMS).</p><br>', '2026-03-10 13:22:03', 380, 1, '2026-03-10 14:15:54', 1),
(54, 127, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Resource duration changed from 12 to 6.<br>on 10-03-2026, 01:23 PM', '2026-03-10 13:23:15', 380, 1, '2026-03-10 14:15:42', 1),
(55, 127, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <ul>\r\n<li>Master in management/public policy/finance/Chartered Accountant</li>\r\n<li>At least 5+ years of work experience in procurement in Govt. Sector/PSUs Procurement Expert</li>\r\n<li>Relevant experience with government stakeholders in India (Health Insurance, Health Financing, Contracts, IEC, Procurement &amp; PPP)</li>\r\n</ul> to <ul>\r\n<li>Master in management/public policy/finance/Chartered Accountant</li>\r\n<li>At least 5+ years of work experience in procurement in Govt. Sector/PSUs Procurement Expert</li>\r\n<li>Relevant experience with government stakeholders in India (Health Insurance, Health Financing, Contracts, IEC, Procurement & PPP)</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>Remark changed from <p>Financial Expert (Full Time at Raipur)</p> to <p>Finance Expert (Full Time at Raipur)</p>.<br>on 10-03-2026, 01:28 PM', '2026-03-10 13:28:55', 380, 1, '2026-03-10 14:15:34', 1),
