District level Agencies for facilitating and expediting field-level implementation.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Acting as an interface between district administration and common public for outreach of government schemes.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Collection of credible data from District level, Line Departments and other stakeholders for convergence planning and fund optimization.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Support in bringing financial discipline in the DMFT including internal control, procurement compliance, documentation, support in audit and statutory reviews.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Lead procurement management for DMF projects including preparation of Annual Procurement Plan, drafting of RFPs/NITs, technical specifications, bid evaluation support, contract finalization and monitoring of contractual obligations.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Ensuring transparent, competitive and value-for-money procurement processes in accordance with applicable procurement rules and policies.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Facilitating generation of periodic MIS reports for concurrent monitoring of project formulation, approvals, implementation progress, outputs and outcomes.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Documentation of best practices and creation of a data repository for cross-learning among implementing agencies.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Designing performance assessment frameworks to monitor convergence activities undertaken by Line Departments.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Conducting periodic monitoring and evaluation of programmatic interventions, quality control, ensuring value for money and financial accountability.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Support in management and maintenance of centralized web-based MIS on convergence, and enhancement of the existing DMF Portal for real-time monitoring.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Provide guidance in preparation of Annual Plan and Perspective Plan aligned with the Comprehensive District Plan.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Conduct social audit/impact assessment studies of beneficiary villages.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Overall assessment of schemes &amp; benefits, ident