ing generation of periodic MIS reports for concurrent monitoring of project formulation, approvals, implementation progress, outputs and outcomes.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Documentation of best practices and creation of a data repository for cross-learning among implementing agencies.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Designing performance assessment frameworks to monitor convergence activities undertaken by Line Departments.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Conducting periodic monitoring and evaluation of programmatic interventions, quality control, ensuring value for money and financial accountability.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Support in management and maintenance of centralized web-based MIS on convergence, and enhancement of the existing DMF Portal for real-time monitoring.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Provide guidance in preparation of Annual Plan and Perspective Plan aligned with the Comprehensive District Plan.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Conduct social audit/impact assessment studies of beneficiary villages.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Overall assessment of schemes &amp; benefits, identification of implementation gaps and proposing corrective measures.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Any other task assigned by the District Collector.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Provide technical and facilitation support to the DMF Trust Board and Executive Committee for informed governance and oversight.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Develop and implement a comprehensive IEC strategy including target audience segmentation, key messaging, communication channels, and annual communication calendar aligned with the DMF Action Plan.</p>\r\n<p>&bull; Maintain records of IEC activities and generate periodic reports on outreach coverage and effectiveness.</p><br>', '2026-03-10 14:05:37', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 14:10:30', 1),
(65, 126, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Master&rsquo;s Degree (or<br>equivalent) in Management,<br>Development<br>Studies/Practice, Social<br>Work, or related field(s) from<br>a reputed<br>National/International<br>University/Institution.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum of 7&nbsp; years of total<br>work experience related to<br>project management in<br>private/public/not-for-profit<br>sector.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum of 7 years of<br>experience in<br>implementation of<br>government<br>schemes/projects</li>\r\n</ul> to <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Master&rsquo;s Degree (or equivalent) in Management,&nbsp;Development&nbsp;Studies/Practice, Social&nbsp;Work, or related field(s) from&nbsp;a reputed&nbsp;National/International&nbsp;University/Institution.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum of 7&nbsp; years of total work experience related to&nbsp;project management in&nbsp;private/public/not-for-profit&nbsp;sector.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum of 7 years of&nbsp;experience in&nbsp;implementation of&nbsp;government&nbsp;schemes/projects</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 10-03-2026, 02:06 PM', '2026-03-10 14:06:12', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 14:10:20', 1),
(66, 126, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Master&rsquo;s Degree (or<br>equivalent) in Management,<br>Development<br>Studies/Practice, Social<br>Work, or related field(s).</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 5years experience<br>in Health &amp; Nutrition<br>management.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 5 years experience<br>in implementation of government<br>schemes/projects.<br>&bull; Expertise in Drinking Water,<br>Sanitation, Healthcare,<br>Hospital Administration,<br>Nutrition, Women &amp; Child Development.</li>\r\n</ul> to <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Master&rsquo;s Degree (or equivalent) in Management,&nbsp;Development&nbsp;Studies/Practice, Social&nbsp;Work, or related field(s).</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 5years experience&nbsp;in Health &amp; Nutrition&nbsp;management.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 5 years experience in implementation of government schemes/projects.</li>\r\n<li>Expertise in Drinking Water,&nbsp;Sanitation, Healthcare,&nbsp;Hospital Administration,&nbsp;Nutrition, Women &amp; Child Development.</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 10-03-2026, 02:07 PM', '2026-03-10 14:07:05', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 14:10:11', 1);
INSERT INTO `log_eoi_updates` (`recordid`, `requestid`, `particular`, `updatedon`, `updatedby`, `isviewed`, `viewedon`, `viewedby`) VALUES
(67, 126, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Master&rsquo;s Degree (or<br>equivalent) in Management,<br>Development<br>Studies/Practice, Social<br>Work, or related field(s).</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 5&nbsp; years experience<br>in Social &amp; Livelihood<br>management.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 5&nbsp; years experience<br>in implementation of<br>government<br>schemes/projects. &bull;<br>Expertise in Livelihood, Skill<br>Development, Education,<br>Environment Conservation,<br>Alternate/Renewable Energy<br>Development.</li>\r\n<li>Experience in ST dominated<br>areas.</li>\r\n</ul> to <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Master&rsquo;s Degree (or equivalent) in Management,&nbsp;Development&nbsp;Studies/Practice, Social&nbsp;Work, or related field(s).</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 5&nbsp; years experience in Social &amp; Livelihood&nbsp;management.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 5&nbsp; years experience in implementation of&nbsp;government&nbsp;schemes/projects. &bull;&nbsp;Expertise in Livelihood, Skill&nbsp;Development, Education,&nbsp;Environment Conservation,&nbsp;Alternate/Renewable Energy&nbsp;Development.</li>\r\n<li>Experience in ST dominated&nbsp;areas.</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 10-03-2026, 02:07 PM', '2026-03-10 14:07:48', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 14:10:03', 1),
(68, 126, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <ul>\r\n<li>B.E./B.Tech in Civil<br>Engineering / B.Arch from<br>recognized<br>University/Institute.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 5&nbsp; years experience<br>in design, estimation,<br>execution and supervision<br>of civil engineering projects.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 5&nbsp; years experience<br>in government infrastructure<br>projects.</li>\r\n<li>Proficient in AutoCAD.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Expertise in Environment<br>Conservation, Watershed &amp;<br>Natural Resource<br>Management, Infrastructure<br>Development, Urban &amp; Town<br>Planning, Irrigation, Water<br>Harvestin</li>\r\n</ul> to <ul>\r\n<li>B.E./B.Tech in Civil&nbsp;Engineering / B.Arch from&nbsp;recognized&nbsp;University/Institute.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 5&nbsp; years experience in design, estimation,&nbsp;execution and supervision&nbsp;of civil engineering projects.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 5&nbsp; years experience in government infrastructure&nbsp;projects.</li>\r\n<li>Proficient in AutoCAD.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Expertise in Environment Conservation, Watershed &amp;&nbsp;Natural Resource&nbsp;Management, Infrastructure&nbsp;Development, Urban &amp; Town&nbsp;Planning, Irrigation, Water&nbsp;Harvesting.</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 10-03-2026, 02:08 PM', '2026-03-10 14:08:22', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 14:09:56', 1),
(69, 126, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Masters Degree in Finance<br>or Chartered Accountant<br>(CA) or equivalent<br><br></li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 5 years experience<br>in accounting, auditing and<br>financial management in Government/Development<br>Sector/reputed NGOs.</li>\r\n<li>Familiarity with Government<br>of Chhattisgarh accounting<br>standards.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Knowledge of<br>CGSPR/GFR/e-procurement<br>system/Tender drafting and<br>Bid-evaluation/ contract<br>management</li>\r\n</ul> to <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Masters Degree in Finance or Chartered Accountant&nbsp;(CA) or equivalent</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 5 years experience in accounting, auditing and&nbsp;financial management in Government/Development&nbsp;Sector/reputed NGOs.</li>\r\n<li>Familiarity with Government&nbsp;of Chhattisgarh accounting&nbsp;standards.</li>\r\n<li>Knowledge of&nbsp;CGSPR/GFR/e-procurement&nbsp;system/Tender drafting and&nbsp;Bid-evaluation/ contract&nbsp;management</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 10-03-2026, 02:08 PM', '2026-03-10 14:08:56', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 14:09:49', 1),
(70, 126, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <ul>\r\n<li>Postgraduate degree in<br>Mass Communication,<br>Journalism, Social Work,<br>Development Studies or<br>related fields.</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 3&nbsp; years experience<br>in large-scale IEC<br>programmes for<br>Government/International<br>organizations.</li>\r\n</ul> to <ul>\r\n<li>Postgraduate degree in&nbsp;Mass Communication,&nbsp;Journalism, Social Work,&nbsp;Development Studies or&nbsp;related fields.</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 3&nbsp; years experience in large-scale IEC&nbsp;programmes for&nbsp;Government/International&nbsp;organizations.</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 10-03-2026, 02:09 PM', '2026-03-10 14:09:19', 108, 1, '2026-03-10 14:09:43', 1),
(71, 127, 'Scope of work changed from <p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">1. Support for Ayushman Bharat Yojana and ancillary schemes</strong></strong><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">A. Fraud Detection and Management</strong></strong><br><br>&bull; Assist the Health Department in selecting an optimal tool/software solution. This will be through a comprehensive fraud software solution to detect fraud proactively, develop algorithms that can be used on a large volume of data to identify suspect transactions and entities for checking and validating claims (a zero-tolerance approach to any kind of fraud viz. suspect/non-genuine medical treatment claims, impersonation and upcoding of treatment packages/procedures etc.)<br><br>&bull; Ensure that the chosen software tool/software aligns with the program\'s requirements and objectives to prevent, detect, mitigate associated risks and deter fraud. Provision of strategic guidance to the Department in selecting appropriate tools and technologies for fraud management.<br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">B. SOP Development</strong></strong><br><br>&bull; Technical inputs for preparation of robust Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) tailored to the specific needs of fraud detection within Ayushman Bharat for overall monitoring and implementation.<br><br>&bull; Ensuring SOPs are comprehensive, efficient, and in compliance with industry standards.<br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">C. Training and Supervision</strong></strong><br><br>&bull; Technical inputs for development and delivery of structured training programs for department staff involved in fraud detection and control.<br><br>&bull; Oversee implementation of a supervision framework with robust monitoring mechanisms to ensure continuous feedback and support.<br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">D. Feedback Loop Implementation</strong></strong><br><br>&bull; Establishment of a continuous feedback loop to address evolving challenges and adapt strategies for efficient fraud detection.<br><br>&bull; Enable ongoing support to the department for refining and optimizing fraud control measures.<br><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">2. Project Report and Infrastructure Planning</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">A. Project Report Preparation</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Monitoring of the implementation plan and providing monthly Progress reports within the 2-year initial contract of the SPMU</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">In order to undertake the above, the SPMU will prepare the following deliverables:</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Initial Project Concept Notes (Seven)</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Detailed Report for operationalization of the approved projects including the business and operational model (including PPP where applicable)</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Request for Proposals &ndash; Bid Management</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Response Evaluation Report including draft agreements</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Implementation Roadmap</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Monthly Progress Reports</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">B. Infrastructure Planning</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; To assist the State/Department to establish in every Division a Chhattisgarh Institute of Medical Science (CIMS), on the lines of All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS) leveraging aspects like PMJAY as well as CGHS pricing.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Provide an enabling environment to set up 500 new Jan Aushadhi Kendras in the State to provide affordable and quality medicines.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; In line with National Sickle Cell Anaemia Elimination Mission (NSCEM) which aims to eliminate Sickle Cell Anaemia by 2047, provide technical guidance to establish a &ldquo;Sickle Cell Screening Centre&rdquo; in every Block (in a phased manner) of the State to eradicate the problem from its root and issue a Sickle Cell Anaemia Card to every citizen in the State.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Provide strategic directions to establish in every Division a Chhattisgarh Institute of Medical Science (CIMS), on the lines of All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS) and to operationalize a Dialysis Centre across the State.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Strategic planning and design of the required infrastructure to support the successful implementation of the project.<br>&bull; Detailed proposals for the necessary physical and technological infrastructure, ensuring alignment with project goals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Assist the State to launch 150 Mobile Clinics, in which there will be a volunteer from a tribal community for public awareness. This will ensure health services are accessible to the last mile via efficient Mobile clinics in state in a phased manner ensuring accessibility and affordability to remote and tribal areas.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Any other program, as decided by Director Health Services.<br><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">3. Public Private Partnership (PPP)</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Preparation and Submission of Detailed Project Report for securing budgetary support as well as PPP model &ndash; where applicable as well as VGF financing, as applicable by GoI/MoF</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Evaluation and incorporation of Public-Private Partnership (PPP) elements where applicable, ensuring alignment with project goals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Comprehensive analysis of potential partnerships, risk assessments, and recommended structures for successful PPP implementation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Development of a detailed business and operational model for the approved projects, outlining key processes and strategies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Integration of best practices and industry standards to ensure optimal project functionality.<br><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">4. Project Management and Key Performance Indicator (KPI)</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">A. Project Management</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; To facilitate expansion of PMJAY to expand to 100% beneficiaries in State. Generate evidence to facilitate the State and to create and enabling environment to increase efficiency of schemes.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; To bring into force the Chhattisgarh Medical Establishments Act to reduce the compliance burden on less than 50-bed hospitals and nursing homes in the State.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; To make a provision for annual free comprehensive physical health check-ups of all senior citizens in the State ensuring efficient primary health care delivery.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Assist the State/Department to effectively plan to double the Budget allocation of the Health Department.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Preparation of an Initial Project Concept Notes (PCN) for operationalization of the Project objective (the objectives are expected to be converted into seven project reports).</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Preparation of the Procurement Roadmap and execution of the same including pre-bid, RFP, and model concession/contract agreements for implementing the projects.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Supporting the Selection of the Implementation Agency and preparing a detailed plan for its implementation with the selected agency.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Develop and implement a comprehensive project management plan outlining key milestones, timelines, and deliverables.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Establish efficient communication channels and protocols to facilitate seamless coordination among project stakeholders.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Provide ongoing monitoring and reporting on project progress, identifying and mitigating potential risks.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Any other project, as decided by Director Health Services.<br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">B. Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) and Coordination with the Central Government</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Preparation of an operational and business plan for implementing the approved concept notes that would also include coordination and discussion with GoI and institutions like CGHS, ESIC, and NHA.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Facilitate seamless coordination and communication with relevant authorities within the central government.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Coordination for Budgetary approval for agencies outside of the State Government</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Ensure compliance with central government policies and guidelines governing the project.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Oversee and maintain detailed documentation to track and analyse project performance against established KPIs.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Collaborate with stakeholders to define clear and measurable KPIs aligned with project objectives.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Design and implement a robust KPI tracking system to measure project performance against established benchmarks.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Regularly assess and report on KPI outcomes, making data-driven recommendations for continuous improvement.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">C. Other Responsibilities</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; The PMU is typically a team responsible for overseeing and managing various aspects of the project. They are expected to handle any extra work or adjustments that arise during the project\'s execution.<br><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">5. Key Indicators/Deliverables (KPIs)</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of persons with Ayushman cards.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of families with atleast one Ayushman card.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of active Public hospitals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of active Private hospitals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; No. of claim, paid, pending and rejected.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Amount of claim, paid, pending and rejected.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of complaints resolved (as received in SNA or 104).</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of complaints resolved (as received in CGRMS and CPGRAMS).</p> to <p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">1. Support for Ayushman Bharat Yojana and ancillary schemes</strong></strong><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">A. Fraud Detection and Management</strong></strong><br><br>&bull; Assist the Health Department in selecting an optimal tool/software solution. This will be through a comprehensive fraud software solution to detect fraud proactively, develop algorithms that can be used on a large volume of data to identify suspect transactions and entities for checking and validating claims (a zero-tolerance approach to any kind of fraud viz. suspect/non-genuine medical treatment claims, impersonation and upcoding of treatment packages/procedures etc.)<br><br>&bull; Ensure that the chosen software tool/software aligns with the program\'s requirements and objectives to prevent, detect, mitigate associated risks and deter fraud. Provision of strategic guidance to the Department in selecting appropriate tools and technologies for fraud management.<br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\"><br>B. SOP Development</strong></strong><br><br>&bull; Technical inputs for preparation of robust Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs) tailored to the specific needs of fraud detection within Ayushman Bharat for overall monitoring and implementation.<br><br>&bull; Ensuring SOPs are comprehensive, efficient, and in compliance with industry standards.<br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\"><br>C. Training and Supervision</strong></strong><br><br>&bull; Technical inputs for development and delivery of structured training programs for department staff involved in fraud detection and control.<br><br>&bull; Oversee implementation of a supervision framework with robust monitoring mechanisms to ensure continuous feedback and support.<br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\"><br>D. Feedback Loop Implementation</strong></strong><br><br>&bull; Establishment of a continuous feedback loop to address evolving challenges and adapt strategies for efficient fraud detection.<br><br>&bull; Enable ongoing support to the department for refining and optimizing fraud control measures.<br><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">2. Project Report and Infrastructure Planning<br><br></strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">A. Project Report Preparation</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Monitoring of the implementation plan and providing monthly Progress reports within the 2-year initial contract of the SPMU</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">In order to undertake the above, the SPMU will prepare the following deliverables:</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Initial Project Concept Notes (Seven)</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Detailed Report for operationalization of the approved projects including the business and operational model (including PPP where applicable)</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Request for Proposals &ndash; Bid Management</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Response Evaluation Report including draft agreements</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Implementation Roadmap</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Monthly Progress Reports<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">B. Infrastructure Planning</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; To assist the State/Department to establish in every Division a Chhattisgarh Institute of Medical Science (CIMS), on the lines of All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS) leveraging aspects like PMJAY as well as CGHS pricing.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Provide an enabling environment to set up 500 new Jan Aushadhi Kendras in the State to provide affordable and quality medicines.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; In line with National Sickle Cell Anaemia Elimination Mission (NSCEM) which aims to eliminate Sickle Cell Anaemia by 2047, provide technical guidance to establish a &ldquo;Sickle Cell Screening Centre&rdquo; in every Block (in a phased manner) of the State to eradicate the problem from its root and issue a Sickle Cell Anaemia Card to every citizen in the State.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Provide strategic directions to establish in every Division a Chhattisgarh Institute of Medical Science (CIMS), on the lines of All India Institute of Medical Sciences (AIIMS) and to operationalize a Dialysis Centre across the State.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Strategic planning and design of the required infrastructure to support the successful implementation of the project.<br>&bull; Detailed proposals for the necessary physical and technological infrastructure, ensuring alignment with project goals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Assist the State to launch 150 Mobile Clinics, in which there will be a volunteer from a tribal community for public awareness. This will ensure health services are accessible to the last mile via efficient Mobile clinics in state in a phased manner ensuring accessibility and affordability to remote and tribal areas.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Any other program, as decided by Director Health Services.<br><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">3. Public Private Partnership (PPP)</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Preparation and Submission of Detailed Project Report for securing budgetary support as well as PPP model &ndash; where applicable as well as VGF financing, as applicable by GoI/MoF</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Evaluation and incorporation of Public-Private Partnership (PPP) elements where applicable, ensuring alignment with project goals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Comprehensive analysis of potential partnerships, risk assessments, and recommended structures for successful PPP implementation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Development of a detailed business and operational model for the approved projects, outlining key processes and strategies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Integration of best practices and industry standards to ensure optimal project functionality.<br><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">4. Project Management and Key Performance Indicator (KPI)<br><br></strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">A. Project Management</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; To facilitate expansion of PMJAY to expand to 100% beneficiaries in State. Generate evidence to facilitate the State and to create and enabling environment to increase efficiency of schemes.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; To bring into force the Chhattisgarh Medical Establishments Act to reduce the compliance burden on less than 50-bed hospitals and nursing homes in the State.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; To make a provision for annual free comprehensive physical health check-ups of all senior citizens in the State ensuring efficient primary health care delivery.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Assist the State/Department to effectively plan to double the Budget allocation of the Health Department.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Preparation of an Initial Project Concept Notes (PCN) for operationalization of the Project objective (the objectives are expected to be converted into seven project reports).</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Preparation of the Procurement Roadmap and execution of the same including pre-bid, RFP, and model concession/contract agreements for implementing the projects.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Supporting the Selection of the Implementation Agency and preparing a detailed plan for its implementation with the selected agency.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Develop and implement a comprehensive project management plan outlining key milestones, timelines, and deliverables.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Establish efficient communication channels and protocols to facilitate seamless coordination among project stakeholders.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Provide ongoing monitoring and reporting on project progress, identifying and mitigating potential risks.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Any other project, as decided by Director Health Services.<br><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">B. Key Performance Indicators (KPIs) and Coordination with the Central Government</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Preparation of an operational and business plan for implementing the approved concept notes that would also include coordination and discussion with GoI and institutions like CGHS, ESIC, and NHA.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Facilitate seamless coordination and communication with relevant authorities within the central government.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Coordination for Budgetary approval for agencies outside of the State Government</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Ensure compliance with central government policies and guidelines governing the project.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Oversee and maintain detailed documentation to track and analyse project performance against established KPIs.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Collaborate with stakeholders to define clear and measurable KPIs aligned with project objectives.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Design and implement a robust KPI tracking system to measure project performance against established benchmarks.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Regularly assess and report on KPI outcomes, making data-driven recommendations for continuous improvement.<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\"><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">C. Other Responsibilities</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; The PMU is typically a team responsible for overseeing and managing various aspects of the project. They are expected to handle any extra work or adjustments that arise during the project\'s execution.<br><br><br><strong><strong class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__textBold\">5. Key Indicators/Deliverables (KPIs)</strong></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of persons with Ayushman cards.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of families with atleast one Ayushman card.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of active Public hospitals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of active Private hospitals.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; No. of claim, paid, pending and rejected.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; Amount of claim, paid, pending and rejected.</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of complaints resolved (as received in SNA or 104).</p>\r\n<p class=\"PlaygroundEditorTheme__paragraph\">&bull; % of complaints resolved (as received in CGRMS and CPGRAMS).</p><br>', '2026-03-10 14:21:51', 380, 1, '2026-03-10 14:22:10', 1),
