(79, 126, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Masters Degree in Finance or Chartered Accountant&nbsp;(CA) or equivalent</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 5 years experience in accounting, auditing and financial management in Government/Development Sector/reputed NGOs.</li>\r\n<li>Familiarity with Government&nbsp;of Chhattisgarh accounting&nbsp;standards.</li>\r\n<li>Knowledge of&nbsp;CGSPR/GFR/e-procurement&nbsp;system/Tender drafting and&nbsp;Bid-evaluation/ contract&nbsp;management</li>\r\n</ul> to <ul>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Masters Degree in Finance or Chartered Accountant&nbsp;(CA) or equivalent</li>\r\n<li>&nbsp;Minimum 3 years experience in accounting, auditing and financial management in Government/Development Sector/reputed NGOs.</li>\r\n<li>Familiarity with Government&nbsp;of Chhattisgarh accounting&nbsp;standards.</li>\r\n<li>Knowledge of&nbsp;CGSPR/GFR/e-procurement&nbsp;system/Tender drafting and&nbsp;Bid-evaluation/ contract&nbsp;management</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 10-03-2026, 06:19 PM', '2026-03-10 18:19:49', 108, 1, '2026-03-11 17:05:16', 1),
(80, 128, 'Project objective changed from <p>CHIPS is inviting all empaneled agencies (as per No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firms/2025 Raipur, Dated 20/02/2025) to submit a proposal based on Evaluation Criteria, Scope of Work, Proposed Team, Qualification, TOR and Deployment Duration as mentioned in this EOI. Tender The primary objective of the selected firm is to provide technical, governance, financial, legal, and social sector support to DMF JC for optimal utilization of DMF funds in accordance with state guidelines, district priorities, and principles of transparency, accountability, and sustainability.</p> to <p>The Selection of firm for District Mineral Foundation Trust (DMFT), Janjgir-Champa District, will provide professional support to ensure effective planning, execution, monitoring, and evaluation of DMFT programs aimed at welfare in mining-affected areas.</p><br>Scope of work changed from <p>The selected agency shall assist the district authorities in preparation of the Five-Year Perspective Plan and Annual Action Plans for effective utilization of District Mineral Foundation (DMF) JC funds ensuring systematic and comprehensive coverage of all affected areas and beneficiaries.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>1. Baseline Assessment and Data Collection&nbsp;<br>&bull; Conduct a baseline survey in the concerned district through appropriate methodologies.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Engage with Gram Sabhas, local bodies, community representatives, and relevant stakeholders to&nbsp;<br>identify development gaps and priority needs.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Review and utilize any existing surveys, studies, or reports prepared by government departments,&nbsp;<br>wherever available.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Prepare a comprehensive Needs Assessment Report highlighting key development priorities and&nbsp;<br>sectoral gaps.&nbsp;<br>2. Preparation of Five-Year Perspective Plan&nbsp;<br>&bull; Based on survey findings and identified development gaps, prepare a strategic Five-Year&nbsp;<br>Perspective Plan for the district.&nbsp;<br>&bull; The plan shall consider available DMF funds, expected future accruals, and district development&nbsp;<br>priorities.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Ensure that the perspective plan outlines sector-wise development strategies, project pipelines,&nbsp;<br>and implementation frameworks.&nbsp;<br>3. Sectoral Planning&nbsp;<br>The perspective plan shall cover priority sectors, including but not limited to:&nbsp;<br>&bull; Drinking Water&nbsp;<br>&bull; Health&nbsp;<br>&bull; Education&nbsp;<br>&bull; Women and Child Welfare&nbsp;<br>&bull; Roads&nbsp;<br>&bull; Irrigation&nbsp;<br>&bull; Other relevant development sectors&nbsp;<br>&bull; Each sector shall include specific objectives, proposed interventions, expected outcomes, and&nbsp;<br>estimated budgets.&nbsp;<br>4. Preparation of Annual Action Plans&nbsp;<br>&bull; Break down the Five-Year Perspective Plan into year-wise Annual Action Plans.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Annual plans shall include specific projects, timelines, cost estimates, and implementation&nbsp;<br>responsibilities.&nbsp;<br>&bull; The annual plan shall also consider performance and achievements of previous years while&nbsp;<br>setting priorities for the upcoming year.&nbsp;<br>5. Stakeholder Consultation and Validation&nbsp;<br>&bull; Facilitate consultations with district administration, line departments, Gram Sabhas, and other&nbsp;<br>stakeholders during plan preparation.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Incorporate feedback received from stakeholders to ensure that the plans reflect local&nbsp;<br>development needs and priorities.&nbsp;<br>6. Documentation and Submission&nbsp;<br>&bull; Prepare and submit comprehensive reports and presentations for the Five-Year Perspective Plan&nbsp;<br>and Annual Action Plans.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Provide all relevant data sets, survey results, and analytical documentation used in preparation of&nbsp;<br>the plans.&nbsp;<br>7. Support in Approval Process&nbsp;<br>&bull; Assist the district administration in presenting the plans before the DMF Governing Council for&nbsp;<br>approval.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Provide necessary clarifications, documentation, and revisions as required during the approval&nbsp;<br>process.&nbsp;</p> to <p>The selected agency shall assist the district authorities in preparation of the Five-Year Perspective Plan and Annual Action Plans for effective utilization of District Mineral Foundation (DMF) JC funds ensuring systematic and comprehensive coverage of all affected areas and beneficiaries.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>1. Baseline Assessment and Data Collection</strong>&nbsp;<br>&bull; Conduct a baseline survey in the concerned district through appropriate methodologies.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Engage with Gram Sabhas, local bodies, community representatives, and relevant stakeholders to identify development gaps and priority needs.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Review and utilize any existing surveys, studies, or reports prepared by government departments, wherever available.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Prepare a comprehensive Needs Assessment Report highlighting key development priorities and sectoral gaps.&nbsp;<br><strong>2. Preparation of Five-Year Perspective Plan&nbsp;</strong><br>&bull; Based on survey findings and identified development gaps, prepare a strategic Five-Year Perspective Plan for the district.&nbsp;<br>&bull; The plan shall consider available DMF funds, expected future accruals, and district development priorities.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Ensure that the perspective plan outlines sector-wise development strategies, project pipelines, and implementation frameworks.&nbsp;<br><strong>3. Sectoral Planning&nbsp;</strong><br>The perspective plan shall cover priority sectors, including but not limited to:&nbsp;<br>&bull; Drinking Water&nbsp;<br>&bull; Health&nbsp;<br>&bull; Education&nbsp;<br>&bull; Women and Child Welfare&nbsp;<br>&bull; Roads&nbsp;<br>&bull; Irrigation&nbsp;<br>&bull; Other relevant development sectors&nbsp;<br>&bull; Each sector shall include specific objectives, proposed interventions, expected outcomes, and estimated budgets.&nbsp;<br><strong>4. Preparation of Annual Action Plans&nbsp;</strong><br>&bull; Break down the Five-Year Perspective Plan into year-wise Annual Action Plans.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Annual plans shall include specific projects, timelines, cost estimates, and implementation responsibilities.&nbsp;<br>&bull; The annual plan shall also consider performance and achievements of previous years while setting priorities for the upcoming year.&nbsp;<br><strong>5. Stakeholder Consultation and Validation&nbsp;</strong><br>&bull; Facilitate consultations with district administration, line departments, Gram Sabhas, and other stakeholders during plan preparation.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Incorporate feedback received from stakeholders to ensure that the plans reflect local development needs and priorities.&nbsp;<br><strong>6. Documentation and Submission</strong>&nbsp;<br>&bull; Prepare and submit comprehensive reports and presentations for the Five-Year Perspective Plan and Annual Action Plans.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Provide all relevant data sets, survey results, and analytical documentation used in preparation of the plans.&nbsp;<br><strong>7. Support in Approval Process&nbsp;</strong><br>&bull; Assist the district administration in presenting the plans before the DMF Governing Council for approval.&nbsp;<br>&bull; Provide necessary clarifications, documentation, and revisions as required during the approval process.&nbsp;</p><br>', '2026-03-13 12:01:46', 112, 1, '2026-03-13 12:02:09', 1),
