(103, 131, 'Project objective changed from <p class=\"p1\">Atal Monitoring Portal (AMP) is the State&rsquo;s integrated monitoring platform for departmental KPIs, schemes, and district performance. Phase II strengthens data reliability, enables dynamic KPIs, embeds exception‑based monitoring and action‑tracking, and institutionalizes usage across governance levels, with the State PMU providing strategic program management under Department of Good Governance and Convergence (DoGGC) and technical coordination with CHiPS.</p> to <p class=\"p1\">Atal Monitoring Portal (AMP) is the State&rsquo;s integrated monitoring platform for departmental KPIs, schemes, and district performance. Phase II strengthens data reliability, enables dynamic KPIs, embeds exception‑based monitoring and action‑tracking, and institutionalizes usage across governance levels, with the State PMU providing strategic program management under Department of Good Governance and Convergence (DoGGC).</p><br>Scope of work changed from <p class=\"p1\">A Statelevel Project Management Unit (PMU) shall be positioned under the Department of Good Governance &amp; Convergence (DoGGC) for facilitating structured implementation of AMP Phase II. The PMU will consist of six domain specialists providing governance, data, performance, technical and capacitybuilding support. Operating under DoGGC and in coordination with line departments, the PMU will anchor system facilitation, KPI governance, platform improvement support, and actiontracking functions required for Statewide adoption and compliance. The PMU will function in the following activities:</p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The State PMU will support coordinated implementation of AMP Phase II under the direction of DoGGC.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will strengthen data governance by standardizing definitions, validation rules and reporting timelines across Departments and Districts.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will anchor KPI rationalization by reviewing existing indicators and enabling dynamic addition, modification or retirement of KPIs.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will ensure accurate and timely data validation on AMP and coordinate resolution of data gaps and inconsistencies.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will facilitate review readiness through improved exceptionbased monitoring, drilldowns and comparative insights needed for administrative reviews.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will coordinate with CHiPS on system integrations, performance optimization, security protocols and accesscontrol requirements.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will support implementation of workflow and actiontracking mechanisms to monitor followup actions arising from Statelevel reviews.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will drive Statewide adoption of AMP by conducting structured trainings, demonstrations and capacitybuilding programs.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will promote uniform and consistent use of AMP dashboards, workflows and reporting formats across administrative units.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will provide ongoing usersupport and handholding to Departments and Districts for operational usage of AMP</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will track platform usage, reporting discipline and KPI update status, and flag deviations for corrective action.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will maintain complete documentation, logs and compliance records required for monitoring and governance oversight.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will gather feedback from Departments and Districts and provide recommendations for system/process improvements.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will ensure alignment of AMP operations with governance priorities issued by DoGGC.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li2\">The PMU will support interoperability and MISAMP integration activities as required for seamless data flow.</li>\r\n</ul> to <p class=\"p1\">A Statelevel Project Management Unit (PMU) shall be positioned under the Department of Good Governance &amp; Convergence (DoGGC) for facilitating structured implementation of AMP Phase II. The PMU will consist of six domain specialists providing governance, data, performance, technical and capacitybuilding support. Operating under DoGGC and in coordination with line departments, the PMU will anchor system facilitation, KPI governance, platform improvement support, and actiontracking functions required for Statewide adoption and compliance. The PMU will function in the following activities:</p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The State PMU will support coordinated implementation of AMP Phase II under the direction of DoGGC, ensuring alignment of all operations with governance priorities.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will strengthen data governance by standardizing definitions, validation rules and reporting timelines across Departments and Districts.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will anchor KPI rationalization by identifying schemes, source data and KPIs for CM and Departmental Dashboards, coordinating with Departments to define and map KPIs, and enabling dynamic addition, modification or retirement of KPIs.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will ensure accurate and timely data validation on AMP, review work delivered by the System Integrator, validate data received from Departments and published on dashboards and portals, and coordinate resolution of data gaps and inconsistencies.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will facilitate review readiness through improved exception-based monitoring, drill-downs and comparative insights needed for administrative reviews.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will coordinate with the existing SI on system integrations, API integrations with nodal agencies (state/central), performance optimization, security protocols and access control requirements, and support interoperability and MIS-AMP integration for seamless data flow.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will support implementation of workflow and action tracking mechanisms to monitor follow-up actions arising from State level reviews.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will drive State-wide adoption of AMP by conducting structured trainings, demonstrations and capacity building programs, and provide ongoing user support and handholding to Departments and Districts for operational usage.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will promote uniform and consistent use of AMP dashboards, workflows and reporting formats across all administrative units.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will manage project monitoring and coordination with Districts, Departments and CMO, including coordination with District Collectors and their teams for dashboard and data entry portal activities.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will track platform usage, reporting discipline and KPI update status, and flag deviations for corrective action.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will conduct Unit, System and UAT testing of any new developed components/changes and submit reports accordingly; validate work milestone completion and recommend payments including for change requests issued to the SI and O&amp;M activities.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will coordinate and review the work given District governance data expert, validate their MPR&rsquo;s, invoices and put up with recommendation</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will maintain complete documentation, logs and compliance records required for monitoring and governance oversight.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">The PMU will gather feedback from Departments and Districts, create and present updates to various stakeholders, and provide recommendations for system and process improvements.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Any other work assigned by DoGGC.</li>\r\n</ul><br>Special condition of contract changed from <p><strong>Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment<br></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The duration of the assignment is 12 months from the date of work order. The duration of the project may be extended based on agreement between the selected consulting firm, CHiPS and Department of Good Governance and Convergence, Government of Chhattisgarh.&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>&nbsp;</strong></p> to <p><strong>4. Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment<br></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The duration of the assignment is 12 months from the date of work order. The duration of the project may be extended based on agreement between the selected consulting firm and Department of Good Governance and Convergence, Government of Chhattisgarh.&nbsp;<br><br><strong>5. Indicative Minimum Eligibility Criteria</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The above qualifications/experience are <strong>indicative minimums</strong> consistent with the <strong>AMP DPR </strong>functions (data governance, KPI rationalization, technical coordination with SI, capacity building, review enablement, workflows, security/compliance). DoGGC may verify original documents/certifications at the time of interview/selection<strong>&nbsp;</strong></p><br>', '2026-03-24 14:54:22', 78, 1, '2026-03-24 15:16:06', 1),
(104, 131, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <p class=\"p1\"><strong>Educational Qualification</strong></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li2\">Any Graduation AND Master’s in Public Policy/ Public Administration / Management / IT / Data / Economics (or equivalent)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class=\"p2\"><strong>Preferred Experience </strong></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li3\">Minimum 2 years of relevant experience in managing Reforms/ Policy Advisory projects/government performance management systems, largescale institutional reform initiatives, KPIdriven governance mechanisms, and digital governance Projects.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>Work Profile</strong></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Lead implementation of AMP PhaseII under DoGGC.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Coordinate all Departments, Districts and CHiPS for data governance, KPI updates and system operations.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Manage PMU workflows, timelines, compliance and risk mitigation.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Provide oversight on performance monitoring, exception handling, and reviewreadiness.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Ensure adherence to State guidelines and governance protocols.</li>\r\n</ul> to <p class=\"p1\"><strong>Educational Qualification</strong></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Any Graduation And Master&rsquo;s in Public Policy/ Public Administration / Management / IT / Data / Economics (or equivalent)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class=\"p2\"><strong>Preferred Experience </strong></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Minimum 5 years of relevant experience in managing Reforms/ Policy Advisory projects/government performance management systems, largescale institutional reform initiatives, KPIdriven governance mechanisms, and digital governance Projects.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>Work Profile</strong></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Lead implementation of AMP PhaseII under DoGGC.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Coordinate all Departments, Districts and CHiPS for data governance, KPI updates and system operations.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Manage PMU workflows, timelines, compliance and risk mitigation.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Provide oversight on performance monitoring, exception handling, and reviewreadiness.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Ensure adherence to State guidelines and governance protocols.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Undertake handholding support to the user departments about AMP and conduct capacity building program</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 24-03-2026, 02:57 PM', '2026-03-24 14:57:24', 78, 1, '2026-03-24 15:15:57', 1),
