 take appropriate legal and administrative action for any breach of <span class=\"s2\">confidentiality.</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">CHiPS reserve the right to accept or reject any or all proposals without assigning any <span class=\"s2\">reason.</span></li>\r\n</ul> to <p><strong>1. Change</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><span class=\"s2\"><strong>Management</strong></span></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li3\">The selected agency needs to give 1 (One) Month of advance notice to CHiPS for any change of deployed resource during the course of the assignment.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li4\">The selected agency needs to ensure knowledge transfer and handover during<span class=\"s5\"> the </span>change of any resource for a smooth transition.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li5\">The replacement of any resource should be approved by <span class=\"s2\">CHiPS</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><strong style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">2. Duration</strong><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\"><strong> </strong></span><strong style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\">of the</strong><span class=\"s1\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\"><strong> </strong></span><span class=\"s2\" style=\"font-family: -apple-system, BlinkMacSystemFont, \'Segoe UI\', Roboto, Oxygen, Ubuntu, Cantarell, \'Open Sans\', \'Helvetica Neue\', sans-serif;\"><strong>Assignment</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The initial engagement is for 12 months from Work Order issuance. The assignment will be initially valid for the mentioned period from the date of issuance of the Work Order. CHiPS may extend the Agreement, terms and conditions and monetary value as per the Tender No. 160137 /CEO/ CHiPS/ EMPL/ Application and Website development /2024 dated 18/10/2024.</p>\r\n<p><strong>3. HR</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><span class=\"s2\"><strong>Policy</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The selected candidate shall work on the payroll of the empanelled agency. The empanelled agency shall manage the HR {Salary, PF, leaves (as per CHIPS Policy) and other compliances} of the selected resources (As per Empanelment of Manpower Service Provider Firms for Government of Chhattisgarh for a period of 3 years RFP &amp; Agreement).</p>\r\n<p><strong>4. Termination Clause</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p4\">Termination will be done as per Empanelment of Manpower Service Provider Firms for Government of Chhattisgarh for a period of 3 years RFP &amp; Agreement</p>\r\n<p>5. <strong>Confidentiality</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><span class=\"s2\"><strong>Clause</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The selected agency and its deployed personnel shall treat all information, documents, and data accessed or obtained during the course of this assignment&mdash;whether oral, written, or in electronic forms strictly confidential.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">The agency shall ensure <span class=\"s5\">that:</span></p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li4\">No information pertaining to video conferencing sessions, network configurations, login credentials, IP schemas, bandwidth details, or any other operational or administrative activity at CM House or CHiPS Office is disclosed, shared, published, or reproduced in any form without prior written consent from CHiPS.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li5\">Confidentiality obligations shall continue to apply even after the termination or completion of the assignment.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li5\">Any breach of confidentiality shall be treated as a serious violation, and CHiPS reserves the right to initiate legal and administrative action, including termination of contract and blacklisting from future assignments.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li5\">CHiPS reserves the right to take appropriate legal and administrative action for any breach of <span class=\"s2\">confidentiality.</span></li>\r\n<li class=\"li6\">CHiPS reserve the right to accept or reject any or all proposals without assigning any <span class=\"s2\">reason.</span></li>\r\n</ul><br>', '2026-04-02 22:40:08', 69, 1, '2026-04-02 22:40:21', 1),
(114, 135, 'Project objective changed from <p class=\"p1\">The Government of Chhattisgarh envisions transforming the State into a globally recognized knowledge society, committed to improving citizens&rsquo; quality of life through high-quality education, healthcare, enhanced agricultural productivity, and employment generation by promoting IT and Electronics industries. Achieving this vision hinges on providing robust, high-speed broadband connectivity as a fundamental right, enabling inclusive access to digital services across urban and rural geographies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">While urban areas have witnessed substantial broadband penetration, rural regions continue to suffer a pronounced digital divide due to the lack of viable business cases for private sector investment. The State recognizes the urgent need to bridge this gap through government-led initiatives, creating a vibrant ecosystem for digital service delivery. Chhattisgarh has pioneered a State Enterprise Architecture to ensure integrated, coordinated, and standards-based e-Governance, leveraging core databases and common infrastructure for timely, efficient service delivery.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">Significant strides have been made in deploying Digital India initiatives, including the use of GIS and geo-spatial technologies to support rural livelihoods. The focus is on universal access to high-bandwidth internet&mdash;essential for enabling digital literacy, large-scale skilling, e-health, e-education, and promoting IT and Electronics industries. High-bandwidth availability will also attract data centers, R&amp;D facilities, and high-tech industries, propelling Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s digital economy.<br><br></p>\r\n<p><strong>1. Vision</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>of Chhattisgarh </strong><span class=\"s2\"><strong>Government</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The Chhattisgarh Government is deeply aligned with the National vision of a Digital India and eager to make Chhattisgarh one of the first states to embrace and deliver this vision to the people of Chhattisgarh. Therefore, Chhattisgarh wants to establish Fiber infrastructure under BharatNet project up to the village level so as to spur economic development and to provide Integrated Services to the <span class=\"s2\">Citizens.<br><br></span><strong>2. Purpose</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">This Expression of Interest (EOI) is issued to hire one experienced project resources to support the timely completion of administrative, monitoring, and coordination activities for both the CGSWAN Project and CSIICL. The selected individuals will provide dedicated manpower to assist the Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS) in maintaining smooth project operations and ensuring all documentation and filing related to these initiatives are handled efficiently.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">The primary role of these resources will be to facilitate active coordination between CHiPS and various stakeholders, including System Integrators (SI), Internet Service Providers (ISP), and Third-Party Auditors (TPA). They will be responsible for supervising day-to-day audit work, monitoring project compliances, and ensuring that all activities align with the specific tender requirements of the CGSWAN and CSIICL frameworks.<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">In addition to vendor coordination, the deployed resources will act as a bridge between CHiPS and various user departments regarding Video Conferencing (VC) and CGSWAN connectivity needs. Operating from locations designated by CHiPS, these resources will perform all tasks necessary to meet project timelines and maintain the physical and digital records essential for project monitoring.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p> to <p class=\"p1\"><strong>Introduction<br><br></strong>The Government of Chhattisgarh envisions transforming the State into a globally recognized knowledge society, committed to improving citizens&rsquo; quality of life through high-quality education, healthcare, enhanced agricultural productivity, and employment generation by promoting IT and Electronics industries. Achieving this vision hinges on providing robust, high-speed broadband connectivity as a fundamental right, enabling inclusive access to digital services across urban and rural geographies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">While urban areas have witnessed substantial broadband penetration, rural regions continue to suffer a pronounced digital divide due to the lack of viable business cases for private sector investment. The State recognizes the urgent need to bridge this gap through government-led initiatives, creating a vibrant ecosystem for digital service delivery. Chhattisgarh has pioneered a State Enterprise Architecture to ensure integrated, coordinated, and standards-based e-Governance, leveraging core databases and common infrastructure for timely, efficient service delivery.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">Significant strides have been made in deploying Digital India initiatives, including the use of GIS and geo-spatial technologies to support rural livelihoods. The focus is on universal access to high-bandwidth internet&mdash;essential for enabling digital literacy, large-scale skilling, e-health, e-education, and promoting IT and Electronics industries. High-bandwidth availability will also attract data centers, R&amp;D facilities, and high-tech industries, propelling Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s digital economy.<br><br></p>\r\n<p><strong>1. Vision</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>of Chhattisgarh </strong><span class=\"s2\"><strong>Government</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The Chhattisgarh Government is deeply aligned with the National vision of a Digital India and eager to make Chhattisgarh one of the first states to embrace and deliver this vision to the people of Chhattisgarh. Therefore, Chhattisgarh wants to establish Fiber infrastructure under BharatNet project up to the village level so as to spur economic development and to provide Integrated Services to the <span class=\"s2\">Citizens.<br><br></span><strong>2. Purpose</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">This Expression of Interest (EOI) is issued to hire one experienced project resources to support the timely completion of administrative, monitoring, and coordination activities for both the CGSWAN Project and CSIICL. The selected individuals will provide dedicated manpower to assist the Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS) in maintaining smooth project operations and ensuring all documentation and filing related to these initiatives are handled efficiently.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">The primary role of these resources will be to facilitate active coordination between CHiPS and various stakeholders, including System Integrators (SI), Internet Service Providers (ISP), and Third-Party Auditors (TPA). They will be responsible for supervising day-to-day audit work, monitoring project compliances, and ensuring that all activities align with the specific tender requirements of the CGSWAN and CSIICL frameworks.<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">In addition to vendor coordination, the deployed resources will act as a bridge between CHiPS and various user departments regarding Video Conferencing (VC) and CGSWAN connectivity needs. Operating from locations designated by CHiPS, these resources will perform all tasks necessary to meet project timelines and maintain the physical and digital records essential for project monitoring.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p><br>', '2026-04-02 22:49:45', 69, 1, '2026-04-02 22:49:56', 1),
(115, 135, 'Project objective changed from <p class=\"p1\"><strong>Introduction<br><br></strong>The Government of Chhattisgarh envisions transforming the State into a globally recognized knowledge society, committed to improving citizens&rsquo; quality of life through high-quality education, healthcare, enhanced agricultural productivity, and employment generation by promoting IT and Electronics industries. Achieving this vision hinges on providing robust, high-speed broadband connectivity as a fundamental right, enabling inclusive access to digital services across urban and rural geographies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">While urban areas have witnessed substantial broadband penetration, rural regions continue to suffer a pronounced digital divide due to the lack of viable business cases for private sector investment. The State recognizes the urgent need to bridge this gap through government-led initiatives, creating a vibrant ecosystem for digital service delivery. Chhattisgarh has pioneered a State Enterprise Architecture to ensure integrated, coordinated, and standards-based e-Governance, leveraging core databases and common infrastructure for timely, efficient service delivery.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">Significant strides have been made in deploying Digital India initiatives, including the use of GIS and geo-spatial technologies to support rural livelihoods. The focus is on universal access to high-bandwidth internet&mdash;essential for enabling digital literacy, large-scale skilling, e-health, e-education, and promoting IT and Electronics industries. High-bandwidth availability will also attract data centers, R&amp;D facilities, and high-tech industries, propelling Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s digital economy.<br><br></p>\r\n<p><strong>1. Vision</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>of Chhattisgarh </strong><span class=\"s2\"><strong>Government</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The Chhattisgarh Government is deeply aligned with the National vision of a Digital India and eager to make Chhattisgarh one of the first states to embrace and deliver this vision to the people of Chhattisgarh. Therefore, Chhattisgarh wants to establish Fiber infrastructure under BharatNet project up to the village level so as to spur economic development and to provide Integrated Services to the <span class=\"s2\">Citizens.<br><br></span><strong>2. Purpose</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">This Expression of Interest (EOI) is issued to hire one experienced project resources to support the timely completion of administrative, monitoring, and coordination activities for both the CGSWAN Project and CSIICL. The selected individuals will provide dedicated manpower to assist the Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS) in maintaining smooth project operations and ensuring all documentation and filing related to these initiatives are handled efficiently.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">The primary role of these resources will be to facilitate active coordination between CHiPS and various stakeholders, including System Integrators (SI), Internet Service Providers (ISP), and Third-Party Auditors (TPA). They will be responsible for supervising day-to-day audit work, monitoring project compliances, and ensuring that all activities align with the specific tender requirements of the CGSWAN and CSIICL frameworks.<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">In addition to vendor coordination, the deployed resources will act as a bridge between CHiPS and various user departments regarding Video Conferencing (VC) and CGSWAN connectivity needs. Operating from locations designated by CHiPS, these resources will perform all tasks necessary to meet project timelines and maintain the physical and digital records essential for project monitoring.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p> to <p class=\"p1\"><strong>Introduction<br></strong>The Government of Chhattisgarh envisions transforming the State into a globally recognized knowledge society, committed to improving citizens&rsquo; quality of life through high-quality education, healthcare, enhanced agricultural productivity, and employment generation by promoting IT and Electronics industries. Achieving this vision hinges on providing robust, high-speed broadband connectivity as a fundamental right, enabling inclusive access to digital services across urban and rural geographies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">While urban areas have witnessed substantial broadband penetration, rural regions continue to suffer a pronounced digital divide due to the lack of viable business cases for private sector investment. The State recognizes the urgent need to bridge this gap through government-led initiatives, creating a vibrant ecosystem for digital service delivery. Chhattisgarh has pioneered a State Enterprise Architecture to ensure integrated, coordinated, and standards-based e-Governance, leveraging core databases and common infrastructure for timely, efficient service delivery.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">Significant strides have been made in deploying Digital India initiatives, including the use of GIS and geo-spatial technologies to support rural livelihoods. The focus is on universal access to high-bandwidth internet&mdash;essential for enabling digital literacy, large-scale skilling, e-health, e-education, and promoting IT and Electronics industries. High-bandwidth availability will also attract data centers, R&amp;D facilities, and high-tech industries, propelling Chhattisgarh&rsquo;s digital economy.<br><br></p>\r\n<p><strong>1. Vision</strong><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>of Chhattisgarh </strong><span class=\"s2\"><strong>Government</strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The Chhattisgarh Government is deeply aligned with the National vision of a Digital India and eager to make Chhattisgarh one of the first states to embrace and deliver this vision to the people of Chhattisgarh. Therefore, Chhattisgarh wants to establish Fiber infrastructure under BharatNet project up to the village level so as to spur economic development and to provide Integrated Services to the <span class=\"s2\">Citizens.<br><br></span><strong>2. Purpose</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">This Expression of Interest (EOI) is issued to hire one experienced project resources to support the timely completion of administrative, monitoring, and coordination activities for both the CGSWAN Project and CSIICL. The selected individuals will provide dedicated manpower to assist the Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society (CHiPS) in maintaining smooth project operations and ensuring all documentation and filing related to these initiatives are handled efficiently.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p3\">The primary role of these resources will be to facilitate active coordination between CHiPS and various stakeholders, including System Integrators (SI), Internet Service Providers (ISP), and Third-Party Auditors (TPA). They will be responsible for supervising day-to-day audit work, monitoring project compliances, and ensuring that all activities align with the specific tender requirements of the CGSWAN and CSIICL frameworks.<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">In addition to vendor coordination, the deployed resources will act as a bridge between CHiPS and various user departments regarding Video Conferencing (VC) and CGSWAN connectivity needs. Operating from locations designated by CHiPS, these resources will perform all tasks necessary to meet project timelines and maintain the physical and digital records essential for project monitoring.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p><br>', '2026-04-02 22:50:20', 69, 1, '2026-04-02 22:50:30', 1),
(116, 136, 'Project objective changed from <p>About the Polavaram Irrigation Project <br><br>The Polavaram multi-purpose Major Irrigation Project, accorded National Project Status by the Government of India, is intended to enhance the Irrigation capacity of the Godavari River basin by a gross potential of 436.825 hectares. The project also includes the Installation of hydroelectric facilities with potable water to an estimated population of 2.85 million across 611 villages. Given that the a total capacity of 960 MW. Additionally, it aims to provide Godavari River basin is classified as surplus and the Krishna River basin as deficit, the project also plans to facilitate the transfer of 80 TMC (thousand million cubic feet) of water from the Godavari River basin to the Krishna River basin. <br><br>However, the project\'s backwater is anticipated to extend into parts of Chhattisgarh, resulting in submergence and displacement of local populations in the state, specifically in Konta Tehsil in Sukma district and Bhopalpattanam Tehsil in Bijapur district. <br><br>It is estimated that approximately 2700 Ha of land and 13,000 people across 12 villages and Konta town in Sukma will be impacted by the potential submergence.<br><br></p>\r\n<table data-path-to-node=\"4\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Level</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Affected Villages</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Private Land (Ha)</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Government Land (Ha)</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Total Land (Ha)</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Number of Houses</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Population</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,0,0\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"4,1,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Upto 150 feet</strong></span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,1,0\">9</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,2,0\">459.572</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,3,0\">930.615</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,4,0\">1390.107</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,5,0\">252</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,6,0\">1492</span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,0,0\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"4,2,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Upto 177 feet</strong></span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,1,0\">12</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,2,0\">1488.400</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,3,0\">1216.38</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,4,0\">2704.780</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,5,0\">2519</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,6,0\">13262</span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>Similarly, it is estimated that approximately 73.451 Ha of land and 0 people across O villages in Bijapur will be impacted by the potential submergence.</p>\r\n<table data-path-to-node=\"1\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Level</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Affected Villages</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Private Land (Ha)</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Government Land (Ha)</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Total Land (Ha)</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Number of Houses</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Population</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,0,0\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"1,1,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Upto 83mtr.</strong></span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,1,0\">2</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,2,0\">13.061</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,3,0\">60.39</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,4,0\">73.451</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,5,0\">0</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,6,0\">0</span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Need Identified -&nbsp;</strong><br>To address this, the Water Resources Department requires consultancy support to evaluate the potential social impacts of submergence and displacement in Konta Tehsil, focusing on aspects such as land acquisition, compensation, rehabilitation, and resettlement.<br><br><strong>Objective(s) of the project -&nbsp;<br></strong>a) Estimation of the number of affected families, including those likely to be displaced. <br>b) Analysis of the extent of impact on land both public and private - residential structures, settlements, and other common properties likely to be affected.<br>c) Assessment of the social impacts of the project on various components such as livelihood of affected families, public and community properties, assets and infrastructure particularly roads, public transport, drainage, sanitation, sources of drinking water, sources of water for cattle, community ponds, grazing land, plantations, public utilities such as post offices, fair price shops, food storage godowns, electricity supply, health care facilities, schools and educational or training facilities, anganwadis, children parks, places of worship, land for traditional tribal institutions and burial and cremation grounds. <br>d) Preparation of a Social Impact Management Plan (SIMP), listing the ameliorative measures required to be undertaken for addressing the impacts, including the nature and costs associated.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p> to <p><strong>About the Polavaram Irrigation Project </strong><br><br>The Polavaram multi-purpose Major Irrigation Project, accorded National Project Status by the Government of India, is intended to enhance the Irrigation capacity of the Godavari River basin by a gross potential of 436.825 hectares. The project also includes the Installation of hydroelectric facilities with potable water to an estimated population of 2.85 million across 611 villages. Given that the a total capacity of 960 MW. Additionally, it aims to provide Godavari River basin is classified as surplus and the Krishna River basin as deficit, the project also plans to facilitate the transfer of 80 TMC (thousand million cubic feet) of water from the Godavari River basin to the Krishna River basin. <br><br>However, the project\'s backwater is anticipated to extend into parts of Chhattisgarh, resulting in submergence and displacement of local populations in the state, specifically in Konta Tehsil in Sukma district and Bhopalpattanam Tehsil in Bijapur district. <br><br>It is estimated that approximately 2700 Ha of land and 13,000 people across 12 villages and Konta town in Sukma will be impacted by the potential submergence.<br><br></p>\r\n<table data-path-to-node=\"4\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Level</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Affected Villages</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Private Land (Ha)</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Government Land (Ha)</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Total Land (Ha)</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Number of Houses</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Population</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,0,0\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"4,1,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Upto 150 feet</strong></span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,1,0\">9</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,2,0\">459.572</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,3,0\">930.615</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,4,0\">1390.107</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,5,0\">252</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,1,6,0\">1492</span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,0,0\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"4,2,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Upto 177 feet</strong></span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,1,0\">12</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,2,0\">1488.400</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,3,0\">1216.38</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,4,0\">2704.780</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,5,0\">2519</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"4,2,6,0\">13262</span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>Similarly, it is estimated that approximately 73.451 Ha of land and 0 people across O villages in Bijapur will be impacted by the potential submergence.</p>\r\n<table data-path-to-node=\"1\">\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><strong>Level</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Affected Villages</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Private Land (Ha)</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Government Land (Ha)</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Total Land (Ha)</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Number of Houses</strong></td>\r\n<td><strong>Population</strong></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,0,0\"><strong data-path-to-node=\"1,1,0,0\" data-index-in-node=\"0\">Upto 83mtr.</strong></span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,1,0\">2</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,2,0\">13.061</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,3,0\">60.39</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,4,0\">73.451</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,5,0\">0</span></td>\r\n<td><span data-path-to-node=\"1,1,6,0\">0</span></td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><strong>Need Identified -&nbsp;</strong><br>To address this, the Water Resources Department requires consultancy support to evaluate the potential social impacts of submergence and displacement in Konta Tehsil, focusing on aspects such as land acquisition, compensation, rehabilitation, and resettlement.<br><br><strong>Objective(s) of the project -&nbsp;<br></strong>a) Estimation of the number of affected families, including those likely to be displaced. <br>b) Analysis of the extent of impact on land both public and private - residential structures, settlements, and other common properties likely to be affected.<br>c) Assessment of the social impacts of the project on various components such as livelihood of affected families, public and community properties, assets and infrastructure particularly roads, public transport, drainage, sanitation, sources of drinking water, sources of water for cattle, community ponds, grazing land, plantations, public utilities such as post offices, fair price shops, food storage godowns, electricity supply, health care facilities, schools and educational or training facilities, anganwadis, children parks, places of worship, land for traditional tribal institutions and burial and cremation grounds. <br>d) Preparation of a Social Impact Management Plan (SIMP), listing the ameliorative measures required to be undertaken for addressing the impacts, including the nature and costs associated.</p>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p><br>', '2026-04-03 17:49:19', 75, 1, '2026-04-03 17:49:31', 1),
