f recommended schemes from line departments, public representatives, and other sources, along with their status.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"13j6sgx\" data-start=\"357\" data-end=\"397\">Provide support to DMFT as required.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"clxmei\" data-start=\"398\" data-end=\"449\">Provide support in documentation and reporting.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"19caqwv\" data-start=\"450\" data-end=\"496\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Perform any other duties as may be assigned.</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 30-04-2026, 01:17 PM', '2026-04-30 13:17:43', 405, 1, '2026-04-30 13:19:20', 1),
(146, 146, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Remark changed from <p class=\"Default\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Health Cum Education Consultant <em>(One)</em> </span></strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\" style=\"margin-left: 17.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -17.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 17.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; color: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">•<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">      </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\">Provide technical and strategic advisory support for planning and implementation of DMFT-funded initiatives in the Health, Education, and Sanitation sectors.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\" style=\"margin-left: 17.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -17.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 17.0pt;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-family: \'Arial\',sans-serif; mso-fareast-font-family: Arial; color: windowtext;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">•<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">      </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><span lang=\"EN-US\">Support district/state authorities in needs assessment, sector gap analysis, and prioritisation of interventions aligned with local development requirements and government policies.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"Default\"><span lang=\"EN-US\"><em><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 12.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 10.5pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Aptos\',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-font-family: Aptos; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-font-family: Mangal; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: MR;\">Assist in designing sector-specific programmes and projects, including defining objectives, activities, timelines, and expected outcomes.</span></em></span></p> to <p class=\"Default\"><strong><span lang=\"EN-US\">Health Cum Education Consultant&nbsp;<em>(One)</em> </span></strong></p>\r\n<div class=\"flex flex-col text-sm pb-25\">\r\n<section class=\"text-token-text-primary w-full focus:outline-none [--shadow-height:45px] has-data-writing-block:pointer-events-none has-data-writing-block:-mt-(--shadow-height) has-data-writing-block:pt-(--shadow-height) [&amp;:has([data-writing-block])&gt;*]:pointer-events-auto scroll-mt-[calc(var(--header-height)+min(200px,max(70px,20svh)))]\" dir=\"auto\" data-turn-id=\"request-69df37fe-bf4c-83a6-b6c4-5b5f50ffe1ea-148\" data-testid=\"conversation-turn-252\" data-scroll-anchor=\"true\" data-turn=\"assistant\">\r\n<div class=\"text-base my-auto mx-auto pb-10 [--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-xs,calc(var(--spacing)*4))] @w-sm/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-sm,calc(var(--spacing)*6))] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-margin:var(--thread-content-margin-lg,calc(var(--spacing)*16))] px-(--thread-content-margin)\">\r\n<div class=\"[--thread-content-max-width:40rem] @w-lg/main:[--thread-content-max-width:48rem] mx-auto max-w-(--thread-content-max-width) flex-1 group/turn-messages focus-visible:outline-hidden relative flex w-full min-w-0 flex-col agent-turn\">\r\n<div class=\"flex max-w-full flex-col gap-4 grow\">\r\n<div class=\"min-h-8 text-message relative flex w-full flex-col items-end gap-2 text-start break-words whitespace-normal outline-none keyboard-focused:focus-ring [.text-message+&amp;]:mt-1\" dir=\"auto\" tabindex=\"0\" data-message-author-role=\"assistant\" data-message-id=\"5eb43190-8f26-4f33-8169-b1290e66c691\" data-message-model-slug=\"gpt-5-3\" data-turn-start-message=\"true\">\r\n<div class=\"flex w-full flex-col gap-1 empty:hidden\">\r\n<div class=\"markdown prose dark:prose-invert w-full wrap-break-word dark markdown-new-styling\">\r\n<ul data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"487\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ropulc\" data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"161\">Provide technical and strategic advisory support for planning and implementation of DMFT-funded initiatives in the health, education, and sanitation sectors.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1tb226k\" data-start=\"162\" data-end=\"347\">Support district/state authorities in needs assessment, sector gap analysis, and prioritisation of interventions aligned with local development requirements and government policies.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1obieit\" data-start=\"348\" data-end=\"487\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Assist in designing sector-specific programmes and projects, including defining objectives, activities, timelines, and expected outcomes.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<div class=\"mt-3 w-full empty:hidden\">&nbsp;</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n</section>\r\n</div>.<br>on 30-04-2026, 01:18 PM', '2026-04-30 13:18:13', 405, 1, '2026-04-30 13:19:14', 1),
(147, 146, 'Project objective changed from <p><strong>Introduction</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The District Mineral Trust Fund (DMF), Kanker, Chhattisgarh is a statutory trust constituted to work for the welfare of communities and areas affected by mining activities in the district. Kanker district, located in the southern part of Chhattisgarh, is endowed with significant mineral resources, particularly iron ore, and forms a critical part of the state&rsquo;s mineral economy. While mining has contributed to regional development, the mining-affected and peripheral areas of Kanker continue to face multiple socio-economic challenges, dependence on agriculture and forest-based livelihoods, and environmental stress.<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>About Kanker District</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Kanker district is located in the southern region of Chhattisgarh. Formerly part of the undivided Bastar district, it was constituted as an independent district in 1998. The district covers a geographical area of about 5,285.01 sq. km and lies between 20.6&deg;&ndash;20.24&deg; North latitude and 80.48&deg;&ndash;81.48&deg; East longitude. Kanker is situated approximately 140 km from Raipur and 160 km from Jagdalpur, and is well connected by national and state highways.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span>The topography of the district comprises ancient hill systems of the Vindhyan, Archean, and Dharwar groups, along with extensive plains. Nearly 80% of the area consists of plains, mainly forming the Mahanadi and Kotri plains. Several important rivers&mdash;Milk, Mahanadi, Hukkul, Sindur, and Turu&mdash;flow through the district, supporting agriculture and natural ecosystems.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Administratively, Kanker district consists of 7 tehsils&mdash;Kanker, Charama, Narharpur, Bhanupratappur, Antagarh, Durgukondal, and Koyalibeda&mdash;comprising 1,004 villages, of which 995 are revenue villages and 9 are forest villages.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Agriculture is the backbone of the district economy, with around <strong>70&ndash;75%</strong> of the population directly or indirectly dependent on agriculture and allied activities. As per the land utilization pattern (2015), the total reported area is approximately 4.57 lakh hectares, including about 1.09 lakh hectares under forest cover and nearly 50,447 hectares under non‑agricultural use, besides cultivable barren land.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The district predominantly follows rainfed agriculture. During the Kharif season, the major crops grown are paddy (rice)&mdash;the principal crop&mdash;along with maize, small millets (kodo, kutki), pulses such as arhar and urad, and oilseeds like groundnut and soybean.<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">In the Rabi season, agriculture is limited but important crops include wheat, gram (chickpea), lentil, mustard, and linseed, largely dependent on residual soil moisture and limited irrigation facilities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Livestock rearing is an important supplementary livelihood, with a substantial population of cattle, buffaloes, and goats. The district has about 95 agro‑based industrial units, mainly linked to rice milling, oil extraction, forest produce processing, and minor food‑processing activities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Kanker district is also endowed with mineral resources. Major minerals found in the district include iron ore (notably the Rowghat iron ore belt), limestone, bauxite, laterite, dolomite, quartz, and granite. Mining activities are primarily concentrated in Antagarh, Bhanupratappur, Durgukondal, and Koyalibeda blocks, contributing to industrial development and employment generation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>DMF Kanker</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">District Mineral Foundation Trust (DMFT) is a statutory, non‑profit trust constituted in all mining‑affected districts of Chhattisgarh under Section 9B of the Mines and Minerals (Development and Regulation) Act, 1957, as amended in January 2015. Established by the State Government as a perpetual body, DMFT is financed through contributions made by mining lease holders as a prescribed share of royalty. The primary objective of DMFT is to safeguard the interests and promote the socio‑economic welfare of individuals and areas affected by mining and allied operations. The composition, governance, and functioning of the Trust are guided by constitutional provisions under Article 244, the Fifth and Sixth Schedules, the PESA Act, 1996, and the Forest Rights Act, 2006, ensuring inclusivity and community participation. DMFT funds are utilized through the implementation of the Pradhan Mantri Khanij Kshetra Kalyan Yojana (PMKKKY) to support developmental and welfare interventions that complement State and Central Government schemes, mitigate environmental and socio‑economic impacts of mining, and enable long‑term sustainable livelihoods in mining‑affected areas<strong>.</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">DMF Kanker plays a vital role in addressing these challenges by planning and implementing targeted development interventions in priority sectors such as agriculture water, nutrition, skill development, livelihood enhancement, and environmental conservation. Through need-based and community-focused initiatives, DMF seeks to promote inclusive growth and improve the overall quality of life of the mining-impacted population, with particular emphasis on tribal and vulnerable communities prevalent in the district.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Hence, the Authority seeks to engage a competent agency for establishing and operating a Program Management Unit (PMU) for the District Mineral Foundation (DMF), Kanker. The key objectives of this engagement shall include the following:</p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li2\">As per Section 5 of the Pradhan Mantri Khanij Kshetra Kalyan Yojana (PMKKKY) Guidelines: Conduct a comprehensive baseline survey across mining-affected areas of the&nbsp;district and prepare a 5-Year Perspective Plan along with Annual Action Plans to enable systematic, evidence-based, and need-driven development interventions.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">As per PMKKKY Guidelines, Section 2 &ndash; General Guidelines, Subsection (b): Given that DMF Kanker has substantial annual accruals, establish and operate a Program Management Unit (PMU) to provide planning, technical, project management, and monitoring support for the effective implementation of DMF-funded projects and programs.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Strengthening institutional capacity through adoption of innovative approaches, integration of best practices, capacity-building and training of stakeholders, development of robust monitoring and knowledge management systems, and provision of technical support to the DMF Trust Board and Executive Committee.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p> to <p><strong>Introduction</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The District Mineral Trust Fund (DMF), Kanker, Chhattisgarh is a statutory trust constituted to work for the welfare of communities and areas affected by mining activities in the district. Kanker district, located in the southern part of Chhattisgarh, is endowed with significant mineral resources, particularly iron ore, and forms a critical part of the state&rsquo;s mineral economy. While mining has contributed to regional development, the mining-affected and peripheral areas of Kanker continue to face multiple socio-economic challenges, dependence on agriculture and forest-based livelihoods, and environmental stress.<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>About Kanker District</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Kanker district is located in the southern region of Chhattisgarh. Formerly part of the undivided Bastar district, it was constituted as an independent district in 1998. The district covers a geographical area of about 5,285.01 sq. km and lies between 20.6&deg;&ndash;20.24&deg; North latitude and 80.48&deg;&ndash;81.48&deg; East longitude. Kanker is situated approximately 140 km from Raipur and 160 km from Jagdalpur, and is well connected by national and state highways.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span>The topography of the district comprises ancient hill systems of the Vindhyan, Archean, and Dharwar groups, along with extensive plains. Nearly 80% of the area consists of plains, mainly forming the Mahanadi and Kotri plains. Several important rivers&mdash;Milk, Mahanadi, Hukkul, Sindur, and Turu&mdash;flow through the district, supporting agriculture and natural ecosystems.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Administratively, Kanker district consists of 7 tehsils&mdash;Kanker, Charama, Narharpur, Bhanupratappur, Antagarh, Durgukondal, and Koyalibeda&mdash;comprising 1,004 villages, of which 995 are revenue villages and 9 are forest villages.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Agriculture is the backbone of the district economy, with around <strong>70&ndash;75%</strong> of the population directly or indirectly dependent on agriculture and allied activities. As per the land utilization pattern (2015), the total reported area is approximately 4.57 lakh hectares, including about 1.09 lakh hectares under forest cover and nearly 50,447 hectares under non‑agricultural use, besides cultivable barren land.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The district predominantly follows rainfed agriculture. During the Kharif season, the major crops grown are paddy (rice)&mdash;the principal crop&mdash;along with maize, small millets (kodo, kutki), pulses such as arhar and urad, and oilseeds like groundnut and soybean.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">In the Rabi season, agriculture is limited but important crops include wheat, gram (chickpea), lentil, mustard, and linseed, largely dependent on residual soil moisture and limited irrigation facilities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Livestock rearing is an important supplementary livelihood, with a substantial population of cattle, buffaloes, and goats. The district has about 95 agro‑based industrial units, mainly linked to rice milling, oil extraction, forest produce processing, and minor food‑processing activities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Kanker district is also endowed with mineral resources. Major minerals found in the district include iron ore (notably the Rowghat iron ore belt), limestone, bauxite, laterite, dolomite, quartz, and granite. Mining activities are primarily concentrated in Antagarh, Bhanupratappur, Durgukondal, and Koyalibeda blocks, contributing to industrial development and employment generation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>DMF Kanker</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">District Mineral Foundation Trust (DMFT) is a statutory, non‑profit trust constituted in all mining‑affected districts of Chhattisgarh under Section 9B of the Mines and Minerals (Development and Regulation) Act, 1957, as amended in January 2015. Established by the State Government as a perpetual body, DMFT is financed through contributions made by mining lease holders as a prescribed share of royalty. The primary objective of DMFT is to safeguard the interests and promote the socio‑economic welfare of individuals and areas affected by mining and allied operations. The composition, governance, and functioning of the Trust are guided by constitutional provisions under Article 244, the Fifth and Sixth Schedules, the PESA Act, 1996, and the Forest Rights Act, 2006, ensuring inclusivity and community participation. DMFT funds are utilized through the implementation of the Pradhan Mantri Khanij Kshetra Kalyan Yojana (PMKKKY) to support developmental and welfare interventions that complement State and Central Government schemes, mitigate environmental and socio‑economic impacts of mining, and enable long‑term sustainable livelihoods in mining‑affected areas<strong>.</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">DMF Kanker plays a vital role in addressing these challenges by planning and implementing targeted development interventions in priority sectors such as agriculture water, nutrition, skill development, livelihood enhancement, and environmental conservation. Through need-based and community-focused initiatives, DMF seeks to promote inclusive growth and improve the overall quality of life of the mining-impacted population, with particular emphasis on tribal and vulnerable communities prevalent in the district.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Hence, the Authority seeks to engage a competent agency for establishing and operating a Program Management Unit (PMU) for the District Mineral Foundation (DMF), Kanker. The key objectives of this engagement shall include the following:</p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li2\">As per Section 5 of the Pradhan Mantri Khanij Kshetra Kalyan Yojana (PMKKKY) Guidelines: Conduct a comprehensive baseline survey across mining-affected areas of the&nbsp;district and prepare a 5-Year Perspective Plan along with Annual Action Plans to enable systematic, evidence-based, and need-driven development interventions.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">As per PMKKKY Guidelines, Section 2 &ndash; General Guidelines, Subsection (b): Given that DMF Kanker has substantial annual accruals, establish and operate a Program Management Unit (PMU) to provide planning, technical, project management, and monitoring support for the effective implementation of DMF-funded projects and programs.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Strengthening institutional capacity through adoption of innovative approaches, integration of best practices, capacity-building and training of stakeholders, development of robust monitoring and knowledge management systems, and provision of technical support to the DMF Trust Board and Executive Committee.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p><br>', '2026-04-30 13:30:52', 405, 1, '2026-04-30 13:31:29', 1),
(148, 146, 'Project objective changed from <p><strong>Introduction</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The District Mineral Trust Fund (DMF), Kanker, Chhattisgarh is a statutory trust constituted to work for the welfare of communities and areas affected by mining activities in the district. Kanker district, located in the southern part of Chhattisgarh, is endowed with significant mineral resources, particularly iron ore, and forms a critical part of the state&rsquo;s mineral economy. While mining has contributed to regional development, the mining-affected and peripheral areas of Kanker continue to face multiple socio-economic challenges, dependence on agriculture and forest-based livelihoods, and environmental stress.<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>About Kanker District</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Kanker district is located in the southern region of Chhattisgarh. Formerly part of the undivided Bastar district, it was constituted as an independent district in 1998. The district covers a geographical area of about 5,285.01 sq. km and lies between 20.6&deg;&ndash;20.24&deg; North latitude and 80.48&deg;&ndash;81.48&deg; East longitude. Kanker is situated approximately 140 km from Raipur and 160 km from Jagdalpur, and is well connected by national and state highways.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span>The topography of the district comprises ancient hill systems of the Vindhyan, Archean, and Dharwar groups, along with extensive plains. Nearly 80% of the area consists of plains, mainly forming the Mahanadi and Kotri plains. Several important rivers&mdash;Milk, Mahanadi, Hukkul, Sindur, and Turu&mdash;flow through the district, supporting agriculture and natural ecosystems.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Administratively, Kanker district consists of 7 tehsils&mdash;Kanker, Charama, Narharpur, Bhanupratappur, Antagarh, Durgukondal, and Koyalibeda&mdash;comprising 1,004 villages, of which 995 are revenue villages and 9 are forest villages.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Agriculture is the backbone of the district economy, with around <strong>70&ndash;75%</strong> of the population directly or indirectly dependent on agriculture and allied activities. As per the land utilization pattern (2015), the total reported area is approximately 4.57 lakh hectares, including about 1.09 lakh hectares under forest cover and nearly 50,447 hectares under non‑agricultural use, besides cultivable barren land.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The district predominantly follows rainfed agriculture. During the Kharif season, the major crops grown are paddy (rice)&mdash;the principal crop&mdash;along with maize, small millets (kodo, kutki), pulses such as arhar and urad, and oilseeds like groundnut and soybean.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">In the Rabi season, agriculture is limited but important crops include wheat, gram (chickpea), lentil, mustard, and linseed, largely dependent on residual soil moisture and limited irrigation facilities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Livestock rearing is an important supplementary livelihood, with a substantial population of cattle, buffaloes, and goats. The district has about 95 agro‑based industrial units, mainly linked to rice milling, oil extraction, forest produce processing, and minor food‑processing activities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Kanker district is also endowed with mineral resources. Major minerals found in the district include iron ore (notably the Rowghat iron ore belt), limestone, bauxite, laterite, dolomite, quartz, and granite. Mining activities are primarily concentrated in Antagarh, Bhanupratappur, Durgukondal, and Koyalibeda blocks, contributing to industrial development and employment generation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>DMF Kanker</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">District Mineral Foundation Trust (DMFT) is a statutory, non‑profit trust constituted in all mining‑affected districts of Chhattisgarh under Section 9B of the Mines and Minerals (Development and Regulation) Act, 1957, as amended in January 2015. Established by the State Government as a perpetual body, DMFT is financed through contributions made by mining lease holders as a prescribed share of royalty. The primary objective of DMFT is to safeguard the interests and promote the socio‑economic welfare of individuals and areas affected by mining and allied operations. The composition, governance, and functioning of the Trust are guided by constitutional provisions under Article 244, the Fifth and Sixth Schedules, the PESA Act, 1996, and the Forest Rights Act, 2006, ensuring inclusivity and community participation. DMFT funds are utilized through the implementation of the Pradhan Mantri Khanij Kshetra Kalyan Yojana (PMKKKY) to support developmental and welfare interventions that complement State and Central Government schemes, mitigate environmental and socio‑economic impacts of mining, and enable long‑term sustainable livelihoods in mining‑affected areas<strong>.</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">DMF Kanker plays a vital role in addressing these challenges by planning and implementing targeted development interventions in priority sectors such as agriculture water, nutrition, skill development, livelihood enhancement, and environmental conservation. Through need-based and community-focused initiatives, DMF seeks to promote inclusive growth and improve the overall quality of life of the mining-impacted population, with particular emphasis on tribal and vulnerable communities prevalent in the district.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Hence, the Authority seeks to engage a competent agency for establishing and operating a Program Management Unit (PMU) for the District Mineral Foundation (DMF), Kanker. The key objectives of this engagement shall include the following:</p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li2\">As per Section 5 of the Pradhan Mantri Khanij Kshetra Kalyan Yojana (PMKKKY) Guidelines: Conduct a comprehensive baseline survey across mining-affected areas of the&nbsp;district and prepare a 5-Year Perspective Plan along with Annual Action Plans to enable systematic, evidence-based, and need-driven development interventions.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">As per PMKKKY Guidelines, Section 2 &ndash; General Guidelines, Subsection (b): Given that DMF Kanker has substantial annual accruals, establish and operate a Program Management Unit (PMU) to provide planning, technical, project management, and monitoring support for the effective implementation of DMF-funded projects and programs.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Strengthening institutional capacity through adoption of innovative approaches, integration of best practices, capacity-building and training of stakeholders, development of robust monitoring and knowledge management systems, and provision of technical support to the DMF Trust Board and Executive Committee.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p> to <p><strong>Introduction</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">The District Mineral Trust Fund (DMF), Kanker, Chhattisgarh is a statutory trust constituted to work for the welfare of communities and areas affected by mining activities in the district. Kanker district, located in the southern part of Chhattisgarh, is endowed with significant mineral resources, particularly iron ore, and forms a critical part of the state&rsquo;s mineral economy. While mining has contributed to regional development, the mining-affected and peripheral areas of Kanker continue to face multiple socio-economic challenges, dependence on agriculture and forest-based livelihoods, and environmental stress.<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span><strong>About Kanker District</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Kanker district is located in the southern region of Chhattisgarh. Formerly part of the undivided Bastar district, it was constituted as an independent district in 1998. The district covers a geographical area of about 5,285.01 sq. km and lies between 20.6&deg;&ndash;20.24&deg; North latitude and 80.48&deg;&ndash;81.48&deg; East longitude. Kanker is situated approximately 140 km from Raipur and 160 km from Jagdalpur, and is well connected by national and state highways.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><span class=\"s1\"><strong> </strong></span>The topography of the district comprises ancient hill systems of the Vindhyan, Archean, and Dharwar groups, along with extensive plains. Nearly 80% of the area consists of plains, mainly forming the Mahanadi and Kotri plains. Several important rivers&mdash;Milk, Mahanadi, Hukkul, Sindur, and Turu&mdash;flow through the district, supporting agriculture and natural ecosystems.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Administratively, Kanker district consists of 7 tehsils&mdash;Kanker, Charama, Narharpur, Bhanupratappur, Antagarh, Durgukondal, and Koyalibeda&mdash;comprising 1,004 villages, of which 995 are revenue villages and 9 are forest villages.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Agriculture is the backbone of the district economy, with around <strong>70&ndash;75%</strong> of the population directly or indirectly dependent on agriculture and allied activities. As per the land utilization pattern (2015), the total reported area is approximately 4.57 lakh hectares, including about 1.09 lakh hectares under forest cover and nearly 50,447 hectares under non‑agricultural use, besides cultivable barren land.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p2\">The district predominantly follows rainfed agriculture. During the Kharif season, the major crops grown are paddy (rice)&mdash;the principal crop&mdash;along with maize, small millets (kodo, kutki), pulses such as arhar and urad, and oilseeds like groundnut and soybean.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">In the Rabi season, agriculture is limited but important crops include wheat, gram (chickpea), lentil, mustard, and linseed, largely dependent on residual soil moisture and limited irrigation facilities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Livestock rearing is an important supplementary livelihood, with a substantial population of cattle, buffaloes, and goats. The district has about 95 agro‑based industrial units, mainly linked to rice milling, oil extraction, forest produce processing, and minor food‑processing activities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Kanker district is also endowed with mineral resources. Major minerals found in the district include iron ore (notably the Rowghat iron ore belt), limestone, bauxite, laterite, dolomite, quartz, and granite. Mining activities are primarily concentrated in Antagarh, Bhanupratappur, Durgukondal, and Koyalibeda blocks, contributing to industrial development and employment generation.<br><br></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\"><strong>DMF Kanker</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">District Mineral Foundation Trust (DMFT) is a statutory, non‑profit trust constituted in all mining‑affected districts of Chhattisgarh under Section 9B of the Mines and Minerals (Development and Regulation) Act, 1957, as amended in January 2015. Established by the State Government as a perpetual body, DMFT is financed through contributions made by mining lease holders as a prescribed share of royalty. The primary objective of DMFT is to safeguard the interests and promote the socio‑economic welfare of individuals and areas affected by mining and allied operations. The composition, governance, and functioning of the Trust are guided by constitutional provisions under Article 244, the Fifth and Sixth Schedules, the PESA Act, 1996, and the Forest Rights Act, 2006, ensuring inclusivity and community participation. DMFT funds are utilized through the implementation of the Pradhan Mantri Khanij Kshetra Kalyan Yojana (PMKKKY) to support developmental and welfare interventions that complement State and Central Government schemes, mitigate environmental and socio‑economic impacts of mining, and enable long‑term sustainable livelihoods in mining‑affected areas<strong>.</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">DMF Kanker plays a vital role in addressing these challenges by planning and implementing targeted development interventions in priority sectors such as agriculture water, nutrition, skill development, livelihood enhancement, and environmental conservation. Through need-based and community-focused initiatives, DMF seeks to promote inclusive growth and improve the overall quality of life of the mining-impacted population, with particular emphasis on tribal and vulnerable communities prevalent in the district.</p>\r\n<p class=\"p1\">Hence, the Authority seeks to engage a competent agency for establishing and operating a Program Management Unit (PMU) for the District Mineral Foundation (DMF), Kanker. The key objectives of this engagement shall include the following:</p>\r\n<ul class=\"ul1\">\r\n<li class=\"li2\">As per Section 5 of the Pradhan Mantri Khanij Kshetra Kalyan Yojana (PMKKKY) Guidelines: Conduct a comprehensive baseline survey across mining-affected areas of the&nbsp;district and prepare a 5-Year Perspective Plan along with Annual Action Plans to enable systematic, evidence-based, and need-driven development interventions.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">As per PMKKKY Guidelines, Section 2 &ndash; General Guidelines, Subsection (b): Given that DMF Kanker has substantial annual accruals, establish and operate a Program Management Unit (PMU) to provide planning, technical, project management, and monitoring support for the effective implementation of DMF-funded projects and programs.</li>\r\n<li class=\"li1\">Strengthening institutional capacity through adoption of innovative approaches, integration of best practices, capacity-building and training of stakeholders, development of robust monitoring and knowledge management systems, and provision of technical support to the DMF Trust Board and Executive Committee.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p><br>', '2026-04-30 13:32:37', 405, 1, '2026-04-30 13:32:46', 1);
INSERT INTO `log_eoi_updates` (`recordid`, `requestid`, `particular`, `updatedon`, `updatedby`, `isviewed`, `viewedon`, `viewedby`) VALUES
(149, 147, 'Project objective changed from <p><span lang=\"EN-US\">The key objective of engaging the resource is to strengthen the institutional capacity of the State Aviation Department in the following areas:</span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;i. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Formulation of the State Aviation Policy including policy research, stakeholder consultations, benchmarking with national and global practices, and drafting.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">ii. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Providing end-to-end PMU support for:</span>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot; </span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Drafting of tenders (RFPs, RFQs, EOIs) </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot;&nbsp; </span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Procurement of goods and services </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot; </span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Airport upgradation and infrastructure development activities </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot; </span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Activities related to airports under Regional Connectivity Scheme (RCS) </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot; </span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Operationalisation and development of the New State Hangar</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;iii. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Supporting the state in:</span>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot;&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Effective implementation of aviation norms, rules, regulations, and industry best practices.</span>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot;</span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Promotion of employment in the aviation sector, including pilot training, cabin crew training, and other aviation-related skill development initiatives.</span>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot; </span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Promotion of aviation-related activities including Flying Training Organisations (FTOs).</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;iv. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Coordination with national level flying academies for training, capacity building, and expansion opportunities</span></p> to <p><span lang=\"EN-US\"><strong>Background</strong> <br></span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">The State Aviation Department is responsible for overseeing and promoting civil aviation activities within the state, including airport development, regulatory compliance, and sectoral growth initiatives. To meet the growing demands of aviation sector development, including policy formulation, infrastructure upgrades, and promotion of aviation-related employment opportunities, the Department requires dedicated professional resource with specialized expertise. &nbsp;The deployed resource will form part of a Project Management Unit (PMU) for the Department\'s strategic initiatives, ensuring timely execution of projects and adherence to national and international aviation standards.&nbsp;<br><br><strong>Objective&nbsp;</strong><br></span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">The key objective of engaging the resource is to strengthen the institutional capacity of the State Aviation Department in the following areas:</span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;i. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Formulation of the State Aviation Policy including policy research, stakeholder consultations, benchmarking with national and global practices, and drafting.</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">ii. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Providing end-to-end PMU support for:</span>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot; </span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Drafting of tenders (RFPs, RFQs, EOIs) </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot;&nbsp; </span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Procurement of goods and services </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot; </span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Airport upgradation and infrastructure development activities </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot; </span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Activities related to airports under Regional Connectivity Scheme (RCS) </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot; </span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Operationalisation and development of the New State Hangar</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;iii. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Supporting the state in:</span>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot;&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Effective implementation of aviation norms, rules, regulations, and industry best practices.</span>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot;</span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Promotion of employment in the aviation sector, including pilot training, cabin crew training, and other aviation-related skill development initiatives.</span>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot; </span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Promotion of aviation-related activities including Flying Training Organisations (FTOs).</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;iv. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Coordination with national level flying academies for training, capacity building, and expansion opportunities</span></p><br>Scope of work changed from <p><span lang=\"EN-US\">The key objective of engaging the resource is to strengthen the institutional capacity of the State Aviation Department in the following areas:</span>&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;<br>i. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Formulation of the State Aviation Policy including policy research, stakeholder consultations, benchmarking with national and global practices, and drafting.</span></p>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">ii.&nbsp;</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Providing end-to-end PMU support for:</span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Drafting of tenders (RFPs, RFQs, EOIs)</span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Procurement of goods and services</span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Airport upgradation and infrastructure development activities</span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Activities related to airports under Regional Connectivity Scheme (RCS)</span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Operationalisation and development of the New State Hangar</span><span lang=\"EN-US\">&nbsp;</span></li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">iii. </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Supporting the state in:</span>&nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\">&middot;&nbsp; </span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Effective implementation of aviation norms, rules, regulations, and industry best practices.</span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Promotion of employment in the aviation sector, including pilot training, cabin crew training, and other aviation-related skill development initiatives.</span></li>\r\n<li><span lang=\"EN-US\">Promotion of aviation-related activities including Flying Training Organisations (FTOs).</span>&nbsp;</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p><span lang=\"EN-US\">iv.&nbsp; </span><span lang=\"EN-US\">Coordination with national level flying academies for training, capacity building, and expansion opportunities</span></p> to <p>The State Aviation Department seeks to engage a highly qualified professional resource to strengthen its institutional capacity in policy formulation, project management, and sectoral development for civil aviation. This engagement represents a strategic initiative to enhance the Department\'s capabilities in aviation sector development, infrastructure planning, and regulatory compliance. The selected professionals/firm will be responsible for:&nbsp;</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"0\" data-end=\"27\">I. <strong data-start=\"3\" data-end=\"25\">Policy Development</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"28\" data-end=\"259\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"agfic7\" data-start=\"28\" data-end=\"139\">Conduct comprehensive research on aviation sector trends, regulatory frameworks, and emerging technologies.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"gfx5lr\" data-start=\"140\" data-end=\"189\">Draft and finalize the State Aviation Policy.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"rjftet\" data-start=\"190\" data-end=\"259\">Undertake stakeholder consultations, workshops, and coordination.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"261\" data-end=\"303\">II. <strong data-start=\"265\" data-end=\"301\">PMU Support &amp; Project Management</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"304\" data-end=\"739\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cjno1k\" data-start=\"304\" data-end=\"397\">Draft technical and financial documents including RFPs, RFQs, DPRs, contracts, MoUs, etc.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"3xa69m\" data-start=\"398\" data-end=\"511\">Assist the Department in the procurement of goods and services as per applicable State/GoI procurement norms.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"yttczr\" data-start=\"512\" data-end=\"598\">Support airport development and upgradation under RCS and other State initiatives.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"xx17nd\" data-start=\"599\" data-end=\"667\">Monitor and report progress of aviation infrastructure projects.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"188za10\" data-start=\"668\" data-end=\"739\">Provide technical assistance for operationalising the State Hangar.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"741\" data-end=\"785\">III. <strong data-start=\"746\" data-end=\"783\">Sectoral Coordination &amp; Promotion</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"786\" data-end=\"1263\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9sa9of\" data-start=\"786\" data-end=\"883\">Guide the Department in implementing aviation rules, safety norms, and compliance frameworks.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9v52rm\" data-start=\"884\" data-end=\"970\">Facilitate partnerships with FTOs, aviation institutes, and industry stakeholders.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"hvurcj\" data-start=\"971\" data-end=\"1126\">Liaise with National Aviation Academies and DGCA-approved institutions for training, collaboration, and establishment of training centres in the State.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"hcbwbe\" data-start=\"1127\" data-end=\"1263\">Develop initiatives to promote aviation employment opportunities such as pilot training, cabin crew training, AME/ATC training, etc.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1265\" data-end=\"1310\">IV. <strong data-start=\"1269\" data-end=\"1308\">Administrative &amp; Analytical Support</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1311\" data-end=\"1577\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1eh2iz4\" data-start=\"1311\" data-end=\"1384\">Prepare presentations, briefs, proposals, reports, and documentation.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4ejipj\" data-start=\"1385\" data-end=\"1470\">Assist in stakeholder communication, meeting coordination, and follow-up actions.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6m56ci\" data-start=\"1471\" data-end=\"1577\" data-is-last-node=\"\">Perform any other task assigned by the State Aviation Department related to aviation sector development.</li>\r\n</ul><br>', '2026-04-30 13:46:50', 94, 1, '2026-04-30 13:47:24', 1),
(150, 144, 'Project name changed from WETLAND AND BIODIVERSITY CONSERVATION to Setting up of Project Management Unit (PMU) for WETLAND AND BIODIVERSITY CONSERVATION WORKS<br>', '2026-04-30 14:42:31', 401, 1, '2026-05-04 15:51:37', 1),
(151, 148, 'The department has uploaded new files. Kindly review the details.', '2026-04-30 19:30:32', 108, 1, '2026-05-04 16:04:31', 1);
INSERT INTO `log_eoi_updates` (`recordid`, `requestid`, `particular`, `updatedon`, `updatedby`, `isviewed`, `viewedon`, `viewedby`) VALUES
(152, 149, 'Project objective changed from <p data-start=\"169\" data-end=\"778\">Chhattisgarh is one of the few states that have implemented the e-Procurement system as early as 2007 through CHiPS in a Public Private Partnership mode (PPP) partnering with an SI selected through an RFP process. Since then, the e-Procurement system was quickly adopted by majority of the departments, and the value and volumes of procurement through the e-Procurement system during this period indicates the success of this initiative. The total of 48,991 tenders having worth of Rs. 92,396.38 Cr was processed using e-Procurement System till the new system in place.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"780\" data-end=\"1629\">However, with the expiry of the arrangement with the SI and changing needs of the user departments and the need for a holistic approach to e-GP implementation to meet the goal of an end-to-end Procurement system for all the government and public sector entities in the State, CHiPS, under Department of Electronics and Information Technology, Government of Chhattisgarh, thereafter in the year 2015, through M/s Mjunction (System Integrator) has designed &amp; implemented the ERP-based Commercial-Off-The-Shelf (COTS) Integrated e-Procurement solution for all the departments and organizations of the Chhattisgarh government. It may be appreciated that, based on advanced business intelligence tools and unique algorithms, the analytics-powered e-Procurement solution has a high degree of visibility and control.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1631\" data-end=\"2177\">The Integrated e-Procurement System implemented in the state is its uniqueness and has the most advanced feature of analytics to identify features like PAN number, segregation of bidders and department officials, mapping of the basic business rules of tendering like multiple bidding, collusion or probability of any cartel formation which no other system in the entire country has. These features helped nodal agency, CHiPS to alert the departments about probability of collusion and other material facts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2179\" data-end=\"2274\">The Integrated e-Procurement model goes beyond the existing e-tendering process. It includes:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2276\" data-end=\"2317\">Registration of suppliers / contractors</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2319\" data-end=\"2338\">Indent management</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2340\" data-end=\"2353\">e-Tendering</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2355\" data-end=\"2366\">e-Auction</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2368\" data-end=\"2389\">Contract management</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2391\" data-end=\"2403\">e-Payments</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2405\" data-end=\"2417\">Accounting</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2419\" data-end=\"2450\">Management Information System</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2452\" data-end=\"3049\">The entire Integrated e-Procurement process has designed to avoid human interface i.e., supplier and buyer interaction during pre-bidding and post-bidding stages. The application ensures total anonymity of the participating suppliers, even to the buyers, until the bids are opened on the platform. The e-Procurement application provides automatic bid evaluation based on the evaluation parameters given to the system. These improved processes have eliminated subjectivity in receipt and evaluation of bids and has reduced corruption to a significant extent.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3051\" data-end=\"3773\">To bring in transparency in Integrated e-Procurement, tender documents containing all details are hosted on the Integrated e-Procurement website. The documents can be downloaded by the interested suppliers free of cost, from the day of publication of a tender. Suppliers/bidders are no more dependent on the officials for various details. At any time in the procurement cycle, any person associated with the transaction can check and know the status of the transaction and also at every stage of the tender activities bidders/suppliers get the email/SMS alert on their mail-id/mobile no. This saves time and effort involved in finding out the status of a tender, purchase order etc.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3775\" data-end=\"4103\">An e-Payment Facility (Multiple Payment Gateway) is integrated with Integrated e-Procurement System for payment of Tender Processing Fees, Earnest Money Deposit (EMD). This is to be done to &lsquo;Minimize Human Intervention&rsquo; thereby minimizing any possibility of disclosure of bidder identity.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4105\" data-end=\"4184\">Online payments can be done through Credit/Debit card, Net banking, NeFT/RTGS</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4186\" data-end=\"4222\">Completely secure and confidential</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4224\" data-end=\"4269\">Online EMD refunds are done within T+2 days</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4271\" data-end=\"4352\">No need for bidders to visit the department office for any payments and refunds</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4354\" data-end=\"5129\">However, with the expiry of the arrangement with the existing SI (Ms. Mjunction Services Limited) and changing needs of the user departments and the need for a holistic approach to e-Procurement implementation to meet the goal of an end-to-end e-Government Procurement system for all the government and public sector entities in the State, CHiPS is looking forward to implement Government e-Procurement System of National Informatics Centre, GePNIC&copy; &mdash; a single product to cater to varied requirements, to provide software as a service, agile development and deployment, segregation of development and implementation, seamless incremental version changes, load handling, process to handle malfunction or unforeseen events and many more.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5131\" data-end=\"5494\">Reason for GePNIC:<br data-start=\"5149\" data-end=\"5152\">The existing e-Procurement solution implemented in the State has high dependency on System Integrators as well as high cost of implementation. However, National Informatics Centre, MeitY has developed e-Procurement software system as a product for facilitating Electronic Procurement across Government.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5496\" data-end=\"5583\">GePNIC is implemented in 24 states, 7 UT&rsquo;s and 750+ Central Government Organizations.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5585\" data-end=\"5646\">86% of India uses GePNIC for electronic procurement system.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5648\" data-end=\"5860\">Apart from above, after the completion of the project period, department will not have to go through a new tender process every time for selection of new system integrator.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5862\" data-end=\"5920\">Current Implementation Status:<br data-start=\"5892\" data-end=\"5895\">Module Adoption Status:<br><br></p>\r\n<table>\r\n<thead>\r\n<tr>\r\n<th align=\"right\">Sr. No.</th>\r\n<th>Modules Adopted</th>\r\n<th>Department</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td align=\"right\">1</td>\r\n<td>e-Tendering</td>\r\n<td>166 Departments</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td align=\"right\">2</td>\r\n<td>Vendor Registration</td>\r\n<td>166 Departments</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td align=\"right\">3</td>\r\n<td>MIS &amp; Accounting</td>\r\n<td>166 Departments</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td align=\"right\">4</td>\r\n<td>Online Payment</td>\r\n<td>166 Departments</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td align=\"right\">5</td>\r\n<td>Contract</td>\r\n<td>17 Departments</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td align=\"right\">6</td>\r\n<td>e-Auction</td>\r\n<td>MRD Department, CMDC, Civil Supply, and UADD</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr>\r\n<td align=\"right\">7</td>\r\n<td>Indent</td>\r\n<td>1 Department</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table> to <h3 data-section-id=\"109dsgo\" data-start=\"183\" data-end=\"214\">BACKGROUND INFORMATION</h3>\r\n<h4 data-start=\"216\" data-end=\"255\">ABOUT e-Procurement Project:</h4>\r\n<p data-start=\"257\" data-end=\"827\">Chhattisgarh is one of the few states that have implemented the e-Procurement system as early as 2007 through CHiPS in a Public Private Partnership mode (PPP) partnering with an SI selected through an RFP process. Since then, the e-Procurement system was quickly adopted by majority of the departments and the value and volumes of procurement through the e-Procurement system during this period indicates the success of this initiative. The total of 48,991 tenders having worth of Rs. 92,396.38 Cr was processed using e-Procurement System till the new system in place.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"829\" data-end=\"1639\">However, with the expiry of the arrangement with the SI and changing needs of the user departments and the need for a holistic approach to e-GP implementation to meet the goal of an end-to-end Procurement system for all the government and public sector entities in the State, CHiPS, under Department of Electronics and Information Technology, Government of Chhattisgarh, thereafter in the year 2015, through M/s Mjunction (System Integrator) has designed &amp; implemented the ERP based Commercial-Off-The-Shelf (COTS) Integrated e-Procurement solution for all the departments and organization of the Chhattisgarh government. It may be appreciated that, based on advanced business intelligence tools and unique algorithms, the analytics-powered e-Procurement solution has a high degree of visibility and control.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1641\" data-end=\"2149\">The Integrated e-Procurement System implemented in the state is its uniqueness and has the most advanced feature of analytics to identify features like PAN number, segregation of bidders and department officials, mapping of the basic business rules of tendering like multiple bidding, collusion or probability of any cartel formation which no other system in the entire country has. These features helped Nodal agency, CHiPS to alert the departments about probability of collusion and other material facts.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2151\" data-end=\"2246\">The Integrated e-Procurement model goes beyond the existing e-tendering process. It includes:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2248\" data-end=\"2431\">&bull; Registration of suppliers / contractors<br data-start=\"2289\" data-end=\"2292\">&bull; Indent management<br data-start=\"2311\" data-end=\"2314\">&bull; e-Tendering<br data-start=\"2327\" data-end=\"2330\">&bull; e-Auction<br data-start=\"2341\" data-end=\"2344\">&bull; Contract management<br data-start=\"2365\" data-end=\"2368\">&bull; e-Payments<br data-start=\"2380\" data-end=\"2383\">&bull; Accounting<br data-start=\"2395\" data-end=\"2398\">&bull; Management Information System</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2433\" data-end=\"2992\">The entire Integrated e-Procurement process has designed to avoid human interface i.e., supplier and buyer interaction during pre-bidding and post-bidding stages. The application ensures total anonymity of the participating suppliers, even to the buyers, until the bids are opened on the platform. The e-Procurement application provides automatic bid evaluation based on the evaluation parameters given to the system. These improved processes have eliminated subjectivity in receipt and evaluation of bids and has reduced corruption to a significant extent.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2994\" data-end=\"3678\">To bring in transparency in Integrated e-Procurement, tender documents containing all details are hosted on the Integrated e-Procurement website. The documents can be downloaded by the interested suppliers free of cost, from the day of publication of a tender. Suppliers/bidders are no more dependent on the officials for various details. At any time in the procurement cycle, any person associated with the transaction can check and know the status of the transaction and also at every stage of the tender activities bidders/suppliers get the email/SMS alert on their mail-id/mobile no. This saves time and effort involved in finding out the status of a tender, purchase order etc.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3680\" data-end=\"3970\">An e-Payment Facility (Multiple Payment Gateway) is integrated with Integrated e-Procurement System for payment of Tender Processing Fees, Earnest Money Deposit (EMD). This is to be done to &lsquo;Minimize Human Intervention&rsquo; thereby minimizing any possibility of disclosure of bidder identity.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3972\" data-end=\"4224\">&bull; Online payments can be done through Credit/Debit card, Net banking, NEFT/RTGS<br data-start=\"4051\" data-end=\"4054\">&bull; Completely secure and confidential<br data-start=\"4090\" data-end=\"4093\">&bull; Online EMD refunds are done within T+2 days<br data-start=\"4138\" data-end=\"4141\">&bull; No need for bidders to visit the department office for any payments and refunds</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4226\" data-end=\"4963\">However, with the expiry of the arrangement with the existing SI (Ms. Mjunction Services Limited) and changing needs of the user departments and the need for a holistic approach to e-Procurement implementation to meet the goal of an end-to-end e-Government Procurement system for all the government and public sector entities in the State, CHiPS is looking forward to implement Government eProcurement System of National Informatics Centre, GePNIC&copy; -- a single product to cater to varied requirements, to provide software as a service, agile development and deployment, segregation of development and implementation, seamless incremental version changes, load handling, process to handle malfunction or unforeseen events and many more.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4965\" data-end=\"5294\"><strong data-start=\"4965\" data-end=\"4987\">Reason for GePNIC:</strong><br data-start=\"4987\" data-end=\"4990\">The existing e-Procurement solution implemented in the State has high dependency on System Integrators as well as high cost of implementation. However, National Informatics Centre, MeitY has developed e-Procurement software system as a product for facilitating Electronic Procurement across Government.</p>\r\n<ol data-start=\"5296\" data-end=\"5629\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hiy5v3\" data-start=\"5296\" data-end=\"5386\">GePNIC is implemented in 24 states, 7 UT&rsquo;s and 750+ Central Government Organizations.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"jrjk7u\" data-start=\"5387\" data-end=\"5451\">86% of India uses GePNIC for electronic procurement system.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"leug5b\" data-start=\"5452\" data-end=\"5629\">Apart from above, after the completion of the project period, department will not have to go through a new tender process every time for selection of new system integrator.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p data-start=\"5631\" data-end=\"5667\"><strong data-start=\"5631\" data-end=\"5665\">Current Implementation Status:</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5669\" data-end=\"5698\"><strong data-start=\"5669\" data-end=\"5696\">Module Adoption Status:</strong></p>\r\n<div class=\"TyagGW_tableContainer\">\r\n<div class=\"group TyagGW_tableWrapper flex flex-col-reverse w-fit\" tabindex=\"-1\">\r\n<table class=\"w-fit min-w-(--thread-content-width)\" data-start=\"5700\" data-end=\"6501\">\r\n<thead data-start=\"5700\" data-end=\"5789\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"5700\" data-end=\"5789\">\r\n<th class=\"\" data-start=\"5700\" data-end=\"5710\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Sr. No.</th>\r\n<th class=\"\" data-start=\"5710\" data-end=\"5733\" data-col-size=\"sm\">Modules Adopted</th>\r\n<th class=\"\" data-start=\"5733\" data-end=\"5789\" data-col-size=\"md\">Department</th>\r\n</tr>\r\n</thead>\r\n<tbody data-start=\"5879\" data-end=\"6501\">\r\n<tr data-start=\"5879\" data-end=\"5967\">\r\n<td data-start=\"5879\" data-end=\"5889\" data-col-size=\"sm\">1</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"5889\" data-end=\"5911\">e-Tendering</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"5911\" data-end=\"5967\">166 Departments</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"5968\" data-end=\"6056\">\r\n<td data-start=\"5968\" data-end=\"5978\" data-col-size=\"sm\">2</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"5978\" data-end=\"6000\">Vendor Registration</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"6000\" data-end=\"6056\">166 Departments</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"6057\" data-end=\"6145\">\r\n<td data-start=\"6057\" data-end=\"6067\" data-col-size=\"sm\">3</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"6067\" data-end=\"6089\">MIS &amp; Accounting</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"6089\" data-end=\"6145\">166 Departments</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"6146\" data-end=\"6234\">\r\n<td data-start=\"6146\" data-end=\"6156\" data-col-size=\"sm\">4</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"6156\" data-end=\"6178\">Online Payment</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"6178\" data-end=\"6234\">166 Departments</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"6235\" data-end=\"6323\">\r\n<td data-start=\"6235\" data-end=\"6245\" data-col-size=\"sm\">5</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"6245\" data-end=\"6267\">Contract</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"6267\" data-end=\"6323\">17 Departments</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"6324\" data-end=\"6412\">\r\n<td data-start=\"6324\" data-end=\"6334\" data-col-size=\"sm\">6</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"6334\" data-end=\"6356\">e-Auction</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"6356\" data-end=\"6412\">MRD Department, CMDC, Civil Supply, and UADD</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n<tr data-start=\"6413\" data-end=\"6501\">\r\n<td data-start=\"6413\" data-end=\"6423\" data-col-size=\"sm\">7</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"sm\" data-start=\"6423\" data-end=\"6445\">Indent</td>\r\n<td data-col-size=\"md\" data-start=\"6445\" data-end=\"6501\">1 Department</td>\r\n</tr>\r\n</tbody>\r\n</table>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p>\r\n</div>\r\n</div>\r\n<hr data-start=\"6503\" data-end=\"6506\">\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"14ks6ae\" data-start=\"6508\" data-end=\"6525\">PURPOSE</h3>\r\n<p data-start=\"6527\" data-end=\"6897\">This EOI is raised with an intention to selection of PMU as mentioned above for a period of 12 months from the date of issuance of the Work Order (WO). Empaneled Consultancy Service Firms will be required to provide assistance to CHiPS for smooth operation &amp; implementation of e-Procurement Project. The selected PMU will operate from the location as desired by CHiPS.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6899\" data-end=\"7294\">CHiPS is looking forward to implement Government eProcurement System of National Informatics Centre, GePNIC &mdash; a single product to cater to varied requirements, to provide software as a service, agile development and deployment, segregation of development and implementation, seamless incremental version changes, load handling, process to handle malfunction or unforeseen events and many more.</p><br>Scope of work changed from <p class=\"ui-text-block-detail font-13\">1. Sr. Consultant (Information Technology) (01 Post)</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"221\" data-end=\"3139\">\r\n<li data-start=\"221\" data-end=\"423\">\r\n<p data-start=\"223\" data-end=\"423\"><strong data-start=\"223\" data-end=\"270\">e-Procurement System Design &amp; Architecture:</strong>&nbsp;Lead the design and architecture of the e-Procurement system, ensuring it aligns with best practices, business requirements, and regulatory standards.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"424\" data-end=\"603\">\r\n<p data-start=\"426\" data-end=\"603\"><strong data-start=\"426\" data-end=\"459\">Project Planning &amp; Execution:</strong>&nbsp;Develop detailed project plans for the e-Procurement implementation, ensuring timely delivery, resource management, and adherence to budgets.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"604\" data-end=\"812\">\r\n<p data-start=\"606\" data-end=\"812\"><strong data-start=\"606\" data-end=\"644\">Technical Consultation &amp; Strategy:</strong>&nbsp;Provide expert advice on the selection and integration of technologies that will optimize the e-Procurement process, including automation, security, and scalability.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"813\" data-end=\"988\">\r\n<p data-start=\"815\" data-end=\"988\"><strong data-start=\"815\" data-end=\"838\">System Integration:</strong>&nbsp;Oversee the integration of the e-Procurement platform with other existing systems (ERP, CRM, etc.), ensuring smooth data flow and interoperability.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"989\" data-end=\"1186\">\r\n<p data-start=\"991\" data-end=\"1186\"><strong data-start=\"991\" data-end=\"1025\">Vendor Selection &amp; Management:</strong>&nbsp;Support the process of selecting and managing technology vendors and service providers for the e-Procurement system, ensuring they meet performance standards.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1187\" data-end=\"1371\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1189\" data-end=\"1371\"><strong data-start=\"1189\" data-end=\"1236\">Customization, Development &amp; Configuration:</strong>&nbsp;Guide the development or customization of features within the e-Procurement platform to meet the specific needs of the organization.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1372\" data-end=\"1576\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1374\" data-end=\"1576\"><strong data-start=\"1374\" data-end=\"1400\">Security &amp; Compliance:</strong>&nbsp;Ensure the e-Procurement system adheres to all security protocols, data privacy regulations, and industry standards, such as ISO/IEC 27001, IT Acts, GFR, CVC, and GDPR, etc.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1577\" data-end=\"1773\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1579\" data-end=\"1773\"><strong data-start=\"1579\" data-end=\"1621\">Performance Monitoring &amp; Optimization:</strong>&nbsp;Oversee the monitoring of system performance, troubleshooting issues, and implementing improvements to enhance system efficiency and user experience.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1774\" data-end=\"1962\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1776\" data-end=\"1962\"><strong data-start=\"1776\" data-end=\"1815\">Stakeholder Engagement &amp; Reporting:</strong>&nbsp;Act as the primary point of contact for all technical stakeholders, providing regular updates on project status, risks, and performance metrics.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1963\" data-end=\"2160\">\r\n<p data-start=\"1965\" data-end=\"2160\"><strong data-start=\"1965\" data-end=\"1998\">Training &amp; Capacity Building:</strong>&nbsp;Develop and conduct training programs for internal stakeholders (procurement team, users, etc.) on the e-Procurement system&rsquo;s functionality and best practices.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2161\" data-end=\"2336\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2163\" data-end=\"2336\"><strong data-start=\"2163\" data-end=\"2185\">Change Management:</strong>&nbsp;Lead efforts to manage change within the organization as new e-Procurement tools and processes are adopted, ensuring smooth transition and adoption.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2337\" data-end=\"2541\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2339\" data-end=\"2541\"><strong data-start=\"2339\" data-end=\"2371\">Post-Implementation Support:</strong>&nbsp;Provide ongoing technical support after the system is live, ensuring continuous operation, troubleshooting, and enhancements based on user feedback and evolving needs.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2542\" data-end=\"2726\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2544\" data-end=\"2726\"><strong data-start=\"2544\" data-end=\"2574\">Documentation &amp; Reporting:</strong>&nbsp;Create and maintain comprehensive technical documentation, including system design, process flows, and user manuals for future reference and updates.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2727\" data-end=\"2911\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2729\" data-end=\"2911\"><strong data-start=\"2729\" data-end=\"2756\">Continuous Improvement:</strong>&nbsp;Identify opportunities for continuous improvement in the e-Procurement system, driving innovations that optimize procurement processes and reduce costs.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2912\" data-end=\"3011\">\r\n<p data-start=\"2914\" data-end=\"3011\"><strong data-start=\"2914\" data-end=\"2948\">Migration and Exit Management:</strong>&nbsp;Manage migration and exit from the current system to GePNIC.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3012\" data-end=\"3139\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3014\" data-end=\"3139\"><strong data-start=\"3014\" data-end=\"3036\">Additional Duties:</strong>&nbsp;Perform any additional duties related to finance or any other task as assigned by senior management.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<hr data-start=\"3141\" data-end=\"3144\">\r\n<p>2. Consultant (Information Technology) (02 Posts)</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3201\" data-end=\"5740\">\r\n<li data-start=\"3201\" data-end=\"3371\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3203\" data-end=\"3371\"><strong data-start=\"3203\" data-end=\"3236\">System Requirements Analysis:</strong>&nbsp;Assist in gathering and analyzing business requirements for the e-Procurement system, ensuring they align with organizational goals.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3372\" data-end=\"3555\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3374\" data-end=\"3555\"><strong data-start=\"3374\" data-end=\"3400\">Technology Evaluation:</strong>&nbsp;Assist in evaluating and recommending appropriate technologies, platforms, and tools for the development and implementation of the e-Procurement system.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3556\" data-end=\"3716\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3558\" data-end=\"3716\"><strong data-start=\"3558\" data-end=\"3584\">System Design Support:</strong>&nbsp;Collaborate in the design and architecture of the e-Procurement platform, ensuring scalability, performance, and user-centricity.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3717\" data-end=\"3894\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3719\" data-end=\"3894\"><strong data-start=\"3719\" data-end=\"3743\">Integration Support:</strong>&nbsp;Assist in integrating the e-Procurement system with other internal systems (ERP, CRM, etc.), ensuring seamless data exchange and process automation.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"3895\" data-end=\"4073\">\r\n<p data-start=\"3897\" data-end=\"4073\"><strong data-start=\"3897\" data-end=\"3931\">Customization &amp; Configuration:</strong>&nbsp;Support the customization and configuration of the e-Procurement platform to meet specific business requirements and procurement workflows.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4074\" data-end=\"4243\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4076\" data-end=\"4243\"><strong data-start=\"4076\" data-end=\"4102\">Security &amp; Compliance:</strong>&nbsp;Ensure the e-Procurement system complies with security standards and legal regulations (e.g., data privacy laws, procurement rules, etc.).</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4244\" data-end=\"4423\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4246\" data-end=\"4423\"><strong data-start=\"4246\" data-end=\"4278\">Testing &amp; Quality Assurance:</strong>&nbsp;Assist in testing the system for functionality, performance, security, and usability, ensuring that it meets quality standards before go-live.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4424\" data-end=\"4567\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4426\" data-end=\"4567\"><strong data-start=\"4426\" data-end=\"4447\">Training Support:</strong>&nbsp;Help develop training materials and provide training to end-users on how to effectively use the e-Procurement system.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4568\" data-end=\"4743\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4570\" data-end=\"4743\"><strong data-start=\"4570\" data-end=\"4609\">Troubleshooting &amp; Issue Resolution:</strong>&nbsp;Provide technical support for troubleshooting and resolving system issues during the implementation and post-implementation phases.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4744\" data-end=\"4915\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4746\" data-end=\"4915\"><strong data-start=\"4746\" data-end=\"4764\">Documentation:</strong>&nbsp;Assist in creating technical documentation, including system specifications, user guides, and operational manuals for future reference and training.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"4916\" data-end=\"5090\">\r\n<p data-start=\"4918\" data-end=\"5090\"><strong data-start=\"4918\" data-end=\"4942\">Vendor Coordination:</strong>&nbsp;Coordinate with third-party vendors, ensuring smooth delivery of the e-Procurement system components as per project timelines and specifications.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5091\" data-end=\"5285\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5093\" data-end=\"5285\"><strong data-start=\"5093\" data-end=\"5125\">Post-Implementation Support:</strong>&nbsp;Provide ongoing technical support to ensure the smooth operation of the e-Procurement system, including resolving bugs and implementing minor system updates.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5286\" data-end=\"5472\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5288\" data-end=\"5472\"><strong data-start=\"5288\" data-end=\"5330\">Monitoring &amp; Performance Optimization:</strong>&nbsp;Assist in monitoring system performance, identifying potential issues, and recommending enhancements to optimize the platform&rsquo;s efficiency.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5473\" data-end=\"5634\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5475\" data-end=\"5634\"><strong data-start=\"5475\" data-end=\"5502\">Continuous Improvement:</strong>&nbsp;Suggest and implement improvements to the system based on user feedback, changing business needs, and technological advancements.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"5635\" data-end=\"5740\">\r\n<p data-start=\"5637\" data-end=\"5740\"><strong data-start=\"5637\" data-end=\"5659\">Additional Duties:</strong> Perform additional accounting tasks as assigned by senior management or CHiPS.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul> to <p data-start=\"171\" data-end=\"238\">❖ Principal Consultant and Sr. Consultant (Information Technology):</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"240\" data-end=\"268\">&bull; Exit Management Process: -</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"272\" data-end=\"444\">&bull; Creation of the Exit Management Process, Migration Process, and Time lines and scheduled, creation of the archival Server and Access policy of the archival server data.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"448\" data-end=\"708\">&bull; Stake holder departments Consultation for Concluding all the tenders from earlier e-Procurement System and thereafter the user data of all Departments/Vendors from the Integrated e-Procurement System needs to be ported /migrated into &lsquo;GePNIC e-Procurement.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"712\" data-end=\"983\">&bull; Preparing the Exit Management Report and As a part of Exit Management Process, ensure the complete Data backup on final date of exit along with hashing will be obtained from Current System Integrator &amp; will be archived on CHiPS designated Server at State Data Center.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"987\" data-end=\"1198\">&bull; Also responsible for handing over and taking over of data set, Quality Check, Authenticity of the backup data, Audit Procedure. Litigation/Dispute handling if any which may arise in future may be choked out.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1202\" data-end=\"1406\">&bull; Ensure the current &ldquo;Integrated e-Procurement System&rdquo; for future query &amp; statutory auditing purpose, needs to remain up and running with all the users &ldquo;having only viewing rights&rdquo; at State Data Center.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1410\" data-end=\"1590\">&bull; Ensure all the compliance has to complete all the relevant activity of Exit Management Process as per terms &amp; condition defined in the Agreement under Exit Management Services.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1594\" data-end=\"1778\">&bull; Preparing Strategy &amp; Sequencing and procedure to maintain the Current Integrated e-Procurement Server &amp; Solution remain up and running for future query &amp; statutory auditing purpose</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1780\" data-end=\"1798\">&bull; Migration Plan</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1802\" data-end=\"1922\">&bull; Creation of the Migration Process to GePNIC. Preparing Documents, Report and all the related documents for the same.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1926\" data-end=\"2180\">&bull; Data Migration and Validation: They actively participate in migrating critical data (suppliers, contracts, item catalogs, e-Procurement work flow and historical information) from legacy systems to the GePNIC platform, ensuring accuracy and integrity.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2182\" data-end=\"2250\">&bull; Customization &amp; Configuration &amp; Implementation Support of GePNIC</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2254\" data-end=\"2497\">&bull; Customization &amp; Configuration &amp; Implementation of the GePNIC: Support the customization &amp; Configuration of the e-Procurement platform (GePNIC) system. Support to Creation of the workflow to meet specific department&rsquo;s procurement workflows.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2501\" data-end=\"2672\">&bull; Supplier On boarding: They manage the process of transitioning suppliers to the new GePNIC System, often providing guidance and support to ensure smooth collaboration.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2692\" data-end=\"2835\">&bull; Departments on boarding: - arrange the Kick Off Meeting and consultation with the Departments for adopting the GePNIC e-Procurement System.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2839\" data-end=\"3059\">&bull; Stakeholder Alignment: They work with various stakeholders (finance, procurement teams, leadership, suppliers) to promote collaboration, manage cultural shifts, and ensure enterprise-wide acceptance of the new tools.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3063\" data-end=\"3228\">&bull; Training and Development: provide or oversee training for internal teams and suppliers to equip them with the necessary skills to use the new system effectively.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3232\" data-end=\"3367\">&bull; User Acceptance Testing (UAT): They support testing efforts to identify and resolve system defects or errors before full deployment</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3371\" data-end=\"3606\">&bull; Integration Support: Assist in integrating the GePNIC e-Procurement system with other internal systems (ERP, CRM, Payment Gateway, Legacy System of the User Departments etc.), ensuring seamless data exchange and process automation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3610\" data-end=\"3775\">&bull; Security &amp;Compliance : Ensure the e-Procurement system complies with security standards and legal regulations (e.g., data privacy laws, procurement rules, etc.).</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3779\" data-end=\"3954\">&bull; Testing &amp; Quality Assurance: Assist in testing the system for functionality, performance, security, and usability, ensuring that it meets quality standards before go-live.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3958\" data-end=\"4142\">&bull; Training Support: Help develop training materials and provide training to end-users on how to effectively use the e-Procurement system for the stake holder Departments and Vendors.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4146\" data-end=\"4317\">&bull; Troubleshooting &amp; Issue Resolution: Provide technical support for troubleshooting and resolving system issues during the implementation and post-implementation phases.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4321\" data-end=\"4586\">&bull; Documentation: Assist in creating technical documentation, including system specifications, user guides, and operational manuals for future reference and training, FAQ, Audit Documents and any other documents related to e-Procurements or assigned work by CHiPS.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4590\" data-end=\"4876\">&bull; Vendor Coordination: Coordinate with third-party vendors, ensuring smooth Integration of the third party system &amp; delivery of the e-Procurement system components such as Payment Gateway, Legacy System of the other Departments, ERP System as per project timelines and specifications.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4880\" data-end=\"5070\">&bull; Post-Implementation Support: Provide ongoing technical support to ensure the smooth operation of the e-Procurement system, including resolving bugs and implementing minor system updates.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5074\" data-end=\"5256\">&bull; Monitoring &amp; Performance Optimization: Assist in monitoring system performance, identifying potential issues, and recommending enhancements to optimize the platform&rsquo;s efficiency.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5260\" data-end=\"5417\">&bull; Continuous Improvement: Suggest and implement improvements to the system based on user feedback, changing business needs, and technological advancements.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5421\" data-end=\"5507\">&bull; Perform additional accounting tasks as assigned by senior management or the CHiPS.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5509\" data-end=\"5987\">This scope defines a broad, end-to-end role that ensures a smooth transition from legacy systems to innovative procurement platforms, maintaining data integrity, compliance, user readiness, and vendor collaboration throughout the project lifecycle. The Principal Consultant would typically lead strategy and oversight, the Senior Consultant would manage critical execution and coordination, and the Consultant may focus more on technical implementation and user support tasks.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"6005\" data-end=\"6008\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6010\" data-end=\"6059\">❖ Principal Consultant (Information Technology)</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6061\" data-end=\"6453\">&bull; Leads overall strategy and governance of exit management and migration.<br data-start=\"6134\" data-end=\"6137\">&bull; Oversees compliance with contracts and regulatory requirements.<br data-start=\"6202\" data-end=\"6205\">&bull; Coordinates with senior stakeholders to ensure smooth handovers.<br data-start=\"6271\" data-end=\"6274\">&bull; Provides strategic direction on system integration, data integrity, and enterprise-wide adoption.<br data-start=\"6373\" data-end=\"6376\">&bull; Ensures risk management during transition and post-implementation phases.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"6455\" data-end=\"6458\">\r\n<p data-start=\"6460\" data-end=\"6506\">❖ Senior Consultant (Information Technology)</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6508\" data-end=\"7454\">&bull; Manages critical execution of exit management processes, including data archival, backup, verification, and reporting.<br data-start=\"6628\" data-end=\"6631\">&bull; Leads migration planning and validation activities for complex data sets.<br data-start=\"6706\" data-end=\"6709\">&bull; Coordinates workflow customization and departmental onboarding.<br data-start=\"6774\" data-end=\"6777\">&bull; Facilitates stakeholder engagement and training program oversight.<br data-start=\"6845\" data-end=\"6848\">&bull; Ensures User Acceptance Testing and quality assurance management.<br data-start=\"6915\" data-end=\"6918\">&bull; Handles vendor coordination for seamless integration with Payment Gateway, ERP, and legacy systems.<br data-start=\"7019\" data-end=\"7022\">&bull; Executes technical tasks such as customization, configuration, and implementation support for the GePNIC platform.<br data-start=\"7138\" data-end=\"7141\">&bull; Assists in supplier on boarding and departmental consultations.<br data-start=\"7206\" data-end=\"7209\">&bull; Supports creation and delivery of training materials and sessions.<br data-start=\"7277\" data-end=\"7280\">&bull; Provides troubleshooting, bug fixes, and minor system updates during and after implementation.<br data-start=\"7376\" data-end=\"7379\">&bull; Supports development of system documentation including guides and FAQs.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7456\" data-end=\"7955\">This hierarchical approach ensures that leadership focuses on strategy and compliance (Principal Consultant), mid-level management handles critical project coordination and stakeholder engagement (Senior Consultant), and technical staff concentrate on implementation, training, and support (Consultant). The scope reflects an endto-end responsibility to guarantee smooth transition from legacy to modern e-Procurement systems, maintaining operational continuity, data security, and user readiness.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"7957\" data-end=\"7960\">\r\n<p data-start=\"7962\" data-end=\"7997\">❖ Sr. Consultant (Infrastructure)</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7999\" data-end=\"8269\">The scope of work for an infrastructure consultant related to the Integrated e-Procurement System focuses on maintaining system availability, data integrity, and secure archiving during and after the transition phase. Here&rsquo;s an elaboration of the key responsibilities:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8271\" data-end=\"8533\">&bull; System Availability for Audits: Ensure the existing Integrated e-Procurement System remains operational at the State Data Center with users having strictly view-only rights. This supports future queries and statutory audits without risking data modification.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8535\" data-end=\"8748\">&bull; Server and Solution Maintenance: Continuously maintain the hardware and software infrastructure hosting the legacy e-Procurement system to guarantee uptime and reliability during the exit and post-exit period.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8750\" data-end=\"9038\">&bull; Archival Server Setup and Access Policy: Design, implement, and manage a dedicated archival server to store backup data securely. Develop and enforce access control policies that regulate who can view or retrieve archived data, ensuring compliance with security and privacy standards.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9056\" data-end=\"9388\">&bull; Data Backup with Hashing for Exit Management: As part of the exit process, ensure all data is fully backed up on the final exit date. Obtain these backups from the current System Integrator, verify their integrity using hashing techniques, and archive the data safely on the CHiPS-designated server within the State Data Center.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9390\" data-end=\"9568\">&bull; Pre-Migration Backup Preparation: Before starting any migration activities, confirm that comprehensive and consistent data backups exist to prevent data loss during transfer.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9570\" data-end=\"9801\">This scope prioritizes robust infrastructure support to uphold data availability, integrity, and security throughout the transition from the legacy procurement system to a new platform, with full compliance to audit requirements.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"9803\" data-end=\"9806\">\r\n<p data-start=\"9808\" data-end=\"9862\">❖ Scope of work Sr. Consultant (Financial &amp; Legal):-</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"9864\" data-end=\"10146\">Scope of work of Financial &amp; Legal Consultant is a comprehensive set of tasks and responsibilities across several domains&mdash;reconciliation, legal review, contract and procurement support, regulatory compliance, financial planning, legal risk management, and documentation/reporting.</p>\r\n<ol data-start=\"10148\" data-end=\"11574\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hxe8en\" data-start=\"10148\" data-end=\"10405\">Reconciliation<br data-start=\"10165\" data-end=\"10168\">&bull; Perform account reconciliation for financial accuracy.<br data-start=\"10224\" data-end=\"10227\">&bull; Reconcile payment gateway transactions.<br data-start=\"10268\" data-end=\"10271\">&bull; Match EMD (Earnest Money Deposit) and tender document fees with records.<br data-start=\"10345\" data-end=\"10348\">&bull; Reconcile refunds related to bidders and departments.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"duadep\" data-start=\"10407\" data-end=\"10735\">Legal Review &amp; Regulatory Advisory<br data-start=\"10444\" data-end=\"10447\">&bull; Review laws, regulations, contracts, and policy documents.<br data-start=\"10507\" data-end=\"10510\">&bull; Identify legal risks, gaps, and compliance issues.<br data-start=\"10562\" data-end=\"10565\">&bull; Recommend legal alignments with national/state and sector-specific guidelines.<br data-start=\"10645\" data-end=\"10648\">&bull; Draft, vet, and revise MoUs, agreements, RFPs, contracts, and legal case documents.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"mllwvx\" data-start=\"10737\" data-end=\"11062\">Contract &amp; Procurement Support<br data-start=\"10770\" data-end=\"10773\">&bull; Develop procurement-related documents: RFPs, RFQs, bid documents, evaluation criteria.<br data-start=\"10861\" data-end=\"10864\">&bull; Aid in contract drafting, negotiation, and finalization.<br data-start=\"10922\" data-end=\"10925\">&bull; Ensure procurement complies with legal and financial requirements.<br data-start=\"10993\" data-end=\"10996\">&bull; Assist with vendor evaluation and mitigating associated risks.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"18w7772\" data-start=\"11064\" data-end=\"11333\">Regulatory Compliance &amp; Governance<br data-start=\"11101\" data-end=\"11104\">&bull; Ensure compliance with financial, tax, corporate, and statutory requirements.<br data-start=\"11183\" data-end=\"11186\">&bull; Advise on governance frameworks including roles and accountability.<br data-start=\"11255\" data-end=\"11258\">&bull; Monitor audit processes, regulatory adherence, and reporting standards.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1675hdg\" data-start=\"11335\" data-end=\"11574\">Financial Planning &amp; Budget Management<br data-start=\"11376\" data-end=\"11379\">&bull; Support budget preparation, fund allocation, and expenditure planning.<br data-start=\"11451\" data-end=\"11454\">&bull; Monitor financial performance and analyze variances.<br data-start=\"11508\" data-end=\"11511\">&bull; Develop financial control guidelines and reporting formats.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"16nft9g\" data-start=\"11593\" data-end=\"11845\">Legal Risk Assessment &amp; Mitigation<br data-start=\"11630\" data-end=\"11633\">&bull; Identify potential legal risks in contracts, regulations, and operations.<br data-start=\"11708\" data-end=\"11711\">&bull; Recommend risk mitigation and legal safeguards.<br data-start=\"11760\" data-end=\"11763\">&bull; Provide support on dispute resolution, arbitration, and compliance challenges.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12tscod\" data-start=\"11847\" data-end=\"12107\">Documentation &amp; Reporting<br data-start=\"11875\" data-end=\"11878\">&bull; Prepare financial, legal, compliance, and advisory reports.<br data-start=\"11939\" data-end=\"11942\">&bull; Create standard templates, checklists, and documentation formats.<br data-start=\"12009\" data-end=\"12012\">&bull; Deliver monthly, quarterly, and final reports summarizing key insights and recommendations.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1mfyaej\" data-start=\"12109\" data-end=\"12330\">Stakeholder Coordination<br data-start=\"12136\" data-end=\"12139\">&bull; Coordinate with government departments, legal authorities, finance teams, auditors, and external stakeholders.<br data-start=\"12251\" data-end=\"12254\">&bull; Support interactions with regulators, consultants, and project partners.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"16qfsmn\" data-start=\"12332\" data-end=\"12536\">Capacity Building<br data-start=\"12353\" data-end=\"12356\">&bull; Conduct training sessions on financial management, legal compliance, and contract management.<br data-start=\"12451\" data-end=\"12454\">&bull; Prepare manuals, SOPs, and knowledge material for institutional strengthening.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p data-start=\"12538\" data-end=\"12633\">10 Others: Perform additional accounting tasks as assigned by senior management or the CHiPS.</p>\r\n<hr data-start=\"12635\" data-end=\"12638\">\r\n<p data-start=\"12640\" data-end=\"12693\">❖ Scope of work Sr. Consultant (Procurement Expert)</p>\r\n<ol data-start=\"12695\" data-end=\"13499\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1qbfgoe\" data-start=\"12695\" data-end=\"12999\">Contract Management<br data-start=\"12717\" data-end=\"12720\">&bull; Draft, review, and manage procurement contracts in line with organizational standards.<br data-start=\"12808\" data-end=\"12811\">&bull; Negotiate contract terms and conditions with vendors to ensure favorable outcomes.<br data-start=\"12895\" data-end=\"12898\">&bull; Track contract lifecycle, renewals, amendments, expirations, and maintain complete documentation.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1w2lidh\" data-start=\"13001\" data-end=\"13175\">Vendor Negotiation<br data-start=\"13022\" data-end=\"13025\">&bull; Lead negotiations on pricing, delivery terms, and service-level agreements.<br data-start=\"13102\" data-end=\"13105\">&bull; Conduct comparative evaluation of vendor quotations and proposals.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1r7l6y5\" data-start=\"13177\" data-end=\"13499\">Compliance Management<br data-start=\"13201\" data-end=\"13204\">&bull; Ensure all procurement activities comply with Government of India (GoI) and Government of Chhattisgarh (GoCG) rules and regulations.<br data-start=\"13338\" data-end=\"13341\">&bull; Maintain expertise in:<br data-start=\"13365\" data-end=\"13368\">o CVC Guidelines<br data-start=\"13386\" data-end=\"13389\">o General Financial Rules (GFR)<br data-start=\"13422\" data-end=\"13425\">o IT Act 2000<br data-start=\"13440\" data-end=\"13443\">o Other public procurement frameworks and guidelines</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p data-start=\"13501\" data-end=\"13595\">&bull; Provide guidance to CHiPS departments to ensure adherence to government procurement norms.</p>\r\n<ol start=\"4\" data-start=\"13597\" data-end=\"13893\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1v51ujt\" data-start=\"13597\" data-end=\"13893\">RFP/EoI/Procurement Document Creation<br data-start=\"13637\" data-end=\"13640\">&bull; Draft comprehensive procurement documents including:<br data-start=\"13694\" data-end=\"13697\">o Request for Proposal (RFP)<br data-start=\"13727\" data-end=\"13730\">o Expression of Interest (EoI)<br data-start=\"13762\" data-end=\"13765\">o Request for Quotation (RFQ)<br data-start=\"13796\" data-end=\"13799\">o Bid Documents, Scope of Work, Evaluation Criteria, Eligibility Conditions, Formats, etc.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p data-start=\"13912\" data-end=\"14225\">&bull; Coordinate with technical and project teams to convert technical requirements into well-structured procurement documents.<br data-start=\"14035\" data-end=\"14038\">&bull; Ensure all RFP/EoI documents are compliant with CVC, GFR, and GoI/GoCG procurement rules.<br data-start=\"14129\" data-end=\"14132\">&bull; Manage publication, clarification responses, corrigenda, and the overall bidding process.</p>\r\n<ol start=\"5\" data-start=\"14227\" data-end=\"16013\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"nxr26a\" data-start=\"14227\" data-end=\"14506\">Supplier Performance Management<br data-start=\"14261\" data-end=\"14264\">&bull; Conduct periodic evaluations of suppliers based on quality, delivery, cost, and responsiveness.<br data-start=\"14361\" data-end=\"14364\">&bull; Maintain supplier performance scorecards and initiate corrective actions where needed.<br data-start=\"14452\" data-end=\"14455\">&bull; Identify and onboard new vendors when required.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1dfslp8\" data-start=\"14508\" data-end=\"14773\">Reporting &amp; Documentation<br data-start=\"14536\" data-end=\"14539\">&bull; Prepare daily, monthly, and quarterly procurement reports.<br data-start=\"14599\" data-end=\"14602\">&bull; Maintain audit-ready documentation for all procurement processes.<br data-start=\"14669\" data-end=\"14672\">&bull; Track procurement KPIs such as savings achieved, vendor performance, procurement cycle time, etc.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1dlq7v7\" data-start=\"14775\" data-end=\"15064\">Supplier Relationship Management<br data-start=\"14810\" data-end=\"14813\">&bull; Build and maintain effective, long-term relationships with vendors.<br data-start=\"14882\" data-end=\"14885\">&bull; Act as the primary point of contact for vendor communications, dispute resolution, and negotiations.<br data-start=\"14987\" data-end=\"14990\">&bull; Organize vendor meetings, performance reviews, and follow-up sessions.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1t88ntb\" data-start=\"15066\" data-end=\"15322\">Cross-Departmental Coordination<br data-start=\"15100\" data-end=\"15103\">&bull; Collaborate with finance, legal, technical, and project teams for the smooth execution of procurement activities.<br data-start=\"15218\" data-end=\"15221\">&bull; Support teams in terms of procurement planning, budgeting, and preparing accurate specifications.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"qji0ni\" data-start=\"15324\" data-end=\"15613\">Risk Management<br data-start=\"15342\" data-end=\"15345\">&bull; Identify procurement-related risks such as supply chain delays, non-performance, or contract deviations.<br data-start=\"15451\" data-end=\"15454\">&bull; Develop mitigation plans to ensure business continuity and compliance.<br data-start=\"15526\" data-end=\"15529\">&bull; Conduct due diligence on vendors and proposals to recognize potential red flags.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"pblvmr\" data-start=\"15615\" data-end=\"16013\">Advisory Role for CHiPS<br data-start=\"15642\" data-end=\"15645\">&bull; Provide expert procurement advisory support to CHiPS projects.<br data-start=\"15709\" data-end=\"15712\">&bull; Ensure consistency and compliance in all procurement actions across CHiPS initiatives.<br data-start=\"15800\" data-end=\"15803\">&bull; Conduct internal trainings/awareness sessions on CVC guidelines, GFR rules, and public procurement practices.<br data-start=\"15914\" data-end=\"15917\">&bull; Support internal and external audits by providing required documentation and clarifications.</li>\r\n</ol><br>', '2026-05-01 12:32:56', 90, 1, '2026-05-01 12:43:09', 1);
