(221, 171, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <h3 dir=\"ltr\">Qualification</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">B.E./B.Tech in Civil Engineering.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">M.E./M.Tech/ Master\'s Degree in Business Administration / Infrastructure Management / Construction Management / Project Management / Public Policy / Rural Development or equivalent.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">Minimum 3+ years experience as mentioned in the letter .</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p> to <ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">B.E./B.Tech in Civil Engineering.</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">M.E./M.Tech/ Master\'s Degree in Business Administration / Infrastructure Management / Construction Management / Project Management / Public Policy / Rural Development or equivalent.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">Minimum 3+ years experience as mentioned in the letter.</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>Remark changed from <h3 dir=\"ltr\">Remarks</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Strong ability to assess technical aspects of infrastructure projects.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Experience in physical verification and quality assessment of public infrastructure.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to review and appraise DPRs and technical proposals.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Knowledge of project feasibility assessment, cost estimation, benchmarking, and infrastructure planning.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Exposure to geotagging, GIS-based asset mapping, and infrastructure monitoring systems.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to support projects across sectors, including health, education, livelihood, water supply, sanitation, tribal development, skill development, and public infrastructure.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to work in remote and tribal areas and undertake extensive field visits.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p> </p> to <ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Strong ability to assess technical aspects of infrastructure projects.</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Experience in physical verification and quality assessment of public infrastructure.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to review and appraise DPRs and technical proposals.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Knowledge of project feasibility assessment, cost estimation, benchmarking, and infrastructure planning.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Exposure to geotagging, GIS-based asset mapping, and infrastructure monitoring systems.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to support projects across sectors, including health, education, livelihood, water supply, sanitation, tribal development, skill development, and public infrastructure.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to work in remote and tribal areas and undertake extensive field visits.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 14-06-2026, 10:53 AM', '2026-06-14 10:53:40', 623, 1, '2026-06-14 10:55:04', 1),
(222, 171, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <h3 dir=\"ltr\">Qualification</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Any relevant Bachelor&rsquo;s degree.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Master of Social Work (MSW)/Master\'s Degree in Business Administration / Project Management / Public Policy / Rural Development/ Public Health/ Education or equivalent.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 3+ years experience as mentioned in the letter.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p>&nbsp;</p> to <ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Any relevant Bachelor&rsquo;s degree.</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Master of Social Work (MSW)/Master\'s Degree in Business Administration / Project Management / Public Policy / Rural Development/ Public Health/ Education or equivalent.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Minimum 3+ years experience as mentioned in the letter.</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>Remark changed from <h3 dir=\"ltr\">Remarks</h3>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Demonstrated experience in social development programmes, community mobilization, stakeholder engagement, participatory planning, and implementation of development interventions in rural, tribal, and vulnerable communities.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Experience in working with Government departments, local governance institutions, civil society organizations, community-based organizations, Self Help Groups (SHGs), and grassroots stakeholders.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to support projects across health, education, livelihood promotion, tribal development, women and child development, governance, infrastructure, and other development sectors.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Experience in conducting field assessments, beneficiary consultations, need assessments, social audits, impact assessments, and monitoring & evaluation studies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to facilitate community consultations, focus group discussions, participatory rural appraisal exercises, and stakeholder workshops.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Experience in project planning, implementation support, documentation, reporting, and outcome tracking for social sector initiatives.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Proficiency in digital survey design, mobile data collection platforms, and data digitization.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to develop dashboards, MIS systems, analytical reports, and data visualization tools.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Working knowledge of AI-enabled tools for analytics, reporting, knowledge management, and decision-support systems.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to undertake extensive field visits, beneficiary interactions, stakeholder consultations, and community engagement activities in remote and tribal areas.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p> </p> to <ul>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Demonstrated experience in social development programmes, community mobilization, stakeholder engagement, participatory planning, and implementation of development interventions in rural, tribal, and vulnerable communities.</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Experience in working with Government departments, local governance institutions, civil society organizations, community-based organizations, Self Help Groups (SHGs), and grassroots stakeholders.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to support projects across health, education, livelihood promotion, tribal development, women and child development, governance, infrastructure, and other development sectors.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Experience in conducting field assessments, beneficiary consultations, need assessments, social audits, impact assessments, and monitoring &amp; evaluation studies.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to facilitate community consultations, focus group discussions, participatory rural appraisal exercises, and stakeholder workshops.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Experience in project planning, implementation support, documentation, reporting, and outcome tracking for social sector initiatives.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Proficiency in digital survey design, mobile data collection platforms, and data digitization.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to develop dashboards, MIS systems, analytical reports, and data visualization tools.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Working knowledge of AI-enabled tools for analytics, reporting, knowledge management, and decision-support systems.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Ability to undertake extensive field visits, beneficiary interactions, stakeholder consultations, and community engagement activities in remote and tribal areas.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul>.<br>on 14-06-2026, 10:54 AM', '2026-06-14 10:54:10', 623, 1, '2026-06-14 10:54:57', 1),
(223, 172, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Sector changed from FINANCIAL AND LEGAL to GOVERNANCE.<br>on 14-06-2026, 01:55 PM', '2026-06-14 13:55:37', 94, 1, '2026-06-14 15:27:49', 1);
INSERT INTO `log_eoi_updates` (`recordid`, `requestid`, `particular`, `updatedon`, `updatedby`, `isviewed`, `viewedon`, `viewedby`) VALUES
(224, 172, 'Scope of work changed from <p>The deployed team shall carry out the following tasks during the term of the engagement:</p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li><strong>Transaction Advisory and Bid Process Management</strong>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Provide end-to-end transaction advisory and bid process management support for procurement of goods, services, and works across the aviation sector, covering the full bid cycle from need assessment to contract award and contract management.</li>\r\n<li>Techno-commercial assessment for proposed aviation procurements and advise on appropriate procurement and contracting strategies.</li>\r\n<li>Prepare, review, and finalise procurement documents including Expressions of Interest (EoIs), Requests for Proposal (RFPs), Requests for Qualification (RFQs), bid documents, draft contracts, concession agreements, Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs), and related documentation.</li>\r\n<li>Design qualification criteria, evaluation frameworks, and bid evaluation methodologies in alignment with the General Financial Rules (GFR) 2017, Central Vigilance Commission (CVC) guidelines, and applicable State of Chhattisgarh procurement rules.</li>\r\n<li>Manage the complete bid process, including pre-bid meetings, issuance of clarifications and corrigendum, bid opening, evaluation support, and preparation of evaluation reports and recommendations for the competent authority.</li>\r\n<li>Provide transaction advisory and bid process management support for empanelment of, and tendering for, the following primary aviation services and infrastructure but not limited to:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Ground handling agencies for airports and airstrips in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Helicopter services, including charter, regional connectivity, and emergency / medical evacuation services.</li>\r\n<li>Agencies for capacity building and training of aviation sector personnel and for institutional strengthening of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li>Suppliers of safety, security, and firefighting equipment for aviation facilities.</li>\r\n<li>Agencies for the development, upgradation, and maintenance of airstrips and allied aviation infrastructure.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Prepare empanelment frameworks, eligibility criteria, and rate-contract or panel-based selection structures for recurring aviation service requirements of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li>Support the Directorate in tender publication, bidder coordination, evaluation, award, and onboarding of empanelled service providers.</li>\r\n<li>Develop contract management and performance monitoring frameworks for empanelled agencies and selected service providers.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>2. Policy, Schemes, and Skill Development</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Support in the formulation of the State Aviation Policy, including policy research, benchmarking with national and global practices, stakeholder consultations, and drafting.</li>\r\n<li>Support the Directorate in the design and development of aviation sector schemes for promotion of air connectivity, aviation services, infrastructure, and investment in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate and assist the Directorate in the selection of specialised agencies for the development of training modules and curricula for skill development of local youth in aviation and allied trades, including pilot training, cabin crew training, aircraft maintenance engineering (AME), air traffic control (ATC), and ground handling.</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate partnerships and coordination with Flying Training Organisations (FTOs), national aviation academies, DGCA-approved institutions, and skill development agencies for establishment of training centres and skilling initiatives in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Suggestion on initiatives to promote aviation-related employment opportunities for local youth and to strengthen the aviation skilling ecosystem in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Conduct a comparative study of aviation services, schemes, and best practices implemented by other States, including regional connectivity, helicopter services, aviation infrastructure, aviation skilling, investment promotion, and allied aviation services. Identify replicable practices and prepare recommendations for adoption and contextual adaptation in Chhattisgarh, including implementation roadmaps and institutional arrangements required for roll-out.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>3. Project Monitoring, Reporting, and Departmental Handholding</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Provide project management support for aviation infrastructure and service delivery projects, including activities under the Regional Connectivity Scheme (RCS), airport and airstrip development, and operationalisation of State aviation assets.</li>\r\n<li>PMU shall support for monitoring of all ongoing projects and track upcoming and future projects, including their onboarding, progress, timelines, and overall implementation status.</li>\r\n<li>Establish and maintain a structured project monitoring framework covering all aviation projects, procurements, and empanelment processes, including project timelines, milestones, deliverables, and physical and financial progress against approved targets.</li>\r\n<li>Track the implementation status of selected and empanelled service providers, contractors, and agencies, and prepare progress reviews highlighting delays, bottlenecks, deviations from approved scope, and corrective actions required.</li>\r\n<li>Prepare periodic monitoring and progress reports, including weekly status updates, monthly progress reports, and quarterly review reports, in formats approved by the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li>Verify bills and invoices submitted by selected agencies, contractors, and service providers against the terms and conditions of the tender, work order, and contract. Recommend approval or rejection of bills with supporting verification notes.</li>\r\n<li>Support the Directorate in compilation of data and preparation of replies, status notes, and information sought by the State Government, the Legislative Assembly, audit authorities, and other competent forums.</li>\r\n<li>Coordinate with regulatory authorities, national aviation institutions, and industry stakeholders, and support stakeholder communication, meeting coordination, and follow-up actions.</li>\r\n<li>Carry out any other task assigned by the Directorate of Aviation related to aviation sector development, transaction advisory, bid process management, and routine departmental work.</li>\r\n</ol> to <p>The deployed team shall carry out the following tasks during the term of the engagement:</p>\r\n<p><strong>1. Transaction Advisory and Bid Process Management</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Provide end-to-end transaction advisory and bid process management support for procurement of goods, services, and works across the aviation sector, covering the full bid cycle from need assessment to contract award and contract management.</li>\r\n<li>Techno-commercial assessment for proposed aviation procurements and advise on appropriate procurement and contracting strategies.</li>\r\n<li>Prepare, review, and finalise procurement documents including Expressions of Interest (EoIs), Requests for Proposal (RFPs), Requests for Qualification (RFQs), bid documents, draft contracts, concession agreements, Memoranda of Understanding (MoUs), and related documentation.</li>\r\n<li>Design qualification criteria, evaluation frameworks, and bid evaluation methodologies in alignment with the General Financial Rules (GFR) 2017, Central Vigilance Commission (CVC) guidelines, and applicable State of Chhattisgarh procurement rules.</li>\r\n<li>Manage the complete bid process, including pre-bid meetings, issuance of clarifications and corrigendum, bid opening, evaluation support, and preparation of evaluation reports and recommendations for the competent authority.</li>\r\n<li>Provide transaction advisory and bid process management support for empanelment of, and tendering for, the following primary aviation services and infrastructure but not limited to:\r\n<ul>\r\n<li>Ground handling agencies for airports and airstrips in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Helicopter services, including charter, regional connectivity, and emergency / medical evacuation services.</li>\r\n<li>Agencies for capacity building and training of aviation sector personnel and for institutional strengthening of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li>Suppliers of safety, security, and firefighting equipment for aviation facilities.</li>\r\n<li>Agencies for the development, upgradation, and maintenance of airstrips and allied aviation infrastructure.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n<li>Prepare empanelment frameworks, eligibility criteria, and rate-contract or panel-based selection structures for recurring aviation service requirements of the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li>Support the Directorate in tender publication, bidder coordination, evaluation, award, and onboarding of empanelled service providers.</li>\r\n<li>Develop contract management and performance monitoring frameworks for empanelled agencies and selected service providers.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>2. Policy, Schemes, and Skill Development</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Support in the formulation of the State Aviation Policy, including policy research, benchmarking with national and global practices, stakeholder consultations, and drafting.</li>\r\n<li>Support the Directorate in the design and development of aviation sector schemes for promotion of air connectivity, aviation services, infrastructure, and investment in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate and assist the Directorate in the selection of specialised agencies for the development of training modules and curricula for skill development of local youth in aviation and allied trades, including pilot training, cabin crew training, aircraft maintenance engineering (AME), air traffic control (ATC), and ground handling.</li>\r\n<li>Facilitate partnerships and coordination with Flying Training Organisations (FTOs), national aviation academies, DGCA-approved institutions, and skill development agencies for establishment of training centres and skilling initiatives in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Suggestion on initiatives to promote aviation-related employment opportunities for local youth and to strengthen the aviation skilling ecosystem in the State.</li>\r\n<li>Conduct a comparative study of aviation services, schemes, and best practices implemented by other States, including regional connectivity, helicopter services, aviation infrastructure, aviation skilling, investment promotion, and allied aviation services. Identify replicable practices and prepare recommendations for adoption and contextual adaptation in Chhattisgarh, including implementation roadmaps and institutional arrangements required for roll-out.</li>\r\n</ol>\r\n<p><strong>3. Project Monitoring, Reporting, and Departmental Handholding</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li>Provide project management support for aviation infrastructure and service delivery projects, including activities under the Regional Connectivity Scheme (RCS), airport and airstrip development, and operationalisation of State aviation assets.</li>\r\n<li>PMU shall support for monitoring of all ongoing projects and track upcoming and future projects, including their onboarding, progress, timelines, and overall implementation status.</li>\r\n<li>Establish and maintain a structured project monitoring framework covering all aviation projects, procurements, and empanelment processes, including project timelines, milestones, deliverables, and physical and financial progress against approved targets.</li>\r\n<li>Track the implementation status of selected and empanelled service providers, contractors, and agencies, and prepare progress reviews highlighting delays, bottlenecks, deviations from approved scope, and corrective actions required.</li>\r\n<li>Prepare periodic monitoring and progress reports, including weekly status updates, monthly progress reports, and quarterly review reports, in formats approved by the Directorate.</li>\r\n<li>Verify bills and invoices submitted by selected agencies, contractors, and service providers against the terms and conditions of the tender, work order, and contract. Recommend approval or rejection of bills with supporting verification notes.</li>\r\n<li>Support the Directorate in compilation of data and preparation of replies, status notes, and information sought by the State Government, the Legislative Assembly, audit authorities, and other competent forums.</li>\r\n<li>Coordinate with regulatory authorities, national aviation institutions, and industry stakeholders, and support stakeholder communication, meeting coordination, and follow-up actions.</li>\r\n<li>Carry out any other task assigned by the Directorate of Aviation related to aviation sector development, transaction advisory, bid process management, and routine departmental work.</li>\r\n</ol><br>', '2026-06-14 15:20:04', 94, 1, '2026-06-14 15:27:41', 1),
