(258, 179, 'Special condition changed from <p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"39\" data-end=\"61\"><strong data-start=\"39\" data-end=\"61\">1. Team Deployment</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"63\" data-end=\"364\">The Successful Agency shall deploy a team of consultants on a full-time/Intermittent/part-time/remote-working basis at office of Client. Collectively, the team shall demonstrate adequate experience in the field of implementation of government programs to ensure quality service delivery to the client.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"366\" data-end=\"429\"><strong data-start=\"366\" data-end=\"429\">2. Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"431\" data-end=\"743\">Initial Contract Period for the project shall be 12 months which is extendable for next 12 Months on mutual consent. However, based on the performance of the consultant and approval form the competent authority, the contract duration may be extended further for 12 months or beyond based on the mutual agreement.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"775\"><strong data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"775\">3. Human Resource Policies</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1yogdgn\" data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"801\">3.1 Employment Terms</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"803\" data-end=\"1180\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hxzp9v\" data-start=\"803\" data-end=\"931\">All resources will be engaged on a full-time/part-time/remote basis (as per the need and approval of the competent authority).</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1p9ssd9\" data-start=\"932\" data-end=\"1180\"><strong data-start=\"934\" data-end=\"964\">Mobilization/ Replacement:</strong> RFP No. -165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025 Dated 20 Feb 2025. Issued by Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society for &ldquo;Empanelment of Consultancy Firms for a period of 3 years&rdquo; and amendments thereof.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"us5gs\" data-start=\"1182\" data-end=\"1206\">3.2 Team Composition</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1208\" data-end=\"1539\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1vnc9qf\" data-start=\"1208\" data-end=\"1278\">The PMU team will include resources as mentioned in the table above.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"r74kls\" data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1539\">The Department may seek for additional resources/ Subject Matter Experts during the project implementation as per its requirement. Consultant shall be given sufficient time (minimum 60 days) for deployment of the additional resources/ Subject Matter Experts.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1541\" data-end=\"1575\"><strong data-start=\"1541\" data-end=\"1575\">4. Leave and Other HR Policies</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"18f6cly\" data-start=\"1577\" data-end=\"1597\">4.1 Leave Policy</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1599\" data-end=\"2414\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cw84ku\" data-start=\"1599\" data-end=\"1736\">Each position shall be eligible for the entitlement of 2 leave in a month which can be carry forward for the next month if not availed.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9qb3s8\" data-start=\"1737\" data-end=\"1908\">Each position can avail maximum of 3 leaves in a month (if cumulated/carried forward) without deductions, subsequently amount would be deducted as per the approved rate.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12bcd5c\" data-start=\"1909\" data-end=\"1999\">Unused leave can be carried forward to the next year/ till the end of contract duration.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4a82xc\" data-start=\"2000\" data-end=\"2102\">The proposed team must follow the working hours, working days and Holidays of State of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11t5u05\" data-start=\"2103\" data-end=\"2310\">In case of Travel/ Boarding/ Lodging/ Communication and printing and stationery for any official travel for Authority related work or to cover the work as per scope of work would be borne by the Authority.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1lyokhv\" data-start=\"2311\" data-end=\"2414\">The PMU team will follow the work schedule and timing of client as per the norms of Government of CG.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1up6e70\" data-start=\"2416\" data-end=\"2437\">4.2 Working Hours</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2439\" data-end=\"2717\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"xmltiq\" data-start=\"2439\" data-end=\"2580\">Consultants are expected to work as per calendar and office hours of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh and complete the given task on time.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1vmhbb6\" data-start=\"2581\" data-end=\"2717\">Flexibility in working hours may be allowed based on the project requirements and approval from the CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"vhvewx\" data-start=\"2719\" data-end=\"2749\">4.3 Performance Evaluation</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2751\" data-end=\"3078\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4b9cgf\" data-start=\"2751\" data-end=\"2899\">Regular performance evaluations will be conducted to ensure consultants meet their targets and contribute effectively to the mission\'s objectives.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"wt2lra\" data-start=\"2900\" data-end=\"2993\">Evaluations will be based on predefined key performance indicators (KPIs) and deliverables.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ghrrd1\" data-start=\"2994\" data-end=\"3078\">Continuous performance below expectations may lead to termination of the contract.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3080\" data-end=\"3122\"><strong data-start=\"3080\" data-end=\"3122\">5. Data Management and Confidentiality</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"pvrkun\" data-start=\"3124\" data-end=\"3147\">5.1 Data Management</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3149\" data-end=\"3392\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"f767sz\" data-start=\"3149\" data-end=\"3250\">Consultants are responsible for maintaining accurate and up-to-date records related to their tasks.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12k64xy\" data-start=\"3251\" data-end=\"3392\">All data must be stored securely and managed in compliance with the data protection policies outlined by CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"q8v6u1\" data-start=\"3394\" data-end=\"3417\">5.2 Confidentiality</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3419\" data-end=\"3715\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"iyhvmg\" data-start=\"3419\" data-end=\"3544\">Consultant must maintain the confidentiality of all sensitive information related to the CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"nrzosc\" data-start=\"3545\" data-end=\"3715\">Disclosure of any confidential information to unauthorized persons is strictly prohibited and will result in disciplinary action, including termination of the contract.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1l8qwid\" data-start=\"3717\" data-end=\"3746\">5.3 Intellectual Property</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3748\" data-end=\"3989\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1fss1at\" data-start=\"3748\" data-end=\"3867\">Any intellectual property created during the course of employment will be owned by CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1awxvpf\" data-start=\"3868\" data-end=\"3989\">Consultants must agree to transfer all intellectual property rights to CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh upon creation.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3991\" data-end=\"4020\"><strong data-start=\"3991\" data-end=\"4020\">6. Operational Guidelines</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1q25ol4\" data-start=\"4022\" data-end=\"4057\">6.1 Reporting and Documentation</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4059\" data-end=\"4351\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17fet12\" data-start=\"4059\" data-end=\"4198\">Consultants are required to submit regular progress reports, including monthly, quarterly, and annual reports, as specified in their ToR.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"s63p6x\" data-start=\"4199\" data-end=\"4351\">All reports must be submitted to the CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh and relevant Dept. of E&amp;IT, Government of Chhattisgarh for review and approval.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"t6yanu\" data-start=\"4353\" data-end=\"4382\">6.2 Compliance and Ethics</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4384\" data-end=\"4651\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1fzmj1t\" data-start=\"4384\" data-end=\"4512\">Consultants must adhere to the ethical guidelines and professional standards established by CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l3rhbk\" data-start=\"4513\" data-end=\"4651\">Any form of misconduct, including fraud, corruption, or harassment, will be dealt with severely and may result in immediate termination.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"u45o84\" data-start=\"4653\" data-end=\"4691\">6.3 Capacity Building and Training</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4693\" data-end=\"4950\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"93bcgt\" data-start=\"4693\" data-end=\"4833\">Consultants are expected to participate in ongoing capacity-building programs and training sessions to enhance their skills and knowledge.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1mfh3x3\" data-start=\"4834\" data-end=\"4950\">CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh will provide necessary resources and opportunities for professional development.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1dgylj8\" data-start=\"4952\" data-end=\"4990\">6.4 Coordination with Stakeholders</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4992\" data-end=\"5264\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1nthaq1\" data-start=\"4992\" data-end=\"5147\">Consultants must coordinate effectively with stakeholders to ensure seamless implementation of schemes and programs of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1bbdsi8\" data-start=\"5148\" data-end=\"5264\">Regular meetings and consultations with stakeholders are mandatory to discuss progress, challenges, and solutions.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5266\" data-end=\"5306\"><strong data-start=\"5266\" data-end=\"5306\">7. Travel and Reimbursement Policies</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"x98ipi\" data-start=\"5308\" data-end=\"5322\">7.1 Travel</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5324\" data-end=\"5595\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"j2jy7a\" data-start=\"5324\" data-end=\"5450\">Consultants shall be required to travel within the state and to other locations as necessary for project-related activities.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1nn26ht\" data-start=\"5451\" data-end=\"5595\">Travel arrangements and itineraries must be approved in advance by the Project Manager or representative of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"pmaha7\" data-start=\"5597\" data-end=\"5618\">7.2 Reimbursement</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5620\" data-end=\"6418\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15u8tlu\" data-start=\"5620\" data-end=\"5814\">The inter-city/state conveyance charges for any official travel for Authority related work or to cover the work as per scope of RFP would be borne by the Authority subjected to prior approval.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1q8mt64\" data-start=\"5815\" data-end=\"6137\">The entitlement for reimbursement of visits would be as per the provisions of the RFP Issued by CHiPS, for RFP No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025 Dated 20 Feb 2025 issued by Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society for &ldquo;Empanelment of Consultancy Firms for a period of 3 years&rdquo; and amendments thereof.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"3ofl17\" data-start=\"6138\" data-end=\"6307\">Consultants will be reimbursed for any other travel and other expenses incurred during the course of their duties as per policies of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"5f4wz9\" data-start=\"6308\" data-end=\"6418\">All reimbursement claims must be supported by valid receipts and submitted within the stipulated time frame.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"6420\" data-end=\"6454\"><strong data-start=\"6420\" data-end=\"6454\">8. Additional Responsibilities</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"6456\" data-end=\"6679\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"bmf1ve\" data-start=\"6456\" data-end=\"6573\">Consultants may be assigned additional responsibilities related to day-to-day operations as required by the client.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"x62hbz\" data-start=\"6574\" data-end=\"6679\">Flexibility and adaptability in handling diverse tasks and projects are essential for all team members.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"6681\" data-end=\"6871\">By adhering to these terms and conditions, the PMU will ensure a high standard of professionalism, efficiency, and accountability in achieving the goals of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6873\" data-end=\"7380\">The client is expected to provide the consultants with available data, information, maps or drawings relevant to the task at no cost to the consultant as per availability. The DPRs/Reports/Documents will be shared with the consultant for their review. In case any additional information is needed, the client will arrange for access to all relevant information and to key officials in the local government and agencies concerned with subjects related to the project. No survey is required by the consultant.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7382\" data-end=\"7473\">The client will also help consultants in obtaining permission/data from other stakeholders.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7475\" data-end=\"7938\">The consultants shall verify the correctness of the data/information provided by the client and satisfy them about the accuracy of data/information/material before these are used. Data/information/material provided to the consultants shall remain the property of the originating agency and shall be provided solely for the purpose of the work to be done under this contract. All such borrowed material shall be returned to the client upon completion of the study.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7940\" data-end=\"8201\">Client shall provide sitting space, office furniture and wifi access to the consultants, however, arranging the IT assets like the Laptop/computer and auxiliary hardware and software required for performing the services shall be arranged by the consulting firm.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8203\" data-end=\"8227\"><strong data-start=\"8203\" data-end=\"8227\">9. Change Management</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"8229\" data-end=\"8853\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1n9sz1q\" data-start=\"8229\" data-end=\"8376\">The selected consulting firm shall preferably give 2 weeks of advance notice to client for any change in deployed resource during the assignment.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1aqze4q\" data-start=\"8377\" data-end=\"8519\">The selected consulting firm needs to ensure that the knowledge transfer and handover during change of any resource for a smooth transition.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ulup6\" data-start=\"8520\" data-end=\"8587\">The replacement of any resource should be approved by the client.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"qapg81\" data-start=\"8588\" data-end=\"8853\" data-is-last-node=\"\">The change of resource should be in accordance to RFP No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025 Dated 20 Feb 2025 issued by Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society for &ldquo;Empanelment of Consultancy Firms for a period of 3 years&rdquo; and amendments thereof.</li>\r\n</ul> to <p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"39\" data-end=\"61\"><strong data-start=\"39\" data-end=\"61\">1. Team Deployment</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"63\" data-end=\"364\">The Successful Agency shall deploy a team of consultants on a full-time/Intermittent/part-time/remote-working basis at office of Client. Collectively, the team shall demonstrate adequate experience in the field of implementation of government programs to ensure quality service delivery to the client.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"366\" data-end=\"429\"><strong data-start=\"366\" data-end=\"429\">2. Duration and Resource Deployment Plan for the Assignment</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"431\" data-end=\"743\">Initial Contract Period for the project shall be 12 months which is extendable for next 12 Months on mutual consent. However, based on the performance of the consultant and approval form the competent authority, the contract duration may be extended further for 12 months or beyond based on the mutual agreement.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"775\"><strong data-start=\"745\" data-end=\"775\">3. Human Resource Policies</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1yogdgn\" data-start=\"777\" data-end=\"801\">3.1 Employment Terms</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"803\" data-end=\"1180\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hxzp9v\" data-start=\"803\" data-end=\"931\">All resources will be engaged on a full-time/part-time/remote basis (as per the need and approval of the competent authority).</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1p9ssd9\" data-start=\"932\" data-end=\"1180\"><strong data-start=\"934\" data-end=\"964\">Mobilization/ Replacement:</strong> RFP No. -165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025 Dated 20 Feb 2025. Issued by Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society for &ldquo;Empanelment of Consultancy Firms for a period of 3 years&rdquo; and amendments thereof.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"us5gs\" data-start=\"1182\" data-end=\"1206\">3.2 Team Composition</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1208\" data-end=\"1539\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1vnc9qf\" data-start=\"1208\" data-end=\"1278\">The PMU team will include resources as mentioned in the table above.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"r74kls\" data-start=\"1279\" data-end=\"1539\">The Department may seek for additional resources/ Subject Matter Experts during the project implementation as per its requirement. Consultant shall be given sufficient time (minimum 60 days) for deployment of the additional resources/ Subject Matter Experts.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1541\" data-end=\"1575\"><strong data-start=\"1541\" data-end=\"1575\">4. Leave and Other HR Policies</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"18f6cly\" data-start=\"1577\" data-end=\"1597\">4.1 Leave Policy</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1599\" data-end=\"2414\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cw84ku\" data-start=\"1599\" data-end=\"1736\">Each position shall be eligible for the entitlement of 2 leave in a month which can be carry forward for the next month if not availed.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9qb3s8\" data-start=\"1737\" data-end=\"1908\">Each position can avail maximum of 3 leaves in a month (if cumulated/carried forward) without deductions, subsequently amount would be deducted as per the approved rate.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12bcd5c\" data-start=\"1909\" data-end=\"1999\">Unused leave can be carried forward to the next year/ till the end of contract duration.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4a82xc\" data-start=\"2000\" data-end=\"2102\">The proposed team must follow the working hours, working days and Holidays of State of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11t5u05\" data-start=\"2103\" data-end=\"2310\">In case of Travel/ Boarding/ Lodging/ Communication and printing and stationery for any official travel for Authority related work or to cover the work as per scope of work would be borne by the Authority.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1lyokhv\" data-start=\"2311\" data-end=\"2414\">The PMU team will follow the work schedule and timing of client as per the norms of Government of CG.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1up6e70\" data-start=\"2416\" data-end=\"2437\">4.2 Working Hours</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2439\" data-end=\"2717\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"xmltiq\" data-start=\"2439\" data-end=\"2580\">Consultants are expected to work as per calendar and office hours of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh and complete the given task on time.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1vmhbb6\" data-start=\"2581\" data-end=\"2717\">Flexibility in working hours may be allowed based on the project requirements and approval from the CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"vhvewx\" data-start=\"2719\" data-end=\"2749\">4.3 Performance Evaluation</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2751\" data-end=\"3078\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4b9cgf\" data-start=\"2751\" data-end=\"2899\">Regular performance evaluations will be conducted to ensure consultants meet their targets and contribute effectively to the mission\'s objectives.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"wt2lra\" data-start=\"2900\" data-end=\"2993\">Evaluations will be based on predefined key performance indicators (KPIs) and deliverables.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1ghrrd1\" data-start=\"2994\" data-end=\"3078\">Continuous performance below expectations may lead to termination of the contract.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3080\" data-end=\"3122\"><strong data-start=\"3080\" data-end=\"3122\">5. Data Management and Confidentiality</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"pvrkun\" data-start=\"3124\" data-end=\"3147\">5.1 Data Management</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3149\" data-end=\"3392\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"f767sz\" data-start=\"3149\" data-end=\"3250\">Consultants are responsible for maintaining accurate and up-to-date records related to their tasks.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12k64xy\" data-start=\"3251\" data-end=\"3392\">All data must be stored securely and managed in compliance with the data protection policies outlined by CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"q8v6u1\" data-start=\"3394\" data-end=\"3417\">5.2 Confidentiality</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3419\" data-end=\"3715\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"iyhvmg\" data-start=\"3419\" data-end=\"3544\">Consultant must maintain the confidentiality of all sensitive information related to the CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"nrzosc\" data-start=\"3545\" data-end=\"3715\">Disclosure of any confidential information to unauthorized persons is strictly prohibited and will result in disciplinary action, including termination of the contract.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1l8qwid\" data-start=\"3717\" data-end=\"3746\">5.3 Intellectual Property</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3748\" data-end=\"3989\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1fss1at\" data-start=\"3748\" data-end=\"3867\">Any intellectual property created during the course of employment will be owned by CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1awxvpf\" data-start=\"3868\" data-end=\"3989\">Consultants must agree to transfer all intellectual property rights to CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh upon creation.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3991\" data-end=\"4020\"><strong data-start=\"3991\" data-end=\"4020\">6. Operational Guidelines</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1q25ol4\" data-start=\"4022\" data-end=\"4057\">6.1 Reporting and Documentation</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4059\" data-end=\"4351\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17fet12\" data-start=\"4059\" data-end=\"4198\">Consultants are required to submit regular progress reports, including monthly, quarterly, and annual reports, as specified in their ToR.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"s63p6x\" data-start=\"4199\" data-end=\"4351\">All reports must be submitted to the CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh and relevant Dept. of E&amp;IT, Government of Chhattisgarh for review and approval.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"t6yanu\" data-start=\"4353\" data-end=\"4382\">6.2 Compliance and Ethics</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4384\" data-end=\"4651\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1fzmj1t\" data-start=\"4384\" data-end=\"4512\">Consultants must adhere to the ethical guidelines and professional standards established by CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l3rhbk\" data-start=\"4513\" data-end=\"4651\">Any form of misconduct, including fraud, corruption, or harassment, will be dealt with severely and may result in immediate termination.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"u45o84\" data-start=\"4653\" data-end=\"4691\">6.3 Capacity Building and Training</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4693\" data-end=\"4950\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"93bcgt\" data-start=\"4693\" data-end=\"4833\">Consultants are expected to participate in ongoing capacity-building programs and training sessions to enhance their skills and knowledge.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1mfh3x3\" data-start=\"4834\" data-end=\"4950\">CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh will provide necessary resources and opportunities for professional development.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"1dgylj8\" data-start=\"4952\" data-end=\"4990\">6.4 Coordination with Stakeholders</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4992\" data-end=\"5264\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1nthaq1\" data-start=\"4992\" data-end=\"5147\">Consultants must coordinate effectively with stakeholders to ensure seamless implementation of schemes and programs of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1bbdsi8\" data-start=\"5148\" data-end=\"5264\">Regular meetings and consultations with stakeholders are mandatory to discuss progress, challenges, and solutions.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5266\" data-end=\"5306\"><strong data-start=\"5266\" data-end=\"5306\">7. Travel and Reimbursement Policies</strong></p>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"x98ipi\" data-start=\"5308\" data-end=\"5322\">7.1 Travel</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5324\" data-end=\"5595\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"j2jy7a\" data-start=\"5324\" data-end=\"5450\">Consultants shall be required to travel within the state and to other locations as necessary for project-related activities.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1nn26ht\" data-start=\"5451\" data-end=\"5595\">Travel arrangements and itineraries must be approved in advance by the Project Manager or representative of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<h3 data-section-id=\"pmaha7\" data-start=\"5597\" data-end=\"5618\">7.2 Reimbursement</h3>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5620\" data-end=\"6418\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15u8tlu\" data-start=\"5620\" data-end=\"5814\">The inter-city/state conveyance charges for any official travel for Authority related work or to cover the work as per scope of RFP would be borne by the Authority subjected to prior approval.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1q8mt64\" data-start=\"5815\" data-end=\"6137\">The entitlement for reimbursement of visits would be as per the provisions of the RFP Issued by CHiPS, for RFP No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025 Dated 20 Feb 2025 issued by Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society for &ldquo;Empanelment of Consultancy Firms for a period of 3 years&rdquo; and amendments thereof.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"3ofl17\" data-start=\"6138\" data-end=\"6307\">Consultants will be reimbursed for any other travel and other expenses incurred during the course of their duties as per policies of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"5f4wz9\" data-start=\"6308\" data-end=\"6418\">All reimbursement claims must be supported by valid receipts and submitted within the stipulated time frame.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"6420\" data-end=\"6454\"><strong data-start=\"6420\" data-end=\"6454\">8. Additional Responsibilities</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"6456\" data-end=\"6679\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"bmf1ve\" data-start=\"6456\" data-end=\"6573\">Consultants may be assigned additional responsibilities related to day-to-day operations as required by the client.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"x62hbz\" data-start=\"6574\" data-end=\"6679\">Flexibility and adaptability in handling diverse tasks and projects are essential for all team members.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"6681\" data-end=\"6871\">By adhering to these terms and conditions, the PMU will ensure a high standard of professionalism, efficiency, and accountability in achieving the goals of CHiPS, Government of Chhattisgarh.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"6873\" data-end=\"7380\">The client is expected to provide the consultants with available data, information, maps or drawings relevant to the task at no cost to the consultant as per availability. The DPRs/Reports/Documents will be shared with the consultant for their review. In case any additional information is needed, the client will arrange for access to all relevant information and to key officials in the local government and agencies concerned with subjects related to the project. No survey is required by the consultant.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7382\" data-end=\"7473\">The client will also help consultants in obtaining permission/data from other stakeholders.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7475\" data-end=\"7938\">The consultants shall verify the correctness of the data/information provided by the client and satisfy them about the accuracy of data/information/material before these are used. Data/information/material provided to the consultants shall remain the property of the originating agency and shall be provided solely for the purpose of the work to be done under this contract. All such borrowed material shall be returned to the client upon completion of the study.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"7940\" data-end=\"8201\">Client shall provide sitting space, office furniture and wifi access to the consultants, however, arranging the IT assets like the Laptop/computer and auxiliary hardware and software required for performing the services shall be arranged by the consulting firm.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"8203\" data-end=\"8227\"><strong data-start=\"8203\" data-end=\"8227\">9. Change Management</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"8229\" data-end=\"8853\" data-is-last-node=\"\" data-is-only-node=\"\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1n9sz1q\" data-start=\"8229\" data-end=\"8376\">The selected consulting firm shall preferably give 2 weeks of advance notice to client for any change in deployed resource during the assignment.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1aqze4q\" data-start=\"8377\" data-end=\"8519\">The selected consulting firm needs to ensure that the knowledge transfer and handover during change of any resource for a smooth transition.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ulup6\" data-start=\"8520\" data-end=\"8587\">The replacement of any resource should be approved by the client.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"qapg81\" data-start=\"8588\" data-end=\"8853\" data-is-last-node=\"\">The change of resource should be in accordance to RFP No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025 Dated 20 Feb 2025 issued by Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society for &ldquo;Empanelment of Consultancy Firms for a period of 3 years&rdquo; and amendments thereof.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\"><strong>Note:</strong></p>\r\n<ol>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">The CVs of all Key Experts needs to be submitted.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">CV of candidates submitted against respective positions must fulfil all the qualification requirements.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">Apart from the above-mentioned personnel, Client may ask, at any time during execution of the Contract, for any additional personnel that it deems necessary for carrying the scope of work under this Contract. Upon such request by the Client, the Consultant shall submit to the Client for review and approval a copy of the Curriculum Vitae (CVs) of the proposed Expert. The remuneration payable towards the services of additional personnel shall be payable on the basis of the man month rate approved as per RFP No. 165081/CEO/CHiPS/Empanelment/Consultancy Firm/2025 Dated 20 Feb 2025 issued by Chhattisgarh Infotech Promotion Society for &ldquo;Empanelment of Consultancy Firms for a period of 3 years&rdquo; and amendments thereof. The payment shall be on actual number of man days spent under this Consultancy Agreement.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n<li dir=\"ltr\" aria-level=\"1\">\r\n<p dir=\"ltr\" role=\"presentation\">The Consultant proposed team shall be deployed within 90 days of the issuance of the Letter of Award/ Work Order.</p>\r\n</li>\r\n</ol><br>', '2026-07-27 16:47:07', 90, 1, '2026-07-27 16:49:54', 1);
INSERT INTO `log_eoi_updates` (`recordid`, `requestid`, `particular`, `updatedon`, `updatedby`, `isviewed`, `viewedon`, `viewedby`) VALUES
(259, 179, 'Scope of work changed from <p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"78\" data-end=\"127\">The PMU shall undertake the following activities:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"129\" data-end=\"427\">The selected PMU shall provide end-to-end consultancy, technical advisory, project management, procurement support, implementation monitoring, and governance support for establishment and operationalization of the Managed Security Operations Centre (Managed SOC) for the Government of Chhattisgarh.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"429\" data-end=\"508\">The detailed scope of work shall include, but not be limited to, the following:</p>\r\n<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"209\" data-end=\"233\"><strong data-start=\"209\" data-end=\"233\">3.1 Project Planning</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"235\" data-end=\"473\">Understand the existing cybersecurity ecosystem of the State, including State Data Centre (SDC), Disaster Recovery (DR), Cloud infrastructure, departmental data centres, network infrastructure, security devices, and critical applications.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"475\" data-end=\"567\">Conduct stakeholder consultations with CHIPS, user departments, and other relevant agencies.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"569\" data-end=\"723\">Prepare a Report detailing the project approach, implementation methodology, timelines, governance structure, deliverables, and risk management framework.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"725\" data-end=\"823\">Prepare a comprehensive implementation roadmap for establishment and operation of the Managed SOC.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"825\" data-end=\"855\"><strong data-start=\"825\" data-end=\"855\">3.2 Bid Process Management</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"857\" data-end=\"938\">The PMU shall provide complete support during the procurement process, including:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"940\" data-end=\"970\"><strong data-start=\"940\" data-end=\"970\">3.2.1 Procurement Strategy</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"972\" data-end=\"1033\">Develop the procurement strategy and implementation approach.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1035\" data-end=\"1125\">Recommend appropriate contracting methodology (e.g., EPC, Managed Services, Output-based).</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1127\" data-end=\"1171\">Define project scope and service boundaries.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1173\" data-end=\"1214\"><strong data-start=\"1173\" data-end=\"1214\">3.2.2 Preparation of Tender Documents</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1216\" data-end=\"1316\">Prepare RFP, technical specifications, BoQ, SLAs, KPIs, payment milestones, and contract conditions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1318\" data-end=\"1325\">Define:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1327\" data-end=\"1591\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1rjbw5h\" data-start=\"1327\" data-end=\"1359\">Technical Eligibility Criteria</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"sxcum7\" data-start=\"1360\" data-end=\"1392\">Financial Eligibility Criteria</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"vr0183\" data-start=\"1393\" data-end=\"1417\">Evaluation Methodology</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jqp40o\" data-start=\"1418\" data-end=\"1470\">Bid Security and Performance Security requirements</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1rpyg8q\" data-start=\"1471\" data-end=\"1504\">Service Level Agreements (SLAs)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1qflqnl\" data-start=\"1505\" data-end=\"1539\">Penalty and incentive mechanisms</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1dcc10o\" data-start=\"1540\" data-end=\"1562\">Exit Management Plan</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1n4umf\" data-start=\"1563\" data-end=\"1591\">Transition Management Plan</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1593\" data-end=\"1617\"><strong data-start=\"1593\" data-end=\"1617\">3.2.3 Bid Management</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1619\" data-end=\"1661\">Publish and manage bid-related activities.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1663\" data-end=\"1699\">Prepare responses to bidder queries.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1701\" data-end=\"1727\">Organize pre-bid meetings.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1729\" data-end=\"1758\">Issue corrigenda and addenda.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1760\" data-end=\"1792\">Assist CHIPS during bid opening.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1794\" data-end=\"1818\"><strong data-start=\"1794\" data-end=\"1818\">3.2.4 Bid Evaluation</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1820\" data-end=\"1849\">Develop evaluation templates.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1851\" data-end=\"1880\">Support technical evaluation.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1882\" data-end=\"1930\">Review compliance with technical specifications.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1932\" data-end=\"2016\">Support Proof of Concept (PoC), presentations, and demonstrations, where applicable.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2018\" data-end=\"2087\">Assist in financial evaluation and preparation of evaluation reports.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2089\" data-end=\"2145\">Support contract negotiations and award recommendations.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2147\" data-end=\"2182\"><strong data-start=\"2147\" data-end=\"2182\">3.3 Technical Advisory Services</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2184\" data-end=\"2235\">The PMU shall provide expert technical guidance on:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2237\" data-end=\"2271\"><strong data-start=\"2237\" data-end=\"2271\">3.3.1 Managed SOC Architecture</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2273\" data-end=\"2499\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"7m8pcr\" data-start=\"2273\" data-end=\"2302\">SOC architecture and design</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"tz5tq0\" data-start=\"2303\" data-end=\"2342\">SIEM sizing (Events Per Second - EPS)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11y1582\" data-start=\"2343\" data-end=\"2362\">SOAR architecture</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"d716aq\" data-start=\"2363\" data-end=\"2405\">Threat Intelligence Platform integration</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jbzjd1\" data-start=\"2406\" data-end=\"2430\">Security orchestration</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"13ipio3\" data-start=\"2431\" data-end=\"2455\">Log retention strategy</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1tve4w9\" data-start=\"2456\" data-end=\"2499\">Disaster Recovery and Business Continuity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2501\" data-end=\"2532\"><strong data-start=\"2501\" data-end=\"2532\">3.3.2 Technology Validation</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2534\" data-end=\"2595\">Review and validate the proposed technology stack, including:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2597\" data-end=\"2927\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1j4cn22\" data-start=\"2597\" data-end=\"2603\">SIEM</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1j4crvr\" data-start=\"2604\" data-end=\"2610\">SOAR</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"sc8zcq\" data-start=\"2611\" data-end=\"2620\">XDR/EDR</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1o4cq8\" data-start=\"2621\" data-end=\"2626\">NDR</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"gfz6v0\" data-start=\"2627\" data-end=\"2657\">Threat Intelligence Platform</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1arwir3\" data-start=\"2658\" data-end=\"2684\">Vulnerability Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"pjyecd\" data-start=\"2685\" data-end=\"2717\">Web Application Firewall (WAF)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zgo1c5\" data-start=\"2718\" data-end=\"2754\">Database Activity Monitoring (DAM)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"a1vmxl\" data-start=\"2755\" data-end=\"2791\">Privileged Access Management (PAM)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1in70ob\" data-start=\"2792\" data-end=\"2828\">Identity &amp; Access Management (IAM)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"2e8fii\" data-start=\"2829\" data-end=\"2871\">Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hix7lp\" data-start=\"2872\" data-end=\"2891\">Endpoint Security</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"741tma\" data-start=\"2892\" data-end=\"2908\">Email Security</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4lsko0\" data-start=\"2909\" data-end=\"2927\">Network Security</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2929\" data-end=\"2957\"><strong data-start=\"2929\" data-end=\"2957\">3.3.3 Security Use Cases</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2959\" data-end=\"3014\">Review and recommend security monitoring use cases for:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3016\" data-end=\"3251\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1sfcvwk\" data-start=\"3016\" data-end=\"3035\">State Data Centre</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"dkwybz\" data-start=\"3036\" data-end=\"3060\">Disaster Recovery Site</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1i9cx24\" data-start=\"3061\" data-end=\"3088\">Cloud-hosted applications</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"89w5qg\" data-start=\"3089\" data-end=\"3116\">Departmental applications</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15bmvfs\" data-start=\"3117\" data-end=\"3130\">API Gateway</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1w57mf2\" data-start=\"3131\" data-end=\"3142\">Databases</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17nhjod\" data-start=\"3143\" data-end=\"3160\">Network devices</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cirl79\" data-start=\"3161\" data-end=\"3172\">Firewalls</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1o4wkg\" data-start=\"3173\" data-end=\"3178\">VPN</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12m8zvz\" data-start=\"3179\" data-end=\"3195\">Email gateways</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"del5vx\" data-start=\"3196\" data-end=\"3214\">Active Directory</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1bwdg9k\" data-start=\"3215\" data-end=\"3226\">Endpoints</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"601tsw\" data-start=\"3227\" data-end=\"3251\">Citizen-facing portals</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3253\" data-end=\"3283\"><strong data-start=\"3253\" data-end=\"3283\">3.4 Implementation Support</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3285\" data-end=\"3359\">The PMU shall monitor and facilitate implementation activities, including:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3361\" data-end=\"3806\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"srosz2\" data-start=\"3361\" data-end=\"3391\">Review implementation plans.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"s8zxz0\" data-start=\"3392\" data-end=\"3434\">Validate detailed solution architecture.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15s5d9l\" data-start=\"3435\" data-end=\"3463\">Monitor project schedules.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"3wtnqr\" data-start=\"3464\" data-end=\"3499\">Review implementation milestones.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zwcdnw\" data-start=\"3500\" data-end=\"3545\">Facilitate coordination among stakeholders.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1rjfms2\" data-start=\"3546\" data-end=\"3582\">Monitor onboarding of log sources.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6vim3g\" data-start=\"3583\" data-end=\"3658\">Validate integration of all identified security devices and applications.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12y8zsi\" data-start=\"3659\" data-end=\"3708\">Review configuration of SIEM correlation rules.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"e0inbu\" data-start=\"3709\" data-end=\"3745\">Monitor testing and commissioning.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l0p7z3\" data-start=\"3746\" data-end=\"3776\">Validate acceptance testing.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6rf9nq\" data-start=\"3777\" data-end=\"3806\">Recommend Go-Live approval.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3808\" data-end=\"3834\"><strong data-start=\"3808\" data-end=\"3834\">3.5 Project Governance</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3836\" data-end=\"3892\">The PMU shall establish a governance framework covering:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3894\" data-end=\"4096\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1w6erb6\" data-start=\"3894\" data-end=\"3930\">Project Steering Committee support</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"rdfhmn\" data-start=\"3931\" data-end=\"3967\">Weekly and Monthly Review Meetings</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1vk5fqw\" data-start=\"3968\" data-end=\"3985\">Risk Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zp9k9u\" data-start=\"3986\" data-end=\"4004\">Issue Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"nvbezw\" data-start=\"4005\" data-end=\"4032\">Change Request Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6dus1j\" data-start=\"4033\" data-end=\"4052\">Decision Tracking</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9kh0zi\" data-start=\"4053\" data-end=\"4076\">Escalation Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"10rdtii\" data-start=\"4077\" data-end=\"4096\">Quality Assurance</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4098\" data-end=\"4120\">The PMU shall prepare:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4122\" data-end=\"4286\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"jpej29\" data-start=\"4122\" data-end=\"4147\">Weekly Progress Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17ieril\" data-start=\"4148\" data-end=\"4174\">Monthly Progress Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cciiez\" data-start=\"4175\" data-end=\"4201\">Steering Committee Notes</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"10fmsrj\" data-start=\"4202\" data-end=\"4224\">Executive Dashboards</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15pbqsi\" data-start=\"4225\" data-end=\"4240\">Risk Register</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ymim48\" data-start=\"4241\" data-end=\"4257\">Issue Register</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17ufy8o\" data-start=\"4258\" data-end=\"4286\">Action Taken Reports (ATR)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4288\" data-end=\"4333\"><strong data-start=\"4288\" data-end=\"4333\">3.6 SLA and Vendor Performance Monitoring</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4335\" data-end=\"4357\">The PMU shall monitor:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4359\" data-end=\"4619\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"blrg23\" data-start=\"4359\" data-end=\"4375\">SLA compliance</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1h5eyi0\" data-start=\"4376\" data-end=\"4400\">Incident Response Time</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"yu8qyb\" data-start=\"4401\" data-end=\"4418\">Resolution Time</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"rzv5g9\" data-start=\"4419\" data-end=\"4433\">Availability</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"80023\" data-start=\"4434\" data-end=\"4453\">Device onboarding</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1romid8\" data-start=\"4454\" data-end=\"4475\">False Positive Rate</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"njnmry\" data-start=\"4476\" data-end=\"4504\">Mean Time to Detect (MTTD)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"vf1ydq\" data-start=\"4505\" data-end=\"4534\">Mean Time to Respond (MTTR)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"fu5pdm\" data-start=\"4535\" data-end=\"4562\">Threat Hunting activities</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"jjxazf\" data-start=\"4563\" data-end=\"4600\">Vulnerability remediation timelines</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1mhu0pn\" data-start=\"4601\" data-end=\"4619\">Patch compliance</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4621\" data-end=\"4699\">The PMU shall recommend penalties and service credits in case of SLA breaches.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4701\" data-end=\"4746\"><strong data-start=\"4701\" data-end=\"4746\">3.7 Security Compliance and Audit Support</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4748\" data-end=\"4785\">The PMU shall ensure compliance with:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4787\" data-end=\"5080\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6ax1o4\" data-start=\"4787\" data-end=\"4807\">CERT-In Directions</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1xx7diy\" data-start=\"4808\" data-end=\"4841\">MeitY Cyber Security Guidelines</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"pxzgpb\" data-start=\"4842\" data-end=\"4874\">National Cyber Security Policy</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"oy9tqh\" data-start=\"4875\" data-end=\"4890\">ISO/IEC 27001</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"gmjszz\" data-start=\"4891\" data-end=\"4921\">ISO 27701 (where applicable)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9cjism\" data-start=\"4922\" data-end=\"4951\">State Cyber Security Policy</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"hku4dc\" data-start=\"4952\" data-end=\"5022\">Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act, 2023 (where applicable)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1djvd21\" data-start=\"5023\" data-end=\"5080\">Cloud Security Guidelines issued by Government of India</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5082\" data-end=\"5104\">The PMU shall support:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5106\" data-end=\"5205\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1rp35ev\" data-start=\"5106\" data-end=\"5132\">Internal Security Audits</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"xmiac6\" data-start=\"5133\" data-end=\"5153\">Third-party Audits</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"113f02m\" data-start=\"5154\" data-end=\"5182\">CERT-In Audit observations</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"qq66xn\" data-start=\"5183\" data-end=\"5205\">Compliance reporting</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5207\" data-end=\"5248\"><strong data-start=\"5207\" data-end=\"5248\">3.8 Cloud Security Monitoring Support</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5250\" data-end=\"5310\">The PMU shall ensure that the Managed SOC adequately covers:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5312\" data-end=\"5615\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"w9a0ji\" data-start=\"5312\" data-end=\"5356\">State Government cloud-hosted applications</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"tt2l8z\" data-start=\"5357\" data-end=\"5387\">Private cloud infrastructure</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4f9bdp\" data-start=\"5388\" data-end=\"5399\">NIC Cloud</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"10krw2b\" data-start=\"5400\" data-end=\"5427\">Hybrid cloud environments</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"7325jw\" data-start=\"5428\" data-end=\"5452\">APIs and microservices</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1cdz1zt\" data-start=\"5453\" data-end=\"5490\">Containers and Kubernetes platforms</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"tz4wbj\" data-start=\"5491\" data-end=\"5509\">Virtual Machines</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"sa8m2j\" data-start=\"5510\" data-end=\"5533\">Cloud-native services</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ftj8r4\" data-start=\"5534\" data-end=\"5553\">Identity services</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"s98lj7\" data-start=\"5554\" data-end=\"5572\">Cloud audit logs</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"2e8fii\" data-start=\"5573\" data-end=\"5615\">Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5617\" data-end=\"5665\"><strong data-start=\"5617\" data-end=\"5665\">3.9 Capacity Building and Knowledge Transfer</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5667\" data-end=\"5681\">The PMU shall:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5683\" data-end=\"5954\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"eu9dm4\" data-start=\"5683\" data-end=\"5732\">Conduct awareness sessions for CHIPS officials.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1brff9y\" data-start=\"5733\" data-end=\"5787\">Train departmental nodal officers on SOC governance.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1kgy1tt\" data-start=\"5788\" data-end=\"5835\">Develop Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs).</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"151n93g\" data-start=\"5836\" data-end=\"5874\">Prepare incident response playbooks.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"78fw0m\" data-start=\"5875\" data-end=\"5905\">Prepare operational manuals.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"gce0e8\" data-start=\"5906\" data-end=\"5954\">Support transition to BAU (Business as Usual).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5956\" data-end=\"5992\"><strong data-start=\"5956\" data-end=\"5992\">3.10 Reporting and Documentation</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5994\" data-end=\"6029\">The PMU shall prepare and maintain:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\r\n<ul data-start=\"6031\" data-end=\"6343\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"bkdyff\" data-start=\"6031\" data-end=\"6049\">Inception Report</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"iol0ot\" data-start=\"6050\" data-end=\"6075\">Project Management Plan</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cxhoej\" data-start=\"6076\" data-end=\"6098\">Risk Management Plan</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1030aju\" data-start=\"6099\" data-end=\"6122\">Procurement Documents</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"a9f42r\" data-start=\"6123\" data-end=\"6143\">Evaluation Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17ieril\" data-start=\"6144\" data-end=\"6170\">Monthly Progress Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"10fmsrj\" data-start=\"6171\" data-end=\"6193\">Executive Dashboards</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1pxmqmz\" data-start=\"6194\" data-end=\"6214\">Governance Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1i9grvr\" data-start=\"6215\" data-end=\"6239\">SLA Monitoring Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hvvf0q\" data-start=\"6240\" data-end=\"6264\">Incident Trend Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"14hmr21\" data-start=\"6265\" data-end=\"6291\">Security Posture Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"g3k6g5\" data-start=\"6292\" data-end=\"6318\">Go-Live Readiness Report</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"begc5e\" data-start=\"6319\" data-end=\"6343\">Project Closure Report</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul> to <p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"78\" data-end=\"127\">The PMU shall undertake the following activities:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"129\" data-end=\"427\">The selected PMU shall provide end-to-end consultancy, technical advisory, project management, procurement support, implementation monitoring, and governance support for establishment and operationalization of the Managed Security Operations Centre (Managed SOC) for the Government of Chhattisgarh.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"429\" data-end=\"508\">The detailed scope of work shall include, but not be limited to, the following:</p>\r\n<p class=\"PDq2pG_selectionAnchorContainer\" data-start=\"209\" data-end=\"233\"><strong data-start=\"209\" data-end=\"233\">3.1 Project Planning</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"235\" data-end=\"473\">Understand the existing cybersecurity ecosystem of the State, including State Data Centre (SDC), Disaster Recovery (DR), Cloud infrastructure, departmental data centres, network infrastructure, security devices, and critical applications.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"475\" data-end=\"567\">Conduct stakeholder consultations with CHIPS, user departments, and other relevant agencies.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"569\" data-end=\"723\">Prepare a Report detailing the project approach, implementation methodology, timelines, governance structure, deliverables, and risk management framework.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"725\" data-end=\"823\">Prepare a comprehensive implementation roadmap for establishment and operation of the Managed SOC.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"825\" data-end=\"855\"><strong data-start=\"825\" data-end=\"855\">3.2 Bid Process Management</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"857\" data-end=\"938\">The PMU shall provide complete support during the procurement process, including:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"940\" data-end=\"970\"><strong data-start=\"940\" data-end=\"970\">3.2.1 Procurement Strategy</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"972\" data-end=\"1033\">Develop the procurement strategy and implementation approach.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1035\" data-end=\"1125\">Recommend appropriate contracting methodology (e.g., EPC, Managed Services, Output-based).</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1127\" data-end=\"1171\">Define project scope and service boundaries.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1173\" data-end=\"1214\"><strong data-start=\"1173\" data-end=\"1214\">3.2.2 Preparation of Tender Documents</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1216\" data-end=\"1316\">Prepare RFP, technical specifications, BoQ, SLAs, KPIs, payment milestones, and contract conditions.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"1318\" data-end=\"1325\">Define:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"1327\" data-end=\"1591\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1rjbw5h\" data-start=\"1327\" data-end=\"1359\">Technical Eligibility Criteria</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"sxcum7\" data-start=\"1360\" data-end=\"1392\">Financial Eligibility Criteria</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"vr0183\" data-start=\"1393\" data-end=\"1417\">Evaluation Methodology</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jqp40o\" data-start=\"1418\" data-end=\"1470\">Bid Security and Performance Security requirements</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1rpyg8q\" data-start=\"1471\" data-end=\"1504\">Service Level Agreements (SLAs)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1qflqnl\" data-start=\"1505\" data-end=\"1539\">Penalty and incentive mechanisms</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1dcc10o\" data-start=\"1540\" data-end=\"1562\">Exit Management Plan</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1n4umf\" data-start=\"1563\" data-end=\"1591\">Transition Management Plan</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1593\" data-end=\"1617\"><strong data-start=\"1593\" data-end=\"1617\">3.2.3 Bid Management</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"1619\" data-end=\"1661\">Publish and manage bid-related activities.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1663\" data-end=\"1699\">Prepare responses to bidder queries.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1701\" data-end=\"1727\">Organize pre-bid meetings.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1729\" data-end=\"1758\">Issue corrigenda and addenda.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1760\" data-end=\"1792\">Assist CHIPS during bid opening.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"1794\" data-end=\"1818\"><strong data-start=\"1794\" data-end=\"1818\">3.2.4 Bid Evaluation</strong></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li data-start=\"1820\" data-end=\"1849\">Develop evaluation templates.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1851\" data-end=\"1880\">Support technical evaluation.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1882\" data-end=\"1930\">Review compliance with technical specifications.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"1932\" data-end=\"2016\">Support Proof of Concept (PoC), presentations, and demonstrations, where applicable.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2018\" data-end=\"2087\">Assist in financial evaluation and preparation of evaluation reports.</li>\r\n<li data-start=\"2089\" data-end=\"2145\">Support contract negotiations and award recommendations.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2147\" data-end=\"2182\"><strong data-start=\"2147\" data-end=\"2182\">3.3 Technical Advisory Services</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2184\" data-end=\"2235\">The PMU shall provide expert technical guidance on:</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2237\" data-end=\"2271\"><strong data-start=\"2237\" data-end=\"2271\">3.3.1 Managed SOC Architecture</strong></p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2273\" data-end=\"2499\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"7m8pcr\" data-start=\"2273\" data-end=\"2302\">SOC architecture and design</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"tz5tq0\" data-start=\"2303\" data-end=\"2342\">SIEM sizing (Events Per Second - EPS)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"11y1582\" data-start=\"2343\" data-end=\"2362\">SOAR architecture</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"d716aq\" data-start=\"2363\" data-end=\"2405\">Threat Intelligence Platform integration</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1jbzjd1\" data-start=\"2406\" data-end=\"2430\">Security orchestration</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"13ipio3\" data-start=\"2431\" data-end=\"2455\">Log retention strategy</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1tve4w9\" data-start=\"2456\" data-end=\"2499\">Disaster Recovery and Business Continuity</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2501\" data-end=\"2532\"><strong data-start=\"2501\" data-end=\"2532\">3.3.2 Technology Validation</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2534\" data-end=\"2595\">Review and validate the proposed technology stack, including:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"2597\" data-end=\"2927\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1j4cn22\" data-start=\"2597\" data-end=\"2603\">SIEM</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1j4crvr\" data-start=\"2604\" data-end=\"2610\">SOAR</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"sc8zcq\" data-start=\"2611\" data-end=\"2620\">XDR/EDR</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1o4cq8\" data-start=\"2621\" data-end=\"2626\">NDR</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"gfz6v0\" data-start=\"2627\" data-end=\"2657\">Threat Intelligence Platform</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1arwir3\" data-start=\"2658\" data-end=\"2684\">Vulnerability Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"pjyecd\" data-start=\"2685\" data-end=\"2717\">Web Application Firewall (WAF)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zgo1c5\" data-start=\"2718\" data-end=\"2754\">Database Activity Monitoring (DAM)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"a1vmxl\" data-start=\"2755\" data-end=\"2791\">Privileged Access Management (PAM)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1in70ob\" data-start=\"2792\" data-end=\"2828\">Identity &amp; Access Management (IAM)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"2e8fii\" data-start=\"2829\" data-end=\"2871\">Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hix7lp\" data-start=\"2872\" data-end=\"2891\">Endpoint Security</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"741tma\" data-start=\"2892\" data-end=\"2908\">Email Security</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4lsko0\" data-start=\"2909\" data-end=\"2927\">Network Security</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"2929\" data-end=\"2957\"><strong data-start=\"2929\" data-end=\"2957\">3.3.3 Security Use Cases</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"2959\" data-end=\"3014\">Review and recommend security monitoring use cases for:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3016\" data-end=\"3251\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1sfcvwk\" data-start=\"3016\" data-end=\"3035\">State Data Centre</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"dkwybz\" data-start=\"3036\" data-end=\"3060\">Disaster Recovery Site</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1i9cx24\" data-start=\"3061\" data-end=\"3088\">Cloud-hosted applications</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"89w5qg\" data-start=\"3089\" data-end=\"3116\">Departmental applications</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15bmvfs\" data-start=\"3117\" data-end=\"3130\">API Gateway</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1w57mf2\" data-start=\"3131\" data-end=\"3142\">Databases</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17nhjod\" data-start=\"3143\" data-end=\"3160\">Network devices</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cirl79\" data-start=\"3161\" data-end=\"3172\">Firewalls</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1o4wkg\" data-start=\"3173\" data-end=\"3178\">VPN</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12m8zvz\" data-start=\"3179\" data-end=\"3195\">Email gateways</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"del5vx\" data-start=\"3196\" data-end=\"3214\">Active Directory</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1bwdg9k\" data-start=\"3215\" data-end=\"3226\">Endpoints</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"601tsw\" data-start=\"3227\" data-end=\"3251\">Citizen-facing portals</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3253\" data-end=\"3283\"><strong data-start=\"3253\" data-end=\"3283\">3.4 Implementation Support</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3285\" data-end=\"3359\">The PMU shall monitor and facilitate implementation activities, including:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3361\" data-end=\"3806\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"srosz2\" data-start=\"3361\" data-end=\"3391\">Review implementation plans.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"s8zxz0\" data-start=\"3392\" data-end=\"3434\">Validate detailed solution architecture.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15s5d9l\" data-start=\"3435\" data-end=\"3463\">Monitor project schedules.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"3wtnqr\" data-start=\"3464\" data-end=\"3499\">Review implementation milestones.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zwcdnw\" data-start=\"3500\" data-end=\"3545\">Facilitate coordination among stakeholders.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1rjfms2\" data-start=\"3546\" data-end=\"3582\">Monitor onboarding of log sources.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6vim3g\" data-start=\"3583\" data-end=\"3658\">Validate integration of all identified security devices and applications.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"12y8zsi\" data-start=\"3659\" data-end=\"3708\">Review configuration of SIEM correlation rules.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"e0inbu\" data-start=\"3709\" data-end=\"3745\">Monitor testing and commissioning.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1l0p7z3\" data-start=\"3746\" data-end=\"3776\">Validate acceptance testing.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6rf9nq\" data-start=\"3777\" data-end=\"3806\">Recommend Go-Live approval.</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"3808\" data-end=\"3834\"><strong data-start=\"3808\" data-end=\"3834\">3.5 Project Governance</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"3836\" data-end=\"3892\">The PMU shall establish a governance framework covering:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"3894\" data-end=\"4096\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1w6erb6\" data-start=\"3894\" data-end=\"3930\">Project Steering Committee support</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"rdfhmn\" data-start=\"3931\" data-end=\"3967\">Weekly and Monthly Review Meetings</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1vk5fqw\" data-start=\"3968\" data-end=\"3985\">Risk Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"zp9k9u\" data-start=\"3986\" data-end=\"4004\">Issue Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"nvbezw\" data-start=\"4005\" data-end=\"4032\">Change Request Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6dus1j\" data-start=\"4033\" data-end=\"4052\">Decision Tracking</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9kh0zi\" data-start=\"4053\" data-end=\"4076\">Escalation Management</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"10rdtii\" data-start=\"4077\" data-end=\"4096\">Quality Assurance</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4098\" data-end=\"4120\">The PMU shall prepare:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4122\" data-end=\"4286\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"jpej29\" data-start=\"4122\" data-end=\"4147\">Weekly Progress Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17ieril\" data-start=\"4148\" data-end=\"4174\">Monthly Progress Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cciiez\" data-start=\"4175\" data-end=\"4201\">Steering Committee Notes</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"10fmsrj\" data-start=\"4202\" data-end=\"4224\">Executive Dashboards</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"15pbqsi\" data-start=\"4225\" data-end=\"4240\">Risk Register</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ymim48\" data-start=\"4241\" data-end=\"4257\">Issue Register</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17ufy8o\" data-start=\"4258\" data-end=\"4286\">Action Taken Reports (ATR)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4288\" data-end=\"4333\"><strong data-start=\"4288\" data-end=\"4333\">3.6 SLA and Vendor Performance Monitoring</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4335\" data-end=\"4357\">The PMU shall monitor:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4359\" data-end=\"4619\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"blrg23\" data-start=\"4359\" data-end=\"4375\">SLA compliance</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1h5eyi0\" data-start=\"4376\" data-end=\"4400\">Incident Response Time</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"yu8qyb\" data-start=\"4401\" data-end=\"4418\">Resolution Time</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"rzv5g9\" data-start=\"4419\" data-end=\"4433\">Availability</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"80023\" data-start=\"4434\" data-end=\"4453\">Device onboarding</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1romid8\" data-start=\"4454\" data-end=\"4475\">False Positive Rate</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"njnmry\" data-start=\"4476\" data-end=\"4504\">Mean Time to Detect (MTTD)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"vf1ydq\" data-start=\"4505\" data-end=\"4534\">Mean Time to Respond (MTTR)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"fu5pdm\" data-start=\"4535\" data-end=\"4562\">Threat Hunting activities</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"jjxazf\" data-start=\"4563\" data-end=\"4600\">Vulnerability remediation timelines</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1mhu0pn\" data-start=\"4601\" data-end=\"4619\">Patch compliance</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"4621\" data-end=\"4699\">The PMU shall recommend penalties and service credits in case of SLA breaches.</p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4701\" data-end=\"4746\"><strong data-start=\"4701\" data-end=\"4746\">3.7 Security Compliance and Audit Support</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"4748\" data-end=\"4785\">The PMU shall ensure compliance with:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"4787\" data-end=\"5080\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"6ax1o4\" data-start=\"4787\" data-end=\"4807\">CERT-In Directions</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1xx7diy\" data-start=\"4808\" data-end=\"4841\">MeitY Cyber Security Guidelines</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"pxzgpb\" data-start=\"4842\" data-end=\"4874\">National Cyber Security Policy</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"oy9tqh\" data-start=\"4875\" data-end=\"4890\">ISO/IEC 27001</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"gmjszz\" data-start=\"4891\" data-end=\"4921\">ISO 27701 (where applicable)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"9cjism\" data-start=\"4922\" data-end=\"4951\">State Cyber Security Policy</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"hku4dc\" data-start=\"4952\" data-end=\"5022\">Digital Personal Data Protection (DPDP) Act, 2023 (where applicable)</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1djvd21\" data-start=\"5023\" data-end=\"5080\">Cloud Security Guidelines issued by Government of India</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5082\" data-end=\"5104\">The PMU shall support:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5106\" data-end=\"5205\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1rp35ev\" data-start=\"5106\" data-end=\"5132\">Internal Security Audits</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"xmiac6\" data-start=\"5133\" data-end=\"5153\">Third-party Audits</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"113f02m\" data-start=\"5154\" data-end=\"5182\">CERT-In Audit observations</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"qq66xn\" data-start=\"5183\" data-end=\"5205\">Compliance reporting</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5207\" data-end=\"5248\"><strong data-start=\"5207\" data-end=\"5248\">3.8 Cloud Security Monitoring Support</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5250\" data-end=\"5310\">The PMU shall ensure that the Managed SOC adequately covers:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5312\" data-end=\"5615\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"w9a0ji\" data-start=\"5312\" data-end=\"5356\">State Government cloud-hosted applications</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"tt2l8z\" data-start=\"5357\" data-end=\"5387\">Private cloud infrastructure</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"4f9bdp\" data-start=\"5388\" data-end=\"5399\">NIC Cloud</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"10krw2b\" data-start=\"5400\" data-end=\"5427\">Hybrid cloud environments</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"7325jw\" data-start=\"5428\" data-end=\"5452\">APIs and microservices</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1cdz1zt\" data-start=\"5453\" data-end=\"5490\">Containers and Kubernetes platforms</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"tz4wbj\" data-start=\"5491\" data-end=\"5509\">Virtual Machines</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"sa8m2j\" data-start=\"5510\" data-end=\"5533\">Cloud-native services</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"ftj8r4\" data-start=\"5534\" data-end=\"5553\">Identity services</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"s98lj7\" data-start=\"5554\" data-end=\"5572\">Cloud audit logs</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"2e8fii\" data-start=\"5573\" data-end=\"5615\">Cloud Security Posture Management (CSPM)</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5617\" data-end=\"5665\"><strong data-start=\"5617\" data-end=\"5665\">3.9 Capacity Building and Knowledge Transfer</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5667\" data-end=\"5681\">The PMU shall:</p>\r\n<ul data-start=\"5683\" data-end=\"5954\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"eu9dm4\" data-start=\"5683\" data-end=\"5732\">Conduct awareness sessions for CHIPS officials.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1brff9y\" data-start=\"5733\" data-end=\"5787\">Train departmental nodal officers on SOC governance.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1kgy1tt\" data-start=\"5788\" data-end=\"5835\">Develop Standard Operating Procedures (SOPs).</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"151n93g\" data-start=\"5836\" data-end=\"5874\">Prepare incident response playbooks.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"78fw0m\" data-start=\"5875\" data-end=\"5905\">Prepare operational manuals.</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"gce0e8\" data-start=\"5906\" data-end=\"5954\">Support transition to BAU (Business as Usual).</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n<p data-start=\"5956\" data-end=\"5992\"><strong data-start=\"5956\" data-end=\"5992\">3.10 Reporting and Documentation</strong></p>\r\n<p data-start=\"5994\" data-end=\"6029\">The PMU shall prepare and maintain:</p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li style=\"list-style-type: none;\">\r\n<ul data-start=\"6031\" data-end=\"6343\">\r\n<li data-section-id=\"bkdyff\" data-start=\"6031\" data-end=\"6049\">Inception Report</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"iol0ot\" data-start=\"6050\" data-end=\"6075\">Project Management Plan</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"cxhoej\" data-start=\"6076\" data-end=\"6098\">Risk Management Plan</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1030aju\" data-start=\"6099\" data-end=\"6122\">Procurement Documents</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"a9f42r\" data-start=\"6123\" data-end=\"6143\">Evaluation Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"17ieril\" data-start=\"6144\" data-end=\"6170\">Monthly Progress Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"10fmsrj\" data-start=\"6171\" data-end=\"6193\">Executive Dashboards</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1pxmqmz\" data-start=\"6194\" data-end=\"6214\">Governance Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1i9grvr\" data-start=\"6215\" data-end=\"6239\">SLA Monitoring Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"1hvvf0q\" data-start=\"6240\" data-end=\"6264\">Incident Trend Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"14hmr21\" data-start=\"6265\" data-end=\"6291\">Security Posture Reports</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"g3k6g5\" data-start=\"6292\" data-end=\"6318\">Go-Live Readiness Report</li>\r\n<li data-section-id=\"begc5e\" data-start=\"6319\" data-end=\"6343\">Project Closure Report</li>\r\n</ul>\r\n</li>\r\n</ul><br>', '2026-07-27 17:04:46', 90, 1, '2026-07-27 17:08:40', 1);
INSERT INTO `log_eoi_updates` (`recordid`, `requestid`, `particular`, `updatedon`, `updatedby`, `isviewed`, `viewedon`, `viewedby`) VALUES
(260, 182, 'Scope of work changed from <h1 style=\"margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933835\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt;\">3.1 Database Admin &ndash;Level 7</span></strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"isselectedend\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The <strong>Database Administrator (DBA)</strong> will be responsible for the installation, configuration, administration, monitoring, performance optimization, backup, recovery, security, and maintenance of enterprise databases supporting the State Portal Project. This role is suitable for experienced professionals who can independently manage production databases, ensure high availability, optimize database performance, and maintain data integrity and security.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933836\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.1.1 Key Responsibilities</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><strong>Database Administration:</strong> Install, configure, administer, and maintain MySQL/PostgreSQL/MariaDB databases across development, testing, and production environments.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></span><strong>Database Performance &amp; Optimization:</strong> Monitor database performance, optimize queries, indexes, stored procedures, and database structures to ensure efficient system performance.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><strong>Backup &amp; Recovery:</strong> Plan, implement, monitor, and periodically test database backup, restoration, disaster recovery, and business continuity procedures.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Database Security:</strong> Implement database security measures including user access control, privilege management, encryption, auditing, and compliance with security best practices.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Database Monitoring &amp; Troubleshooting:</strong> Monitor database health, identify performance bottlenecks, troubleshoot database-related issues, and ensure maximum uptime.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><strong>Database Migration &amp; Deployment:</strong> Perform database installation, migration, upgrades, patch management, replication setup, and deployment activities with minimal downtime.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Documentation:</strong> Prepare and maintain database architecture documents, configuration details, backup procedures, recovery plans, and operational documentation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Work closely with application developers, system administrators, DevOps engineers, and project managers for database design, deployment, and support.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></span><strong>Security &amp; Compliance:</strong> Ensure data integrity, database availability, and compliance with organizational policies and Government security standards.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933837\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.1.2 Requirements</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Bachelor\'s/Master\'s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, MCA, or related field.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Minimum 6 years of professional experience.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp; </span></span></span>Strong knowledge of <strong>MySQL, PostgreSQL, MariaDB, SQL, PL/SQL, database design, indexing, query optimization, replication, backup &amp; recovery, performance tuning, and database security</strong><strong>.</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Experience in database installation, configuration, migration, clustering, high availability, and disaster recovery solutions.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Ability to work independently and manage enterprise database environments.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span></span>The candidate will not be required to work exclusively on a single database platform; however, basic knowledge of other database technologies and readiness to learn emerging database platforms as per project requirements is essential.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>The candidate should also have working knowledge of server-related activities including database deployment, configuration, monitoring, and troubleshooting.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Preference will be given to experienced candidates who have worked in Government Organizations.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933838\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.1.3 Desirable</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo4;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Familiarity with cloud database platforms and containerization technologies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo4;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Knowledge of Linux/Windows server administration and database deployment environments.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo4;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Experience with Git, GitLab, Bitbucket, and database automation tools.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo4;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Understanding of High Availability, replication, clustering, and disaster recovery architecture.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo4;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Understanding of Agile/Scrum methodologies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo4;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Strong communication skills in English and Hindi.</p>\r\n<h1 style=\"margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933839\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt;\">3.2 Graphic Designer&ndash;Level 6</span></strong></h1>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The <strong>Graphic Designer</strong> will be <a name=\"_Toc234933843\"></a>responsible for creating intuitive, user-centered design solutions that enhance the usability and user experience of web and mobile applications. The role involves collaborating closely with UI designers, developers, project managers, and stakeholders to gather requirements, conduct user research, and translate insights into wireframes, prototypes, and user flows.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\">The ideal candidate is creative, detail-oriented, and passionate about improving user experience through thoughtful design and usability practices.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><a name=\"_Toc195092065\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.6.1 Key Responsibilities</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo7; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>User Research</strong>: Conduct user research, interviews, surveys, and usability tests to understand user needs and behaviours.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo7; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Wire framing &amp; Prototyping</strong>: Create wireframes, mockups, and interactive prototypes using tools like Figma, Adobe XD, or Sketch.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo7; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>User Journey Mapping</strong>: Develop user personas, journey maps, and user flows to guide design decisions.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo7; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Collaboration</strong>: Work closely with UI designers, developers, and project teams to ensure seamless user experience integration.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo7; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Feedback &amp; Testing</strong>: Incorporate feedback from stakeholders and users to refine designs; conduct A/B testing where applicable.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo7; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Design Documentation</strong>: Prepare design specifications and documentation to support development teams.</span></p>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><a name=\"_Toc195092066\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.6.2 Requirements</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 115%; mso-list: l8 level1 lfo8; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></span>Bachelor\'s or Master&rsquo;s Degree in Computer Science<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span>or<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span>Bacorhelor&rsquo;s/Master&rsquo;s Degree in Design, Human-Computer Interaction (HCI),&nbsp; &nbsp; Computer Science, or a related field.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 115%; mso-list: l8 level1 lfo8; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->5 years of experience in UX/UI design or a similar role.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 115%; mso-pagination: none; mso-list: l8 level1 lfo8; tab-stops: list 36.0pt; text-autospace: none; margin: 3.45pt 5.85pt .0001pt 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Preference<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>will<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>be<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>given<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>to<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>experienced<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>candidates<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>of<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>work in Govt.<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>Organization.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 115%; mso-list: l8 level1 lfo8; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Proficient in UX/UI tools such as Figma, Adobe XD, Sketch, InVision, or Balsamiq.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 115%; mso-list: l8 level1 lfo8; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Understanding of design principles, responsive design, accessibility, and user-centered methodologies.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 115%; mso-list: l8 level1 lfo8; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Familiarity with HTML/CSS is a plus (for effective developer communication).</span></p>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><a name=\"_Toc195092067\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.6.3 Desirable</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo9; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Basic understanding of UX/UI design and visual design principles.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo9; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Experience working on government, enterprise, or public-facing applications.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo9; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Strong communication and presentation skills in<strong> </strong>English and Hindi.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"isselectedend\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt;\">&nbsp;</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"isselectedend\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt;\">3.3 Assistant Manager &ndash; Level 4</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"isselectedend\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Assistant Manager will be responsible for assisting in the overall coordination, monitoring, documentation, and administrative management of the State Portal Project. The role involves maintaining project records and files, preparing official correspondence and reports, monitoring project progress, and ensuring timely execution of project activities in accordance with Government procedures. This role is suitable for experienced professionals who can independently handle project coordination, documentation, stakeholder communication, and administrative functions while supporting the successful implementation of the State Portal Project.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933844\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.3.1 Key Responsibilities</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;</span></span></span><strong>Project Coordination:</strong> Coordinate with Government Departments, District Administrations, vendors, and technical teams for implementation, maintenance, and enhancement of the State Portal.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span></span><strong>File Management:</strong> Process and maintain project files, official records, correspondence, approvals, office notes, and related documentation in accordance with Government procedures.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Documentation:</strong> Prepare and maintain DPRs, TORs, proposals, meeting minutes, technical notes, project reports, presentations, utilization reports, and other project-related documents.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span></span><strong>Administrative Support:</strong> Assist in processing administrative and financial proposals, manpower deployment, contract-related documents, and other official matters pertaining to the project.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Monitoring &amp; Reporting:</strong> Monitor project progress, timelines, milestones, resource deployment, and deliverables, and prepare periodic progress reports for higher authorities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Compliance:</strong> Ensure project documentation and activities comply with Government rules, departmental guidelines, contractual obligations, and applicable standards.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Meeting Coordination:</strong> Organize meetings, prepare agendas, record minutes of meetings (MoMs), and follow up on action points with concerned stakeholders.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Support to Management:</strong> Provide administrative and coordination support to senior officers in project planning, review meetings, and decision-making processes.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933845\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.3.2 Requirements</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span></span>Bachelor\'s/Master\'s degree in Engineering (B.E./B.Tech.) in any discipline, MBA, Management, or any other equivalent professional qualification from a recognized University/Institution.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Minimum<strong> </strong>4 years of professional experience.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Experience in project coordination, Government correspondence, file processing, documentation, report preparation, and stakeholder management.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Working knowledge of MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), project documentation, and office management practices.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp; </span></span></span>Ability to independently handle official correspondence, prepare reports, maintain project records, and coordinate with multiple stakeholders.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Basic understanding of e-Governance projects, website management will be preferred.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Preference will be given to candidates having experience of working in Government Organizations or Government IT/e-Governance projects.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933846\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.3.3 Desirable</span></h2>\r\n<ul style=\"margin-top: 0cm;\" type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 115%; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">Experience in handling Government files, official noting and drafting, DPR preparation, and procurement-related documentation.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 115%; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">Knowledge of Government administrative procedures, project monitoring.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 115%; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">Familiarity with project management and documentation tools.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 115%; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">Understanding of e-Governance initiatives and digital service delivery frameworks.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 115%; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">Strong communication, drafting, presentation, and interpersonal skills in English and Hindi.</li>\r\n</ul> to <h1 style=\"margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933835\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt;\">3.1 Database Admin &ndash;Level 7</span></strong></h1>\r\n<p class=\"isselectedend\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The <strong>Database Administrator (DBA)</strong> will be responsible for the installation, configuration, administration, monitoring, performance optimization, backup, recovery, security, and maintenance of enterprise databases supporting the State Portal Project. This role is suitable for experienced professionals who can independently manage production databases, ensure high availability, optimize database performance, and maintain data integrity and security.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933836\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.1.1 Key Responsibilities</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><strong>Database Administration:</strong> Install, configure, administer, and maintain MySQL/PostgreSQL/MariaDB databases across development, testing, and production environments.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></span><strong>Database Performance &amp; Optimization:</strong> Monitor database performance, optimize queries, indexes, stored procedures, and database structures to ensure efficient system performance.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><strong>Backup &amp; Recovery:</strong> Plan, implement, monitor, and periodically test database backup, restoration, disaster recovery, and business continuity procedures.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Database Security:</strong> Implement database security measures including user access control, privilege management, encryption, auditing, and compliance with security best practices.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Database Monitoring &amp; Troubleshooting:</strong> Monitor database health, identify performance bottlenecks, troubleshoot database-related issues, and ensure maximum uptime.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><strong>Database Migration &amp; Deployment:</strong> Perform database installation, migration, upgrades, patch management, replication setup, and deployment activities with minimal downtime.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Documentation:</strong> Prepare and maintain database architecture documents, configuration details, backup procedures, recovery plans, and operational documentation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Work closely with application developers, system administrators, DevOps engineers, and project managers for database design, deployment, and support.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l7 level1 lfo2;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></span><strong>Security &amp; Compliance:</strong> Ensure data integrity, database availability, and compliance with organizational policies and Government security standards.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933837\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.1.2 Requirements</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Bachelor\'s/Master\'s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, MCA, or related field.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Minimum 6 years of professional experience.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp; </span></span></span>Strong knowledge of <strong>MySQL, PostgreSQL, MariaDB, SQL, PL/SQL, database design, indexing, query optimization, replication, backup &amp; recovery, performance tuning, and database security</strong><strong>.</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Experience in database installation, configuration, migration, clustering, high availability, and disaster recovery solutions.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Ability to work independently and manage enterprise database environments.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span></span>The candidate will not be required to work exclusively on a single database platform; however, basic knowledge of other database technologies and readiness to learn emerging database platforms as per project requirements is essential.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>The candidate should also have working knowledge of server-related activities including database deployment, configuration, monitoring, and troubleshooting.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l5 level1 lfo3;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Preference will be given to experienced candidates who have worked in Government Organizations.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933838\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.1.3 Desirable</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo4;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Familiarity with cloud database platforms and containerization technologies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo4;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Knowledge of Linux/Windows server administration and database deployment environments.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo4;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Experience with Git, GitLab, Bitbucket, and database automation tools.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo4;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Understanding of High Availability, replication, clustering, and disaster recovery architecture.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo4;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Understanding of Agile/Scrum methodologies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo4;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Strong communication skills in English and Hindi.</p>\r\n<h1 style=\"margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933839\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.5pt;\">3.2 Graphic Designer&ndash;Level 6</span></strong></h1>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\">The <strong>Graphic Designer</strong> will be <a name=\"_Toc234933843\"></a>responsible for creating intuitive, user-centered design solutions that enhance the usability and user experience of web and mobile applications. The role involves collaborating closely with UI designers, developers, project managers, and stakeholders to gather requirements, conduct user research, and translate insights into wireframes, prototypes, and user flows.</p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\">The ideal candidate is creative, detail-oriented, and passionate about improving user experience through thoughtful design and usability practices.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\">&nbsp;</span></p>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><a name=\"_Toc195092065\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.6.1 Key Responsibilities</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo7; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>User Research</strong>: Conduct user research, interviews, surveys, and usability tests to understand user needs and behaviours.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo7; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Wire framing &amp; Prototyping</strong>: Create wireframes, mockups, and interactive prototypes using tools like Figma, Adobe XD, or Sketch.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo7; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>User Journey Mapping</strong>: Develop user personas, journey maps, and user flows to guide design decisions.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo7; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Collaboration</strong>: Work closely with UI designers, developers, and project teams to ensure seamless user experience integration.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo7; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Feedback &amp; Testing</strong>: Incorporate feedback from stakeholders and users to refine designs; conduct A/B testing where applicable.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l2 level1 lfo7; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Design Documentation</strong>: Prepare design specifications and documentation to support development teams.</span></p>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><a name=\"_Toc195092066\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.6.2 Requirements</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 115%; mso-list: l8 level1 lfo8; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></span>Bachelor\'s or Master&rsquo;s Degree in Computer Science<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span>or<span style=\"mso-spacerun: yes;\">&nbsp; </span>Bacorhelor&rsquo;s/Master&rsquo;s Degree in Design, Computer Science, or a related field.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 115%; mso-list: l8 level1 lfo8; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->5 years of experience in UX/UI design or a similar role.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoBodyText\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 115%; mso-pagination: none; mso-list: l8 level1 lfo8; tab-stops: list 36.0pt; text-autospace: none; margin: 3.45pt 5.85pt .0001pt 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Preference<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>will<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>be<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>given<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>to<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>experienced<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>candidates<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>of<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>work in Govt.<span style=\"letter-spacing: .05pt;\"> </span>Organization.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 115%; mso-list: l8 level1 lfo8; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Proficient in UX/UI tools such as Figma, Adobe XD, Sketch, InVision, or Balsamiq.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 115%; mso-list: l8 level1 lfo8; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Understanding of design principles, responsive design, accessibility, and user-centered methodologies.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; line-height: 115%; mso-list: l8 level1 lfo8; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Familiarity with HTML/CSS is a plus (for effective developer communication).</span></p>\r\n<h3 style=\"text-align: justify;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><a name=\"_Toc195092067\"></a><strong><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.6.3 Desirable</span></strong></span></h3>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo9; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Basic understanding of UX/UI design and visual design principles.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo9; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Experience working on government, enterprise, or public-facing applications.</span></p>\r\n<p style=\"margin-left: 36.0pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l1 level1 lfo9; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-size: 10.0pt; mso-bidi-font-size: 12.0pt; font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Strong communication and presentation skills in<strong> </strong>English and Hindi.</span></p>\r\n<p class=\"isselectedend\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt;\">&nbsp;</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"isselectedend\"><span style=\"mso-bookmark: _Toc234933843;\"><strong><span style=\"font-size: 13.5pt;\">3.3 Assistant Manager &ndash; Level 4</span></strong></span></p>\r\n<p class=\"isselectedend\" style=\"text-align: justify;\">The Assistant Manager will be responsible for assisting in the overall coordination, monitoring, documentation, and administrative management of the State Portal Project. The role involves maintaining project records and files, preparing official correspondence and reports, monitoring project progress, and ensuring timely execution of project activities in accordance with Government procedures. This role is suitable for experienced professionals who can independently handle project coordination, documentation, stakeholder communication, and administrative functions while supporting the successful implementation of the State Portal Project.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933844\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.3.1 Key Responsibilities</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;</span></span></span><strong>Project Coordination:</strong> Coordinate with Government Departments, District Administrations, vendors, and technical teams for implementation, maintenance, and enhancement of the State Portal.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span></span><strong>File Management:</strong> Process and maintain project files, official records, correspondence, approvals, office notes, and related documentation in accordance with Government procedures.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Documentation:</strong> Prepare and maintain DPRs, TORs, proposals, meeting minutes, technical notes, project reports, presentations, utilization reports, and other project-related documents.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span></span><strong>Administrative Support:</strong> Assist in processing administrative and financial proposals, manpower deployment, contract-related documents, and other official matters pertaining to the project.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Monitoring &amp; Reporting:</strong> Monitor project progress, timelines, milestones, resource deployment, and deliverables, and prepare periodic progress reports for higher authorities.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Compliance:</strong> Ensure project documentation and activities comply with Government rules, departmental guidelines and applicable standards.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Meeting Coordination:</strong> Organize meetings, prepare agendas, record minutes of meetings (MoMs), and follow up on action points.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l6 level1 lfo5;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Support to Management:</strong> Provide administrative and coordination support to senior officers in project planning, review meetings, and decision-making processes.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933845\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.3.2 Requirements</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span></span>Bachelor\'s/Master\'s degree in Engineering (B.E./B.Tech.) in any discipline, MBA, Management, or any other equivalent professional qualification from a recognized University/Institution.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Minimum<strong> </strong>4 years of professional experience.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Experience in project coordination, Government correspondence, file processing, documentation, report preparation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></span>Working knowledge of MS Office (Word, Excel, PowerPoint), project documentation, and office management practices.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></span>Ability to independently handle official correspondence, prepare reports, maintain project records, and coordinate with team.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;</span></span></span>Basic understanding of e-Governance projects, website management will be preferred.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l4 level1 lfo6;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span>Preference will be given to candidates having experience of working in Government Organizations or Government IT/e-Governance projects.</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><a name=\"_Toc234933846\"></a><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">3.3.3 Desirable</span></h2>\r\n<ul style=\"margin-top: 0cm;\" type=\"disc\">\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 115%; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">Experience in handling Government files, official noting and drafting, DPR preparation, and procurement-related documentation.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 115%; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">Knowledge of Government administrative procedures, project monitoring.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 115%; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">Familiarity with project management and documentation tools.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 115%; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">Understanding of e-Governance initiatives and digital service delivery frameworks.</li>\r\n<li class=\"MsoNormal\" style=\"line-height: 115%; mso-list: l3 level1 lfo1; tab-stops: list 36.0pt;\">Strong communication, drafting, presentation, and interpersonal skills in English and Hindi.</li>\r\n</ul><br>', '2026-09-03 15:32:02', 60, 1, '2026-09-03 16:39:31', 1);
INSERT INTO `log_eoi_updates` (`recordid`, `requestid`, `particular`, `updatedon`, `updatedby`, `isviewed`, `viewedon`, `viewedby`) VALUES
(261, 182, 'The following details were updated for the resource <br>Qualification changed from <p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Bachelor\'s/Master\'s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, MCA, or related field.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Minimum <strong>6 years</strong> of professional experience.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"> &nbsp; </span></span></span>Strong knowledge of <strong>MySQL, PostgreSQL, MariaDB, SQL, PL/SQL, database design, indexing, query optimization, replication, backup &amp; recovery, performance tuning, and database security</strong><strong>.</strong></p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Experience in database installation, configuration, migration, clustering, high availability, and disaster recovery solutions.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Ability to work independently and manage enterprise database environments.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->The candidate will not be required to work exclusively on a single database platform; however, basic knowledge of other database technologies and readiness to learn emerging database platforms as per project requirements is essential.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->The candidate should also have working knowledge of server-related activities including database deployment, configuration, monitoring, and troubleshooting.</p> to <p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Bachelor\'s/Master\'s degree in Computer Science, Information Technology, MCA, or related field from a recognized University/Institution.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Minimum <strong>6 years</strong> of professional experience.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;<span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Calibri\',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-font-family: Mangal; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\"> Strong knowledge of MySQL, PostgreSQL, MariaDB, SQL, PL/SQL, database design, indexing, query optimization, replication, backup &amp; recovery, performance tuning and database security. </span></span></span></span></p>\r\n<ul>\r\n<li class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"text-align: justify; text-indent: -18pt;\"><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-weight: bold;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\"><span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"><span lang=\"EN-US\" style=\"font-size: 11.0pt; line-height: 115%; font-family: \'Calibri\',sans-serif; mso-ascii-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-fareast-font-family: Calibri; mso-fareast-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-hansi-theme-font: minor-latin; mso-bidi-font-family: Mangal; mso-bidi-theme-font: minor-bidi; mso-ansi-language: EN-US; mso-fareast-language: EN-US; mso-bidi-language: AR-SA;\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;Experience in database installation, configuration, migration, clustering, high availability and disaster recovery solutions.</span></span></span></span></li>\r\n</ul>.<br>Remark changed from <h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">Key Responsibilities</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Database Administration:</strong> Install, configure, administer, and maintain MySQL/PostgreSQL/MariaDB databases across development, testing, and production environments.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Database Performance &amp; Optimization:</strong> Monitor database performance, optimize queries, indexes, stored procedures, and database structures to ensure efficient system performance.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Backup &amp; Recovery:</strong> Plan, implement, monitor, and periodically test database backup, restoration, disaster recovery, and business continuity procedures.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Database Security:</strong> Implement database security measures including user access control, privilege management, encryption, auditing, and compliance with security best practices.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Database Monitoring &amp; Troubleshooting:</strong> Monitor database health, identify performance bottlenecks, troubleshoot database-related issues, and ensure maximum uptime.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Database Migration &amp; Deployment:</strong> Perform database installation, migration, upgrades, patch management, replication setup, and deployment activities with minimal downtime.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp; &nbsp; &nbsp;</span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Documentation:</strong> Prepare and maintain database architecture documents, configuration details, backup procedures, recovery plans, and operational documentation.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Collaboration:</strong> Work closely with application developers, system administrators, DevOps engineers, and project managers for database design, deployment, and support.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]--><strong>Security &amp; Compliance:</strong> Ensure data integrity, database availability, and compliance with organizational policies and Government security standards.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-align: justify; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\">&nbsp;</p>\r\n<h2 style=\"text-indent: 0cm; line-height: normal; margin: 10.4pt 0cm .0001pt 0cm;\"><span style=\"font-size: 12.0pt;\">Desirable</span></h2>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Familiarity with cloud database platforms and containerization technologies.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Knowledge of Linux/Windows server administration and database deployment environments.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\">&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp;&nbsp; </span></span></span><!--[endif]-->Experience with Git, GitLab, Bitbucket, and database automation tools.</p>\r\n<p class=\"MsoListParagraph\" style=\"mso-margin-top-alt: auto; mso-margin-bottom-alt: auto; margin-left: 35.45pt; text-indent: -18.0pt; mso-list: l0 level1 lfo1;\"><!-- [if !supportLists]--><span style=\"font-family: Symbol; mso-fareast-font-family: Symbol; mso-bidi-font-family: Symbol;\"><span style=\"mso-list: Ignore;\">&middot;<span style=\"font: 7.0pt \'Times New Roman\';\"